PVD("indonesia_ndp_2020-2024",{"docs":["","INDO NDP 2020 2024","INDO NDP 2020 24 Bahasa"],"s":{"1":[[1,"26","9","Bureaucratic Reform for High-Quality Public Services","Reforming the bureaucracy to ensure high-quality public services;",""],[1,"53","3","Community-Based Policy Planning and Formulation","Local knowledge, local wisdom, and public social institutions as the embodiment of communal socio- cultural values must be considered in the process of planning and formulating national development policies and programs.",""],[1,"273","12","Civil Service Merit System Expansion and Echelon Simplification","Furthermore, five-levels echelon system makes decision- making process is inefficient, therefore it is necessary to simplify the",""],[1,"282","6","State Civil Apparatus Management Reform","Strengthening the management of the state civil apparatus, or ASN, by applying ASN national talent management, enhancing the ASN merit system, simplifying bureaucracy echelon system, and improving functional jobs and positions;",""],[1,"282","8","Performance Accountability System Reform","3. Reforming the performance accountability system by expanding",""],[1,"282","9","Integrity System and Bureaucratic Reform Strengthening","the implementation of the integrity system, strengthening the management of bureaucratic reforms, and the accountability of organizational performance, as well as reforming the planning and budgeting system;",""],[1,"293","20","Revision of National Social Security Board Regulations","Revision of Perpres No. 46/2014 on organizational structure and procedures regarding work, appointment, replacement, and dismissal of members of the national social security board.",""],[1,"296","2","Draft Presidential Regulation on Merit System Sanctions","a. Perpres draft on sanctions against staffing officers who violate the principle of the merit system in the management of the state civil apparatus.",""],[1,"296","4","Institutional Framework for Development Program Delivery","The policy focus of the institutional framework in the 2020-2024 RPJMN is aimed at government organizations, and is concerned with the formulation of duties, functions, authorities, roles, and structures, as described in the framework for the implementation of 2020-2024 RPJMN (see Figure 9.1).",""],[1,"296","7","Grand Design for Bureaucratic Institutional Reform Draft Presidential Regulation","Perpres draft on the grand design for bureaucratic institutional reform.",""],[1,"297","19","Institutional Framework Feasibility Analysis","To ensure that the institutional framework supports the implementation of the 2020- 2024 RPJMN, a number of stages of feasibility analysis needs to be carried out.",""],[2,"257","5","Civil Service Merit System Strengthening","Selanjutnya, hirarki eselonisasi saat ini terdiri dari 5 level membuat proses pengambilan keputusan tidak efisien, sehingga perlu penyederhanaan eselonisasi serta perluasan jabatan fungsional dengan keahlian dan kompetensi yang semakin spesifik.",""],[2,"257","5","ASN Competency and Education Improvement","Dari sisi kompetensi, jumlah tenaga spesialis di lingkungan ASN masih kurang, serta rendahnya kompetensi dan tingkat pendidikan ASN, terutama di luar Jawa.",""],[2,"257","5","Merit-Based ASN Distribution Reform","Dari sisi distribusi, persebaran ASN dengan keahlian tertentu/fungsional belum berbasiskan sektor unggulan kewilayahan.",""],[2,"257","5","Civil Service Political Interference Reduction","Selain itu, masih terdapat intervensi politik terutama dari Kepala Daerah dalam pengelolaan kepegawaian.",""],[2,"257","5","ASN Welfare and Pension System Improvement","Dari sisi kesejahteraan, perlu terus diupayakan perbaikan sistem kesejahteraan ASN dan pensiunan ASN.",""],[2,"257","5","Implementing Regulation Acceleration for ASN Law","Dari aspek regulasi, perlu percepatan penerbitan peraturan pelaksana UU No.5/2014 tentang ASN.",""],[2,"265","10","Civil Service Management Strengthening","Penguatan implementasi manajemen ASN, melalui: penerapan manajemen talenta nasional ASN, peningkatan sistem merit ASN, penyederhanaan eselonisasi, serta penataan jabatan fungsional;",""],[2,"277","24","Presidential Regulation on Sanctions for Merit System Violations in Civil Service Management","RPerpres tentang Ketentuan Sanksi bagi Pejabat Pembina Kepegawaian atas pelanggaran prinsip sistem merit dalam manajemen Aparatur Sipil Negara",""]],"2":[[1,"26","18","Justice System Improvement and Cybersecurity Governance Reform","Improving the justice system, and structuring regulations and governance over cyber security;",""],[1,"62","5","Strengthening NSOC-SOC and Establishing CSIRTs","Strengthening NSOC-SOC and establishing 121 CSIRT",""],[1,"281","5","Restorative Justice Implementation Framework","Implementing restorative justice approach by optimizing the use of regulations that are stipulated in legislation that supports restorative justice; by optimizing the role of traditional institutions and institutions that administer alternative dispute resolution proceedings; by prioritizing efforts to provide rehabilitation, compensation and restitution for victims, including victims of human rights violations;",""],[1,"281","6","Legal Sector IT Support and Data Sharing System","IT support in the legal field through the provision, management, and sharing of data between law enforcers, including to strengthen database management in each law enforcement agency;",""],[1,"281","7","Judicial Competence and Integrity Improvement Programme","Improving the competence and integrity of judges through education and training, public education, and improving use of IT on Judges supervision.",""],[1,"281","9","Corruption Prevention Actions Implementation","Strengthening corruption prevention efforts, through the implementation of corruption prevention actions in accordance with the national strategy for corruption prevention;",""],[1,"281","10","Asset Recovery and Management Mechanism for Corruption Proceeds","Optimizing the mechanism of recovery and management in the judicial system as a whole of assets resulting from corruption and utilizing these assets to support national development.",""],[1,"281","12","Justice Services Strengthening and Legal Aid Expansion","Strengthening justice services for the public by improving the quality of legal aid services, of formal and informal mechanisms, and expanding the affordability of justice services;",""],[1,"281","13","Legal Empowerment and Access to Justice Initiative","Legal empowerment for the public by increasing public understanding of the law and public access to justice, and build community capacity and encourage the community to take an active role in utilizing mechanisms and services for and by the people in an effort to obtain legal certainty.",""],[1,"293","5","Proper Accommodation for Persons with Disabilities in Law Enforcement Draft Policy","PP draft on proper accommodation for persons with disabilities in law enforcement.",""],[1,"295","14","Ombudsman Law Revision","Revision of Law No. 37/2008 on the Ombudsman of the Republic of Indonesia.",""],[1,"295","18","Narcotics Law Revision","Revision of Law No. 35/2009 on narcotics.",""],[1,"295","19","Revision of Law No. 12/2011 on Forming Regulations","Revision of Law No. 12/2011 on forming regulations.",""],[1,"295","20","Bankruptcy Law Revision","Revision of Law No. 37/2004 on bankruptcy and suspension of debt payment obligations.",""],[1,"295","22","Draft Civil Procedure Bill for Localized Regulations","Draft bill on civil procedures in the following localized regulations: HIR, RBg and Rv.",""],[1,"295","24","Revision of Criminal Procedure Law","Revision of Law No. 8/1981 on criminal procedures.",""],[2,"264","10","Legal Substantive Reform Package","Pembaruan substansi hukum, antara lain perubahan KUHP, KUHAP, KUHAPer, regulasi terkait badan usaha, jaminan benda bergerak, hukum perdata internasional, dan kepailitan.",""],[2,"264","12","Economic Law Reform for Ease of Doing Business","Penyempurnaan Hukum Ekonomi yang Mendukung Kemudahan Berusaha, melalui penyusunan regulasi yang mendukung kemudahan berusaha, penguatan sistem berbasis TI dalam pelayanan dan penanganan permasalahan perdata, dan penguatan kelembagaan yang mendukung pelaksanaan eksekusi putusan pengadilan.",""],[2,"264","13","Restorative Justice Implementation Approach","Penerapan Pendekatan Keadilan Restoratif, melalui optimalisasi penggunaan regulasi yang tersedia dalam peraturan perundang-undangan yang mendukung Keadilan Restoratif, optimalisasi peran lembaga adat dan lembaga yang terkait dengan alternatif penyelesaian sengketa, mengedepankan upaya pemberian rehabilitasi, kompensasi, dan restitusi bagi korban, termasuk korban pelanggaran hak asasi manusia;",""],[2,"264","14","IT Support for Legal and Judicial Data Sharing","Dukungan TI di bidang hukum dan peradilan, melalui penyediaan, pengelolaan serta berbagi pakai data antar penegak hukum, termasuk di dalamnya penguatan pengelolaan database di internal lembaga penegak hukum;",""],[2,"264","15","Judicial Quality and Integrity Improvement Programme","Peningkatan kualitas dan integritas hakim melalui pendidikan dan pelatihan, edukasi publik, dan peningkatan teknologi informasi dalam pengawasan hakim.",""],[2,"265","3","Justice Service Strengthening and Legal Aid Expansion","Penguatan layanan keadilan bagi seluruh kelompok masyarakat dalam bentuk peningkatan pelayanan bantuan hukum yang berkualitas, peningkatan mekanisme formal dan informal yang berkualitas, serta perluasan keterjangkauan layanan keadilan;",""],[2,"265","4","Legal Empowerment and Access to Justice Capacity Building","Pemberdayaan hukum bagi masyarakat dalam bentuk peningkatan kemampuan masyarakat dalam memahami hukum dan mengakses keadilan, serta membangun kapasitas masyarakat untuk berperan aktif menggunakan mekanisme dan layanan dari dan untuk masyarakat dalam upaya memperoleh kepastian hukum.",""],[2,"277","18","Revision of the Bankruptcy and Debt Payment Suspension Law","Revisi UU Nomor 37 Tahun 2004 tentang Kepailitan dan Penundaan Kewajiban Pembayaran Utang",""],[2,"277","21","Revision of the Criminal Procedure Code Law","12) Revisi UU Nomor 8 Tahun 1981 tentang Hukum Acara Pidana",""]],"3":[[1,"48","6","Stakeholder Coordination for Development Financing","The participation of various stakeholders is encouraged and synergized to strengthen the utilization of development funding.",""],[1,"48","6","Private and State-Owned Enterprise Growth Mobilization","The central and regional governments are directed toward providing basic services to citizens, while business entities, both BUMN and private, are focused on strengthening economic growth and achieving development targets.",""],[1,"95","7","Strengthening Overseas Economic Representation and Promotion","it is imperative to strengthen representatives of tourism, trade, and investment abroad; integrate promotion events, and expand Indonesia's active participation in international organizations and initiatives, including ASEAN, the World Trade Organization (WTO), Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation (APEC), Belt Road Initiatives (BRI), Organization for Economic Co- operation and Development (OECD),",""],[1,"117","8","Local Government and Development Partner Cooperation Framework","Expanding cooperation, partnerships, and collaboration between local governments and development partners in public services, natural resource and environmental management, financing and investment development, problem-solving pertaining to public issues, and developing regional competitiveness and innovation.",""],[2,"282","2","Development Financing Framework","Dalam upaya mengoptimalkan dan mensinergikan pemanfaatan sumber-sumber pendanaan pembangunan diperlukan adanya kerangka pendanaan yang mencakup sumber pendanaan, arah pemanfaatan, dan prinsip pelaksanaan pendanaan pembangunan.",""],[2,"282","9","External Loan Financing for Priority Spending and On-Lending","Pinjaman Luar Negeri dapat digunakan untuk membiayai defisit APBN dan kegiatan prioritas Kementerian/Lembaga (K/L); mengelola portofolio utang; diteruspinjamkan kepada Pemerintah Daerah (Pemda) dan BUMN; dan dihibahkan kepada Pemda dengan fokus pembiayaan pada infrastruktur ekonomi dan sosial dengan alih teknologi; praktik baik internasional dan berbagi pengetahuan; proyek piloting yang dapat dilakukan replikasi dengan pendanaan rupiah; serta memiliki daya ungkit yang tinggi.",""],[2,"283","8","Business Entity Investment Financing","Pendanaan Badan Usaha dalam bentuk penanaman modal baik dalam negeri maupun asing yang berasal dari kekayaan badan usaha yang bersangkutan maupun yang diperoleh dari pinjaman lembaga keuangan.",""],[2,"289","4","Creative Financing Development","Pengembangan potensi ruang/ sumber pendanaan baru dilakukan dengan mengembangkan pendanaan kreatif (creative financing).",""],[2,"289","5","Non-Conventional Public Financing Mobilization","Pemerintah dapat melakukan eksplorasi dan memaksimalkan pemanfaatan sumber pendanaan baru dari sumber pendanaan non-konvensional.",""],[2,"289","6","Green Funding and Blended Finance for Public Investment","Pemerintah juga dapat mengandalkan dan mengembangkan pendanaan hijau (green funding) di masa depan.",""],[2,"290","3","Direct Lending for Priority Activities and SOE Capitalization","Pemanfaatan pinjaman langsung (direct lending) diarahkan untuk mengurangi beban pinjaman Pemerintah.",""],[2,"291","2","Private Investment Enabling Framework","Pemerintah juga akan menetapkan syarat dan kondisi serta kerangka kerja dimana investasi swasta diharapkan berperan lebih besar, bahkan melebihi pembiayaan Pemerintah seperti misalnya di sektor energi.",""],[2,"291","2","International Support for Finance, Clean Technology, Capacity, and Governance","dukungan dan kerjasama internasional dalam hal akses keuangan, akses ke teknologi bersih, peningkatan kapasitas dan tatakelola akan tetap diperlukan.",""],[2,"291","4","Priority-Based Development Financing Allocation","Mengalokasikan sumber dana yang terbatas dengan mendahulukan kegiatan atau proyek yang menjadi prioritas nasional khususnya Proyek Prioritas Strategis (Major Project).",""],[2,"291","5","Integrated Development Financing Coordination","Memperkuat sinergi dan integrasi pendanaan pembangunan dengan mensinergikan dan mengintegrasikan pemanfaatan belanja K/L dan Non K/L (antara lain Subsidi, Dana Transfer Khusus, dan Dana Desa) serta sumber pendanaan lainnya, baik pusat, daerah maupun swasta untuk mendukung pembiayaan prioritas nasional.",""],[2,"291","6","National Development Project Coordination and Task-Sharing Framework","Untuk itu, dalam pelaksanaan proyek pembangunan diperlukan identifikasi serta pembagian tugas, kewenangan dan tanggung jawab antara Pemerintah Pusat, Pemerintah Daerah, BUMN, swasta dan masyarakat.",""],[2,"291","7","Alignment of Financing Modalities with Development Goals","Menyesuaikan modalitas pendanaan dengan sasaran pembangunan serta memastikan kesiapan pelaksanaan proyek.",""],[2,"292","2","Optimization of External Loan Utilization","dari pinjaman luar negeri dapat dioptimalkan melalui pemanfaatan pinjaman dari lembaga pembiayaan pembangunan dan pemanfaatan skema pendanaan kerjasama pembangunan, serta fasilitas pembiayaan luar negeri lainnya dengan persyaratan yang menguntungkan.",""],[2,"292","4","Expansion of Thematic and Green Financing Schemes","Pemerintah dapat memperbesar pemanfaatan skema-skema pembiayaan yang bersumber dari berbagai skema pembiayaan tematik (thematic financing windows) termasuk di dalamnya adalah skema pembiayaan hijau (green financing).",""],[2,"292","4","Mobilization of Public Leverage and Private Investment for Development","Selain menjadi sumber, skema-skema pembiayaan ini juga membantu Pemerintah untuk memaksimalkan daya ungkit (leverage) sumber dana publik dan mendatangkan investasi swasta dalam pembangunan.",""],[2,"292","5","Development Financing Innovation Measures","Dalam rangka mendorong inovasi pendanaan pembangunan, maka perlu dilakukan:",""],[2,"292","6","Blended Finance Implementation and Development Measures","Dalam pelaksanaan dan pengembangan bauran pembiayaan (blended finance) tersebut diperlukan beberapa langkah diantaranya:",""],[2,"292","7","Legal and Regulatory Framework for Innovative Financing","Menyediakan dan menyempurnakan kerangka hukum dan peraturan sebagai dasar inovasi pendanaan.",""],[2,"292","8","Government Financing as a Catalyst for Non-Government Funding","Memposisikan pembiayaan Pemerintah sebagai pengungkit (leveraging) dan katalisator untuk mengembangkan sumber pendanaan non-Pemerintah;",""],[2,"292","9","Mobilization of Non-Government Financing Sources","Mengutamakan penggunaan sumber-sumber pendanaan non-Pemerintah sesuai dengan kelayakan finansial, ekonomi, dan sosialnya;",""]],"4":[[1,"115","7","Decentralization and Special Autonomy Capacity Strengthening","Implementing decentralization and special autonomy (Aceh, Papua, and West Papua) through increasing the capacity of autonomous regions and special regions to fulfill minimum service standards, managing regional",""],[1,"115","9","Decentralization and Regional Autonomy Capacity Building","Implementing decentralization and regional autonomy by increasing the capacity of local governments, among others through: (a) applying Minimum",""],[1,"116","1","Regional Service Standards and Complaints Mechanism Improvement","Service Standards (SPM) in the regions in a full and consistent manner, including improving complaints mechanisms that are integrated with performance management;",""],[1,"116","1","Regional Government Institutional Efficiency Reform","(b) arranging institutions and organizations of regional governments that are more efficient and effective;",""],[1,"116","1","Electronic-Based Government Systems Optimization","(c) optimizing the use of Electronic- Based Government Systems (SPBE) to create faster, cheaper and efficient services;",""],[1,"116","1","Regional Research and Innovation for Public Services","(d) increasing regional research and innovation to improve the quality of public services and accelerate development;",""],[1,"116","1","Regional Apparatus Capacity Building Programme","(e) increasing the capacity of the regional apparatus in the management of regional government administration and the capacity of other special expertise in accordance with regional needs, including regional development planning and budgeting;",""],[1,"116","1","Productive Regional Funds Optimization","(f) optimizing regional funds that are more productive and affirmative for regional progress;",""],[1,"116","1","Regional Revenue Enhancement and Data Structuring","(g) increasing regional revenues from both taxes and levies, as well as other sources of revenue through structuring and developing data and information;",""],[1,"116","1","Regional Financial Management Improvement","(h) effective and efficient regional financial management,",""],[1,"116","1","Regional Spending Quality Improvement","(i) improving the quality of regional spending that has an impact on accelerating the achievements of SPM, improving people's welfare, and regional progress.",""],[1,"117","11","Regulatory Harmonization for Planning, Budgeting, Procurement, Control, Evaluation, and Audits","Harmonizing and synchronizing regulations regarding planning, budgeting, procurement of goods and services, control and evaluation, and audits between the central government and other regions;",""],[1,"117","12","Revision of Central-Regional Finance Law","Strengthening the relationship between the central and regional finances through the acceleration of the completion of the revision of Law No. 33/2004 concerning the Relationship of Central and Regional Finances, and other laws and regulations",""],[1,"133","2","Regional Autonomy Implementation Capacity Building","The implementation of regional autonomy is carried out through: (a) increasing the capacity of regional governments (institutional, apparatus, and regional finance);",""],[2,"124","5","Decentralization and Special Autonomy Capacity Strengthening","Pelaksanaan desentralisasi dan otonomi khusus (Provinsi Aceh, Papua, dan Papua Barat) melalui peningkatkan kapasitas daerah otonom dan daerah khusus/daerah istimewa untuk pemenuhan standar pelayanan minimum, pengelolaan keuangan daerah dan pemenuhan pelayanan publik yang lebih efektif dan efisien;",""],[2,"124","6","Full Implementation of Minimum Service Standards in Local Governments","penerapan Standar Pelayanan Minimal (SPM) di daerah secara penuh dan konsisten termasuk perbaikan mekanisme pengaduan yang terintegrasi dengan manajemen kinerja",""],[2,"124","6","Local Government Institutional Restructuring","penataan lembaga dan organisasi Pemerintah Daerah yang lebih efisien dan efektif",""],[2,"124","6","Local Civil Service Capacity Building","peningkatan kapasitas aparatur daerah dalam manajemen pemyelenggaraan pemerintahan daerah dan keahlian khusus lainnya sesuai dengan kebutuhan daerah termasuk perencanaan pembangunan dan penganggaran daerah",""],[2,"124","6","Effective and Efficient Regional Financial Management","pengelolaan keuangan daerah yang efektif dan efisien",""],[2,"124","7","Aceh Special Autonomy Implementation Strengthening","Pelaksanaan otonomi khusus di Aceh diarahkan pada pelaksanaan Undang- undang Nomor 11 Tahun 2006 tentang Pemerintahan Aceh secara sungguh- sungguh, konsisten, nyata dan bertanggung jawab antara lain melalui: (a) penguatan dan pemberdayaan rakyat Aceh berlandaskan budaya dan syariat Islam yang mengutamakan nilai-nilai kemanusiaan; (b) penguatan tata kelola pemerintahan yang partisipatif, transparan, akuntabel, dan adil dengan mengutamakan pelayanan prima; (c) optimalisasi pengelolaan Dana Otonomi Khusus Aceh bagi pelayanan publik dan pengembangan ekonomi untuk meningkatkan kesejahteraan rakyat; serta (d) peningkatan kapasitas aparatur dan pengembangan manajemen berbasis kinerja;",""],[2,"125","3","Special Region Law Implementation and Governance Strengthening in Yogyakarta","Pelaksanaan daerah khusus/daerah istimewa diarahkan pada pelaksanaan Undang-undang Nomor 13 tahun 2012 tentang Keistimewaan Daerah Istimewa Yogyakarta (DIY) secara sungguh-sungguh, konsisten, nyata dan bertanggung jawab antara lain melalui: (a) pemberdayaan masyarakat Daerah Istimewa Yogyakarta dengan berlandaskan pada budaya, adat istiadat dan keistimewaan Daerah Istimewa Yogyakarta; (b) penguatan tata kelola pemerintahan yang partisipatif, transparan, akuntabel, dan adil dengan mengutamakan pelayanan prima; (c) optimalisasi pengelolaan Dana Keistimewaan bagi penguatan ketahanan sosial dan budaya dan pengembangan ekonomi rakyat untuk meningkatkan kesejahteraan rakyat dan kemajuan daerah; serta (d) peningkatan kapasitas aparatur dan pengembangan manajemen berbasis kinerja.",""],[2,"128","3","Special Autonomy Implementation Restructuring","(3) Penataan pelaksanaan otonomi khusus dilakukan melalui antara lain: (a) pembangunan sumber daya manusia, pemberdayaan, dan modal sosial budaya masyarakat kampung; (b) penguatan lembaga adat dan kampung adat, perlindungan hak-hak masyarakat adat sesuai dengan perundangan yang berlaku termasuk hak atas tanah adat/ulayat; (c) peningkatan kapasitas pemerintahan daerah; (d) pengembangan dan penguatan peran distrik sebagai pusat data, informasi dan pengetahuan, pusat pelayanan dasar, pusat pemberdayaan masyarakat, pusat pengembangan inovasi dan kewirausahaan, pusat pengelolaan sumber daya alam dan lingkungan, serta pusat pertumbuhan ekonomi kabupaten; (e) pengembangan 7 wilayah adat; (f) optimalisasi SDM Unggul Orang Asli Papua dalam Badan Usaha Milik Negara dan kementerian/lembaga; (g) pengembangan inovasi dan kreativitas kaum muda Asli Papua (Papua Youth Creative Hub); (h) pemberdayaan pengusaha lokal; (i) pembangunan istana kepresidenan di Kota Jayapura; dan (j) penataan daerah dalam rangka meningkatkan efisiensi dan efektifitas penyelenggaraan pemerintahan daerah dan percepatan pembangunan di Tanah Papua",""],[2,"130","6","Local Government Capacity Strengthening","Pelaksanaan otonomi daerah dilakukan melalui antara lain: (a) peningkatan kapasitas pemerintahan daerah (kelembagaan, aparatur dan keuangan daerah);",""],[2,"130","6","Acceleration of Minimum Service Standards and Investment Licensing","percepatan penerapan SPM, peningkatan pelayanan perizinan investasi, dan perluasan kerjasama antardaerah.",""],[2,"133","2","Local Government Capacity Strengthening","Pelaksanaan otonomi daerah dilakukan melalui antara lain: (a) peningkatan kapasitas pemerintahan daerah (kelembagaan, aparatur dan keuangan daerah);",""],[2,"133","2","Acceleration of Minimum Service Standards, Investment Licensing, and Interregional Cooperation","percepatan penerapan SPM, peningkatan pelayanan perizinan investasi, dan perluasan kerjasama antardaerah.",""],[2,"134","6","Local Government Capacity Strengthening","Pelaksanaan otonomi daerah dilakukan melalui antara lain: (a) peningkatan kapasitas pemerintahan daerah (kelembagaan, aparatur dan keuangan daerah);",""],[2,"135","2","Acceleration of Minimum Service Standards and Investment Licensing Services","percepatan penerapan SPM, peningkatan pelayanan perizinan investasi, dan perluasan kerjasama daerah;",""],[2,"137","2","Local Government Capacity Strengthening","Pelaksanaan otonomi daerah dilakukan melalui antara lain: (a) peningkatan kapasitas pemerintahan daerah (kelembagaan, aparatur dan keuangan daerah);",""],[2,"137","2","Acceleration of Minimum Service Standards, Investment Licensing, and Interregional Cooperation","percepatan penerapan SPM, peningkatan pelayanan perizinan investasi, dan perluasan kerjasama antardaerah.",""],[2,"139","3","Local Government Capacity Strengthening","Pelaksanaan otonomi daerah dilakukan melalui antara lain: (a) peningkatan kapasitas pemerintahan daerah (kelembagaan, aparatur dan keuangan daerah);",""],[2,"139","3","Acceleration of Minimum Service Standards Implementation","percepatan penerapan SPM, termasuk sanitasi dan air bersih, serta pengelolaan sampah dan limbah, peningkatan pelayanan perizinan investasi, dan perluasan kerjasama antardaerah;",""],[2,"140","8","Local Government Capacity Strengthening","Pelaksanaan otonomi daerah dilakukan melalui antara lain: (a) peningkatan kapasitas pemerintahan daerah (kelembagaan, aparatur dan keuangan daerah);",""],[2,"141","2","Acceleration of Minimum Service Standards Implementation","percepatan penerapan SPM antara lain sanitasi, air bersih, pengelolaan sampah, peningkatan pelayanan perizinan investasi, dan perluasan kerjasama antardaerah.",""]],"5":[[1,"116","3","Aceh Special Autonomy Fund Management for Public Services and Economic Development","optimizing the management of the Aceh Special Autonomy Fund for public services and economic development to improve people's welfare",""],[1,"116","3","Participatory and Accountable Governance Strengthening","strengthening participatory, transparent, accountable, and fair governance by prioritizing excellent services",""],[1,"116","3","Apparatus Capacity Building and Performance-Based Management","increasing the capacity of the apparatus and developing performance-based management",""],[1,"116","4","Implementation of Special Autonomy in Papua and West Papua","Implementing special autonomy in Papua and West Papua as directed by the implementation of Law No. 21/2001 concerning the Special Autonomy for the provinces of Papua and West Papua in a serious, consistent, real, and responsible manner",""],[1,"117","1","Apparatus Capacity Building and Performance-Based Management","increasing the capacity of the apparatus and developing performance-based management;",""],[1,"117","2","Special Region of Yogyakarta Special Region Implementation Program","The implementation of special regions as directed by the implementation of Law No. 13/2012 concerning the Special Region of Yogyakarta (DIY) in a serious, consistent, real, and responsible manner, among others through: (a) empowering the people of the Special Region of Yogyakarta based on culture, customs, and privileges of the Special Region of Yogyakarta; (b) strengthening participatory, transparent, accountable, and fair governance by prioritizing excellent services; (c) optimizing the management of the Privileged Funds to strengthen social and cultural resilience, and develop the people's economy to improve people's welfare and regional progress; and (d) increasing the capacity of the apparatus and developing performance-based management.",""],[1,"129","3","Papua Accelerated Development and Special Autonomy Implementation","The development policy for Papua in 2020-2024 is directed at accelerating development to catch up with other regions of Indonesia and implementing special autonomy laws for Papua and West Papua based on Papua's cultural and contextual approaches and based on ecological and indigenous territories.",""],[1,"131","3","Special Autonomy Law Implementation Structuring","The structuring of the implementation of special autonomy laws is carried out, among others through: (a) human resource development, empowerment, and socio-cultural capital of the village communities; (b) strengthening traditional institutions and customary villages, protecting the rights of indigenous people in accordance with applicable laws including customary/communal land rights; (c) increasing the capacity of regional governments; (d) developing and strengthening the district's role as a center for data, information and knowledge; center for basic services; center for community empowerment; center for innovation and",""],[1,"131","4","Regional Government Restructuring Reform","regional restructuring in the context of increasing the efficiency and effectiveness of regional governments and accelerating development in Papua.",""],[1,"132","4","Inter-Ministerial Development Coordination in Papua","Strengthening the coordination of ministries/institutions in planning, implementing, controlling, and evaluating development in Papua.",""],[1,"132","8","Coordination of Development Actors in Disadvantaged Areas","guiding and aligning ministries and other development actors in disadvantaged areas that have been uplifted in 2019, for a maximum of 3 years (2020-2022);",""],[1,"306","3","Aceh Special Autonomy Fund Utilization Framework","Special autonomy funds for Aceh are used to: (1) strengthen and empower the people of Aceh based on Islamic sharia guidelines that prioritize human values; strengthen governance that is participatory, transparent, accountable, and fair; strengthen public services and economic development to improve regional progress and the welfare of the people in Aceh; increase the capacity of the apparatus of the government; develop performance-based management; and (2) strengthen the coordination, cooperation, and partnership among the Aceh provincial government, regency/city governments, and ministries/institutions in planning, allocating, budgeting, channeling, reporting, monitoring, controlling and evaluating the use of funds;",""],[1,"306","4","Special Autonomy Fund Support for Papua and West Papua","Special autonomy funds for Papua and West Papua are used to: (1) strengthen and empower Papuans based on culture and customs that prioritize human values; develop customary territories in support of regional economies; strengthen governance that",""],[1,"306","5","Special Autonomy Fund Governance and Coordination Reform","strengthen the coordination, cooperation, and partnership among the governments of Papua and West Papua, regency/city governments, and ministries/institutions in planning, allocating, budgeting, channeling, reporting, monitoring, controlling, and evaluating the use of funds; and (3) refining the synchronization and integration of the use of special autonomy funds with activities supported by other funding sources, including sources from business entities and development partners.",""],[1,"306","5","Public Service and Regional Development Strengthening","strengthen public services and economic development to improve regional progress and the welfare of Papuans; increase the capacity of the apparatus of the government; develop performance- based management",""],[1,"306","6","Special Funding for Yogyakarta Regional Development and Governance","Special funding for the Special Region of Yogyakarta is used to: (1) strengthen and empower the people based on culture and customs; strengthen governance that is participatory, transparent, accountable, and fair by prioritizing excellent public services; strengthen social and cultural resilience and economic development to improve regional progress and welfare of the people in Yogyakarta; increase the capacity of the apparatus of the government; develop performance- based management; and (2) strengthen coordination, cooperation, and partnership among the government of the Special Province of Yogyakarta, regency/city governments, and ministries/institutions in planning, allocating, budgeting, channeling, reporting, monitoring, controlling and evaluating the use of funds.","ministries/institutions"],[2,"125","2","Participatory and Accountable Governance Strengthening","penguatan tata kelola pemerintahan yang partisipatif, transparan, akuntabel, dan adil dengan mengutamakan pelayanan prima",""],[2,"125","2","Papua Special Autonomy Fund Optimization Mechanism","optimalisasi pengelolaan Dana Otonomi Khusus Papua bagi pelayanan publik dan pengembangan ekonomi untuk meningkatkan kesejahteraan rakyat dan kemajuan daerah",""],[2,"125","2","Civil Service Capacity and Performance Management Reform","peningkatan kapasitas aparatur dan pengembangan manajemen berbasis kinerja",""],[2,"125","2","District Empowerment and Village Supervision Programme","penguatan distrik sebagai pusat perubahan dan pertumbuhan, serta pembinaan dan pengawasan desa",""],[2,"129","10","Strengthening Inter-Ministerial Coordination for Papua Development Planning and Implementation","Penguatan koordinasi kementerian/lembaga dalam perencanaan, pelaksanaan dan pengendalian dan evaluasi pembangunan di Tanah Papua",""],[2,"273","20","Revision of the Special Autonomy Law for Papua Province","Revisi UU Nomor 21 Tahun 2001 tentang Otonomi Khusus Bagi Provinsi Papua",""],[2,"273","24","Revision of Law No. 29 of 2007 on Jakarta Provincial Government","Revisi UU Nomor 29 Tahun 2007 Tentang Pemerintahan Provinsi DKI Jakarta Sebagai Ibukota Negara Kesatuan Republik Indonesia",""],[2,"273","26","Revision of the Fiscal Balance Law","Revisi UU Nomor 33 Tahun 2004 tentang Perimbangan Keuangan antara Pemerintah Pusat dan Pemerintahan Daerah",""],[2,"287","13","Aceh Special Autonomy Fund Utilization Enhancement","Dana Otonomi Khusus Aceh untuk: (1) meningkatkan pemanfaatan dana bagi",""],[2,"288","3","Papua Special Autonomy Fund Support Measures","Dana Otonomi Khusus Papua dan Papua Barat untuk: (1) penguatan dan pemberdayaan Orang Asli Papua berlandaskan budaya dan adat yang mengutamakan nilai-nilai kemanusiaan; pengembangan wilayah adat dalam mendukung perekonomian wilayah; penguatan tata kelola pemerintahan yang partisipatif, transparan, akuntabel, dan adil; pelayanan publik dan pengembangan ekonomi untuk meningkatkan kesejahteraan rakyat dan kemajuan daerah; dan peningkatan kapasitas aparatur dan pengembangan manajemen berbasis kinerja; (2) memperkuat koordinasi, kerjasama dan kemitraan antara Pemerintah Provinsi Papua dan Provinsi Papua Barat dengan Pemerintah Kabupaten/Kota dan K/L dalam perencanaan, pengalokasian, penganggaran, penyaluran, pelaporan, pemantauan, pengendalian dan evaluasi pemanfaatan dana; serta (3) mempertajam sinkronisasi dan integrasi pemanfaatan Dana Otonomi Khusus dengan kegiatan yang didukung oleh sumber pendanaan lainnya, termasuk dunia usaha dan mitra pembangunan.",""],[2,"288","4","Special Autonomy Fund Utilization and Governance Strengthening","Dana Keistimewaan DI Yogyakarta untuk: (1) meningkatkan pemanfaatan dana untuk penguatan dan pemberdayaan rakyat berlandaskan budaya dan adat; penguatan tata kelola pemerintahan yang partisipatif, transparan, akuntabel, dan adil dengan mengutamakan pelayanan prima; penguatan ketahanan sosial dan budaya dan pengembangan ekonomi rakyat untuk meningkatkan kesejahteraan rakyat dan kemajuan daerah; dan peningkatan kapasitas aparatur dan pengembangan manajemen berbasis kinerja; serta (2) memperkuat koordinasi, kerjasama dan kemitraan antara Pemerintah Provinsi Daerah Istimewa Yogyakarta dengan Pemerintah Kabupaten/Kota dan K/L dalam perencanaan, pengalokasian, penganggaran, penyaluran, pelaporan, pemantauan, pengendalian dan evaluasi pemanfaatan dana.","Pemerintah Provinsi Daerah Istimewa Yogyakarta | Pemerintah Kabupaten/Kota | K/L"]],"6":[[1,"147","2","Population Governance and Human Development Policy Package","To achieve these objectives, human development policies are directed at population control and strengthening population governance; fulfillment of basic services and social protection; improving the quality of life for children, women, and youth; alleviating poverty; and increasing labor force productivity and competitiveness.",""],[1,"147","2","Life-Cycle Inclusive Human Development Approach","The human development policy is carried out based on a life-cycle approach, and inclusively considers the needs of the elderly and residents with disabilities, and the management of talented human resources",""],[1,"150","1","Population Administration Expansion and Mobile Positioning Data Integration","by accelerating the expansion of population administration and the use of mobile positioning data (MPD) towards a single population data set",""],[1,"168","20","Expansion of Civil and Population Registration Services","Expanding the reach of civil registration and population registration services for all citizens both in the country and abroad, including: (a) Service-based approach at the village and sub- district level, and in all representative offices of the Republic of Indonesia;",""],[1,"168","23","IT-Based Registration and Civil Registration Systems","registration and civil registration systems based on information technology; and (d) Connecting information systems in various government institutions.",""],[1,"169","1","Community Vital Events Registration Awareness and Incentive Scheme","Increasing awareness and activity of communities in recording demographic and other important events, including: (a) Involving various government sectors and community elements to be active in networking and advocacy; and (b) Developing an appropriate incentive",""],[1,"169","5","Vital Statistics Improvement and Utilization Initiative","Increasing the availability and quality of accurate, complete, and timely vital statistics for development planning and implementation, including: (a) Providing accurate vital statistics from cross-sectoral data; and (b) Optimal utilization of vital statistics for development and public services.",""],[1,"169","6","Intergovernmental Coordination and Synchronization Strengthening","Strengthening coordination, collaboration, and synchronization between ministries/institutions, provincial governments, regency/city governments, and stakeholders",""],[1,"169","7","Civil and Population Registration Policy Framework Development","Compiling civil registration policy and procedure frameworks, as well as comprehensive and harmonious population registration between sectors; and (b) Harmonious administration of population registration and civil registration services between the central and regional governments",""],[2,"146","2","Expansion of Population Administration and One Population Data System","Hal ini antara lain dapat dilakukan dengan percepatan perluasan administrasi kependudukan dan penggunaan mobile positioning data (MPD) menuju satu data kependudukan yang digunakan untuk formulasi kebijakan terkait penduduk dan tata wilayah serta perencanaan pembangunan berdasarkan kondisi kependudukan melalui Grand Design Pembangunan Kependudukan (GPDK).",""],[2,"164","2","Expansion of Population Registration and Civil Registration Services","Perluasan jangkauan layanan pendaftaran penduduk pencatatan sipil bagi seluruh penduduk dan WNI di luar negeri, mencakup: (a) Pendekatan layanan ke tingkat desa dan kelurahan serta layanan di seluruh kantor Perwakilan Republik Indonesia; (b) Peningkatan layanan pendaftaran penduduk dan pencatatan sipil yang mudah dan cepat; (c) Pengembangan sistem pendaftaran penduduk dan pencatatan sipil berbasis teknologi informasi dan terhubung lintas sektor; dan (d) Keterhubungan antar sistem informasi di berbagai lembaga pemerintah.",""],[2,"164","3","Civil Registration Awareness and Incentive System","Peningkatan kesadaran dan keaktifan masyarakat dalam mencatatkan peristiwa kependudukan dan peristiwa penting, mencakup: (a) Pelibatan berbagai sektor pemerintahan dan elemen masyarakat untuk aktif dalam sosialisasi dan advokasi; dan (b) Pengembangan sistem insentif yang tepat untuk mendorong penduduk dan WNI di luar negeri untuk melaporkan peristiwa pendaftaran penduduk dan pencatatan sipil.",""],[2,"164","4","Accelerated Civil Registration and Population Document Ownership for Special Groups","Percepatan kepemilikan dokumen pendaftaran penduduk dan pencatatan sipil bagi kelompok khusus.",""],[2,"164","6","Vital Statistics Improvement and Use Initiative","Peningkatan ketersediaan dan kualitas statistik hayati yang akurat, lengkap, dan tepat waktu untuk perencanaan dan pelaksanaan pembangunan, mencakup: (a) Penyediaan statistik hayati yang akurat dari data lintas sektor; dan (b) Pemanfaatan statistik hayati secara optimal untuk pembangunan dan pelayanan publik.",""],[2,"164","7","Intergovernmental Coordination and Civil Registration Governance Strengthening","Penguatan koordinasi, kolaborasi, dan sinkronisasi antar-kementerian/ lembaga, pemerintah provinsi, pemerintah kabupaten/kota, dan pemangku kepentingan dalam layanan pendaftaran penduduk dan pencatatan sipil serta pengembangan statistik hayati, mencakup: (a) Penyusunan kerangka kebijakan dan prosedur pencatatan sipil dan pendaftaran penduduk yang menyeluruh dan selaras antar sektor; dan (b) Penyelenggaraan tata kelola pendaftaran penduduk dan pencatatan sipil yang selaras antara pemerintah pusat dan daerah.",""]],"7":[[1,"192","5","Strengthening the Forum for Religious Harmony","To strengthen social harmony, various efforts continue to be carried out, among others by strengthening the role of the Forum for Religious Harmony (FKUB) at the provincial, district/city, and sub- district levels as a place for interfaith communication and dialogue to resolve issues surrounding religious life.",""],[1,"197","2","Religious Moderation and Tolerance Promotion Programme","Strengthening a moderate perspective, attitude, and practice of religious beliefs to strengthen brotherhood and togetherness among religious communities, including: (a) developing religious campaign that instills peace and provides benefit to its respective congregation; (b) strengthening the education system from a moderate perspective that includes curriculum development, teaching materials, teaching processes, training of educational personnel, and teacher recruitment; (c) strengthening the role of religious boarding schools in developing religious moderation by increasing understanding and beneficial practice of religious teachings; (d) managing houses of worship as centers of religious tolerance; and (e) utilizing public space for the exchange of ideas among students and youth across cultures, across religions, and across ethnic groups.",""],[1,"197","3","Religious Community Harmony and Rights Protection","Strengthening harmony among religious communities, including: (a) protection of religious communities that guarantees civil and religious rights; (b) promoting the role of religious institutions, religious social organizations, religious leaders,",""],[1,"197","4","Community Mediation for National Harmony","community leaders, state officials, the military, and the police as mediators to strengthen unity and harmony of the nation",""],[1,"197","4","Strengthening the Forum for Religious Harmony","strengthening the Forum for Religious Harmony (FKUB) to build solidarity, tolerance, and cooperation",""],[1,"197","5","Religious and Cultural Relations Strengthening Initiative","Aligning religious and cultural relations, including: (a) appreciating cultural expressions based on religious values; (b) enhancing religious, cultural literacy; (c) preserving religious sites and utilizing religious and cultural celebrations to strengthen tolerance.",""],[1,"197","6","Religious Services Quality Improvement Programme","Improving the quality of religious services, including: (a) increasing facilitation of religious services; (b) improving family planning services; (c) strengthening the implementation of the Halal Product Guarantee Act; and (d) improving the organizational quality of the Hajj pilgrimage and umrah.",""],[1,"197","7","Religious Community Economic Empowerment and Hajj Fund Management","Improving the economy of religious communities and resources by (a) empowering religious social funds; (b) developing economic institutions for religious communities; and (c) managing the Hajj funds in a professional, transparent, and accountable manner.",""],[2,"182","5","Strengthening Interfaith Harmony Forums","Untuk memperkukuh kerukunan berbagai upaya terus dilakukan, antara lain dengan memperkuat peran Forum Kerukunan Umat Beragama (FKUB) di tingkat provinsi, kabupaten/kota, dan kecamatan sebagai wadah komunikasi dan dialog lintas iman untuk menyelesaikan persoalan kehidupan beragama.",""],[2,"187","9","Religious Moderation and Interfaith Harmony Strengthening","Penguatan cara pandang, sikap, dan praktik beragama dalam perspektif jalan tengah untuk memantapkan persaudaraan dan kebersamaan di kalangan umat beragama, mencakup: (a) pengembangan penyiaran agama untuk perdamaian dan kemaslahatan umat; (b) penguatan sistem pendidikan yang berperspektif moderat mencakup pengembangan kurikulum, materi dan proses pengajaran, pendidikan guru dan tenaga kependidikan, dan rekrutmen guru; (c) penguatan peran pesantren dalam mengembangkan moderasi beragama melalui peningkatan pemahaman dan pengamalan ajaran agama untuk kemaslahatan; (d) pengelolaan rumah ibadah",""],[2,"188","3","Religious Harmony and Tolerance Strengthening Initiative","Penguatan harmoni dan kerukunan umat beragama, mencakup: (a) pelindungan umat beragama untuk menjamin hak-hak sipil dan beragama; (b) penguatan peran lembaga agama, organisasi sosial keagamaan, tokoh agama, tokoh masyarakat, ASN, TNI, dan Polri sebagai perekat persatuan dan kesatuan bangsa; dan (c) penguatan Forum Kerukunan Umat Beragama (FKUB) untuk membangun solidaritas sosial, toleransi, dan gotong royong.",""],[2,"188","4","Religious and Cultural Harmony Alignment Initiative","Penyelarasan relasi agama dan budaya, mencakup: (a) penghargaan atas ekspresi budaya berbasis nilai-nilai agama; (b) pengembangan literasi khazanah budaya bernafas agama; (c) pelestarian situs keagamaan dan pemanfaatan perayaan keagamaan dan budaya untuk memperkuat toleransi.",""],[2,"188","5","Religious Services Quality Improvement Programme","Peningkatan kualitas pelayanan kehidupan beragama, mencakup: (a) peningkatan fasilitasi pelayanan keagamaan; (b) peningkatan pelayanan bimbingan perkawinan dan keluarga; (c) penguatan penyelenggaraan jaminan produk halal; dan (d) peningkatan kualitas penyelenggaraan haji dan umrah.",""],[2,"188","6","Religious Social Fund Empowerment","pemberdayaan dana sosial keagamaan",""],[2,"188","6","Community Economic Institution Development","pengembangan kelembagaan ekonomi umat",""],[2,"188","6","Professional Hajj Fund Management","pengelolaan dana haji secara profesional, transparan, dan akuntabel",""]],"8":[[1,"234","6","Expansion of Digital Public Service Delivery","Expanding cashless social assistance services, digital educational content, digital public information, digital health services, and digital agricultural information, by providing start-up incentives that focus on social services, education, health, public information, and agricultural information;",""],[1,"234","11","Utilization of ICT Government Services","Priority projects that support the use of ICT infrastructure include: i) Utilizing ICT government services; and ii) Utilizing ICT services for the public and business actors.",""],[1,"234","11","ICT Services for the Public and Business Actors","Priority projects that support the use of ICT infrastructure include: i) Utilizing ICT government services; and ii) Utilizing ICT services for the public and business actors.",""],[1,"273","10","Public Service Delivery and State Apparatus Policy Implementation","members of the state apparatus are required to carry out their role in implementing policies, delivering public services, and bringing society together on Pancasila and the 1945 Constitution.",""],[1,"282","7","Integrated E-Government Implementation","Re-organising institutional and business processes of institutions by implementing integrated e- government;",""],[1,"282","10","Public Service Transformation Initiative","Transforming public services, through: electronic-based public services (e-services), strengthening public supervision of the performance of public services, strengthening the innovation ecosystem, and strengthening integrated services.",""],[1,"303","10","System and Data Integration Services for Planning, Budgeting, and Evaluation","the government is currently developing system and data integration services to help planning, budgeting, and evaluating by using the same and most up-to-date database",""],[2,"124","6","Expansion of Electronic Government Services","optimalisasi pemanfataan Sistem Pemerintahan Berbasis Elektronik (SPBE) guna menciptakan pelayanan yang lebih cepat, murah dan efisien",""],[2,"126","5","Digital Modernization of Land Services","peningkatan pelayanan pertanahan melalui pelayanan modern berbasis digital dan penerimaan PNS petugas ukur pertanahan",""],[2,"206","7","Information Security Enhancement and Regulatory Improvement","Jaminan keamanan bagi masyarakat, pemerintah, dan dunia usaha dalam mempertukarkan data dan informasi di jaringan internet menjadi tantangan yang perlu dimitigasi seperti melalui peningkatan keamanan teknologi informasi, penyempurnaan regulasi dan peningkatan literasi masyarakat.",""],[2,"222","4","Government ICT Services Utilization","Pemanfaatan TIK layanan pemerintah",""],[2,"222","4","ICT Services for Communities and Businesses","Pemanfaatan TIK layanan masyarakat dan dunia usaha",""],[2,"222","7","Cross-Sector Digital Data Adoption and National Dashboard Initiative","Adopsi pemanfaatan teknologi global (Big Data, IoT, AI, dll) bersifat lintas sektor dalam proses perencanaan, pemantauan, maupun pelaksanaan kinerja, melalui (a) mendorong pelaksanaan satu data dalam rangka pemanfaatan data yang saling interoperabilitas, terstandar serta dapat dibagipakaikan; (b) mendorong pemanfaatan analisa dari Big Data untuk meningkatkan ketepatan perencanaan, kinerja pelaksanaan pembangunan maupun ketepatan pengawasan pembangunan; dan (c) mendorong terbentuknya dashboard data nasional untuk mendukung pengambilan kebijakan dan keputusan berbasis data yang saling interoperabilitas, terstandar, serta dapat dibagipakaikan.",""],[2,"222","8","Secure and Integrated Information Management Infrastructure","Pengelolaan informasi secara aman dan terintegrasi termasuk di dalamnya komponen Major Project \"Infrastruktur TIK untuk Mendukung Transformasi Digital\";",""],[2,"257","6","Government Business Process Architecture Implementation","Salah satu upaya untuk mengatasi persoalan tumpang tindih tersebut adalah dengan menerapkan arsitektur proses bisnis pemerintahan yang juga akan mendukung penerapan Sistem Pemerintahan Berbasis Elektronik (SPBE) dan Satu Data Indonesia (SDI) yang terintegrasi, baik dari sisi tata kelola, infrastruktur TIK, maupun layanan.",""],[2,"258","2","Delegation of Public Service Authority to Integrated Service Hubs","Terkait pelayanan terpadu, perlu adanya pelimpahan/pendelegasian kewenangan pelayanan kepada Mal Pelayanan Publik dan Unit Pelayanan Publik (UPP) di desa, kelurahan, dan kecamatan.",""],[2,"258","2","Integrated Business Process and Shared Data for Public Services","Persoalan lain adalah belum adanya integrasi proses bisinis dan pemanfaatan data terpadu dalam penyediaan layanan.",""],[2,"258","2","Integrated Electronic Public Service Innovation","Selain itu, penerapan inovasi pelayanan publik secara elektronik (e-service) masih belum terintegrasi antar jenis layanan dengan tingkat kematangan (maturitas) yang beragam.",""],[2,"265","11","Institutional Restructuring and Integrated E-Government Business Process Reform","Penataan kelembagaan dan proses bisnis, melalui: penataan kelembagaan instansi pemerintah dan penerapan SPBE terintegrasi;",""],[2,"265","13","Public Service Transformation","Transformasi pelayanan publik, melalui: pelayanan publik berbasis elektronik (e-service), penguatan pengawasan masyarakat atas kinerja pelayanan publik, penguatan ekosistem inovasi, dan penguatan pelayanan terpadu.",""]],"9":[[1,"65","3","Development Data Quality Improvement and Monitoring System","The implementation of these two approaches is supported by improved quality of data, which will serve as a reference for monitoring and evaluating the achievements of the present development agenda, as well as improving policymaking.",""],[1,"96","2","Economic Development Data Improvement","increasing the availability and quality of data on economic development, especially on food, agriculture, maritime affairs, tourism, and the creative and digital economy",""],[1,"97","9","Statistical Coordination and Information Quality Improvement","Improvement in the availability of data and quality of information will be focused on: (1) improving coordination, integration, and synchronization of statistical activities that are organized by the central government, regional government, and private sector;",""],[1,"98","2","Statistical Standards and Quality Assurance Enhancement","increasing the use of international statistical standards and methodologies in Indonesia; and (6) increasing the availability of statistics by applying quality assurance standards.",""],[1,"233","10","Intra-Government Network Development","Encouraging the development of an intra-government network is by utilizing domestic industries to increase national independence and competitiveness;",""],[1,"234","15","One Data Initiative for Cross-Sectoral Performance Management","Adopting the use of global technology (Big Data, IoT, AI, etc.) that is cross-sectoral in the process of planning, monitoring, and implementing performance management systems, by (a) encouraging the implementation of \"One Data\" initiative in the framework of",""],[1,"235","1","National Data Dashboards and Big Data Analytics for Planning","encouraging the utilization of big data analytics to improve the accuracy of planning, the performance of development implementation, and the accuracy of development supervision; and (c) encouraging the establishment of national data dashboards to support data- based policy making and decisions",""],[2,"67","3","Development Data and Policy Quality Improvement","Pelaksanaan kedua fokus tersebut didukung dengan perbaikan data untuk menjadi rujukan pemantauan dan evaluasi capaian pembangunan, serta perbaikan kualitas kebijakan.",""],[2,"72","7","Economic Census and Statistical Data Improvement","Perbaikan dari sisi tata kelola pembangunan juga ditunjukkan dari peningkatan kualitas data dan informasi statistik.",""],[2,"88","13","Agricultural Census 2023 and Food Data Improvement","Pelaksanaan Sensus Pertanian 2023 dan perbaikan data pangan (database)",""],[2,"97","5","Economic Data and Information Improvement","(iv) Penguatan pilar pertumbuhan dan daya saing ekonomi yang dilaksanakan dengan strategi: (6) meningkatkan ketersediaan dan kualitas data dan informasi perkembangan ekonomi, terutama pangan dan pertanian, kemaritiman, pariwisata, ekonomi kreatif, dan ekonomi digital.",""],[2,"99","4","Statistical Data Quality and Availability Improvement Initiative","Peningkatan ketersediaan kualitas data dan informasi difokuskan pada: (1) peningkatan koordinasi, integrasi, dan sinkronisasi kegiatan statistik yang diselenggarakan pemerintah pusat, pemerintah daerah dan swasta; (2) peningkatan hubungan dengan responden dan pengguna data; (3) peningkatan jumlah dan kompetensi SDM; (4) peningkatan sarana dan prasarana, termasuk yang berbasis teknologi informasi dan komunikasi dalam kegiatan statistik; (5) peningkatan penggunaan standar dan metodologi statistik internasional di Indonesia; dan (6) peningkatan ketersediaan statistik dengan menerapkan standar penjaminan kualitas.",""]],"10":[[1,"168","15","Strengthening Development Assistance Presidential Regulation","Issuance of presidential regulation on strengthening development assistance",""],[1,"271","10","South-South and Triangular Cooperation for Trade and Investment","international development cooperation by optimizing \"South- South and Triangular Cooperation\" to support trade and investment.",""],[1,"271","10","Institutional Strengthening for Development Assistance Delivery","The institutional implementation of assistance provision and international development cooperation is strengthened, while new sources and funding mechanisms continue to be developed, for example, export credit schemes can be channeled through export financing providers.",""],[1,"271","11","Private Sector Participation Expansion Initiative","The participation of non-state actors, especially from the private sector, needs to be increased.",""],[1,"272","5","Public Diplomacy Program Synergy Initiative","There is an urgency to synergize public diplomacy programs with our socio-cultural wealth such as cuisine, ethnic diversity, and tolerance.",""],[1,"272","7","Total Diplomacy Leadership and Governance Strengthening","There is the need to strengthen leadership and governance when responding to the dynamic development of international relations using \"total diplomacy\".",""],[1,"272","7","Foreign Policy Institutional Role Structuring","Structuring the roles and functions of ministries/institutions is also needed to streamline the implementation of foreign policy.",""],[1,"280","5","Protection of Indonesian Citizens and Legal Entities Abroad","Strengthening the protection of Indonesian citizens and legal entities at the bilateral, regional, and multilateral levels; and increasing efforts to prevent incidents involving Indonesian citizens abroad;",""],[1,"280","18","Public Diplomacy Policy Coordination Framework","Formulating Indonesia's public diplomacy policy to improve coordination at the national level;",""],[1,"295","16","Revision of the Foreign Relations Law","Revision of Law No. 37/1999 on foreign relations.",""],[2,"163","21","Presidential Regulation on Development Assistance Support Policy","Tersedianya kebijakan pendukung penguatan pendampingan pembangunan a. Penerbitan Peraturan Presiden tentang",""]],"11":[[1,"274","2","Government Business Process Framework for Integrated Governance","An effort to overcome this issue is by implementing a government business process framework that will also support the implementation of e-government and \"One Data Indonesia\" in an integrated manner in terms of governance, ICT infrastructure, and services.",""],[1,"274","5","Integrated Planning and Budgeting System","it is necessary to accelerate the integration of systems and the continuation of the \"Money Follows Program\" policy, so that planning and budgeting can be more results-oriented",""],[1,"274","5","Institutional Performance Management System","Therefore, an institutional performance management system ... are needed.",""],[1,"274","5","Integrity System Implementation","Therefore, ... the implementation of an integrity system are needed.",""],[1,"285","3","Program-Based Performance Budgeting Reform","Strategic planning and budgeting processes with a program-based budgeting approach (\"Money Follows\" principle) through performance-based budgeting.",""],[1,"285","4","Planning and Budgeting Synchronization Reform","Synchronizing planning and budgeting processes to improve the integration of efficient and effective planning and budgeting in the context of achieving national development goals in accordance with the 2005-",""],[1,"285","6","Implementation Framework for Plan Delivery","Conduct of implementation through: i) regulatory framework, ii) institutional framework, iii) funding framework, and iv) evaluation and control framework.",""],[1,"285","7","RPJMN Strategic Plan Alignment and Integration","Each ministry/institution and regional government needs to ensure consistency and integration between the 2020-2024 RPJMN and strategic plans from ministries/institutions or RPJMD according to their respective authorities.",""],[1,"285","7","Integrated Programme Development for National Development Targets","In addition, all stakeholders collaborate and build integrated programs to support the achievement of national development targets in the 2020-2024 RPJMN.",""],[1,"285","7","RPJMN Monitoring, Evaluation, and Control Mechanism","To ensure the effectiveness of the 2020- 2024 RPJMN implementation, the Ministry of National Development Planning/Bappenas monitors and evaluates the elaboration of the RPJMN in the strategic plans from ministries/institutions and from the RPJMD, and controls the implementation of the RPJMN.","Ministry of National Development Planning/Bappenas"],[1,"285","14","Development Agenda Evaluation and Control Mechanism","Implementing evaluation and control of the development agenda, the President's directives, and corrective actions during implementation.",""],[1,"295","15","Revision of the National Development Planning System Law","Revision of law on the national development planning system.",""],[1,"302","3","Medium-Term Expenditure Framework and Performance-Based Budgeting Implementation","The implementation of a medium-term expenditure framework and performance-based budgeting in planning and budgeting continues to be done in stages in accordance with the capacity and conditions of the implementation.",""],[1,"302","4","Improved Development Planning and Priority Project Targeting","Steps by the government to improve the allocation for development priorities must begin with improving the quality of planned programs/activities and priority projects to achieve development goals.",""],[1,"302","4","Focused Development Plan with Clear Targets and Implementers","The development plan must be focused and set clear targets and clear implementers in charge.",""],[1,"303","8","Priority Project Allocation Improvement","Efforts to improve allocation for priority projects are also carried out through continuous improvement in the effectiveness and efficacy of the",""],[1,"308","5","Public Investment Funding Management Approach","For this reason, a funding management approach is needed to encourage growth and performance of public investment.",""],[1,"308","5","Investment Planning Process Improvement","Increasing the efficiency and performance of public investment requires an improvement in the investment planning process in all sectors and all levels",""],[1,"308","9","Public Investment Prioritization and Efficiency Improvement","This includes allocating government investment to the right sectors and the right projects for leverage, carrying out projects on time and with the right cost, and increasing institutional capacity and efficiency.",""],[1,"309","1","Public Investment Planning and Governance Improvement","Increasing the capacity and quality of government financing and investment schemes is carried out by improving public investment planning and policies, management, governance and policies, and project selection based on environmental and social sustainability criteria.",""],[1,"309","1","Long-Term National, Regional, and Sectoral Investment Planning","For this reason, strategies for national, regional, and sectoral development will be detailed by including investment plans to guide public and private investment in the long run.",""],[1,"309","5","Priority Project Funding Integration","Focusing on improving the allocation of funds based on priorities, which target priority projects through funding integration.",""],[1,"309","7","Priority-Based Development Funding Allocation","Allocating limited funding sources by prioritizing activities or projects that are national priorities, such as the Major Projects, among others.",""],[1,"309","7","National Development Strategy-Based Budget Allocation","Development funding must be directed based on a national development strategy, where the focus of the budget allocation is on funding development priorities, especially on meeting the basic needs of the people, which the government is obliged to undertake.",""],[1,"311","8","Priority Project Funding Integration","Focus on improving the allocation of funds based on priorities, which target priority projects through funding integration",""],[1,"311","9","Adjustment of Funding Modalities for Project Implementation Readiness","Adjusting funding modalities to be in line with development goals and ensuring readiness for project implementation.",""],[2,"258","3","Integrated Planning and Budgeting System","Untuk itu perlu percepatan keterpaduan sistem dan melanjutkan money follow program sehingga perencanaan dan penganggaran lebih berorientasi pada hasil yang mendukung pencapaian tujuan pembangunan.",""],[2,"258","3","Institutional Performance Management System","Oleh karena itu, perlu sistem manajemen kinerja kelembagaan, sistem perencanaan dan penganggaran yang terpadu dan andal serta implementasi sistem integritas.",""],[2,"258","3","Integrity System Implementation","Oleh karena itu, perlu sistem manajemen kinerja kelembagaan, sistem perencanaan dan penganggaran yang terpadu dan andal serta implementasi sistem integritas.",""],[2,"265","12","Performance Accountability System Reform","3. Reformasi sistem akuntabilitas kinerja, melalui: perluasan implementasi sistem integritas, penguatan pengelolaan reformasi birokrasi dan akuntabilitas kinerja organisasi, serta reformasi sistem perencanaan dan penganggaran;",""],[2,"268","4","Program-Based Planning and Performance-Based Budgeting","Penyusunan perencanaan dan penganggaran dengan pendekatan penganggaran berbasis program (money follow program) melalui penganggaran berbasis kinerja.",""],[2,"268","5","Planning and Budget Synchronization Reform","Sinkronisasi perencanaan dan penganggaran untuk meningkatkan keterpaduan perencanaan dan penganggaran yang lebih berkualitas dan efektif dalam rangka pencapaian sasaran pembangunan nasional sesuai RPJPN 2005-2025, visi dan misi Presiden/Wakil Presiden, serta arahan Presiden dengan menggunakan pendekatan tematik, holistik, integratif dan spasial",""],[2,"268","6","Implementation Framework for Execution Rules","Pelaksanaan kaidah pelaksanaan melalui: i) kerangka regulasi, ii) kerangka kelembagaan, iii) kerangka pendanaan, serta iv) kerangka evaluasi dan pengendalian.",""],[2,"284","6","Central Government Expenditure Management Reform","Arah Kebijakan pengelolaan belanja pemerintah pusat adalah meningkatkan kualitas alokasi pendanaan prioritas pembangunan.",""],[2,"284","7","Medium-Term Expenditure Framework and Performance-Based Budgeting Implementation","Implementasi Kerangka Pengeluaran Jangka Menengah (medium term expenditure framework) dan anggaran berbasis kinerja (performance based budgeting) dalam perencanaan dan penganggaran terus dilakukan secara bertahap sesuai kapasitas dan kondisi pelaksanaan.",""],[2,"285","11","Integrated Planning, Budgeting, and Evaluation Data System","pemerintah melakukan pengembangan integrasi sistem dan data pada dokumen perencanaan, penganggaran, dan evaluasi melalui pemanfaatan basis data yang sama dan termutakhir.",""]],"12":[[1,"280","25","Regulatory Monitoring, Public Participation, and Policy Harmonization Reform","integrating regulatory monitoring and evaluation processes; optimizing public access and participation in the formulation and formation of regulations; strengthening the harmonization and synergy of policies and regulations; and",""],[1,"281","2","Legal and Regulatory Reform Package","Legal reform, including changes in the criminal codes and procedures; and regulations related to business entities, movable property guarantees, international civil law, and bankruptcy.",""],[1,"281","4","Ease of Doing Business Legal and Institutional Reform","Improving economy-related laws that support the ease of doing business by preparing regulations that, strengthen IT-based systems in services and management of civil cases, and strengthen institutions that support the execution of court decisions.",""],[1,"286","2","Regulatory Quality Improvement and Simplification","Improving the quality and quantity of regulations must be carried out with governance that not only takes into account the rules that apply in the formation of regulations, but is also able to produce regulations that are simple, orderly, easy to understand, and provide concrete benefits in the implementation of national development.",""],[1,"286","10","Regulatory Impact Analysis and Evidence-Based Policy Reform","The prevailing mindset -- common in ministries/institutions/regional government -- of making as many regulations as possible must be changed by first studying priority policies and performing regulatory impact analysis by utilizing information technology in order to produce accurate evidence-based regulations and/or policies in the next five years (2020-2024).",""],[1,"286","11","Regulatory Simplification and Framework Rationalization","This approach will reduce the number of unnecessary regulations and save the cost of establishing legislation in order to have a clear regulatory framework",""],[1,"287","6","Omnibus Law Regulatory Simplification Reform","the Omnibus Law approach can be applied, namely by simplifying, revoking, revising, or combining several regulations -- including laws, government regulations, presidential regulations, ministerial regulations, and regional regulations -- whose substance is almost the same as that of another regulation, or whose substance overlaps or is conflicting with that of another.",""],[1,"287","11","Regulatory Evaluation and Policy Assessment Mechanism","The core of the Omnibus Law approach is the evaluation, assessment, and research related to regulations and policy choices to ensure proper, flexible, and accountable regulations.",""],[1,"287","12","Regulatory Simplification and Deregulation Rule","ministries/institutions and regional governments that issues a new regulation must revoke at least two valid regulations whose substance regulates the same aspect.",""],[1,"288","14","Omnibus Law Regulatory Reform","The Omnibus Law approach must be understood as a comprehensive and integrated effort in the framework of structuring and improving the quality of regulations as illustrated in Figure 9.4.",""],[1,"290","11","Legal Metrology Law Revision","Revision of Law No. 2/1981 concerning legal metrology.",""],[1,"290","12","Job Creation Draft Bill","Draft bill on job creation (including bill related to UMKM, using the Omnibus Law approach)",""],[1,"290","13","Draft Omnibus Law on Provisions and Tax Facilitation","Draft bill on provisions and tax facilitation to strengthen the economy (Omnibus Law approach)",""],[1,"290","14","Revision of Business Merging and Consolidation Regulation","a. Revision of PP No. 57/2010 on merging and consolidating business",""],[1,"290","16","Draft Procedures for Handling Unfair Business Competition Cases and Administrative Sanctions","PP Draft on procedures for handling cases and imposing administrative sanctions for unfair business competition;",""],[2,"20","6","Omnibus Law Regulatory Simplification","Menyederhanakan segala bentuk regulasi dengan pendekatan Omnibus Law, terutama menerbitkan 2 undang-undang.",""],[2,"20","6","Job Creation Law","Pertama, UU Cipta Lapangan Kerja.",""],[2,"20","6","MSME Empowerment Law","Kedua, UU Pemberdayaan UMKM.",""],[2,"20","7","Employment Creation Investment and Administrative Simplification Reform","Memprioritaskan investasi untuk penciptaan lapangan kerja, memangkas prosedur dan birokrasi yang panjang, dan menyederhanakan eselonisasi.",""],[2,"24","7","Regulatory Streamlining Reform","Mengurangi tumpang tindih regulasi (membentuk 1 regulasi baru dengan mencabut 2 aturan yang masih berlaku dan substansinya mengatur hal yang sama)",""],[2,"264","9","Regulatory Management Institution Establishment","Pembentukan Lembaga Pengelola Regulasi, dengan fokus: sinkronisasi dengan pemangku kepentingan dalam pembentukan regulasi; integrasi proses monitoring dan evaluasi regulasi; optimalisasi akses dan partisipasi publik dalam penyusunan dan pembentukan regulasi; penguatan harmonisasi dan sinergitas kebijakan dan regulasi; dan dukungan database berbasis teknologi informasi;",""],[2,"269","3","Regulatory Quality Improvement and Simplification Reform","Peningkatan kualitas dan kuantitas regulasi harus dilakukan dengan tatakelola yang tidak saja memperhatikan kaidah-kaidah yang berlaku dalam pembentukan regulasi, namun juga mampu menghasilkan regulasi yang sederhana, mudah dipahami, dan tertib, serta memberikan manfaat konkrit dalam pelaksanaan pembangunan nasional.",""],[2,"269","12","Evidence-Based Regulatory and Policy Reform","Pola pikir yang selama ini dilakukan dan dipahami oleh Kementerian/Lembaga/Pemerintah Daerah dengan membuat regulasi sebanyak-banyaknya, harus diubah dengan terlebih dahulu mempelajari kebijakan prioritas, menganalisis dampak regulasi (Regulatory Impact Analysis), didukung oleh teknologi informasi sehingga akan menghasilkan regulasi dan/ atau kebijakan berdasarkan data-data yang akurat (evidence based) pada lima tahun ke depan (2020-2024).",""],[2,"269","13","Regulatory Streamlining and Cost Reduction","Pendekatan tersebut akan mengurangi jumlah regulasi yang tidak perlu dan menghemat biaya pembentukan peraturan perundangan sehingga terlihat jelas kontribusi kerangka regulasi untuk mendukung Visi-Misi Presiden dan Wakil Presiden 2020-2024, sebagaimana pada Gambar 9.3.",""],[2,"270","8","Omnibus Law Regulatory Simplification","Sebagai salah satu strategi penataan regulasi, pendekatan Omnibus Law dapat diterapkan yaitu dengan opsi penyederhanaan atau pencabutan, perevisian atau penggabungan beberapa regulasi (Undang-Undang (UU), Peraturan Pemerintah (PP), Peraturan Presiden (Perpres), Peraturan Menteri (Permen), dan Peraturan Daerah (Perda) Provinsi serta Kabupaten/Kota) yang substansinya hampir sama satu dengan lainnya, tumpang tindih dan konflik.",""],[2,"270","9","Regulatory Simplification and Deregulation under the Omnibus Law Approach","Pendekatan Omnibus Law dalam praktiknya telah dilakukan melalui simplifikasi regulasi dan deregulasi paket kebijakan ekonomi.",""],[2,"270","10","Omnibus Law Regulatory Review and Policy Research","Inti pendekatan omnibus law adalah evaluasi, pengkajian, penelitian terkait regulasi dan pilihan kebijakan untuk memastikan regulasi yang tepat, fleksibel, namun akuntabel.",""],[2,"270","11","One-in, Two-out Regulatory Simplification Rule","Kementerian/Lembaga dan Pemerintah Daerah yang membuat 1 (satu) regulasi baru harus mencabut paling sedikit 2 (dua) regulasi yang masih berlaku dan substansinya mengatur hal yang sama.",""],[2,"271","17","Policy and Regulatory Formulation Process Improvement","Alur perumusan kebijakan dan/atau perumusan regulasi didorong melalui suatu evaluasi berdasarkan suatu hambatan/dinamika pembangunan",""],[2,"272","3","Omnibus Law Regulatory Reform Approach","Pendekatan Omnibus Law harus dipahami sebagai upaya menyeluruh dan terpadu dalam rangka penataan dan peningkatan kualitas regulasi sebagaimana tergambarkan pada Gambar 9.4.",""]],"13":[[1,"303","5","Improved Regional Transfer and Village Funds","Improved regional transfer and village funds.",""],[1,"303","7","Central-Regional Grant Mechanism Expansion through Output-Based Transfers","Strengthening the integration between the central and regional governments is also carried out by developing and expanding grant mechanisms in regions through output- based transfers.",""],[1,"303","11","Decentralization and Local Autonomy Support Measures","To support the implementation of decentralization, regional autonomy, and village autonomy; and to enhance the",""],[1,"304","3","Implementation Support for Regional Autonomy and Village Governance Laws","Supporting the implementation of Law No. 23/2014 on the regional government, Law No. 11/2011 on the government of Aceh, Law No. 21/2001 on the special autonomy status for the province of Papua, Law No. 13/2012 on the privileges of the Special Region of Yogyakarta, and Law No. 6/2014 on villages in a full, consistent, real, and responsible manner;",""],[1,"304","7","Integrated Utilization of Regional Transfer and Village Funds","Increasing the integrated utilization of regional transfer and village funds by ministries/institutions and other funding sources more efficiently and effectively following the \"value for money\" principle;",""],[1,"304","8","Governance Improvement for Regional Transfer and Village Funds","Improving the quality of governance of regional transfer and village funds when planning, allocating, and implementing, as well as developing IT-based control and evaluation",""],[1,"304","9","Profit-Sharing Governance Reform","improving profit-sharing governance that is more transparent, accountable, fair, responsible, and effective based on performance improvement",""],[1,"304","9","Timely Profit-Sharing Distribution Plan","setting up profit-sharing distribution plans that are timely and fair through commitment to quickly resolve any underpayment or overpayment",""],[1,"304","9","Optimization of Profit-Sharing Plan Management","optimizing the utilization and management of profit- sharing plans to accelerate the improvement of people's welfare and regional progress by taking into account the carrying capacity of the environment in the respective regions",""],[1,"304","10","General Allocation Fund Formula Improvement","The policy directions for general allocation funds are: (1) Improving the allocation formulas by taking into account",""],[1,"305","1","Interregional Fiscal Allocation Formula Reform","perfecting the allocation formulas to ensure interregional equity and balanced regional allocation at the provincial and regency/city levels by improving interregional fiscal distribution; and (5) a minimum of 25% of the general allocations funds is directed toward regional infrastructure spending.",""],[1,"305","2","Regional Basic Services and Infrastructure Development Support","Enhancing the ability of regional governments to provide basic services according to minimum service standards, accelerate infrastructure development that would have a direct impact on the welfare of the people (regular scheme), which includes education, health, drinking water, sanitation, housing, and transportation;",""],[1,"305","3","Regional Government Support for Priority Goals and Affirmative Action Schemes","Enhancing the ability of regional governments to support the achievement of national priority goals and objectives, and achieve global development goals through cross- sectoral schemes, including by supporting conservation zones, and strategic and regional areas (assignment scheme); and encourage affirmative action (affirmation scheme) for disadvantaged, outermost, and frontier areas, border regions, small outermost islands, and island groups;",""],[1,"305","6","Special Transfer Fund Allocation Efficiency Reform","Increasing efficiency, effectiveness, and fairness in the allocation and utilization of special transfer funds by calculating: (1) unit costs, expenditure standards, and Regional Expensiveness Index; (2) the previous year's implementation costs; (3) the relationship between allocation and performance of development with incentives to achieve performance (reward); and (4) the application of disincentives for regions that exchange special transfer fund budget with regional budget;",""],[1,"305","7","Output-Based Regional Grant Allocation Scheme","Encouraging grant allocation schemes to regions through output-based transfers and regions with high fiscal capacity to initiate infrastructure development;",""],[1,"305","8","Special Transfer Funds Coordination and Management System","Strengthening coordination, cooperation, and partnership among ministries/institutions and regional governments in managing special transfer funds by developing: (1) integrated web-based information systems and databases, (2) facilitation and capacity building of regional governments, (3) performance-based distribution control, and (4) regular reporting;",""],[1,"305","9","Strengthening Government Internal Oversight of Special Transfer Funds","Strengthening the role of the Government Internal Oversight Body (APIP) in improving governance of special transfer funds that is transparent, fair, and accountable.",""],[1,"306","1","Incentive Funds for Regional Governments","incentive funds for regional governments in supporting public services, economic development, and increasing competitiveness in accordance with regional priorities;",""],[1,"306","2","Performance-Based Formula for Regional Incentive Allocation","Improving the formula for calculating the allocation of regional incentives that take into account and directly link the amount of allocated funds with the performance of outputs, outcomes, and tangible impacts resulting from policies, initiatives, innovations, creativity, and achievements by the regional government.",""],[1,"311","6","Output-Based Regional Grant Transfer Mechanism","the central government will continue to develop grants to regions as a form of output-based transfer.",""],[2,"99","2","Performance-Based Fiscal Decentralization Management","memperkuat kualitas desentralisasi fiskal melalui pengelolaan Transfer ke Daerah dan Dana Desa berbasis kinerja, serta perbaikan pengelolaan keuangan daerah yang efisien, efektif, dan akuntabel.",""],[2,"99","3","Innovative and Inclusive Financing Scheme Development","reformasi fiskal ditempuh dengan mendorong pengembangan skema pembiayaan yang inovatif dan inklusif dengan mengutamakan pendalaman pasar keuangan domestik.",""],[2,"124","6","Optimization of Regional Transfer Funds","optimalisasi dana transfer daerah yang lebih produktif dan afirmatif bagi kemajuan daerah",""],[2,"124","6","Regional Revenue Enhancement through Data and Information Systems","peningkatan penerimaan dan pendapatan daerah baik pajak dan retribusi daerah maupun sumber-sumber penerimaan dan pendapatan lainnya melalui penataan dan pengembangan data dan informasi",""],[2,"124","6","Improvement of Regional Budget Quality","peningkatan kualitas belanja daerah yang berdampak bagi percepatan pencapaian SPM, peningkatan kesejahteraan rakyat dan kemajuan daerah",""],[2,"139","3","Improvement of Regional Budget Management and Quality","pengelolaan dan kualitas belanja dana APBD sebagian daerah dan dana Otonomi Khusus Aceh dapat terus ditingkatkan.",""],[2,"285","9","Cross-Ministerial and Intergovernmental Coordination for Planning and Budget Integration","Integrasi dan sinergi antar sumber pendanaan ini dilakukan sejak dari penyusunan Rencana Kerja Pemerintah hingga RAPBN tiap tahunnya.",""],[2,"285","9","Strengthening Central-Local Synergy through Performance-Based Grants","Perkuatan sinergi pusat dan daerah juga dilakukan melalui pengembangan dan perluasan mekananisme hibah ke Daerah melalui transfer berbasis kinerja (output based transfer).",""],[2,"285","9","Program Control to Ensure National Priority Delivery in Regions","Hal ini juga sangat terkait dengan pengendalian program untuk menjamin pencapaian prioritas nasional di daerah.",""],[2,"286","2","Regional and Village Transfer Fund Allocation","Pemerintah akan mengalokasikan Dana Transfer ke Daerah dan Dana Desa (TKDD) yang terdiri atas 4 (empat) komponen, yaitu: (1) Dana Perimbangan yang terbagi menjadi Dana Transfer Umum (DTU) yang mencakup Dana Bagi Hasil (DBH) dan Dana Alokasi Umum (DAU), serta Dana Transfer Khusus (DTK) yang terdiri dari Dana Alokasi Khusus (DAK) Fisik dan Non-Fisik, (2) Dana Insentif Daerah, (3) Dana Otonomi Khusus dan Dana Keistimewaan DI Yogyakarta, dan (4) Dana Desa.",""],[2,"286","4","Full and Consistent Implementation of Decentralization and Special Autonomy Laws","Mendukung pelaksanaan UU Nomor 23 Tahun 2014 tentang Pemerintahan Daerah, UU Nomor 11 Tahun 2011 tentang Pemerintah Aceh, UU Nomor 21 Tahun 2001 tentang Otonomi Khusus bagi Provinsi Papua, UU Nomor 13 Tahun 2012 tentang Keistimewaan Daerah Istimewa Yogyakarta, dan UU No 6 Tahun 2014 tentang Desa secara penuh, konsisten, nyata dan bertanggung jawab;",""],[2,"286","6","Local Government Support for National Priority and SDG Delivery","Mendukung pemerintah daerah mencapai tujuan dan sasaran prioritas nasional seperti peningkatan kemandirian dan keberdayaan masyarakat desa, pertumbuhan ekonomi, perluasan kesempatan kerja, pengurangan kemiskinan, pengurangan kesenjangan, peningkatan Indeks Pembangunan Manusia (IPM), pengurangan angka stunting, penyediaan air bersih dan sanitasi, peningkatan mutu sumber daya manusia siap kerja, pengurangan emisi karbon, pengelolaan kawasan hutan dan daerah konservasi, dan pengurangan risiko bencana; kawasan ekonomi strategis; serta pencapaian tujuan pembangunan global (SDGs);",""],[2,"286","7","Improved Integration of TKDD Funds with Central Government Spending","4. Meningkatkan keterpaduan pemanfaatan Dana TKDD dengan belanja kementerian/ lembaga (K/L) dan sumber dana lainnya secara lebih efisien, efektif dengan prinsip nilai ekonomi (value for money);",""],[2,"286","8","Improved TKDD Fund Governance and Information-Based Monitoring System","Meningkatkan kualitas tata kelola Dana TKDD mulai dari perencanaan, pengalokasian, pelaksanaan hingga mengembangkan sistem pengendalian dan evaluasi berbasis sistem informasi.",""],[2,"286","10","DBH Governance and Allocation Reform","Arah Kebijakan Dana Bagi hasil (DBH) sebagai berikut: (1) Meningkatkan tata kelola DBH yang lebih transparan, akuntabel, adil, bertanggung jawab dan efektif berbasis peningkatan kinerja; (2) Menetapkan alokasi DBH secara tepat waktu dan tepat jumlah melalui komitmen percepatan penyelesaian kurang bayar/lebih bayar; serta (3) Mengoptimalkan pemanfaatan dan pengelolaan DBH bagi percepatan peningkatan kesejahteraan rakyat dan kemajuan daerah dengan memperhitungkan daya dukung lingkungan di daerah.",""],[2,"286","11","General Allocation Fund Allocation Formula Reform","Menyempurnakan formulasi alokasi DAU dengan memperhitungkan perubahan bobot Alokasi Dasar (gaji PNSD), serta kebutuhan pemenuhan standar pelayanan minimum dan kapasitas fiskal;",""],[2,"287","2","Revision of General Allocation Fund and Fiscal Equalization Formula","memberikan bobot luas wilayah laut dalam variabel luas wilayah menjadi 100 persen; (3) mempertimbangkan afirmasi kepada daerah konservasi dengan memperhitungkan kemampuan daerah dalam mempertahankan luas hutan tanaman nasional; (4) menyempurnakan formula alokasi DAU agar terjadi pemerataan antardaerah dan keseimbangan alokasi provinsi dan kabupaten/kota melalui perbaikan indeks pemerataan kemampuan fiskal antardaerah; serta (5) mengarahkan minimal 25 persen dari DTU (DAU dan DBH) untuk belanja infrastruktur daerah.",""],[2,"287","4","Cross-Sector Regional Support Schemes for Local Governments","Meningkatkan kemampuan pemerintah daerah dalam mendukung pencapaian tujuan dan sasaran prioritas nasional, dan pencapaian tujuan pembangunan global melalui skema yang bersifat lintas sektor termasuk mendukung daerah konservasi, kawasan strategis dan kewilayahan (skema penugasan);",""],[2,"287","5","DTK Planning, Allocation, and Management Synchronization and Integration","Mempertajam sinkronisasi dan integrasi perencanaan, pengalokasian dan pengelolaan DTK dengan kegiatan yang didukung oleh sumber pendanaan lainnya;",""],[2,"287","6","DTK Allocation and Utilization Efficiency Reform","Meningkatkan efisiensi, efektivitas dan keadilan dalam pengalokasian dan pemanfaatan DTK dengan memperhitungkan: (1) satuan biaya, standar belanja dan indeks kemahalan daerah; (2) realisasi pelaksanaan tahun sebelumnya; (3) keterkaitan alokasi dan kinerja pembangunan dengan insentif pencapaian kinerja (reward); serta (4) penerapan disinsentif bagi daerah yang melakukan pertukaran anggaran DTK dengan APBD;",""],[2,"287","7","Performance-Based Grant Allocation Scheme for Local Infrastructure Initiatives","Mendorong skema alokasi hibah ke daerah melalui transfer berbasis kinerja (output based transfer), bagi daerah dengan kapasitas fiskal tinggi yang melakukan inisiatif pembangunan infrastruktur;",""],[2,"287","8","Integrated Coastal Area Management Coordination and Capacity Support","Memperkuat koordinasi, kerjasama dan kemitraan K/L dan pemerintah daerah dalam pengelolaan DTK dengan mengembangkan: (1) data dasar dan sistem informasi terpadu berbasis website, (2) pendampingan dan peningkatan kapasitas pemerintah daerah, (3) pengendalian penyaluran berbasis kinerja, dan (4) pelaporan secara rutin;",""],[2,"287","9","Strengthening APIP Role in DTK Governance","Memperkuat peran APIP dalam peningkatan tata kelola DTK yang transparan, adil dan akuntabel.",""],[2,"287","10","Improved Use of Regional Incentive Funds","Meningkatkan efisiensi dan efektivitas pemanfaatan DID sebagai insentif bagi pemerintah daerah dalam mendukung pelayanan publik, pengembangan ekonomi, dan meningkatkan daya saing sesuai dengan prioritas daerah;",""],[2,"287","11","Performance-Based DID Allocation Formula Reform","Menyempurnakan formula penghitungan alokasi DID yang memperhitungkan dan mengaitkan langsung jumlah alokasi dana dengan kinerja keluaran, hasil dan dampak nyata yang dihasilkan dari kebijakan, inisiatif, inovasi, kreativitas, dan capaian keunggulan pemerintah daerah.",""],[2,"288","2","Intergovernmental Coordination and Fund Management Mechanism","memperkuat koordinasi, kerjasama dan kemitraan antara Pemerintah Provinsi Aceh dengan Pemerintah Kabupaten/Kota dan K/L dalam perencanaan, pengalokasian, penganggaran, penyaluran, pelaporan, pemantauan, pengendalian dan evaluasi pemanfaatan dana",""],[2,"293","2","Output-Based Intergovernmental Transfer Mechanism","Untuk memperkuat pengendalian program serta memperkuat sinergi antara Pemerintah Pusat dan Daerah dalam pencapaian sasaran pembangunan Pemerintah akan melanjutkan pengembangan hibah ke daerah sebagai bentuk mekanisme transfer berbasis kinerja (output based transfer).",""]],"14":[[2,"264","17","Corruption Prevention Action Implementation","Penguatan upaya pencegahan korupsi, melalui implementasi Aksi Pencegahan Korupsi sesuai Strategi Nasional Pencegahan Korupsi;",""],[2,"264","18","Asset Recovery and Management Mechanism for Corruption Proceeds","Optimalisasi mekanisme pemulihan dan pengelolaan aset hasil tindak pidana korupsi dalam sistem peradilan secara menyeluruh serta pemanfaatannya untuk mendukung pembangunan.",""]],"15":[[1,"302","7","Project Implementation Control Mechanism","the government will control the development of projects, including priority ones, where the location and the subject in charge have been clearly identified.",""],[1,"302","7","Priority Project Selection and Monitoring Improvement","The improvement of these priority projects will also be continually pursued in terms of the selection criteria and mechanism to control the implementation.",""],[1,"313","1","Integrated Evaluation and Control System","The evaluation and control processes in the next five years are focused on evaluating the performance of the seven development agendas and five presidential directives through integrated evaluation and control",""],[1,"313","3","Evaluation Framework Development","For this reason, an evaluation framework needs to be developed to ensure that the evaluation",""],[1,"314","2","Mid-term RPJMN Evaluation","A mid-term evaluation of the RPJMN, which is carried out in the third year of the 2020-2024 RPJMN period of which the results are used as input in the preparation of the next government work plans (RKP) and as feedback for revisions in the 2020-2024 RPJMN if needed.",""],[1,"314","2","Annual RKP Evaluation","Every year, an RKP evaluation is conducted, which is part of the stage of the RPJMN implementation.",""],[1,"314","3","Final RPJMN Evaluation and Next-Period Planning","The final evaluation of the RPJMN is carried out in the last year of the implementation period.",""],[1,"314","11","RPJMN Evaluation and Feedback Mechanism","The RPJMN evaluation is conducted by the Minister of National Development Planning/Head of Bappenas based on the strategic plan evaluation report from all ministries/institutions, the government work plan (RKP) evaluation report from the current RPJMN period, and other supporting data from survey and research results.","Minister of National Development Planning/Head of Bappenas | all ministries/institutions"],[1,"315","2","Evaluation of Strategic Policies and Programs","Evaluation is carried out on strategic policies or programs that fulfill the criteria of having a large budget, which has a large impact on the target group or community; and of having a large influence on the achievement of national development.",""],[1,"315","4","RPJMN Evaluation Mechanism","The Ministry of National Development Planning/Bappenas evaluates the RPJMN based on the evaluation results of the Renstra K/ and other available data sources.","The Ministry of National Development Planning/Bappenas"],[1,"316","3","Development Plan Implementation Control Framework","it is necessary to develop a control framework as explained below.",""],[1,"316","4","Control Implementation for Priority Program Tracking","The purpose of control implementation is to guarantee and ensure that the implementation of priority programs or activities are in accordance with their respective plans (or on-track) by taking into account recommendations or findings on the monitoring and evaluation results",""],[1,"316","8","Development Control Function in Government Agencies","Function of development control is attached in each government agency both at the central and regional levels, and is carried out by the leader of the ministry/institution or regional government in accordance with their respective duties and authorities in the monitoring and supervising processes.",""],[1,"316","10","Regular On-Site Supervision for Corrective Actions","If the control is accompanied by corrective actions (or alignment) at the level of priority programs or activities mid-implementation of the RPJMN, then supervision is an on-site inspection that is carried out regularly within a certain period.",""],[1,"317","1","Midterm Corrective Action for Priority Program Implementation","corrective actions are taken to ensure that the implementation of priority programs or activities is on track according to the RPJMN document.",""],[1,"317","2","Annual RKP Corrective Action Process","Based on point (a) above and/or on the results of the government work plan (RKP) evaluation that is performed annually, corrective actions are carried out in the second semester of each implementation of RKP on certain",""],[1,"317","4","Priority Program Implementation Control System","Control is a follow-up step taken to ensure that the implementation of priority programs or activities are according to plan.",""],[1,"317","7","Corrective Action on Priority Programs and Activities","Corrective action on certain priority programs and priority activities is performed in the second semester of every RKP period",""],[1,"318","2","Priority Program Implementation Irregularity Detection","Identifying any irregularities that occur during the implementation of priority programs or activities,",""],[1,"319","1","Preventive Control and Suspension of Priority Programs","Preventive action is a control measure to reduce or eliminate the possibility of implementing priority programs or activities that are not on target.",""],[2,"268","7","National Development Plan Monitoring, Evaluation, and Control","Untuk menjamin efektivitas pelaksanaan RPJMN 2020-2024, Kementerian Perencanaan Pembangunan Nasional/Badan Perencanaan Pembangunan Nasional melaksanakan pemantauan dan evaluasi terhadap penjabaran RPJMN dalam Renstra K/L dan RPJMD serta melakukan pengendalian terhadap pelaksanaan RPJMN.","Kementerian Perencanaan Pembangunan Nasional/Badan Perencanaan Pembangunan Nasional"],[2,"284","9","Priority Development Plan Control Mechanism","Untuk itu pemerintah akan mengendalikan rencana pembangunan hingga tingkat proyek prioritas dimana lokasi dan penanggung jawab kegiatannya jelas terukur.",""],[2,"284","9","Priority Project Selection and Control Improvement","Penyempurnaan proyek prioritas juga terus diupayakan baik pada kriteria pemilihan maupun didalam mekanisme pengendalian pelaksanaannya.",""],[2,"285","10","Regular Review of Development Programs","Untuk itu dilakukan tinjau ulang (review) secara berkala terhadap program pembangunan.",""],[2,"285","10","Improved Development Planning Allocation and Delivery Mechanism","Hasil dari tinjau ulang ini kemudian digunakan sebagai salah satu pertimbangan dalam pengalokasian perencanaan pembangunan serta sebagai bagian dari perbaikan mekanisme pendanaan dan pelaksanaan program (delivery mechanism).",""],[2,"294","3","Development Plan Implementation Control, Monitoring, and Evaluation","pengendalian pelaksanaan rencana pembangunan dimaksudkan untuk menjamin tercapainya tujuan dan sasaran pembangunan yang tertuang dalam rencana melalui kegiatan-kegiatan koreksi dan penyesuaian selama pelaksanaan rencana tersebut oleh pimpinan kementerian/lembaga (K/L) atau pemerintah daerah, melalui kegiatan pemantauan dan pengawasan.",""],[2,"294","4","Integrated Development Evaluation and Control System (SITEP)","Pelaksanaan evaluasi dan pengendalian dalam 5 (lima) tahun ke depan difokuskan untuk menilai kinerja pelaksanaan 7 (tujuh) agenda pembangunan dan 5 (lima) arahan Presiden melalui Sistem Informasi Terpadu Evaluasi dan Pengendalian (SITEP) yang pelaksanaannya diharapkan efektif pada pertengahan periode pelaksanaan RPJMN 2020-2024.",""],[2,"295","2","Evaluation Framework Development","Untuk itu perlu disusun kerangka evaluasi untuk memastikan bahwa evaluasi berjalan dengan baik dan hasil evaluasi bermanfaat bagi proses pengambilan kebijakan dan proses penyusunan perencanaan dan penganggaran pada periode berikutnya.",""],[2,"295","3","Development Performance Evaluation and Policy Feedback Mechanism","Tujuan Pelaksanaan Evaluasi, antara lain: (a) mengetahui hasil capaian kinerja pembangunan, identifikasi permasalahan dan tindak lanjut yang direkomendasikan sebagai bahan untuk perumusan dan perbaikan kebijakan/program/kegiatan; dan (b) membantu penentuan penyusunan sasaran dan target kinerja pembangunan secara tepat.",""],[2,"295","6","Midterm RPJMN Evaluation and Annual RKP Review","Evaluasi paruh waktu RPJMN dilakukan pada tahun ketiga pelaksanaan RPJMN 2020-2024, yang hasilnya digunakan sebagai bahan masukan dalam penyusunan RKP dan bahan untuk melakukan revisi RPJMN 2020-2024 jika diperlukan.",""],[2,"295","7","Final Evaluation of the RPJMN","Evaluasi akhir RPJMN dilakukan pada tahun terakhir pelaksanaan RPJMN, yang hasilnya digunakan sebagai input dalam penyusunan RPJMN periode selanjutnya (RPJMN 2025-2029).",""],[2,"296","6","RPJMN Evaluation and Feedback Mechanism","Evaluasi RPJMN dilakukan oleh Menteri Perencanaan Pembangunan Nasional/Kepala Bappenas berdasarkan laporan evaluasi Renstra seluruh K/L, laporan evaluasi RKP pada periode RPJMN berjalan, serta data pendukung lainnya dari hasil survei dan penelitian.","Menteri Perencanaan Pembangunan Nasional/Kepala Bappenas"],[2,"296","6","Government Accountability Reporting to the President","Hasil evaluasi disampaikan oleh Menteri kepada Presiden sebagai bentuk akuntabilitas pemerintah dan digunakan sebagai masukan/feedback dalam rangka pengambilan kebijakan dan proses perencanaan dan penganggaran selanjutnya.","Menteri | Presiden"],[2,"296","10","Strategic Policy and Program Evaluation","Evaluasi Kebijakan/Program Strategis, dilakukan untuk menunjukkan klarifikasi hubungan sebab-akibat kegagalan atau keberhasilan rencana.",""],[2,"296","12","RPJMN Evaluation Mechanism","Kementerian PPN/Bappenas melakukan evaluasi RPJMN berdasarkan hasil evaluasi Renstra K/L dan sumber data lain yang tersedia.","Kementerian PPN/Bappenas"],[2,"296","12","Renstra K/L Evaluation Coordination Mechanism","Pelaksanaan evaluasi Renstra K/L dikoordinasikan oleh Kedeputian yang membidangi Evaluasi dan Pengendalian Pembangunan bersama-sama dengan Kedeputian yang membidangi sektor dan regional.","Kedeputian yang membidangi Evaluasi dan Pengendalian Pembangunan | Kedeputian yang membidangi sektor dan regional"],[2,"297","14","Development Plan Implementation Control Framework","Untuk itu perlu disusun kerangka pengendalian dengan penjelasan sebagai berikut.",""],[2,"297","15","Implementation Control and Monitoring System","Tujuan Pelaksanaan Pengendalian adalah untuk menjamin dan memastikan agar pelaksanaan program prioritas/kegiatan prioritas sesuai dengan rencana (on-track) dengan memperhatikan rekomendasi atau temuan atas hasil pemantauan dan evaluasi.",""],[2,"298","3","Midterm Corrective Actions for Priority Programs and Activities","Berdasarkan hasil Evaluasi paruh waktu RPJMN pada tahun ketiga pelaksanaan RPJMN 2020-2024, dilakukan tindakan korektif untuk memastikan pelaksanaan program prioritas/kegiatan prioritas berjalan on-track sebagaimana tercantum dalam dokumen RPJMN.",""],[2,"298","4","Mid-Year Corrective Actions for Priority Programs and Activities","berdasarkan butir a di atas dan atau hasil evaluasi RKP yang dilaksanakan setiap tahun dilakukan tindakan korektif pada semester kedua setiap pelaksanaan RKP pada program prioritas/kegiatan prioritas tertentu (dengan besaran anggaran minimal tertentu yang ditentukan untuk pemilihan program prioritas/kegiatan prioritas).",""],[2,"298","6","Priority Program Monitoring and Control System","Pengendalian merupakan langkah tindak lanjut yang ditempuh untuk menjamin agar pelaksanaan program prioritas/kegiatan prioritas sesuai dengan rencana.",""],[2,"298","10","Midterm Corrective Action for Priority Programs","dilakukan tindakan korektif pada paruh waktu (tahun ketiga) pelaksanaan RPJMN pada program prioritas/kegiatan prioritas yang berdampak luas.",""],[2,"299","4","Midterm Corrective Actions for Priority Program Implementation","Keputusan untuk melakukan tindakan korektif pada paruh waktu pelaksanaan RPJMN terhadap program prioritas/kegiatan prioritas mencakup 2 hal, yaitu tindakan konstruktif dan tindakan preventif.",""],[2,"299","5","Policy Refocusing for Priority Program Acceleration","Kebijakan pemfokusan kembali (refocusing), yaitu pemfokusan langkah percepatan pencapaian target program prioritas/kegiatan prioritas;",""],[2,"299","6","Policy Reorientation and Review of Priority Programs","(ii Kebijakan peninjauan ulang (reorientasi), yaitu peninjauan atau penyesuaian target dan langkah strategis pelaksanaan program prioritas/kegiatan prioritas; dan",""],[2,"299","8","Preventive Control and Suspension Mechanism for Priority Programs","Tindakan preventif adalah tindakan pengendalian untuk mengurangi atau menghilangkan kemungkinan pelaksanaan program prioritas/kegiatan prioritas yang tidak sesuai target, yang dimungkinkan pula sampai pada keputusan untuk menghentikan pelaksanaan program prioritas/kegiatan prioritas yang sifatnya penghentian sementara ataupun penghentian tetap apabila diperlukan (suspend definitif atau sementara dalam Sistem KRISNA).",""],[2,"299","9","Policy Refocusing for Priority Program Implementation","Sementara untuk tindakan korektif pada semester kedua pelaksanaan RKP hanya mencakup tindakan konstruktif melalui kebijakan pemfokusan kembali (refocusing) atas langkah pencapaian target program prioritas/kegiatan prioritas.",""]],"16":[[1,"94","1","State-Owned Enterprise Capacity and Holding Company Development","enhancement of capacity, capability, and competitiveness of BUMN, by establishing state-owned holding companies and exploring the international market, among others.",""]],"17":[[1,"279","21","Information and Public Communication Governance Strengthening","Strengthening governance on information and public communication in ministries/ institutions/regional government, and providing content and access;",""],[2,"263","12","Public Information and Communication Governance Strengthening","Penguatan tata kelola informasi dan komunikasi publik di K/L/D serta penyediaan konten dan akses;",""],[2,"288","2","Participatory and Accountable Governance Strengthening","penguatan tata kelola pemerintahan yang partisipatif, transparan, akuntabel dan adil",""]],"18":[[1,"291","2","Draft Presidential Regulation on Integrated Tourism Master Plans","Draft Perpres on integrated tourism master plans",""],[1,"291","16","Revision of National Spatial Planning Regulation","Revision of PP 13/2017 on amendments to PP No. 26/2008 concerning national spatial planning (RTRWN)",""],[1,"292","4","Draft Presidential Regulation on Metropolitan Spatial Plans","Perpres draft on spatial plans for the Banjarmasin-Banjarbaru- Banjar-Barito-Kuala-Tanah Laut metropolitan area (Banjarmasin metropolitan area)",""],[1,"292","12","Revision of Island Spatial Planning Presidential Regulation","Revision of Perpres on spatial planning on islands.",""],[1,"292","13","Detailed Spatial Planning Regulation for Border Regions","Perpres draft on detailed spatial planning in border regions.",""],[1,"292","14","Draft Presidential Regulation on Spatial Planning in National Strategic Areas","Perpres draft on spatial planning in national strategy areas.",""],[2,"274","2","Revision of the Abandoned Land Regulation","Revisi PP No. 11/2010 tentang Penertiban dan Pendayagunaan Tanah Terlantar",""]],"19":[[1,"295","13","Political Parties Law Revision","Revision of Law No. 2/2011 on amendments to Law No. 2/2008 concerning political parties.",""],[1,"295","27","Revision of Political Party Financial Assistance Regulation","Revision of the second amendment to PP No. 5/2009 on financial assistance political parties.",""]],"20":[[2,"20","2","Five Main National Development Directives","Presiden menetapkan 5 (lima) arahan utama sebagai strategi dalam pelaksanaan misi Nawacita dan pencapaian sasaran Visi Indonesia 2045.",""],[2,"30","10","Bureaucratic Institutional Reform for Quality Public Services","Reformasi kelembagaan birokrasi untuk pelayanan publik berkualitas;",""],[2,"278","2","Institutional Framework for Development Delivery","Dalam konteks Mekanisme Penghantaran (delivery mechanism), kelembagaan difokuskan pada penataan organisasi pemerintah beserta aturan main di dalamnya, baik yang bersifat inter maupun antar organisasi, yang berfungsi untuk melaksanakan program-program pembangunan.",""],[2,"278","3","Government Organizational Restructuring Based on Strategy","Dengan menekankan nilai 'Struktur Mengikuti Strategi' (structure follow strategy), maka pembentukan organisasi pemerintah didasarkan pada strategi untuk pencapaian tujuan pembangunan.",""],[2,"278","10","Institutional Effectiveness Improvement","Mendorong efektivitas kelembagaan melalui ketepatan struktur organisasi, ketepatan proses (tata laksana) organisasi, serta pencegahan duplikasi tugas dan fungsi organisasi.",""]],"21":[[1,"39","2","Financial Sector Deepening and Inclusion Initiative","Efforts to finance investment needs for 2020-2024 are made by deepening the financial sector-both banks and non- banks-by increasing financial inclusion, expanding financial product innovation, developing financial services infrastructure, and optimizing financing alternatives, among others.",""],[1,"48","7","Integrated Development Funding Mobilization","it is necessary to integrate development funding from government sources that include ministries/institutions, non- ministries/institutions, regional transfers and village funds; from BUMN; from the collaboration between the government and business entities; and from the collaboration with the public sector in which the collaboration is in line with the \"Money Follows\" principle.",""],[1,"48","7","Innovative Public-Private Financing Schemes","the government needs to encourage more funding from sources that come from both the public and private sector through innovative financing schemes, including government-to-business cooperation schemes, among others.",""],[1,"54","4","Innovative Financing Schemes for Development Investment","efforts are also made to encourage innovative financing schemes, such as government-to-business schemes (or KPBU), blended finance, green finance, and output-based regional transfers and/or grants.",""],[1,"96","2","Financial Sector Deepening","deepening the financial sectors",""],[1,"96","3","Financial Sector Deepening Measures","The deepening of the financial sector, both conventional and sharia, is carried out by: (1) increasing public access to financing (financial inclusion); (2) expanding financial product innovation by incorporating technology; (3) developing infrastructure for the financial sector; (4) placing export proceeds in the domestic financial system; and (5) integrating and strengthening fiscal policies based on sovereignty, stability, and integrity of the financial system; the principle of prudence; and the prevention and eradication of money laundering.",""],[1,"97","8","Innovative and Inclusive Financing Scheme Development","fiscal reform is pursued through the development of innovative and inclusive financing schemes by deepening the domestic financial markets.",""],[1,"300","7","Foreign Loan Financing for Priority Public Activities","Foreign loans can be used to finance state deficit and priority activities of ministries/institutions; manage debt portfolios; to fund regional governments and BUMN; as a grant to regional governments with a focus on financing economic and social infrastructure along with technology transfer; for international good practice and knowledge sharing; for pilot projects that can be replicated with funding in the local currency; and have a high leverage value.",""],[1,"307","8","Mobilization of Non-Conventional Financing Sources","the government can explore and maximize the use of funding from non-conventional sources.",""],[1,"307","8","Private Sector Financing for Public Investment Projects","the government needs to seek private sector funding for several types of public investment projects,",""],[1,"307","8","Government Asset Securitization Initiative","to use and securitize government assets,",""],[1,"307","8","Engagement of Philanthropic Development Actors","to invite other development actors such as philanthropists,",""],[1,"308","2","Green Funding and Blended Finance for Public Investment","the government can also rely on and explore green funding in the future.",""],[1,"308","8","Direct Lending for Priority Projects","Nonetheless, the use of direct lending is aimed at reducing the government's loan burden.",""],[1,"308","9","Private Sector Stimulus and Non-Government Financing Incentive Framework","These efforts are performed in conjunction with the provision of stimulus for the private sector and the public, through regulations and policies that provide incentives to optimize the role of non-government financing in national development (or public investment).",""],[1,"310","7","Optimization of Development Financing Sources","Development funding sources that are currently available and in use, such as foreign loans, can be optimized by utilizing loans from development financing institutions and making use of development cooperation funding schemes and other foreign financing facilities with favorable terms and conditions.",""],[1,"310","10","Expansion of Thematic Financing Schemes","the government can expand the utilization of financing schemes sourced from various thematic financing windows, such as green financing schemes.",""],[1,"310","11","Development Financing Diversification and Innovation Measures","Hence, efforts are needed to develop various sources, schemes, and financing instruments in terms of quantity, efficiency, and effectiveness of their utilization.",""],[1,"310","12","Blended Finance Coordination Mechanism","Strengthen coordination between stakeholders in utilizing blended finance to fund programs, projects, or activities using different funding sources, schemes and instruments that are tailored specifically to the time, stage, and type of",""],[1,"311","2","Legal and Regulatory Framework for Innovation Financing","Providing and perfecting the legal and regulatory framework as a basis for funding innovation.",""],[1,"311","12","Innovative Financing Mechanisms for Development","Encourage innovative financing mechanisms for development.",""],[2,"43","3","Financial Sector Deepening and Alternative Financing Expansion","Pembiayaan kebutuhan investasi pada tahun 2020-2024 diupayakan dengan pendalaman sektor keuangan baik bank maupun non-bank, antara lain melalui peningkatan inklusi keuangan, perluasan inovasi produk keuangan, pengembangan infrastruktur sektor jasa keuangan, dan optimalisasi alternatif pembiayaan.",""],[2,"97","5","Financial Sector Deepening Strategy","(iv) Penguatan pilar pertumbuhan dan daya saing ekonomi yang dilaksanakan dengan strategi: (1) meningkatkan pendalaman sektor keuangan;",""],[2,"97","6","Financial Sector Deepening and Reform Package","Pendalaman sektor keuangan, baik konvensional maupun syariah, dilaksanakan dengan: (1) peningkatan akses keuangan masyarakat (inklusi keuangan); (2) perluasan inovasi produk keuangan dengan pemanfaatan teknologi; (3) pengembangan infrastruktur sektor keuangan; (4) penempatan devisa hasil ekspor (DHE) pada sistem keuangan di dalam negeri; dan (5) harmonisasi dan penguatan kebijakan sektor keuangan atas dasar kedaulatan, stabilitas dan integritas sistem keuangan, prinsip kehati-hatian, serta pencegahan dan pemberantasan tindak pidana pencucian uang.",""]],"22":[[1,"96","2","Fiscal Reform Agenda","fiscal reforms",""],[1,"97","2","Fiscal Reform Strategy","The strategy for fiscal reform is focused on optimizing the contribution of state revenue, increasing the quality of state spending, and financing productive and efficient debts.",""],[1,"97","4","Non-Tax Revenue Optimization Reform","Optimizing non-tax revenue (or PNBP) is carried out by improving PNBP regulations, increasing compliance and intensifying PNBP",""],[1,"97","5","Digital-Based Non-Tax Revenue Enhancement and Earmarking","supervision, increasing PNBP from the management of state property (or BMN) and the performance of public service agencies (or BLU), developing digital-based services to increase PNBP, and developing PNBP- earmarks to meet the needs of funding for the construction of the new capital city.",""],[1,"97","6","Improvement of State Spending Quality","Increasing the quality of state spending is carried out by improving spending of goods and strengthening capital expenditure for productive programs and to encourage economic growth.",""],[1,"97","7","Subsidy Targeting Improvement","Management of subsidies is aimed at increasing the effectiveness and efficiency of subsidies through efforts to improve targeting.",""],[2,"97","5","Fiscal Reform","(iv) Penguatan pilar pertumbuhan dan daya saing ekonomi yang dilaksanakan dengan strategi: (5) reformasi fiskal;",""],[2,"98","5","Fiscal Reform Strengthening Strategy","Strategi penguatan reformasi fiskal difokuskan pada optimalisasi kontribusi penerimaan negara dan peningkatan belanja negara yang lebih berkualitas serta pembiayaan utang yang produktif dan efisien.",""],[2,"98","6","Fiscal Incentives to Support the Economy and Business","Optimalisasi penerimaan negara diarahkan untuk mendukung daya saing dengan target yang lebih realistis dan optimal, disertai dukungan terhadap perekonomian dan dunia usaha melalui insentif fiskal.",""],[2,"98","7","Tax Administration and Customs Modernization","Optimalisasi perpajakan mencakup pembaruan sistem inti administrasi perpajakan (core tax system) dan smart customs and excise system, upaya intensifikasi dan ekstensifikasi baik obyek dan subyek pajak maupun perluasan barang kena cukai, penyederhanaan struktur tarif cukai hasil tembakau (HT), peningkatan tarif cukai HT, serta penguatan kelembagaan penerimaan negara.",""],[2,"98","8","Non-Tax State Revenue Optimization Measures","Optimalisasi PNBP dilakukan dengan penyempurnaan regulasi PNBP, peningkatan kepatuhan dan intensifikasi pengawasan PNBP, peningkatan PNBP dari pengelolaan Barang Milik Negara (BMN) dan kinerja Badan Layanan Umum (BLU), pengembangan layanan berbasis digital untuk meningkatkan PNBP, serta pengembangan PNBP- earmark untuk memenuhi kebutuhan pendanaan pembangunan ibu kota negara baru.",""],[2,"98","9","Quality Public Expenditure Enhancement","Peningkatan belanja negara yang berkualitas dilaksanakan melalui penajaman belanja barang dan penguatan belanja modal untuk semakin fokus pada program produktif dan mendorong pertumbuhan ekonomi.",""],[2,"98","10","Subsidy Management Reform","Pengelolaan subsidi ditujukan untuk meningkatan efektivitas dan efisiensi melalui upaya perbaikan ketepatan sasaran.",""]],"23":[[1,"37","1","Low and Stable Inflation Maintenance","The Government of Indonesia and Bank Indonesia are committed to maintaining a low and stable inflation rate in the medium term.","The Government of Indonesia | Bank Indonesia"],[1,"37","2","Inflation Control Policy Package","In the 2020-2024 period, inflation control policies are directed toward: (i) increasing the availability of strategic food commodities; (ii) strengthening the governance of the national logistics systems and interregional connectivity; (iii) increasing cooperation among regions; (iv) anchoring inflationary",""],[1,"37","7","Exchange Rate Stability and Competitiveness Support Measures","For the 2020-2024 period, a stable exchange rate at its fundamental level helps maintain export competitiveness.",""]],"25":[[1,"47","10","Renewable Energy Expansion","renewable energy must be increased to 23% of the national energy mix.",""],[1,"47","10","New Energy Source Exploration","efforts to find new energy sources are needed to anticipate the decline in fossil energy resources in the future.",""],[1,"86","2","New and Renewable Energy Development Programme","Meeting energy demand by prioritizing new and renewable energy, which will be carried out using the following strategies: (1) accelerating the development of new and renewable energy plants; (2) increasing the supply of biofuels; (3) improving the implementation of energy conservation and efficiency programs; (4) fulfilling industrial demand for energy; and (5) developing industries that support new and renewable energy.",""],[1,"86","4","Phased Biofuel Development Programme","Biofuel development will be carried out in stages that cover the production of biodiesel and green fuel.",""],[1,"86","4","Palm Oil-Based Biofuel Capacity Expansion","Capacity for palm oil-based biofuel production is expanded by empowering palm oil smallholders.",""],[1,"86","5","Renewable Energy Development in Industrial Estates","Energy supply for the industry and electricity generation will be delivered by developing renewable energy potential in industrial estates through integration with other sectors.",""],[1,"86","6","Nuclear Power Plant Construction","Improvements to the electricity supply are also pursued through the construction of a nuclear power plant in Kalimantan.",""],[2,"23","27","Oil Refinery Development and Expansion","Pembangunan dan Pengembangan Kilang Minyak (2 Grass Root Refinery/GRR dan 4 Refinery Development Master Plan/RDMP)",""],[2,"51","7","Renewable Energy Share Expansion","pada tahun 2024 porsi energi baru terbarukan harus ditingkatkan hingga menuju 23 persen dari bauran energi nasional.",""],[2,"51","7","New Energy Source Exploration Initiative","diperlukan peningkatan upaya penemuan sumber-sumber energi baru untuk mengantisipasi laju penurunan cadangan sumber daya energi fosil di masa mendatang.",""],[2,"64","22","Urban Gas Network Infrastructure for 4 Million Household Connections","Infrastruktur Jaringan Gas Kota untuk 4 Juta Sambungan Rumah",""],[2,"89","3","Renewable Energy Expansion and Energy Efficiency Programme","Pemenuhan kebutuhan energi dengan mengutamakan peningkatan energi baru terbarukan (EBT) yang dilaksanakan dengan strategi: (1) mempercepat pengembangan pembangkit energi baru dan terbarukan; (2) meningkatkan pasokan bahan bakar nabati; (3) meningkatkan pelaksanaan konservasi dan efisiensi energi; (4) meningkatkan pemenuhan energi bagi industri; serta (5) mengembangkan industri pendukung EBT.",""],[2,"89","5","Biofuel Development and Palm-Based Production Expansion","Pengembangan bahan bakar nabati dilaksanakan secara bertahap, melalui produksi biodiesel dan greenfuel.",""],[2,"89","6","Integrated Renewable Energy Supply for Industrial Estates","Penyediaan energi bagi industri dan kelistrikan akan dipenuhi melalui pengembangan potensi energi terbarukan di Kawasan Industri melalui integrasi dengan sektor lain.",""],[2,"89","6","Integrated Energy Supply Scheme for Industrial Estates","Pola penyediaan energi terintegrasi difokuskan pada Kawasan Industri di Sumatera bagian utara, Sumatera bagian selatan, Jawa, Kalimantan bagian utara, Sulawesi bagian utara dan selatan, Maluku Utara dan Papua Barat.",""],[2,"89","6","Nuclear Power Plant Development in Kalimantan","Peningkatan penyediaan listrik juga diupayakan dengan dimulainya pembangunan Pembangkit Listrik Tenaga Nuklir (PLTN) di Kalimantan.",""],[2,"89","7","Fiscal Incentives for Renewable Energy Industry Development","Pengembangan potensi energi terbarukan didukung dengan pemberian insentif fiskal terhadap industri energi baru terbarukan.",""]],"26":[[1,"232","5","Energy Supply and Electricity Services Expansion","Strengthening and expanding energy supply and electricity services, through (a) meeting electricity needs in priority areas; (b) providing assistance to install new electricity for poor households; (c) supporting and",""],[1,"232","6","Energy Supply and Fuel Infrastructure Expansion","supplying primary energy (gas and coal) for electricity; (d) increasing capacity of domestic oil refineries; (e) improving natural gas infrastructure, particularly gas transmission pipelines and non-pipeline distribution, including LNG receiving terminals; (f) developing fuel and gas buffer/operational reserves; (g) constructing an urban gas network, LPG, and electric clean stoves; (h) increasing national engineering capabilities for energy and electricity supported by domestic industries; (i) expanding a single-price fuel distribution system; and (j) developing supporting infrastructure for electric vehicles.",""],[1,"233","2","Energy and Electricity Access and Affordability Expansion","priority projects that support access to energy and electricity include: i) Expanding energy and electricity access and affordability",""],[1,"233","2","City Gas Network Infrastructure Project","ii) City gas network infrastructure for 4 million house connections (Major Project)",""],[1,"233","3","Trans-Kalimantan Natural Gas Pipeline","iii) Trans-Kalimantan Natural Gas Pipeline (2,219 km) (Major Project).",""],[1,"233","3","Power Generation, Transmission, and Substation Expansion","i) Developing 27,000 MW power plants, 19,000 KMS transmission and 38,000 MVA substation (Major Project);",""],[1,"233","3","Oil Refinery Development and Expansion","ii) Developing and expanding oil refineries (Major Project).",""],[1,"294","11","Revision of 3 kg LPG Cylinder Provision, Distribution, and Pricing Regulation","Revision of Perpres No. 104/2007 on providing, distributing, and pricing 3 kg LPG cylinders.",""],[1,"294","12","Revision of LPG and Water Pump Subsidy Regulation","Revision of Perpres No. 38/2019 on providing, distributing, and pricing LPG for targeted fishing vessels, and water pumps for targeted farmers.",""],[2,"220","5","Expansion of Energy and Electricity Supply Services","Penguatan dan perluasan pelayanan pasokan energi dan tenaga listrik, ditempuh melalui (a) pemenuhan tenaga listrik di kawasan-kawasan prioritas; (b) penyediaan bantuan pasang baru listrik untuk rumah tangga tidak mampu; (c) dukungan penyediaan energi primer (gas dan batubara) untuk listrik; (d) peningkatan kapasitas kilang minyak dalam negeri; (e) peningkatan infrastruktur gas bumi, khususnya seperti jaringan pipa transmisi gas dan distribusi non pipa khususnya LNG receiving terminal; (f) pengembangan cadangan penyangga/operasional BBM dan LPG; (g) pembangunan jaringan gas perkotaan, LPG, dan kompor bersih berbasis listrik; (h) peningkatan kemampuan rekayasa nasional untuk energi dan ketenagalistrikan yang didukung industri dalam negeri; (i) perluasan penyaluran BBM satu harga; dan (j) pengembangan infrastruktur pendukung kendaraan bermotor listrik.",""],[2,"220","8","Energy and Electricity Access and Affordability Expansion","Sementara proyek prioritas mendukung akses dan keterjangkauan energi dan ketenagalistrikan meliputi: i) Perluasan akses dan keterjangkauan energi dan ketenagalistrikan;",""],[2,"220","8","Urban Gas Network Infrastructure for Household Connections","ii) Infrastruktur Jaringan Gas Kota untuk 4 Juta Sambungan Rumah (Major Project);",""],[2,"220","8","Trans-Kalimantan Natural Gas Pipeline Project","iii) Pipa Gas Bumi Trans Kalimantan (2.219 KM) (Major Project).",""],[2,"220","8","Energy Infrastructure Reliability Improvement","Adapun proyek prioritas mendukung kecukupan penyediaan energi dan tenaga listrik adalah peningkatan kehandalan infrastruktur energi dan ketenagalistrikan termasuk di dalamnya dua Major Project;",""],[2,"220","8","27,000 MW Power Generation and Transmission Expansion","i) Pembangkit Listrik 27.000 MW, Transmisi 19.000 KMS dan Gardu Induk 38.000 MVA (Major Project);",""],[2,"220","8","Oil Refinery Development and Expansion","dan ii) Pembangunan dan Pengembangan Kilang Minyak (Major Poject).",""]],"27":[[1,"237","2","Environmental Quality Improvement and Climate Resilience Policy Package","the national priorities are outlined into three policy groups, namely: (1) improving the quality of the environment; (2) increasing resilience against natural disasters and climate change; and (3) applying a low- carbon development approach.",""],[1,"238","9","Climate Change Adaptation Plan Pilot Implementation","Trial implementation of the climate change adaptation plan (RAN-API) in 15 pilot areas; and trial review in 4 priority sectors (sea and coastal, water, agriculture, and health);",""],[1,"241","5","Climate Change Adaptation Plan Trials in Priority Sectors","trials have been carried out on the implementation of climate change adaptation plans in four priority sectors (water, agriculture, coastal and marine, and health) in 15 pilot areas",""],[1,"241","6","Climate Change Adaptation and Disaster Risk Reduction Convergence Agenda","the convergence agenda between climate change adaptation and disaster risk reduction will be further enhanced, through activity plans and integrated efforts across sectors, among regions, stakeholders, and cooperation at the global level.",""],[1,"258","4","Low-Carbon Development Implementation Strengthening","Commitment to implement low-carbon development needs to be strengthened nationally and internationally, not only to build motivation, but also to strengthen capital and capacity of the parties.",""],[1,"258","5","Low-Carbon Development Planning Support","At the national level, support for low- carbon development continues to roll.",""],[1,"258","5","Provincial Low-Carbon Development Planning MoU","This commitment and effort were demonstrated through the signing of a memorandum of understanding (MoU) between the Minister of National Development Planning/Head of Bappenas and the provincial governments on low-carbon development planning.","Minister of National Development Planning/Head of Bappenas"],[1,"258","6","Regional Low-Carbon Development Plan Preparation","preparation of the Regional Low-Carbon Development Plan (RPRKD) documents at the provincial level.",""],[1,"258","7","Non-Governmental Actor Engagement for Low-Carbon Development","Communication and outreach to non- governmental actors to increase awareness need to be intensified, so it is hoped that the involvement of non- governmental actors in the low-carbon development agenda can be further enhanced.",""],[1,"259","2","CSR Support for Low-Carbon Development","the potential for business support through CSR programs in low- carbon development needs to be optimized further.",""],[1,"264","3","Disaster Risk Reduction and Climate Change Adaptation Convergence Strengthening","Improving resilience against disasters and climate change is carried out by strengthening the convergence of disaster risk reduction and climate change adaptation.",""],[1,"264","7","National Climate Change Adaptation Plan Implementation","Improving resilience to climate change, which is carried out with the implementation of the \"National Plan for Climate Change Adaptation\" (RAN-API) in priority sectors, by: (a) addressing the vulnerability of coastal and marine areas and strengthening these ecosystems based on ecosystem adaptation, community awareness, technology, and diversification of the livelihoods of coastal communities; (b) protecting water security in areas vulnerable to climate change by increasing supply of raw water and providing protection against water damage; (c) protecting food security against climate change; and (d) protecting the public health and the environment from the impacts of climate change.",""],[1,"265","1","Low-Carbon Development Efforts","Low-carbon development is carried out through efforts to reduce emissions and emission intensity in priority sectors, including energy, land, waste, industry, and marine.",""],[1,"295","12","Presidential Regulation Draft on Greenhouse Gas Emissions Control Instruments and Low-Carbon Development Plan","Perpres draft on instruments to control greenhouse gas emissions and on low-carbon development plan.",""],[2,"126","6","Climate Change Mitigation and Disaster Risk Reduction Mainstreaming","Penguatan mitigasi perubahan iklim dan penanggulangan bencana untuk mengurangi risiko perubahan iklim dan bencana; dan meningkatkan ketangguhan menghadapi perubahan iklim dan bencana terutama di pusat-pusat pertumbuhan wilayah, kawasan perkotaan dan kota metropolitan antara lain melalui: (i) pengarusutamaan penanggulangan bencana dan adaptasi perubahan iklim;",""],[2,"126","6","Spatial Planning Regulation and Control for Risk Reduction","(ii) pengaturan dan pengendalian pemanfaatan ruang kawasan;",""],[2,"126","6","Disaster Awareness Culture and Preparedness Programme","(iii) pembangunan budaya sadar bencana, dan kesiapsiagaan pemerintah daerah dan masyarakat;",""],[2,"126","6","Minimum Disaster Service Standards and Logistics Capacity Strengthening","(iv) pemenuhan standar pelayanan minimal kebencanaan melalui peningkatan kapasitas Pemerintah Daerah, masyarakat, dan logistik kebencanaan terutama di kawasan strategis nasional yang memiliki risiko bencana tinggi;",""],[2,"126","6","Multi-Hazard Early Warning System Development","(v) pengembangan sistem peringatan dini multiancaman bencana;",""],[2,"126","6","Community Climate Adaptation in Disaster-Prone Areas","(vi) adaptasi masyarakat terhadap perubahan iklim di daerah rawan bencana;",""],[2,"126","6","Disaster Management Capacity Strengthening Across Phases","(vii) peningkatan kapasitas manajemen penanggulangan bencana pada fase prabencana, tanggap darurat, dan pasca bencana;",""],[2,"126","6","Disaster Risk Mitigation Investment Expansion","(viii) peningkatan investasi untuk mitigasi dan pengurangan risiko bencana;",""],[2,"126","6","Multi-Stakeholder Climate and Disaster Risk Partnership Expansion","(ix) perluasan dan penguatan kerjasama dan kemitraan multiphak dan multisektor dalam mitigasi perubahan iklim dan pengurangan risiko bencana;",""],[2,"126","6","Coastal Erosion Control and Protection Measures","(x) peningkatan upaya penanganan abrasi pantai yang dapat mengancam terjadinya pergeseran batas wilayah.",""],[2,"129","9","Disaster Risk Reduction and Climate Change Adaptation Mainstreaming","Pengarusutamaan penanggulangan bencana dan adaptasi perubahan iklim dilakukan melalui antara lain: (a) peningkatan kapaitas masyarakat dan aparat; (b) peningkatan ketahanan kawasan pantai utara Pulau Papua; (c) adaptasi masyarakat terhadap perubahan iklim di daerah rawan bencana berbasis kearifan lokal masyarakat dengan fokus utama pada peningkatan ketahanan wilayah Daerah Aliran Sungai (DAS); (d) peningkatan investigasi mitigasi perubahan iklim dan pengurangan risiko bencana, serta (e) peningkatan penanganan abrasi pantai di daerah kepulauan, dan konservasi hutan.",""],[2,"131","3","Disaster Risk Reduction and Climate Change Adaptation Mainstreaming","Pengarusutamaan penanggulangan bencana dan adaptasi perubahan iklim dilakukan melalui antara lain: (a) peningkatan kapasitas masyarakat dan aparat; (b) peningkatan ketahanan kawasan utara dan selatan Kepulauan Maluku; (c) adaptasi masyarakat terhadap perubahan iklim di daerah rawan bencana berbasis kearifan lokal masyarakat; (d) peningkatan investasi mitigasi perubahan iklim dan pengurangan risiko bencana; dan (e) peningkatan penanganan abrasi pantai di pesisir dan daerah kepulauan, serta konservasi hutan.",""],[2,"133","4","Disaster Risk Reduction and Climate Change Adaptation Mainstreaming","(5) Pengarusutamaan penanggulangan bencana dan adaptasi perubahan iklim dilakukan melalui antara lain: (a) peningkatan kapaitas masyarakat dan aparat; (b) peningkatan ketahanan kawasan utara dan selatan Kepulauan Nusa Tenggara dan pemantapan pemulihan pascabencana di Pulau Lombok dan sekitarnya; (c) adaptasi masyarakat terhadap perubahan iklim di daerah rawan bencana berbasis kearifan lokal masyarakat; (d) peningkatan investasi mitigasi perubahan iklim dan pengurangan risiko bencana; dan (e) peningkatan penanganan abrasi pantai di pesisir dan daerah kepulauan, serta konservasi hutan.",""],[2,"133","9","Disaster-Affected Area Rehabilitation and Reconstruction","Rehabilitasi dan Rekonstruksi Daerah Terdampak Bencana Lombok, Sumbawa dan Kota Mataram",""],[2,"134","2","Sulawesi Disaster Mitigation and Adaptation Approach","Wilayah Sulawesi memiliki potensi bencana alam yang beragam dan tinggi, maka pembangunan wilayah Sulawesi perlu mempertimbangkan pendekatan mitigasi dan adaptasi bencana.",""],[2,"135","5","Disaster Risk Reduction and Climate Change Adaptation Mainstreaming","Pengarusutamaan penanggulangan bencana dan adaptasi perubahan iklim dilakukan melalui antara lain: (a) peningkatan kapaitas masyarakat dan aparat, (b) peningkatan ketahanan kawasan Sulawesi Tengah dan pemantapan pemulihan pascabencana di Kota Palu dan sekitarnya; (c) adaptasi masyarakat terhadap perubahan iklim di daerah rawan bencana berbasis kearifan lokal masyarakat; (d) peningkatan investasi mitigasi perubahan iklim dan pengurangan risiko bencana; dan (e) peningkatan penanganan abrasi pantai di pesisir dan daerah kepulauan, serta konservasi hutan;",""],[2,"137","4","Disaster Risk Reduction and Climate Change Adaptation Mainstreaming","Pengarusutamaan penanggulangan bencana dan adaptasi perubahan iklim dilakukan melalui antara lain: (a) peningkatan kapasitas masyarakat dan aparat; (b) peningkatan ketahanan kawasan wilayah timur Pulau Kalimantan; (c) adaptasi masyarakat terhadap perubahan iklim di daerah rawan bencana berbasis kearifan lokal masyarakat; (d) peningkatan investasi mitigasi perubahan iklim dan pengurangan risiko bencana; dan (e) peningkatan penanganan abrasi pantai di pesisir dan daerah kepulauan, serta konservasi hutan.",""],[2,"139","5","Disaster Risk Reduction and Climate Change Adaptation Mainstreaming","(5) Pengarusutamaan penanggulangan bencana dan adaptasi perubahan iklim dilakukan melalui: (a) peningkatan kapasitas masyarakat dan aparat; (b) peningkatan ketahanan kawasan pantai barat Pulau Sumatera dan pemantapan pemulihan pascabencana Kawasan Selat Sunda dan sekitarnya; (c) adaptasi masyarakat terhadap perubahan iklim di daerah rawan bencana berbasis kearifan lokal; (d) peningkatan investasi mitigasi perubahan iklim dan pengurangan risiko bencana, dan (e) peningkatan penanganan abrasi pantai di pesisir dan daerah kepulauan, serta konservasi hutan.",""],[2,"141","4","Disaster Risk Reduction and Climate Change Adaptation Mainstreaming","(6) Pengarusutamaan penanggulangan bencana dan adaptasi perubahan iklim dilakukan melalui antara lain: (a) peningkatan kapasitas masyarakat dan aparat; (b) peningkatan ketahanan kawasan pantai selatan Pulau Jawa-Bali dan pemantapan pemulihan pascabencana di Kawasan Selat Sunda dan Sekitarnya; (c) adaptasi masyarakat terhadap perubahan iklim di daerah rawan bencana berbasis kearifan lokal; (d) peningkatan investasi mitigasi perubahan iklim dan pengurangan risiko bencana; dan (e) peningkatan penanganan abrasi pantai di pesisir.",""],[2,"163","10","Post-Disaster Prevention and Mitigation Technology Application","Penerapan teknologi untuk pencegahan dan mitigasi pascabencana",""],[2,"224","3","National Environmental Quality Improvement Policy","Secara lebih spesifik, prioritas nasional tersebut diuraikan ke dalam tiga kelompok kebijakan, yakni: (1) meningkatkan kualitas lingkungan hidup;",""],[2,"224","3","Low-Carbon Development Approach","Secara lebih spesifik, prioritas nasional tersebut diuraikan ke dalam tiga kelompok kebijakan, yakni: (3) menerapkan pendekatan pembangunan rendah karbon.",""],[2,"241","7","Integration of Climate Change Mitigation Policy into National Development Programs","Integrasi kebijakan penanggulangan perubahan iklim ke dalam program pembangunan nasional",""],[2,"243","7","Cross-Sector Low-Carbon Development Support","Penerapan pembangunan rendah karbon dalam perencanaan dan pelaksanaan pembangunan nasional membutuhkan dukungan yang bersifat lintas sektor dan multi- pihak, baik dari dalam dan luar negeri.",""],[2,"243","7","Expanded Non-Government Stakeholder Engagement","Pelibatan aktor non-pemerintah perlu ditingkatkan guna mendukung keberhasilan pencapaian target pembangunan.",""],[2,"244","2","Strengthen Low-Carbon Development Commitment","Komitmen untuk menerapkan pembangunan rendah karbon perlu diperkuat secara nasional maupun internasional; bukan hanya untuk membentuk motivasi melainkan juga untuk memperkuat modal dan kapasitas para pihak.",""],[2,"244","3","Low-Carbon Development Planning MoU","Komitmen dan upaya tersebut ditunjukkan melalui penandatanganan Nota Kesepahaman (MoU) antara Menteri Perencanaan Pembangunan Nasional/ Kepala Bappenas dengan Pemerintah Provinsi tentang Perencanaan Pembangunan Rendah Karbon (PPRK).","Menteri Perencanaan Pembangunan Nasional/ Kepala Bappenas"],[2,"244","3","Provincial Low-Carbon Development Plan Preparation","Keterlibatan dan dukungan pemerintah daerah dalam pembangunan rendah karbon perlu semakin ditingkatkan khususnya terkait penyusunan dokumen Rencana Pembangunan Rendah Karbon Daerah (RPRKD) pada tingkat provinsi.",""],[2,"244","3","Integrated Regional Low-Carbon Action Framework","RPRKD akan menjadi dokumen rujukan bagi pemerintah daerah dalam melaksanakan berbagai aksi pembangunan rendah karbon yang terintegrasi dengan dokumen perencanaan daerah lainnya.",""],[2,"244","4","Non-State Actor Engagement and Awareness-Raising for Low-Carbon Development","Komunikasi dan penjangkauan terhadap aktor non-pemerintah untuk peningkatan kesadaran (awareness) perlu semakin digencarkan, sehingga diharapkan keterlibatan aktor non-pemerintah terhadap agenda pembangunan rendah karbon dapat semakin ditingkatkan.",""],[2,"244","6","Low-Emission Technology Development Support","Upaya peningkatan teknologi rendah emisi perlu terus didorong sehingga teknologi rendah karbon dapat semakin terjangkau dan memiliki nilai ekonomi yang lebih menguntungkan.",""],[2,"244","6","Digital Planning and Environmental Monitoring for Low-Carbon Development","Kemajuan teknologi juga perlu dimanfaatkan untuk perencanaan, pengawasan, dan pengendalian pembangunan beserta dampaknya terhadap lingkungan secara lebih efisien.",""],[2,"248","9","Disaster Risk Reduction and Climate Change Adaptation Convergence Strengthening","Peningkatan Ketahanan Bencana dan Iklim dilakukan melalui penguatan konvergensi antara pengurangan risiko bencana dan adaptasi perubahan iklim.",""],[2,"249","3","Disaster Risk Reduction and Response Strengthening","Penanggulangan Bencana, yang dilaksanakan dengan: (a) Penguatan Data, Informasi, dan Literasi Bencana; (b) Penguatan Sistem, Regulasi dan Tata Kelola Bencana; (c) Penguatan Rencana Pengurangan Risiko Bencana melalui Rencana Aksi Pengurangan Risiko Bencana secara nasional dan daerah yang akan diintegrasikan dengan Rencana Aksi Adaptasi Perubahan Iklim; (d) Peningkatan Sarana Prasarana Mitigasi dan Penanggulangan Bencana; (e) Integrasi kerja sama antar daerah terkait kebijakan dan penataan ruang berbasis risiko bencana dan implementasi penanggulangan bencana; (f) Penguatan Penanganan Darurat Bencana; (g) Pelaksanaan rehabilitasi dan rekonstruksi di daerah terdampak bencana; (h) Penguatan sistem mitigasi multi ancaman bencana terpadu, terutama melalui penguatan INATEWS dan MHEWS; dan (i) Penguatan kesiapsiagaan dalam penanganan bencana melalui social re-engineering ketahanan bencana multilevel, terutama level keluarga, komunitas maupun desa; dan (j) Peningkatan pengembangan dan inovasi skema alternatif pembiayaan penanggulangan bencana.",""],[2,"249","4","National Climate Change Adaptation Plan Implementation","Peningkatan Ketahanan Iklim, yang dilaksanakan dengan implementasi Rencana Nasional Adaptasi Perubahan Iklim (RAN-API) pada sektor-sektor prioritas, melalui: (a) Perlindungan Kerentanan Pesisir dan Sektor Kelautan, baik berupa penguatan infrastruktur adaptasi berbasis ekosistem, penyadartahuan masyarakat, pengembangan teknologi, maupun diversifikasi mata pencaharian masyarakat pesisir; (b) Perlindungan Ketahanan Air pada Wilayah Berisiko Iklim, melalui peningkatan penyediaan pasokan air baku dan perlindungan terhadap daya rusak air; (c) Perlindungan Ketahanan Pangan terhadap Perubahan Iklim; serta (d) Perlindungan Kesehatan Masyarakat dan Lingkungan dari Dampak Perubahan Iklim.",""],[2,"249","5","Low-Carbon Development Emissions Reduction Initiative","Pembangunan Rendah Karbon dilakukan melalui upaya penurunan emisi dan intensitas emisi pada bidang-bidang prioritas, yakni meliputi bidang energi, lahan, limbah, industri, dan kelautan.",""],[2,"266","16","Integrated Early Warning System Capacity Strengthening","Penguatan kapasitas sistem peringatan dini terpadu;",""],[2,"277","5","Revision of Disaster Management Government Regulation No. 21 of 2008","Revisi PP Nomor 21 Tahun 2008 tentang Penyelenggaraan Penanggulangan Bencana.",""],[2,"277","10","National Greenhouse Gas Control Instrument and Low-Carbon Development Presidential Regulation","RPerpres tentang Instrumen Pengendalian Gas Rumah Kaca Nasional dan Rencana Pembangunan Rendah Karbon.",""]],"28":[[1,"44","2","Integrated Peatland Conservation and Restoration Efforts","Hence, integrated efforts are needed to conserve and restore peatlands.",""],[1,"44","7","Peatland Restoration Priority Programme","peatland restoration efforts that have been carried out intensively since 2015 need to remain a priority in the 2020-2024 RPJMN.",""],[2,"48","6","Peatland Restoration Priority Programme","Untuk itu, upaya restorasi lahan gambut yang telah dilaksanakan secara intensif sejak tahun 2015 perlu tetap menjadi prioritas dalam RPJMN 2020-2024.",""],[2,"64","27","Critical Watershed Reforestation and Erosion Reduction Programme","Penurunan erosi di wilayah DAS kritis dengan penghijauan lahan kritis 150.000 Ha",""]],"29":[[1,"46","10","Disaster-Risk-Informed Spatial Planning","zones with a high disaster risk need to be prioritized as protected areas during spatial planning",""],[1,"118","2","Climate- and Disaster-Informed Spatial Planning Enforcement","Enforcing spatial plans based on climate change mitigation and disaster risk reduction to ensure the protection of spatial functions and prevention of negative impacts on the environment due to spatial use, among others through: (i) increasing the effectiveness of spatial planning instruments, especially the comprehensiveness of Detailed Spatial Plans (RDTR); (ii) providing large-scale basic maps (1: 5,000) nationally; and (iii) applying incentives and disincentives, and also sanctions for violations of spatial use;",""],[2,"126","3","Climate- and Disaster-Risk-Based Spatial Planning Enforcement","Penegakan rencana tata ruang yang berbasis mitigasi perubahan iklim dan pengurangan risiko bencana untuk menjamin pelindungan fungsi ruang dan pencegahan dampak negatif terhadap lingkungan akibat pemanfaatan ruang antara lain melalui: (i) peningkatan efektivitas instrumen pengendalian pemanfaatan ruang, terutama kelengkapan RDTR; (ii) penyediaan peta dasar skala besar (1:5.000) secara nasional; dan (iii) penerapan insentif dan disinsentif, serta sanksi bagi pelanggaran pemanfaatan ruang;",""],[2,"126","4","Land Rights Certification and Boundary Delineation Reform","Peningkatan kepastian hukum hak atas tanah melalui: (i) sertifikasi hak atas tanah terutama di wilayah yang diarahkan sebagai koridor pertumbuhan ekonomi dan pemerataan serta wilayah sekitarnya termasuk di kawasan transmigrasi; (ii) penataan dan publikasi batas kawasan hutan dan nonhutan dalam skala kadastral; dan (iii) penetapan deliniasi batas wilayah adat;",""]],"30":[[1,"61","15","Watershed Erosion Reduction through Greening","Reduce erosion in critical watershed areas by greening 150,000 ha of land",""]],"31":[[1,"223","4","Waste Reduction Campaigns","Strengthening waste reduction campaigns.",""],[1,"243","2","Integrated Waste Management Program","These efforts are expected to form an integrated waste management program that traces waste from its source to the final processing site.",""],[1,"263","3","Environmental Pollution and Degradation Response Program","This policy direction is carried out by integrating efforts for prevention, mitigation, and recovery of the environment affected by pollution and destruction, and by strengthening institutions and law enforcement in the environment sector.",""],[1,"263","5","Environmental Pollution and Natural Resource Protection Measures","Prevention pollution and destruction of natural resources and the environment, which is carried out by: (a) monitoring air, water and seawater quality; (b) monitoring the performance of environmental management systems in businesses and/or economic activities; (c) providing information on weather and climate; (d) preventing land and forest fires; (e) preventing and controlling pollution in marine and coastal areas, and monitoring the health of the marine ecosystem; (f) increasing the capacity and awareness among the government, private sector, and communities in relation to the environment; (g) preventing biodiversity loss and ecosystem damage through conservation and protection of endangered species both on land and in water;",""],[1,"263","7","Environmental Pollution and Resource Damage Control Measures","Overcome pollution and destruction of natural resources and the environment, which is carried out by: (a) handling pollution and damages in the environment;",""],[1,"263","7","Household and Plastic Waste Management Programme","(b) managing household waste and specifically plastic waste",""],[1,"263","7","Mercury Removal and Replacement in ASGM Sites","(c) Removing and replacing mercury, especially in ASGM sites;",""],[1,"263","7","Integrated Hazardous and Medical Waste Treatment Facilities","(d) developing integrated facilities for of hazardous and medical waste treatment.",""],[1,"265","6","Household and Liquid Waste Management","Managing waste through: (a) household waste management; and (b) liquid waste management.",""],[1,"295","3","Air Pollution Control Regulation Revision","Revision of PP No. 41/1999 on controlling air pollution.",""],[1,"295","4","Revision of Sea Pollution Control Regulation","Revision of PP No. 19/1999 on controlling sea pollution and/or degradation.",""],[1,"295","5","Water Quality and Pollution Control Regulation Revision","Revision of PP No. 82/2001 on managing water quality and controlling water pollution.",""],[2,"212","3","Waste Reduction Campaign","Penguatan kampanye pengurangan sampah.",""],[2,"229","4","Waste Management Infrastructure Development","potensi penurunan emisi GRK utamanya berasal dari kegiatan penyediaan infrastruktur pengelolaan sampah (pembangunan TPA dan pembangunan TPS3R/TPST).",""],[2,"229","4","Integrated Household Waste Management Program","Melalui Jakstranas dan Jakstrada terkait pengelolaan sampah rumah tangga, kegiatan pengelolaan sampah terdiri dari pengurangan sampah sebesar 30 persen dan penanganan sampah sebesar 70 persen pada Tahun 2025, upaya tersebut diharapkan dapat menjadi program pengelolaan sampah yang terintegrasi mulai dari sumber hingga tempat pemrosesan akhir.",""],[2,"248","3","Environmental Pollution and Degradation Prevention, Control, and Restoration","Peningkatan Kualitas Lingkungan Hidup dilakukan dengan mengintegrasikan upaya pencegahan, penanggulangan, dan pemulihan pencemaran dan kerusakan lingkungan hidup, serta penguatan kelembagaan dan penegakan hukum bidang lingkungan hidup.",""],[2,"248","5","Environmental Pollution and Natural Resource Damage Prevention Programme","Pencegahan Pencemaran dan Kerusakan Sumber Daya Alam dan Lingkungan Hidup, yang dilaksanakan dengan: (a) Pemantauan Kualitas Udara, Air, dan Air Laut; (b) Pemantauan Kinerja Pengelolaan Lingkungan pada Usaha dan/atau Kegiatan; (c) Penyediaan Informasi Cuaca dan Iklim; (d) Pencegahan Kebakaran Lahan dan Hutan; (e) Pencegahan dan Pengendalian Pencemaran Laut dan Pesisir, serta Pemantauan Kesehatan Ekosistem Laut; (f) Peningkatan Kesadaran dan Kapasitas Pemerintah, Swasta dan Masyarakat terhadap Lingkungan Hidup; (g) Pencegahan Kehilangan Keanekaragaman Hayati dan Kerusakan Ekosistem melalui konservasi Kawasan dan perlindungan keanekaragaman hayati terancam punah baik di daratan maupun perairan; serta (h) Penyediaan Data dan Informasi Keanekaragaman Hayati dan Ekosistem.",""],[2,"248","6","Pollution and Environmental Damage Control","Penanggulangan Pencemaran dan Kerusakan Sumber Daya Alam dan Lingkungan Hidup yang dilaksanakan dengan: (a) Penanganan Pencemaran dan Kerusakan Lingkungan; (b) Pengelolaan Sampah Rumah Tangga dan Sampah Plastik; serta (d) Pembangunan Fasilitas Pengolahan Limbah B3 dan Limbah Medis secara terpadu.",""],[2,"248","7","Environmental and Natural Resource Restoration Programme","Pemulihan Pencemaran dan Kerusakan Sumber Daya Alam dan Lingkungan Hidup, yang dilaksanakan dengan: (a) Restorasi dan Pemulihan Lahan Gambut; (b) Pemulihan Lahan Bekas Tambang dan Lahan Terkontaminasi Limbah B3; (c) Pemulihan Kerusakan Ekosistem dan Lingkungan Pesisir dan Laut, termasuk ekosistem mangrove, terumbu karang, dan padang lamun; (d) Pemulihan Habitat Spesies Terancam Punah; serta (e) Peningkatan Populasi Spesies Tumbuhan dan Satwa Liar Terancam Punah.",""],[2,"277","2","Revision of Air Pollution Control Regulation","Revisi PP Nomor 41 Tahun 1999 tentang Pengendalian Pencemaran Udara.",""]],"32":[[1,"225","5","Natural Infrastructure Restoration and Conservation","Restoring and conserving natural infrastructure",""],[1,"257","4","Moratorium on Clearing Primary Forests and Peatlands","the government has issued a moratorium on clearing primary forests and peatlands to improve sustainable management of forest resources",""],[1,"263","8","Natural Resource and Ecosystem Restoration Programme","Recovering natural resources and the environment from pollution and destruction, which is carried out by: (a) recovering and restoring peatlands; (b) recovering former mine sites and lands contaminated with hazardous waste; (c) restoring damaged ecosystems and the environment surrounding coastal and marine areas, including mangroves, coral reefs and seagrass beds; (d) restoring the habitat of endangered species; and (e) increasing the population of endangered plant and animal species.",""],[1,"265","4","Sustainable Land Restoration Programme","2. Restoring lands sustainably, which is carried out by: (a) restoring peatlands; (b) rehabilitating forests and lands; (c)",""],[1,"265","8","Coastal and Marine Ecosystem Inventory and Rehabilitation","Low-carbon coasts and marine, which are realized by inventorying and rehabilitating coastal and marine ecosystems",""],[1,"295","1","Revision of the Forest Degradation Prevention and Eradication Law","Revision of Law No. 18/2013 on preventing and eradication forest degradation.",""],[2,"242","9","Moratorium on Conversion of Primary Natural Forest and Peatland","Pada sektor lahan dan gambut, pemerintah telah menerbitkan moratorium alih fungsi hutan alam primer dan lahan gambut untuk meningkatkan pengelolaan sumber daya hutan secara berkelanjutan.",""]],"33":[[1,"239","5","Collaborative Enforcement of Court Judgments","In the future, the execution of judgments will be carried out through a collaborative approach involving other law enforcement institutions.",""],[1,"264","1","Strengthening Natural Resources and Environment Sector Regulation and Institutions","strengthening the regulations and institutions in the natural resources and environment sector at the central and regional levels",""],[1,"264","1","Strengthening Licensing, Supervision, and Security Systems","strengthening the licensing, supervision, and security systems",""],[2,"248","8","Institutional Strengthening and Law Enforcement for Natural Resources and Environment","Penguatan Kelembagaan dan Penegakan Hukum di Bidang Sumber Daya Alam dan Lingkungan Hidup, yang dilaksanakan dengan: (a) Penguatan Regulasi dan Kelembagaan Bidang Sumber Daya Alam dan Lingkungan Hidup di Pusat dan Daerah; (b) Penguatan Sistem Perizinan, Pengawasan, dan Pengamanan Pengelolaan Sumber Daya Alam dan Lingkungan Hidup; serta (c) Penguatan Mekanisme Pidana, Perdata, dan Mediasi dalam Proses Penegakan Hukum Bidang SDA dan LH.",""],[2,"276","25","Revision of the Forest Destruction Prevention and Eradication Law","Revisi UU Nomor 18 Tahun 2013 tentang Pencegahan dan Pemberantasan Perusakan Hutan",""],[2,"277","6","Integrated Environmental Criminal Law Enforcement Regulation","RPP tentang Penegakan Hukum Pidana Terpadu Lingkungan Hidup",""]],"34":[[1,"118","5","Disaster Risk Reduction and Climate Change Adaptation Mainstreaming","Strengthening climate change mitigation and disaster management to reduce the risks of climate change and disasters; and increasing resilience, especially in regional growth centers, urban areas and metropolitan cities, among others through: (i) mainstreaming disaster management and climate change adaptation;",""],[1,"118","5","Regional Spatial Use Regulation for Disaster Risk Reduction","regulating and controlling regional spatial use;",""],[1,"118","5","Disaster Awareness and Preparedness Campaign","building a culture of disaster awareness and of preparedness from local governments and the people;",""],[1,"118","5","Regional Disaster Logistics and Basic Service Capacity Enhancement","fulfilling basic service standards in the event of a disaster through enhancing the capacity of regional governments, communities, and disaster logistics, especially in national strategic areas that have high disaster risks;",""],[1,"118","5","Multi-Hazard Early Warning System Development","developing multi-hazard early warning system;",""],[1,"118","5","Disaster Management Capacity Enhancement Across Phases","increasing capacity of disaster management in pre-disaster, emergency response, and post- disaster phases;",""],[1,"118","5","Disaster Risk Mitigation Investment Expansion","increasing investment to mitigate and reduce disaster risks;",""],[1,"132","2","Disaster Management and Climate Change Adaptation Mainstreaming","Mainstreaming of disaster management and climate change adaptation is carried out, among others through: (a) increasing the capacity of the people and officials; (b) increasing the resilience in the northern coast of",""],[1,"133","25","Disaster Management and Climate Change Adaptation Mainstreaming","Mainstreaming of disaster management and climate change adaptation is carried out, among others through: (a) increasing the capacity of the people and officials; (b) increasing the resilience in the northern and southern regions of the Maluku Islands; (c) adapting the people to climate change",""],[1,"225","3","Regional Disaster Resilience Master Plan","Establishing a master plan for regional resilience to disasters",""],[1,"225","3","Disaster Risk Mapping Initiative","Preparing disaster risk maps based on regional characteristics",""],[1,"225","3","Land Subsidence Monitoring System","Developing a land subsidence monitoring system",""],[1,"225","3","Flood and Landslide Early Warning Systems","Providing early warning systems for floods and landslides",""],[1,"225","5","Integrated Early Warning and Emergency Response System","Providing an integrated system for early warning and emergency response",""],[1,"230","10","Emergency Call Service System Development","2. Developing a 112 emergency call service system, by (a) developing an emergency call service system and operating guidelines for districts/cities;",""],[1,"231","1","Call Service System Expansion","expanding the use of call service systems to districts/cities;",""],[1,"231","2","Public Protection and Disaster Relief System Development","Developing a Public Protection and Disaster Relief (PPDR) system, through (a) developing a PPDR pilot project and testing the use of a special frequency spectrum in case of",""],[1,"231","3","PPDR System Implementation in Disaster-Prone Districts and Cities","implementing the PPDR system, especially in disaster-prone districts/cities.",""],[1,"231","3","PPDR Regulatory and Standards Development","preparing regulations, service standards, and tools for the PPDR system;",""],[1,"238","6","Establishment of Regional Disaster Management Agencies","Establishment of 34 Regional Disaster Management Agencies (BPBD) at the provincial level and 481 BPBD at the regency/city level",""],[1,"240","4","Disaster Risk Mapping and Study Preparation","Preparing studies and disaster risk maps in 34 provinces and 170 regencies/cities",""],[1,"240","5","Disaster Management Plan Preparation in Regencies and Cities","Preparing disaster management plans (RPB) in 118 regencies/cities",""],[1,"240","7","Contingency Plan Compilation","Compiling 64 contingency plans and field",""],[1,"240","8","Disaster-Resilient Villages Programme","Establishing disaster-resilient villages in 594",""],[1,"240","10","Multi-Hazard Early Warning System Installation","Installing multi-hazard early warning systems in 58 locations",""],[1,"240","18","Human Resource Strengthening for Regional and Community Levels","strengthening human resources in regional government level and community level by providing",""],[1,"241","1","Disaster and Climate Resilience Capacity-Building and Regulatory Improvement","counseling activities, training, and disaster simulation drills; and improving regulations related to disaster and climate resilience in priority sectors.",""],[1,"241","2","Disaster Risk Reduction and Disaster Management Strengthening","Increasing resilience to disasters is carried out through several improvements to the legal and institutional regulatory frameworks related to disaster risk reduction and disaster management at both the central and regional levels.",""],[1,"241","2","Disaster Risk Studies, Mapping, and Resilient Infrastructure Planning","In several locations, various disaster risk reduction efforts have been carried out, which are supported by a strong database of meteorology, climatology and geophysics, which includes the preparation of studies and disaster risk maps, the strengthening of geological disaster mitigation analysis in the preparation of spatial planning, and the planning of disaster-resilient infrastructure.",""],[1,"241","2","Disaster Management Planning and Community Preparedness Initiatives","Another achievement was the preparation of disaster management plans (RPB), the preparation of contingency plans, the formation of disaster resilient villages (Destana), and the initiation of a disaster-resilient family program (Katana), the strengthening of disaster management resources, which included the provision of assistance in the form of equipment to control and operation centers (PUSDALOP), disaster relief volunteer training, and the provision of an early warning system for high tides during tropical cyclones and other",""],[1,"264","5","Disaster Risk Mitigation and Management Programme","Mitigating disasters, which is carried out by: (a) strengthening data, information, and literacy on disasters; (b) strengthening systems, regulations, and governance of disasters; (c) strengthening disaster risk reduction plans through the national and regional disaster risk reduction action plans, which are to be integrated with the climate change adaptation action plans; (d) improving infrastructure for disaster mitigation and management; (e) integrating interregional cooperation related to policies and spatial planning based on disaster risk assessment and disaster management; (f) Strengthening disaster and emergency management; (g) implementing the rehabilitation and reconstruction in areas affected by disasters;",""],[1,"264","6","Integrated Disaster Mitigation System Strengthening","strengthening integrated disaster mitigation systems, mainly by improving InaTEWS and MHEWS;",""],[1,"264","6","Community-Based Disaster Preparedness and Resilience Strengthening","strengthening disaster preparedness and resilience through social re-engineering at multiple levels, especially at the family, community, and village levels;",""],[1,"283","6","Search and Rescue Response Strengthening in Vulnerable and Disaster-Prone Areas","Increasing search and rescue response in vulnerable and disaster-prone areas;",""],[1,"283","15","Integrated Early Warning Systems Capacity Strengthening","Strengthening the capacity of integrated early warning systems;",""],[2,"50","8","Disaster Risk-Sensitive Spatial Planning","zona dengan tingkat kerawanan bencana yang tinggi perlu diprioritaskan menjadi kawasan lindung dalam penataan ruang wilayah, alih-alih dijadikan sebagai kawasan budidaya.",""],[2,"50","8","Disaster Adaptation and Risk Reduction Measures","Apabila tidak bisa dihindari sebagai kawasan budidaya, maka perlu didukung dengan adanya peningkatan upaya adaptasi dan pengurangan risiko bencana untuk mengurangi kerugian akibat bencana.",""]],"35":[[1,"70","5","UMKM Capacity and Value-Added Enhancement Initiative","Increasing the capacity and value-added of UMKM is accomplished through ease of doing business initiatives, expanding market access, accelerating financing, increasing human resource capacity, and strengthening cross- sectoral coordination.",""],[1,"89","8","Entrepreneurship, MSME, and Cooperative Strengthening Strategy","Strengthening entrepreneurship; micro, small, and medium enterprises (UMKM); and cooperatives, which will be carried out using the following strategies: (1) improving business partnerships among UMKM; (2) increasing",""],[1,"90","1","Entrepreneur and MSME Financing Schemes","The second strategy is to increase financing for entrepreneurs is carried by providing financing schemes for entrepreneurs and UMKM, including startup capital and assistance in accessing credit and financing.",""],[1,"90","1","Cooperative Capacity and Innovation Support","The third strategy is to increase the capacity of cooperatives and their respective manager, increase group assistance for cooperatives, develop the reach and scope of cooperatives, and build innovation in cooperatives.",""],[1,"90","2","Entrepreneurship Training for Young Entrepreneurs and Vulnerable Groups","Strategies for creating business opportunities and startups include: (1) entrepreneurship training for young entrepreneurs, including youth, women, victims of abuse and human trafficking, students, and the differently-abled;",""],[1,"90","2","Business Incubation Support","Strategies for creating business opportunities and startups include: (2) business incubation;",""],[1,"90","2","Business Service Capacity Strengthening","Strategies for creating business opportunities and startups include: (3) strengthening business service capacity;",""],[1,"90","2","Small and Medium Industrial Center Development","Strategies for creating business opportunities and startups include: (4) developing small and medium industrial centers, and (5) providing fiscal incentives.",""],[1,"90","2","Fiscal Incentives for Startups and Small Businesses","Strategies for creating business opportunities and startups include: (4) developing small and medium industrial centers, and (5) providing fiscal incentives.",""],[1,"90","2","Social Enterprise Capital and Procurement Support","The value-added of social enterprises is increased by facilitating access to capital, developing impact investment structures, building capacity, and facilitating access to government procurement of goods and services.",""],[1,"90","3","Regional Entrepreneurship, MSME, and Cooperative Development","The development of entrepreneurship, UMKM, and cooperatives is directed: (1) according to the economic potential of various regions, and to support the development of special economic zones, industrial estates, tourism zones, national priority rural areas (or KPPN), and increase productive economic activities in frontier, outermost, and least developed regions, and (2) to be integrated with infrastructure development.",""],[1,"91","5","Integrated Investment-Based Industrialization and SME Development","Investment-based industrialization is integrated with policies and strategies for developing entrepreneurship, cooperatives, and UMKM.",""],[1,"91","5","Small and Medium Industrial Centers Development","This type of integration is manifested in the upstream and downstream business partnerships with local businesses to form small and medium industrial centers, including rural agro- industries, which are managed by cooperatives, rural enterprises, and other community-based socio- economic institutions.",""],[1,"131","4","Entrepreneurship Development Initiative","entrepreneurship development;",""],[2,"72","3","MSME Competitiveness and Upgrading Policy","Peningkatan kapasitas dan nilai tambah UMKM dilakukan melalui kemudahan berusaha, perluasan akses pasar, akselerasi pembiayaan, peningkatan kapasitas sumber daya manusia, dan penguatan koordinasi lintas sektor.",""],[2,"78","7","SME Cooperative Facilitation Programme","Fasilitasi UMKM untuk berkoperasi terus dilaksanakan dalam rangka meningkatkan efisiensi dan skala ekonomi.",""],[2,"86","16","Thematic Industrial Zone Facilitation for Halal Industry","Fasilitasi kawasan industri dengan zona tematik: industri halal (kawasan)",""],[2,"92","4","Entrepreneurship, MSME, and Cooperative Strengthening Programme","(i) Penguatan kewirausahaan, usaha mikro, kecil dan menengah (UMKM) dan koperasi yang dilaksanakan dengan strategi: (1) meningkatkan kemitraan usaha antara usaha mikro kecil dan usaha menengah besar; (2) meningkatkan kapasitas usaha dan akses pembiayaan bagi wirausaha; (3) meningkatkan kapasitas, jangkauan, dan inovasi koperasi; (4) meningkatkan penciptaan peluang usaha dan start-up; serta (5) meningkatkan nilai tambah usaha sosial.",""],[2,"92","5","Business Capacity and Product Quality Development","Pelaksanaan strategi pertama mencakup pengembangan kapasitas usaha dan kualitas produk, penguatan kapasitas kelembagaan dan perluasan kemitraan usaha.",""],[2,"92","5","Export-Oriented Fiscal Incentives for MSMEs","Selain itu, pengembangan kapasitas kewirausahaan dan usaha mikro, kecil dan menengah (UMKM) juga didukung melalui penyediaan insentif fiskal yang berorientasi ekspor.",""],[2,"92","5","Entrepreneur and MSME Financing Scheme","Strategi peningkatan pembiayaan bagi wirausaha dilaksanakan melalui penyediaan skema pembiayaan bagi wirausaha dan UMKM, termasuk modal awal usaha, serta pendampingan mengakses kredit/ pembiayaan.",""],[2,"92","5","Cooperative Capacity and Innovation Development","Pelaksanaan strategi ketiga mencakup peningkatan kapasitas pengurus dan manajer koperasi, pendampingan kelompok untuk berkoperasi, pengembangan jangkauan dan cakupan usaha koperasi, serta pengembangan inovasi koperasi.",""],[2,"92","6","Entrepreneurship and Start-up Opportunity Creation Strategy","Pelaksanaan strategi penciptaan peluang usaha dan start-up dilaksanakan melalui: (1) pelatihan kewirausahaan bagi wirausaha pemula termasuk bagi generasi muda, perempuan, termasuk korban kekerasan dan tindak pidana perdagangan orang, santri, dan penyandang disabilitas; (2) inkubasi usaha; (3) penguatan kapasitas layanan usaha; (4) pengembangan sentra industri kecil dan menengah (IKM), dan (5) penyediaan insentif fiskal.",""],[2,"92","6","Social Enterprise Financing and Market Access Support","Nilai tambah usaha sosial ditingkatkan melalui pendampingan akses permodalan, pengembangan impact investment, peningkatan kapasitas, serta fasilitasi akses kepada pengadaan barang dan jasa pemerintah.",""],[2,"92","6","UMKM Data System and Regulatory Simplification Reform","Pelaksanaan strategi tersebut didukung dengan penataan basis data dan penyederhanaan regulasi di bidang pemberdayaan UMKM",""],[2,"92","7","Entrepreneurship, MSME, and Cooperative Development Program","Pengembangan kewirausahaan, UMKM, dan koperasi diarahkan: (1) sesuai potensi daerah dan untuk mendukung pengembangan KEK, Kawasan Industri, kawasan pariwisata, Kawasan Perdesaan Prioritas Nasional (KPPN), serta peningkatan aktivitas ekonomi produktif di wilayah Tertinggal Terdepan Terluar (3T), dan (2) terintegrasi dengan pengembangan infrastruktur.",""],[2,"94","2","Community-Based Small and Medium Industry Centers","bentuk sentra IKM, termasuk agroindustri perdesaan, yang dikelola koperasi, usaha perdesaan, dan lembaga sosial ekonomi lainnya yang berbasis masyarakat.",""],[2,"270","12","Omnibus Law Reform for MSME Empowerment and Job Creation","Pendekatan Omnibus Law dapat diterapkan salah satunya dalam rangka pemberdayaan UMKM dan Cipta Lapangan Kerja",""],[2,"273","6","Job Creation Omnibus Law","3) RUU Cipta Lapangan Kerja (termasuk didalamnya UU terkait UMKM, dengan pendekatan omnibus law)",""]],"36":[[1,"15","1","Economic Transformation Strengthening","To that end, strengthening the process of economic",""],[1,"16","3","Economic Transformation through Downstream Industrial Development","Achieving Vision 2045 through economic transformation, supported by downstream industries by utilizing human resources, regulatory simplification, and bureaucratic reform.",""],[1,"33","16","Structural Reform for Economic Growth","One key to achieving economic growth in the next five years is structural reform.",""],[1,"33","16","Manufacturing Revitalization Initiative","The reform is mainly driven by the revitalization of manufacturing, and also by the continuing efforts to boost the development of other sectors, including agriculture, downstream mining, sustainable infrastructure, and services.",""],[1,"33","16","Sector Development Support for Agriculture, Mining, Infrastructure, and Services","The reform is mainly driven by the revitalization of manufacturing, and also by the continuing efforts to boost the development of other sectors, including agriculture, downstream mining, sustainable infrastructure, and services.",""],[1,"35","1","Manufacturing Revitalization for Export Diversification","The increase in exports of goods in 2020-2024 will be supported by the revitalization of manufacturing that encourages diversification of non- commodity exports-especially exports of high-tech manufactured products- while reducing import dependence.",""],[1,"35","7","Manufacturing Sector Revitalization for Export Diversification","the revitalization of the manufacturing sector that encourages diversification of exports and reduces dependence on imports",""],[1,"90","4","Integrated Commodity-Based Industrialization","boosting industrialization based on the manufacture of various commodities-through the integration of upstream and downstream operations-derived from agriculture, forestry, fishery, and non-agricultural sources",""],[1,"91","2","Industrialization Focus on Upstream and Value-Added Manufacturing","The process of industrialization will be focused on: (1) upstream manufacturing of agricultural, chemical, and metal commodities; and (2) manufacturing that contributes to value-added and high competitiveness that include food and beverages, pharmaceuticals, medical devices, electric vehicles, electronics, machineries, textiles, and footwear.",""],[1,"91","2","Cross-Sector Policy Harmonization for Industrialization","Its implementation is supported by the harmonization of policies among the primary, secondary, and tertiary sectors.",""]],"37":[[1,"33","21","Industrial Modernization through Industry 4.0 Business Environment Reform","Improving the business environment that supports industrial modernization, by applying the tenets of Industry 4.0",""],[1,"96","2","Digital Technology and Industry 4.0 Uptake","optimizing the use of digital technology and aspects of Industry 4.0",""],[1,"96","4","Phased Industry 4.0 Technology Application Programme","The application of technological advancement in the next five years, especially in the context of Industry 4.0, will be carried out in stages in five sub-sectors, namely food and beverages, apparel, automotive, electronics, and chemical, which also covers pharmaceuticals.",""],[1,"96","4","Cross-Sector Technology Expansion for Efficiency and Competitiveness","Its application is expanded to improve efficiency, productivity, and competitiveness in agriculture, fishery, maritime affairs, forestry, energy, tourism, creative economy, transportation, trade, and finance.",""],[2,"97","5","Digital Technology and Industry 4.0 Utilization Strategy","(iv) Penguatan pilar pertumbuhan dan daya saing ekonomi yang dilaksanakan dengan strategi: (2) mengoptimalkan pemanfaatan teknologi digital dan industri 4.0;",""],[2,"97","7","Phased Industry 4.0 Technology Adoption in Priority Subsectors","Penerapan kemajuan teknologi, terutama industri 4.0 dalam lima tahun mendatang dilaksanakan secara bertahap pada lima subsektor yaitu makanan-minuman, tekstil dan pakaian jadi, otomotif, elektronik, dan kimia termasuk farmasi.",""]],"38":[[1,"90","4","Smelter and Industrial Estate Development","boosting industrialization through the development of smelters and industrial areas, especially outside Java",""],[1,"92","1","Development of Priority Industrial Estates Outside Java","Developing industrial estates (or KI) in regions outside Java remains a priority, including nine priority KI that are focused on the acceleration of infrastructure development, licensing facilitation, increased investment, post-disaster revitalization, and government-to-business cooperation.",""],[1,"92","1","Expansion of Industrial Estates Using Existing Infrastructure","In addition, there are 18 KI that will be developed in line with the framework of industrialization by using existing infrastructure, improving regional cooperation, and diversifying the regional economy.",""],[1,"92","2","Detailed Spatial Planning for Industrial Zones","Some industrial zones will also be facilitated by the preparation of detailed spatial plans (or RRTR/RDTR).",""],[1,"92","3","Integrated Support for Industrial Estates in Northern Java","Industrial estates specifically on the northern cost of Java, including KI Brebes and KI Madura, will be supported by integrated connectivity, adequate energy supply, and human resources.",""],[1,"92","5","Smelter Construction for Mineral Downstreaming","The downstreaming process of natural resources will be supported by the construction of smelters that focus on the following metal commodities: nickel (22 smelters), bauxite (5 smelters), iron (2 smelters), lead (1 smelters), and copper (1 smelter).",""],[1,"130","3","Natural Resource Processing and Industrial Estate Development","processing natural resources, which include plantations, mining, fishery, as well as fertilizer and petrochemical plants in Industrial Estates (KI) and Special Economic Zones",""]],"39":[[1,"95","3","Import Management Strategy Integration","The implementation of the import management strategy is integrated with another strategy that aims to increase the domestic content requirement (TKDN) and use of domestic products.",""],[1,"95","3","Domestic Supplier Development and Procurement Quality Improvement","The integration of these two strategies is supported by the development of component suppliers, as well as improvement in the quality of domestic goods and services for industrial and government procurement.",""],[2,"96","8","Import Management and Domestic Content Synergy Strategy","Pelaksanaan strategi pengelolaan impor disinergikan dengan strategi peningkatan TKDN serta penggunaan produk dalam negeri.",""],[2,"96","8","Domestic Supplier Development and Quality Improvement Support","Sinergi kedua strategi ini didukung dengan pengembangan pemasok komponen, serta peningkatan kualitas barang dan jasa dalam negeri untuk pengadaan industri dan pemerintah.",""]],"40":[[1,"242","12","Palm Oil Productivity Improvement and RSPO Sustainability Certification","In addition to increasing the productivity of oil palm, the efforts to certify palm oil sustainability through RSPO certification will also have",""],[1,"259","2","Environmentally Friendly Business Innovation Development","Business innovations that are built on environmentally friendly principles also need to be developed to reduce the negative impacts of pollution, and at the same time increase competition for environmentally friendly businesses.",""],[1,"265","7","Green Industry Development Measures","Developing green industry by: (a) conserving and auditing energy use in the industry; (b) applying process and technological modifications; and through (c) industrial waste management.",""],[2,"249","10","Green Industry Development Programme","Pengembangan Industri Hijau yang dilaksanakan melalui: (a) Konservasi dan Audit Penggunaan Energi pada Industri; (b) Penerapan Modifikasi Proses dan Teknologi; serta (c) Manajemen Limbah Industri.",""]],"41":[[1,"293","27","Licensing and Regulatory Simplification for Innovation Commercialization","Perpres draft on simplifying licensing and regulations on the commercialization of products on innovation.",""],[1,"293","28","Presidential Regulation on Use of Research Prototypes","Perpres draft on using research prototypes for",""],[2,"275","36","Presidential Regulation on Simplifying Licensing and Legal Procedures for Innovation Product Commercialization","RPerpres tentang penyederhanaan proses perizinan dan peraturan perundangan komersialisasi produk inovasi",""],[2,"276","2","Presidential Regulation on Utilization of Research Prototypes","RPerpres tentang pemanfaatan prototype hasil riset untuk Kementerian/Lembaga/ Satuan Kerja Perangkat Daerah (K/L/D) dan BUMN",""]],"42":[[1,"291","18","Revision of Regulation on Facilities and Ease in Special Economic Zones","Revision of PP No. 96/2015 on facilities and ease in special economic zones",""],[1,"292","16","Revision of Presidential Regulation on National Council and Special Economic Zone Council Arrangement","Revision of Perpres on the arrangement of the national council and the special economic zone council.",""]],"43":[[2,"97","2","Inbound and Outbound Investment Cooperation Facilitation","Sinerginya diwujudkan dalam bentuk fasilitasi pengembangan kerja sama investasi di dalam negeri (inbound), serta diplomasi ekonomi dan kerja sama investasi di negara tujuan ekspor (outbound).",""],[2,"256","2","South-South and Triangular Cooperation for Trade and Investment","Untuk itu perlunya penguatan kerja sama pembangunan internasional dengan mengoptimalkan kerja sama Selatan-Selatan dan Triangular (KSST) untuk mendukung perdagangan dan investasi.",""],[2,"256","2","Institutional Strengthening for International Development Assistance","Kelembagaan pelaksana pemberian bantuan dan kerja sama pembangunan internasional diperkuat, adapun sumber-sumber dan mekanisme pendanaan baru terus dikembangkan, misalnya skema kredit ekspor yang disalurkan melalui lembaga penyedia pembiayaan ekspor.",""],[2,"256","3","Private Sector Participation Promotion","Partisipasi aktor non pemerintah, terutama pihak swasta perlu ditingkatkan.",""]],"44":[[1,"90","4","Creative and Digital Business Competitiveness Support","increasing the value-added and competitiveness of creative and digital businesses and products",""],[1,"93","5","Creative Economy Assistance and Incubation Programme","Increasing the value-added of the creative economy will be carried out by: (1) providing assistance and incubation; (2) developing centers of excellence; (3) facilitating innovation",""],[1,"93","6","Creative Industry Cluster and Brand Strengthening Initiative","and brand strengthening, (4) developing and revitalizing creative spaces, creative clusters or cities, and \"Be Creative\" districts (BCD);",""],[1,"93","6","Intellectual Property Commercialization Support","(5) applying and commercializing intellectual property rights;",""],[1,"93","6","Creative Business Supply Chain and Scale-Up Support","(6) strengthening supply chains and scale of creative businesses.",""],[1,"93","6","Digital Cluster Development and Business Facilitation","Increasing the number of digital business actors will also be facilitated by developing digital clusters, including village-based clusters; ensuring ease of business; and providing access to financial services and market.",""],[1,"93","7","Creative Cluster Development and Expansion Programme","To strengthen the creative and digital economy in the future, attention will be directed to eight creative clusters in Java, Bali, Medan, and Makassar.",""],[1,"93","7","Creative Economy Expansion in High-Value Regions","The creative economy along with its activities will be expanded in stages in regions that have great potential for adding value.",""],[2,"95","5","Creative Economy Value-Addition Support Programme","Peningkatan nilai tambah ekonomi kreatif akan dilaksanakan melalui: (1) pendampingan dan inkubasi; (2) pengembangan center of excellence; (3) fasilitasi inovasi dan penguatan brand, (4) pengembangan dan revitalisasi ruang kreatif, klaster/kota kreatif dan Be Creative District (BCD); (5) penerapan dan komersialisasi hak atas kekayaan intelektual; serta (6) penguatan rantai pasok dan skala usaha kreatif.",""],[2,"95","5","Digital Entrepreneur Cluster Development and Market Access Support","Peningkatan populasi pelaku usaha digital juga akan difasilitasi melalui pengembangan klaster digital, termasuk yang berbasis desa, kemudahan usaha, serta akses kepada pembiayaan dan pasar.",""],[2,"95","6","Creative Economy Cluster Expansion","Penguatan ekonomi kreatif dan ekonomi digital ke depan difokuskan pada 8 klaster kreatif di Jawa, Bali, Medan dan Makassar.",""],[2,"95","6","Creative Economy Sector Strengthening","Sektor yang diperkuat yaitu kuliner, fashion, kriya, aplikasi dan konten digital, e-sport dan games, film, dan musik.",""],[2,"95","6","Phased Expansion of Creative Economy Activities","Perluasan aktivitas ekonomi kreatif dilaksanakan secara bertahap di wilayah lain yang memiliki potensi nilai tambah yang besar.",""]],"45":[[2,"37","18","Industrial Business Environment Improvement for Industry 4.0 Modernization","Memperbaiki lingkungan usaha yang mendukung modernisasi industri, termasuk melalui penerapan Industri 4.0",""],[2,"38","4","Private Investment Deregulation and Permitting Harmonization","investasi swasta (asing maupun dalam negeri) didorong melalui deregulasi prosedur investasi, sinkronisasi dan harmonisasi peraturan perizinan",""],[2,"38","4","Ease of Doing Business Improvement","termasuk meningkatkan Ease of Doing Business (EoDB) Indonesia dari peringkat 73 pada tahun 2019 menuju peringkat 40 pada tahun 2024",""],[2,"38","4","Productivity Enhancement for Investment Efficiency","Peningkatan investasi juga dilakukan melalui peningkatan produktivitas, yang mendorong peningkatan efisiensi investasi",""],[2,"67","3","Economic Resource Management and Value-Addition Strategy","Pembangunan ekonomi dilaksanakan melalui dua pendekatan, yaitu: (1) pengelolaan sumber daya ekonomi, dan (2) peningkatan nilai tambah ekonomi.",""],[2,"67","3","Cross-Sector Policy Coordination for Economic Development","Kedua pendekatan ini menjadi landasan bagi sinergi dan keterpaduan kebijakan lintas sektor yang mencakup sektor pangan dan pertanian, kemaritiman, perikanan dan kelautan, industri pengolahan, pariwisata, ekonomi kreatif, dan ekonomi digital.",""],[2,"70","4","Investment Attraction for Downstream Industrialization in Industrial and Special Economic Zones","Salah satu upaya yaitu dengan menarik investasi untuk hilirisasi sumber daya alam di Kawasan Industri (KI) dan Kawasan Ekonomi Khusus (KEK) berbasis industri terutama yang dibangun di luar Jawa.",""],[2,"93","2","Integrated Commodity Processing Industrialization","meningkatkan industrialisasi berbasis pengolahan komoditas pertanian, kehutanan, perikanan, kemaritiman, dan non agro yang terintegrasi hulu-hilir",""],[2,"93","2","Smelter and Industrial Estate Development","meningkatkan industrialisasi melalui pengembangan smelter dan kawasan industri terutama di luar Jawa",""],[2,"93","2","Business Climate Improvement and Investment Reform","memperbaiki iklim usaha dan meningkatkan investasi, termasuk reformasi ketenagakerjaan",""],[2,"93","3","Industrial Productivity and Value Chain Strengthening","Industrialisasi secara umum dilaksanakan melalui: (1) peningkatan produktivitas; (2) penguatan rantai pasok atau nilai melalui harmonisasi kebijakan yang mempengaruhi efisiensi alur input-proses-output-distribusi, dan pengembangan pemasok; (3) diversifikasi dan peningkatan kualitas produk industri hulu, antara dan hilir untuk penyediaan bahan baku, bahan antara/penolong dan barang jadi; (4) perluasan pengembangan permesinan termasuk untuk mendukung pemutakhiran mesin-mesin industri dan perluasan aktivitas industri di perdesaan; (5) penguatan infrastruktur pendukung industri, termasuk untuk standardisasi dan sertifikasi; (6) penguatan jasa industri; (7) penguatan penerapan manajemen industri modern; (8) penguatan circular economy sebagai sumber efisiensi dan nilai tambah; dan (9) penyediaan insentif untuk penumbuhan dan peningkatan skala industri termasuk melalui pembiayaan industri.",""],[2,"93","4","Agricultural and Non-Agricultural Industrialization Acceleration","Akselerasi industrialisasi berbasis pertanian dan non pertanian difokuskan pada: (1) industri pengolahan hulu agro, kimia dan logam; dan (2) industri pengolahan yang memiliki kontribusi nilai tambah dan daya saing yang tinggi yaitu makanan minuman, farmasi dan alat kesehatan, alat transportasi termasuk yang berbahan bakar listrik, elektrikal dan elektronik, mesin dan peralatan, tekstil dan produk tekstil, dan alas kaki.",""],[2,"93","4","Cross-Sector Policy Harmonization for Industrialization","Pelaksanaannya juga didukung oleh harmonisasi dan sinergi kebijakan antara sektor primer, sekunder dan tersier.",""],[2,"94","3","Priority Industrial Estate Development Outside Java","Pengembangan Kawasan Industri (KI) diutamakan untuk KI di luar Pulau Jawa yang mencakup 9 KI prioritas yang difokuskan pada percepatan penyediaan sarana penunjang, fasilitasi perizinan, peningkatan investasi, revitalisasi pasca bencana, serta kerjasama Pemerintah dan Badan Usaha (KPBU).",""],[2,"94","3","Industrialization of Eighteen Industrial Estates","Selain itu, terdapat 18 KI (KI Ladong, KI Kuala Tanjung, KI Tanjung Buton, KI Tenayan, KI Kemingking, KI Tanjung Enim, KI Tanggamus, KI Pesawaran, KI Way Pisang, KI Katibung, KI Brebes, KI Madura, KI Sumbawa Barat, KI Batanjung, KI Jorong, KI Batulucin, KI Tanah Kuning, dan KI Takalar) yang akan dikembangkan dalam kerangka industrialisasi dengan memanfaatkan infrastruktur yang sudah dibangun, kerja sama regional, serta diversifikasi perekonomian daerah.",""],[2,"94","4","Industrial Zone Spatial Planning Support","Beberapa kawasan industri juga akan difasilitasi penyusunan Rencana Rinci Tata Ruang/Rencana Detil Tata Ruang (RRTR/RDTR) di sekitar kawasan industri.",""],[2,"94","5","North Java Industrial Zone Integration Support","Khusus kawasan industri di pantai utara Jawa, termasuk KI Brebes dan KI Madura, akan diintegrasikan dengan dukungan konektivitas, serta pasokan energi dan SDM yang memadai.",""],[2,"94","6","Mineral Smelter Development Programme","Hilirisasi sumber daya alam melalui pembangunan smelter akan difokuskan pada hasil tambang nikel (22 smelter), bauksit (5 smelter), besi (2 smelter), timbal (1 smelter) dan tembaga (1 smelter).",""]],"46":[[2,"114","2","Investment, Promotion, Marketing, and Trade Partnership Expansion","melalui: (v) perluasan kerjasama dan kemitraan dalam investasi, promosi, pemasaran dan perdagangan;",""],[2,"114","4","Multi-Stakeholder Investment, Promotion, Marketing, and Trade Partnership Development","dan (ii) pengembangan kerjasama dan kemitraan dalam investasi, promosi, pemasaran dan perdagangan dengan multipihak.",""]],"47":[[1,"94","5","High Value-Added Export Promotion and Domestic Content Requirement Strengthening","(iii) Increasing high value-added exports and strengthening the domestic content requirement (or TKDN), which will be carried out using the following strategies: (1) increasing diversification, value-added, and competitiveness of exportable products and services; (2) increasing access and deepening the export market; (3) managing imports; (4) increasing the number and use of domestic products through effective government procurement; (5) increasing participation in global production networks; (6) enhancing image and diversifying tourism marketing, including creative and digital products; and (7) increasing the effectiveness of PTA/FTA/CEPA and strengthening economic diplomacy.",""],[1,"94","6","Export Expansion Strategy","The strategy for increasing and expanding exports includes: (1) increasing exports of complex industrial products, including medium and high-technology products; (2) increasing service exports by increasing the capacity of domestic service players based on competency, harmonizing service regulations, and providing data for trade services; (3) strengthening the information platform for exports and imports that includes market information, regulations, procedures, and incentives and advocacy in relation to bilateral and multilateral cooperation; (4) developing export- oriented marketplaces, including those that can be used by UMKM and technology startups to supply",""],[1,"95","2","Export Market Expansion and Trade Financing Support","Increasing access and deepening the export market by financing exports and imports and strengthening business-to-business cooperation schemes, among others.",""],[1,"95","5","International Investment Cooperation with Export Destination Countries","international investment cooperation with export destination countries (outbound).",""],[1,"95","5","Facilitation of Raw Material Imports for Export Production","increasing exports is also carried out by facilitating the importation of raw materials for export purposes.",""],[2,"39","2","Manufacturing Industry Revitalization for Export Diversification","Peningkatan ekspor barang tahun 2020-2024 akan didukung oleh revitalisasi industri pengolahan yang mendorong diversifikasi produk ekspor non-komoditas, terutama ekspor produk manufaktur berteknologi tinggi dan mengurangi ketergantungan impor.",""],[2,"39","2","Tourism Sector Development for Services Export Growth","Peningkatan juga didorong oleh peningkatan ekspor jasa, utamanya jasa perjalanan, melalui pengembangan sektor pariwisata.",""],[2,"39","2","Export Market Diversification and Expansion","Diversifikasi ekspor tidak hanya dilakukan dari sisi produk, namun juga dalam hal negara tujuan ekspor.",""],[2,"39","2","Export Market Expansion to Africa, Latin America, and Eastern Europe","Perluasan pasar ekspor utamanya dilakukan ke kawasan Afrika, Amerika Latin, dan Eropa Timur.",""],[2,"39","7","Manufacturing Sector Revitalization for Export Diversification","Kontribusi net ekspor diharapkan menuju positif, didukung oleh revitalisasi sektor industri pengolahan yang mendorong diversifikasi produk ekspor dan ketergantungan terhadap impor.",""],[2,"39","7","Tourism Sector Development for Export Growth","Peningkatan ekspor juga didukung oleh pengembangan sektor pariwisata",""],[2,"40","2","Fiscal Incentives for Investment and Value Addition","Kebijakan ini juga diimbangi dengan peran kebijakan perpajakan sebagai instrumen pendorong investasi melalui penyediaan insentif fiskal yang mendukung aktivitas penciptaan nilai tambah ekonomi (industri manufaktur, pariwisata, ekonomi kreatif dan digital).",""],[2,"41","4","Exchange Rate Stability and Export Competitiveness Measures","Sepanjang tahun 2020-2024, nilai tukar stabil pada tingkat fundamentalnya untuk menjaga daya saing ekspor.",""]],"48":[[1,"96","2","Logistics System Improvement and Price Stability","improving the logistics system and price stability",""],[1,"96","5","National Logistics System Efficiency Improvement","The management of the logistics system is focused on increasing the efficiency of national distribution for the smooth flow of goods and services among regions.",""],[1,"96","5","Bonded Logistics Centers Development","The implementation is complemented by the construction of facilities and infrastructure to support efficiency of distribution and logistics, including: bonded logistics centers, development of a national logistics ecosystem, and improvement in the quality of local markets through improved governance, application of the Indonesian National Standard (SNI) in markets, and use of digital technology.",""],[1,"96","5","National Logistics Ecosystem Development","The implementation is complemented by the construction of facilities and infrastructure to support efficiency of distribution and logistics, including: bonded logistics centers, development of a national logistics ecosystem, and improvement in the quality of local markets through improved governance, application of the Indonesian National Standard (SNI) in markets, and use of digital technology.",""],[1,"96","5","Local Market Quality Improvement","The implementation is complemented by the construction of facilities and infrastructure to support efficiency of distribution and logistics, including: bonded logistics centers, development of a national logistics ecosystem, and improvement in the quality of local markets through improved governance, application of the Indonesian National Standard (SNI) in markets, and use of digital technology.",""],[1,"96","5","Indonesia National Single Window Integration","The logistics system is also directed to improve the efficiency of international trade by accelerating the flow of imports and exports through the integration of business processes in all related ministries/institutions via the Indonesia National Single Window (INSW) system.",""],[2,"97","5","Logistics System and Price Stability Improvement","(iv) Penguatan pilar pertumbuhan dan daya saing ekonomi yang dilaksanakan dengan strategi: (3) meningkatkan sistem logistik dan stabilitas harga;",""],[2,"98","3","National Logistics System Strengthening","Penguatan sistem logistik difokuskan pada peningkatan efisiensi distribusi nasional untuk kelancaran arus barang dan jasa antarwilayah.",""]],"49":[[1,"22","3","Priority Tourism Destination Development","Developing leading destinations, by improving accessibility, attractions, and amenities at priority tourism destinations.",""],[1,"35","1","Tourism Sector Development for Service Export Growth","This increase is also driven by an increase in service exports, particularly travel, through the development of the tourism sector.",""],[1,"35","7","Tourism Sector Development for Export Growth","The increase in exports is also supported by the development of the tourism sector",""],[1,"90","4","Tourism Competitiveness and Ecosystem Development","increasing the competitiveness of tourism destinations and the tourism industry, which are supported by a strong supply chain and tourism ecosystem",""],[1,"92","6","Tourism Accessibility, Attractions, and Amenities Improvement","In the next five years, the tourism sector will focus on increasing the length of stay and tourism spending by improving accessibility, attractions, and amenities.",""],[1,"92","6","Development of Ten Priority Tourism Destinations","The main focus of development in the tourism sector is to accelerate the development of the ten priority tourism destinations, namely Lake Toba, Borobudur, Lombok-Mandalika, Labuan Bajo, Manado-Likupang, Wakatobi, Raja Ampat, Bangka Belitung, Bromo- Tengger-Semeru, and Morotai.",""],[1,"92","6","Bali Tourism Infrastructure Revitalization","Further, the revitalization of the tourism infrastructure in Bali serves to increase the island's carrying capacity.",""],[1,"92","7","Tourism Destination Development Programme","The tourism sector will also focus on developing 8 tourism destinations and increasing their readiness to accommodate a growing number of tourist arrivals.",""],[1,"93","1","Tourism Diversification Initiative","The types of tourism that will be diversified include: (1) nature tourism (ecotourism, marine tourism, and adventure tourism); (2) cultural tourism (heritage tourism, historical tourism, culinary tourism, city tourism that focuses on cultural heritage regeneration, and village tourism); and (3) artificial tourism (meeting- incentive-convention-",""],[1,"93","3","Tourism Amenities and Destination Development Programme","Such development includes cooperation in financing, improving destination management, applying service standards, strengthening tourism supply chains, structuring cities as tourism service hubs, structuring rural areas to support tourism, and developing tourist villages.",""],[1,"93","4","Ecotourism Destination Development Programme","The future development of tourism destinations will cover 25 ecotourism destinations that function as priority forests, 16 geoparks, and 6 marine tourism destinations that function as aquatic parks and aquatic nature reserves.",""],[1,"130","3","Tourism Destination Development","developing natural, cultural, and historical tourism destinations",""],[1,"133","1","Tourism Destination Development for Local Economic Growth","developing natural, cultural, and historical tourism destinations to drive local economic development through the service sector, which is focused on Priority Tourism Destinations (DPP)/Special Economic Zones (KEK)",""],[2,"26","5","Priority Tourism Destination Improvement","Pengembangan Destinasi Unggulan, melalui: perbaikan aksesibilitas, atraksi, dan amenitas di Destinasi Pariwisata Prioritas",""],[2,"93","2","Tourism Competitiveness and Supply Chain Strengthening","meningkatkan daya saing destinasi dan industri pariwisata yang didukung penguatan rantai pasok dan ekosistem pariwisata",""],[2,"94","7","Priority Tourism Destination Acceleration Program","Fokus utama pengembangan yaitu percepatan 10 Destinasi Pariwisata Prioritas (DPP) yaitu Danau Toba dan sekitarnya, Borobudur dan sekitarnya, Lombok-Mandalika, Labuan Bajo, Manado-Likupang, Wakatobi, Raja Ampat, Bangka Belitung, Bromo-Tengger-Semeru, dan Morotai.",""],[2,"94","7","Bali Revitalization Program","Revitalisasi Bali juga akan dilaksanakan untuk meningkatkan daya dukung.",""],[2,"94","8","Development of Eight Priority Tourism Destinations","Pengembangan 8 destinasi pariwisata difokuskan pada peningkatan kesiapannya untuk menampung peningkatan kunjungan wisatawan.",""],[2,"94","8","Phased Revitalization of Bali Tourism Destination","Revitalisasi destinasi diarahkan pada Bali yang dilaksanakan secara bertahap untuk meningkatkan daya dukungnya.",""],[2,"95","2","Cultural Heritage Regeneration and Diversified Tourism Development","wisata sejarah, wisata kuliner, wisata kota yang difokuskan pada Cultural Heritage Regeneration, dan wisata desa); (3) wisata buatan (meeting-incentive-convention- exhibition/MICE, yacht and cruise, wisata kebugaran/wellness tourism, wisata kesehatan/medical tourism, dan wisata olah raga).",""],[2,"95","2","Tourism-Integrated Knowledge, Education, and Volunteerism Activities","Pengembangan ketiga jenis pariwisata tersebut juga membuka kesempatan bagi wisatawan untuk terlibat dalam kegiatan pengembangan pengetahuan, pendidikan dan kesukarelawanan yang terintegrasi dengan kegiatan wisata.",""],[2,"95","3","Tourism Amenities and Attractions Development","Pelaksanaannya mencakup kerja sama pembiayaan, perbaikan pengelolaan destinasi, penerapan standar layanan, penguatan rantai pasok industri pariwisata, penataan kota sebagai service hub pariwisata, penataan kawasan perdesaan untuk mendukung pariwisata, serta pengembangan desa wisata.",""],[2,"95","4","Development of Priority Forest-Based Ecotourism Destinations","Terkait destinasi pariwisata yang akan dikembangkan, akan mencakup 25 destinasi ekowisata berbasis Kawasan Hutan Prioritas",""],[2,"95","4","Geopark Tourism Development Programme","16 taman bumi (Geopark)",""]],"50":[[1,"108","1","Eastern Indonesia Regional Development Acceleration","the regional development objective that will be achieved is to \"reduce regional disparity by encouraging transformation and acceleration of the development of the eastern region of Indonesia that includes Kalimantan, Nusa Tenggara, Sulawesi, Maluku, and Papua, while still maintaining growth momentum in Java,",""],[1,"114","3","Affirmative Development for Disadvantaged and Border Areas","Developing policies and implementing affirmative development to accelerate the growth of disadvantaged areas, priority border locations, frontier and outermost islands, and transmigration areas, through: (i) expanding access to basic education and health services; (ii) providing basic infrastructure and facilities for housing, clean water, sanitation, and electricity; (iii) improving land, river, sea, and air transportation connectivity; (iv) developing telecommunications and information networks as a basis for digital economy; (v) expanding cooperation and partnerships in investment, promotion, marketing, and trade; (vi) increasing supervision and safeguarding Exclusive Economic Zones (ZEE); and (vii) protecting and fulfilling the rights of transmigrants in accordance with applicable regulatory mandates.",""],[1,"117","1","Public Services and Economic Development Improvement","public services and economic development to improve people's welfare and regional progress;",""],[1,"130","1","Affirmative Development Initiative","implementing affirmative development",""],[1,"132","8","Basic Services and Governance Improvement in Border Districts","fulfilling basic services and improving governance in border districts;",""],[1,"132","8","Affirmative Development Implementation","implementing affirmative development.",""],[1,"133","1","Affirmative Development Measures","implementing affirmative development",""]],"51":[[1,"110","2","Village-Owned Enterprise Revitalization","Total revitalization of village owned enterprises (BUMDes) based on status:",""],[1,"114","4","Integrated Village Development Programme","Accelerating integrated village development to encourage social, cultural and economic transformation of villages, which is supported by: (i) good governance through increasing the capacity of village apparatuses,",""],[1,"114","5","Inclusive Village Development and Governance Support","(ii) determining village borders, (iii) developing tourist villages, digital villages, leading products of villages and rural areas, and developing BUMDesa/BUMDes Bersama; (iv) improving basic services in villages; (v) optimizing the use of village funds to encourage productive activities, empowering village communities including funding local village assistants; and (vi) strengthening the role of sub- districts as centers of change and growth, as well as village development and supervision.",""],[1,"117","1","District Strengthening and Village Development Supervision","strengthening districts as centers of change and growth, as well as village development and supervision;",""],[1,"130","1","Integrated Village Development Programme","accelerating village development in an integrated manner to encourage social, cultural and economic transformation of villages",""],[1,"132","8","Integrated Village Development Acceleration","accelerating village development in an integrated manner to encourage social, cultural, and economic transformation of villages;",""],[1,"133","3","Sub-district Service and Development Center Strengthening","strengthening the role of the sub-district as a center for data, information and knowledge, center for basic services, center for community empowerment, center for innovation and entrepreneurship development, center for natural resource management and the environment, and center for economic growth of the district",""],[2,"114","3","Integrated Village Development Acceleration","Percepatan pembangunan desa secara terpadu untuk mendorong transformasi sosial, budaya dan ekonomi desa yang didukung dengan: (i) tata kelola pemerintahan yang baik melalui peningkatan kapasitas aparatur desa, pendampingan, peran serta masyarakat desa yang inklusif; (ii) penetapan batas desa, (iii) pengembangan desa wisata, desa digital dan produk unggulan desa dan kawasan perdesaan, pengembangan BUMDesa/BUMDes Bersama; (iv) peningkatan pelayanan dasar desa, (v) optimalisasi pemanfaatan dana desa untuk mendorong kegiatan produktif, memberdayakan masyarakat desa termasuk membiayai pendamping lokal desa; dan (vi) penguatan peran kecamatan sebagai pusat perubahan dan pertumbuhan, serta pembinaan dan pengawasan desa.",""],[2,"130","4","Integrated Village Development Acceleration","percepatan pembangunan desa secara terpadu untuk mendorong transformasi sosial, budaya dan ekonomi desa",""],[2,"132","4","Integrated Village Development Acceleration","percepatan pembangunan desa secara terpadu untuk mendorong transformasi sosial, budaya dan ekonomi desa;",""],[2,"134","4","Integrated Village Development Acceleration","percepatan pembangunan desa secara terpadu untuk mendorong transformasi sosial, budaya dan ekonomi desa;",""],[2,"135","6","Integrated Village Development Programme","Pembangunan desa terpadu yang mencakup peningkatan kapasitas aparatur desa untuk meningkatkan tata kelola pemerintahan yang baik termasuk pemanfaatan dana desa dan tata kelola aset desa; penguatan pendamping desa yang fokus pada desa tertinggal dan peran serta masyarakat desa yang inklusif; penetapan batas desa, pengembangan desa wisata, desa digital dan produk unggulan desa dan kawasan perdesaan; transformasi ekonomi desa dan peningkatan peran Badan Usaha Milik Desa (BUMDes); perbaikan pelayanan dasar air minum, sanitasi dan listrik desa; serta pemanfaatan dana desa untuk mendorong sektor-sektor produktif dan pemberdayaan masyarakat desa melalui pendamping lokal desa.",""],[2,"136","5","Integrated Village Development Acceleration","percepatan pembangunan desa secara terpadu untuk mendorong transformasi sosial, budaya dan ekonomi desa;",""],[2,"138","5","Integrated Village Development Acceleration","percepatan pembangunan desa secara terpadu untuk mendorong transformasi sosial, budaya dan ekonomi desa;",""],[2,"140","6","Integrated Village Development Acceleration","(c) percepatan pembangunan desa secara terpadu untuk mendorong transformasi sosial, budaya dan ekonomi desa.",""]],"52":[[1,"114","6","Rural-Urban Linkage Strengthening Initiative","Strengthening rural-urban linkages that support centers of excellence based on village territories, National Priority Rural Areas (KPPN), transmigration areas, and National Border Strategic Activity Centers (PKSN) through: (i) improving accessibility and connectivity including logistics networks from villages to trade centers, both local, regional and international markets; and (ii) developing cooperation and partnerships in investment, promotion, marketing and trade with multiple stakeholders.",""],[1,"130","3","Rural-Urban Linkage Strengthening","strengthening rural- urban linkages that support regional growth centers",""],[1,"133","1","Rural-Urban Linkage Strengthening","strengthening rural-urban linkages that support regional growth centers",""]],"53":[[1,"57","3","Regional Economic Growth and Commodity Distribution Improvement","Increase economic growth, equitable development, and welfare in 10 regencies in Laa Pago and 11 regencies in Domberay",""],[1,"130","2","Regional Growth Center Strengthening Program","Strengthening regional growth centers, among others through: (a) developing leading commodities in Papua, namely sago, nutmeg, pepper, cloves, cocoa, coffee, gold, copper, coal, oil, natural gas, and capture fishery; (b) developing fishery centers in Integrated Marine and Fishery Centers (SKPT)/Fishery Management Areas (WPP); (c) developing agricultural and plantation production centers that are scattered in several National Priority Rural Areas (KPPN); (d) revitalizing transmigration areas; (e) economic development of leading commodity-based border",""],[1,"130","3","Economic Potential Area Development in Customary Areas","developing Economic Potential Areas (KPE) in 7 customary areas (Laa Pago, Saireri, Tabi, Mee Pago, Anim Ha, Bomberay, and Domberay) with due regard to ecological zones and to the preparation of human resources in the context of Industrial Revolution 4.0 through the downstreaming of Papua's economic potentials",""],[1,"131","4","District Economic Growth Center","center for economic growth in the district;",""],[1,"132","9","Regional Growth Center Strengthening","Strengthening regional growth centers through: (a) developing leading commodities in Maluku, namely coconut, pepper, nutmeg, cloves, gold, coal, oil and gas, nickel, and capture fishery; (b) developing fishery centers and fishery processing industries in Marine and Fishery Centers (SKPT)/Fishery Management Areas (WPP); (c) developing agricultural and plantation production centers, which are scattered in several National Priority Rural Areas (KPPN); (d) revitalizing transmigration areas; (e) economic development of leading",""],[1,"133","1","Commodity-Based Border Region Development","commodity-based border regions",""],[1,"133","1","Strategic Area and Mining Development","developing strategic areas and natural resource manufacturing in the form of mining",""],[2,"101","5","Growth Corridor Development Acceleration","Koridor pertumbuhan berorientasi untuk memacu pertumbuhan ekonomi nasional melalui percepatan pengembangan kawasan-kawasan pertumbuhan, meliputi PKN, PKW, KEK, KI, dan KSPN, serta kota-desa serta kawasan aglomerasi perkotaan pada kabupaten/kota yang terletak pada koridor pertumbuhan.",""],[2,"101","5","Equity Corridor Basic Services Expansion","Sementara koridor pemerataan berorientasi untuk pemenuhan pelayanan dasar yang lebih merata melalui pengembangan PKW dan PKL sehingga terbentuk pusat-pusat pelayanan dasar baru yang menjangkau daerah pelayanan yang lebih luas, pada kabupaten/kota pada koridor pemerataan.",""],[2,"113","2","Growth Corridor Development of Regional Growth Centers","Pendekatan melalui koridor pertumbuhan mengutamakan pengembangan pusat-pusat pertumbuhan dengan basis keunggulan wilayah yang dapat mendorong peningkatan nilai tambah, peningkatan peneriman devisa dan atau penghematan devisa, perluasan kesempatan kerja dan pertumbuhan ekonomi secara nyata dalam lima tahun mendatang.",""],[2,"127","6","Regional Growth Center Strengthening through Priority Commodity Development","Penguatan pusat-pusat pertumbuhan wilayah dilakukan melalui antara lain: (a) pengembangan komoditas unggulan Wilayah Papua yaitu sagu, pala, lada, cengkeh, kakao, kopi, emas, tembaga, batubara, minyak dan gas bumi, serta perikanan tangkap; (b) pengembangan sentra perikanan di Sentra Kelautan Perikanan Terpadu (SKPT)/",""],[2,"130","5","Regional Growth Center Strengthening Program","(2) Penguatan pusat-pusat pertumbuhan wilayah dilakukan melalui antara lain: (a) pengembangan komoditas unggulan Wilayah Maluku yaitu kelapa, lada, pala, cengkeh, emas, batubara, minyak dan gas bumi, nikel, serta perikanan tangkap; (b) pengembangan sentra perikanan dan industri pengolahan hasil perikanan di SKPT/ WPP; (c) pengembangan sentra produksi pertanian dan perkebunan yang tersebar di beberapa KPPN; (d) revitalisasi kawasan transmigrasi; (e) pengembangan ekonomi kawasan perbatasan berbasis komoditas unggulan; (f) pengembangan kawasan strategis dan pengolahan sumber daya alam berupa pertambangan; (g) pengembangan destinasi pariwisata alam, budaya dan sejarah sebagai salah satu motor penggerak pengembangan ekonomi lokal melalui sektor jasa yang difokuskan pada Destinasi Pariwisata Prioritas (DPP)/Kawasan Ekonomi Khusus (KEK); (h) pengembangan kawasan perkotaan dan pembangunan kota baru; dan (i) penguatan keterkaitan desa-kota yang mendukung pusat pertumbuhan wilayah.",""],[2,"132","5","Regional Growth Center Strengthening Program","(2) Penguatan pusat-pusat pertumbuhan wilayah dilakukan melalui antara lain: (a) pengembangan komoditas unggulan Wilayah Nusa Tenggara yaitu lada, pala, cengkeh, kopi, kelapa, tebu, garam, tembaga, emas, perikanan budidaya, dan perikanan tangkap; (b) pengembangan sentra perikanan dan industri pengolahan hasil perikanan di SKPT/WPP; (c) pengembangan sentra produksi peternakan dan perkebunan yang tersebar di beberapa KPPN, (d) revitalisasi kawasan transmigrasi; (e) pengembangan ekonomi kawasan perbatasan berbasis komoditas unggulan; (f) pengembangan kawasan strategis, dan pengolahan sumber daya alam berupa perkebunan dan pertambangan; (g) destinasi pariwisata alam, budaya dan sejarah sebagai salah satu motor penggerak pengembangan ekonomi lokal melalui sektor jasa pada Destinasi Pariwisata Prioritas (DPP)/Kawasan Ekonomi Khusus (KEK); (h) pengembangan kawasan perkotaan; (i) pengembangan kawasan pusat pertumbuhan baru dengan bertumpu pada skema investasi swasta; (j) peningkatan peran dan efisiensi pelayanan kota besar, menengah, dan kecil untuk meningkatkan sinergi pembangunan perkotaan dan perdesaan; dan (k) penguatan keterkaitan desa-kota yang mendukung pusat pertumbuhan wilayah.",""],[2,"134","5","Growth Center Strengthening and Regional Economic Development","Penguatan pusat-pusat pertumbuhan dilakukan melalui antara lain: (a) pengembangan komoditas unggulan Wilayah Sulawesi yaitu kelapa, kelapa sawit, lada, cengkeh, pala, kakao, kopi, tebu, emas, nikel, bijih besi, batu bara, minyak dan gas bumi, perikanan tangkap dan perikanan budidaya; (b) pengembangan sentra produksi perikanan di SKPT/WPP; (c) pengembangan sentra produksi pertanian dan perkebunan yang tersebar di beberapa KPPN; (d) revitalisasi kawasan transmigrasi; (e) pengembangan ekonomi kawasan perbatasan berbasis komoditas unggulan; (f) pengembangan komoditas unggulan dan industri pengolahan (hilirisasi) sumber daya alam (pertanian, perkebunan, logam dasar, dan kemaritiman) melalui pemanfaatan dan keterpaduan pembangunan infrastruktur pada KEK dan KI; dan (g) pengembangan kawasan strategis prioritas berbasis pariwisata pada Destinasi Pariwisata Prioritas (DPP); (h) pengembangan kawasan perkotaan termasuk WM sebagai pemacu pertumbuhan ekonomi Pulau Sulawesi dan pembangunan kota baru serta pengembangan kota lainnya; dan (i) penguatan keterkaitan desa-kota yang mendukung pusat pertumbuhan wilayah.",""],[2,"136","6","Regional Growth Center Strengthening Program","Penguatan pusat-pusat pertumbuhan wilayah dilakukan melalui antara lain: (a) pengembangan komoditas unggulan Wilayah Kalimantan antara lain karet, kelapa sawit, kelapa, lada, pala, cengkeh, kakao, bauksit, emas, minyak bumi, gas bumi, batubara, perikanan budidaya dan perikanan tangkap; (b) pengembangan sentra produksi perikanan di SKPT/WPP; (c) pengembangan sentra produksi perkebunan yang tersebar di beberapa KPPN; (d) revitalisasi kawasan transmigrasi; (e) pengembangan ekonomi kawasan perbatasan berbasis komoditas unggulan; (f) pengembangan komoditas unggulan, industri pengolahan (hilirisasi) sumber daya alam perkebunan dan hasil tambang, serta kawasan pertambangan pada Kawasan Industri (KI) dan/atau Kawasan Ekonomi Khusus (KEK); (g) pengembangan destinasi pariwisata alam, budaya dan sejarah pada Destinasi Pariwisata Prioritas (DPP); (h) pengembangan kawasan perkotaan termasuk WM sebagai pemacu pertumbuhan ekonomi Pulau Kalimantan dan pembangunan kota baru serta pengembangan kota lainnya; (i) pembangunan IKN di Kalimantan Timur; dan (j) penguatan keterkaitan desa-kota yang mendukung pusat pertumbuhan wilayah.",""],[2,"138","6","Regional Growth Center Strengthening Program","(2) Penguatan pusat-pusat pertumbuhan wilayah dilakukan melalui antara lain: (a) pengembangan komoditas unggulan Wilayah Sumatera yang meliputi kakao, kelapa, kelapa sawit, karet, kopi, lada, pala, tebu, emas, timah, minyak bumi, gas bumi, batubara, perikanan tangkap, dan perikanan budidaya; (b) pengembangan sentra produksi perikanan di SKPT/WPP; (c) pengembangan sentra produksi pertanian dan perkebunan yang tersebar di beberapa KPPN; (d) pengembangan kawasan strategis dan pengolahan sumber daya alam perkebunan, perikanan, pertambangan, dan industri kedirgantaraan di beberapa Kawasan Ekonomi Khusus (KEK) dan Kawasan industri (KI), serta Kawasan Perdagangan Bebas dan Pelabuhan Bebas (KPBPB); (e) revitalisasi kawasan transmigrasi; (f) pengembangan ekonomi kawasan perbatasan berbasis komoditas unggulan; (g) pembangunan alternatif di Provinsi Aceh untuk mentransformasi kawasan rawan ganja menjadi kawasan ekonomi lokal sebagai bagian terpadu pembangunan daerah; (h) pengembangan pariwisata daerah sebagai salah satu motor penggerak pengembangan ekonomi lokal pada Destinasi Pariwisata",""]],"54":[[1,"129","3","Local Commodity-Based Industry Development","The accelerated development of Papua is also directed to encourage economic transformation from being natural resource-dependent to becoming a more advanced regional economy by encouraging the development of local commodity-based industries in agriculture, plantations, animal husbandry, and forestry;",""],[1,"129","3","Papua Maritime Economy Development","the development of the maritime economy through the development of the fishing industry and marine tourism;",""],[1,"129","3","Cultural and Natural Tourism Development","the development of cultural and natural tourism through developing the socio- cultural potential and biodiversity;",""],[1,"129","3","Downstream Mining and Energy Industries Development","the development of downstream industries that include mining, oil, natural gas, and copper;",""],[2,"127","3","Papua Regional Development Acceleration","Kebijakan pembangunan Wilayah Papua dalam tahun 2020-2024 diarahkan pada percepatan pembangunan untuk mengejar ketertinggalan dibanding wilayah lainnya, dan pelaksanaan Otonomi Khusus Papua dan Papua Barat berlandaskan pendekatan budaya dan kontekstual Papua, dan berbasis ekologis dan wilayah adat.",""],[2,"127","3","Local Commodity-Based Industry Development","mendorong pengembangan industri berbasis komoditas lokal pertanian, perkebunan, peternakan dan kehutanan;",""],[2,"127","3","Marine Economy Development","pengembangan ekonomi kemaritiman melalui pengembangan industri perikanan dan pariwisata bahari;",""],[2,"127","3","Cultural and Nature Tourism Development","pengembangan pariwisata budaya dan alam melalui pengembangan potensi sosial budaya dan keanekaragaman hayati;",""],[2,"127","3","Mining, Oil, Gas, and Copper Downstreaming","pengembangan hilirisasi industri pertambangan, minyak, gas bumi dan tembaga;",""],[2,"127","3","Conservation Area and Environmental Carrying Capacity Enhancement","serta peningkatan kawasan konservasi dan daya dukung lingkungan untuk pembangunan rendah karbon.",""],[2,"128","2","Fisheries Management Area Development","Wilayah Pengelolaan Perikanan (WPP);",""],[2,"128","2","Agricultural and Plantation Production Center Development","pengembangan sentra produksi pertanian dan perkebunan yang tersebar di beberapa Kawasan Perdesaan Prioritas Nasional (KPPN);",""],[2,"128","2","Border Area Commodity-Based Economic Development","pengembangan ekonomi kawasan perbatasan berbasis komoditas unggulan;",""],[2,"128","2","Natural Resource Processing in Industrial and Special Economic Zones","pengolahan sumber daya alam berupa perkebunan, pertambangan, perikanan, serta pengolahan pupuk dan petrokimia pada Kawasan Industri (KI) dan Kawasan Ekonomi Khusus;",""],[2,"128","2","Local Economic Development and Local Entrepreneur Empowerment","pengembangan ekonomi lokal dan pemberdayaan pengusaha lokal;",""],[2,"128","2","Nature, Culture, and Heritage Tourism Destination Development","pengembangan destinasi pariwisata alam, budaya dan sejarah;",""],[2,"128","8","Fishery Downstream Processing and Coastal Tourism Development","Hilirisasi industri perikanan, industri pengalengan ikan dan industri pariwisata budaya dan bahari Kepulauan Padaido dan Kepulauan Ambai",""],[2,"128","10","Sago, Coconut, and Cocoa Downstream Industrialization and Lake Sentani and Marine Tourism Development","Hilirisasi industri sagu, kelapa, kakao dan pengembangan pariwisata Danau Sentani dan wisata bahari",""],[2,"128","12","Sago, Coconut, and Cocoa Downstream Processing and Lake Sentani and Marine Tourism Development","Hilirisasi industri sagu, kelapa, kakao dan pengembangan pariwisata Danau Sentani dan wisata bahari",""],[2,"130","2","Maritime-Based Economic Development Acceleration","Kebijakan pembangunan wilayah Maluku diarahkan untuk mendorong transformasi ekonomi menjadi lebih maju dan bernilai tambah tinggi melalui percepatan pembangunan perekonomian berbasis maritim (kelautan), pengembangan industri pengolahan hasil perkebunan dan hasil nikel dan tembaga; gas, dan pengembangan pariwisata.",""],[2,"130","2","Agricultural and Mineral Processing Industry Development","Kebijakan pembangunan wilayah Maluku diarahkan untuk mendorong transformasi ekonomi menjadi lebih maju dan bernilai tambah tinggi melalui percepatan pembangunan perekonomian berbasis maritim (kelautan), pengembangan industri pengolahan hasil perkebunan dan hasil nikel dan tembaga; gas, dan pengembangan pariwisata.",""],[2,"130","2","Tourism Development for Maluku Region","Kebijakan pembangunan wilayah Maluku diarahkan untuk mendorong transformasi ekonomi menjadi lebih maju dan bernilai tambah tinggi melalui percepatan pembangunan perekonomian berbasis maritim (kelautan), pengembangan industri pengolahan hasil perkebunan dan hasil nikel dan tembaga; gas, dan pengembangan pariwisata.",""],[2,"132","2","Nusa Tenggara Regional Economic Transformation and Cluster-Based Development","Kebijakan pembangunan Wilayah Nusa Tenggara dalam tahun 2020-2024 diarahkan pada optimalisasi keunggulan wilayah dalam perikanan, perkebunan, peternakan, pertambangan dan pariwisata yang mengutamakan pendekatan gugus pulau.",""],[2,"132","2","Ecotourism Gateway and MICE Industry Development","Kebijakan pembangunan Wilayah Nusa Tenggara diarahkan untuk mendorong transformasi perekonomian dengan memperkuat peran sebagai pintu gerbang pariwisata ekologis melalui pengembangan industri Meeting, Incentive, Convetion, Exhibition (MICE); industri kreatif berbasis budaya, percepatan pembangunan perekonomian berbasis maritim (kelautan) melalui pengembangan industri perikanan, garam, dan rumput laut; pengembangan industri berbasis peternakan sapi dan perkebunan jagung; serta pengembangan industri mangan dan tembaga.",""],[2,"134","2","Sulawesi Regional Economic Transformation and Industrial Development","Kebijakan pembangunan Wilayah Sulawesi tahun 2020-2024 diarahkan untuk memperkuat peran Sulawesi sebagai salah satu pintu gerbang Indonesia dalam perdagangan internasional dan pintu gerbang Kawasan Timur Indonesia; pengembangan industri berbasis logistik; lumbung pangan nasional dengan pengembangan industri berbasis kakao, padi, jagung; pengembangan industri berbasis rotan, aspal, nikel, bijih besi dan gas bumi; percepatan pembangunan ekonomi berbasis maritim (kelautan) melalui pengembangan industri perikanan dan pariwisata bahari.",""],[2,"134","2","Sulawesi Industrial Downstreaming Initiative","Transformasi ekonomi di Wilayah Sulawesi diarahkan untuk mewujudkan hilirisasi industri berbasis pertanian, perkebunan, perikanan dan tambang untuk menciptakan nilai tambah melalui pengolahan bahan baku menjadi bahan setengah jadi atau bahan akhir.",""],[2,"136","2","Kalimantan Environmental Conservation and Rehabilitation Programme","maka pembangunan wilayah Pulau Kalimantan dalam lima tahun mendatang diarahkan untuk mempertahankan fungsi Kalimantan sebagai paru-paru dunia (Heart of Borneo) dengan menjaga kawasan berfungsi pelestarian lingkungan dan ekologis; meningkatkan konservasi dan rehabilitasi DAS, lahan kritis, hutan lindung, dan hutan produksi; mengembangkan pencegahan bencana alam banjir dan kebakaran hutan; mempertahankan peran sebagai lumbung energi nasional melalui pengembangan hilirisasi komoditas batu bara, termasuk pengembangan energi baru terbarukan berbasis biomassa dan air atau matahari atau sesuai dengan kondisi wilayah; pengembangan industri berbasis komoditas kelapa sawit, karet, bauksit, bijihbesi, gas alam cair, pasir zirkon dan pasir kuarsa.",""],[2,"138","3","Sumatra Industrial Downstreaming and Economic Corridor Development","Dalam lima tahun mendatang, transformasi ekonomi di Wilayah Sumatera diarahkan untuk mewujudkan hilirisasi industri berbasis pertanian, perikanan dan tambang untuk menciptakan nilai tambah melalui pengolahan bahan baku menjadi bahan setengah jadi dan bahan akhir dengan mengoptimalkan manfaat pembangunan jalan tol Trans Sumatera, bandara dan pelabuhan.",""],[2,"138","3","East Coast Sumatra Economic Zone and Kuala Tanjung International Hub Development","Selain itu, pengembangan kawasan ekonomi di sepanjang koridor pesisir timur Sumatera diarahkan untuk hilirisasi komoditas unggulan dan pusat pertumbuhan yang berorientasi ekspor dengan didukung pengembangan hub internasional di Kuala Tanjung sebagai pusat perdagangan di wilayah Indonesia Bagian Barat.",""],[2,"139","2","Aerospace Industry Development","Prioritas (DPP); (i) pengembangan industri kedirgantaraan;",""],[2,"140","2","Jawa-Bali Industrial and Services Development","Dalam lima tahun mendatang, pembangunan wilayah Jawa yang relatif maju dan berkembang diarahkan untuk memantapkan peran sebagai pusat ekonomi modern dan bersaing di tingkat global dengan bertumpu pada industri manufaktur, ekonomi kreatif dan jasa pariwisata, penghasil produk akhir dan produk antara yang berorientasi ekspor dengan memanfaatkan teknologi tinggi menuju industri 4.0, serta pengembangan destinasi pariwisata berbasis alam, budaya, dan MICE.",""],[2,"140","3","Java-Bali Service and High-Tech Industry Development","pembangunan ekonomi di Pulau Jawa-Bali akan diarahkan pada kegiatan berbasis jasa dan industri teknologi tinggi dengan memperhatikan daya dukung sumber daya alam dan lingkungan untuk memastikan pembangunan yang berkeberlanjutan.",""],[2,"140","7","Java-Bali Growth Defense Development Package","(3) Pertahanan pertumbuhan Jawa-Bali, dilakukan dengan: (a) pengembangan komoditas unggulan Wilayah Jawa-Bali antara lain cengkeh, lada, pala, kelapa, kopi, tebu, kakao, emas, garam, perikanan tangkap, dan perikanan budidaya; (b) pengembangan sektor industri teknologi tinggi, industri kreatif, dan jasa serta pusat industri manufaktur pada beberapa Kawasan Ekonomi Khusus (KEK) dan Kawasan Industri (KI); (c) pengembangan kawasan strategis berbasis pariwisata alam, budaya, dan MICE pada beberapa Destinasi Pariwisata Prioritas (DPP); (d) pengembangan kawasan perkotaan, melalui peningkatan kualitas WM, pembangunan kota baru, serta pengembangan kota lainnya; (e) pengembangan sentra produksi pertanian dan perkebunan yang tersebar di beberapa KPPN; (f) pengembangan kawasan agropolitan; dan (g) pengembangan sentra produksi perikanan di WPP.",""]],"55":[[1,"131","4","Customary Territories Development Programme","developing 7 customary territories;",""],[2,"125","2","Indigenous Papuan Empowerment and Cultural Development Initiative","penguatan dan pemberdayaan Orang Asli Papua berlandaskan budaya dan adat yang mengutamakan nilai-nilai kemanusiaan",""],[2,"125","2","Customary Area Economic Development Programme","pengembangan wilàyah adat Tabi, Saereri, La Pago, Me Pago, Anim Ha, Bomberai dan Domberai dalam mendukung perekonomian wilayah",""],[2,"128","2","Economic Potential Area Development in Customary Regions","pengembangan Kawasan Potensi Ekonomi (KPE) di 7 wilayah adat (Laa Pago, Saireri, Tabi, Mee Pago, Anim Ha, Bomberay, Domberay) dengan memperhatikan zona ekologi dan penyiapan SDM dalam rangka revolusi industri 4.0 melalui hilirisasi potensi ekonomi Papua;",""]],"56":[[1,"38","2","New National Capital Development Investment","investment in the development of the new national capital",""],[1,"115","5","Development of the National Capital Outside Java","Developing the National Capital outside Java in a more spatially and economically balanced position",""],[1,"138","5","State Capital Relocation to Kalimantan","The relocation of the State Capital (IKN) from Java to Kalimantan is expected to help encourage economic diversification",""],[1,"139","3","Urban and Metropolitan Area Development","developing urban areas including metropolitan areas to drive economic growth in Kalimantan and developing new cities and others;",""],[1,"139","3","East Kalimantan State Capital Development","State Capital development in East Kalimantan;",""],[1,"139","3","Rural-Urban Linkage Strengthening","strengthening rural-urban linkages that support regional growth centers.",""],[1,"141","3","Urban and Metropolitan Area Development","developing urban areas including metropolitan areas to drive economic growth in Sumatra and developing new cities and others",""],[1,"141","3","Rural-Urban Linkage Strengthening","strengthening rural-urban linkages that support regional growth centers",""],[1,"143","2","Phased National Capital Relocation to Kalimantan","the transfer of the National Capital (IKN) to Kalimantan will be carried out in stages",""],[1,"143","2","Development of Metropolitan Areas and New Cities Outside Java","supported by the development of metropolitan areas and new cities outside Java",""],[1,"143","4","Relocation of the Central Government and National Capital","Moving the central government and the National Capital outside of Java.",""],[2,"124","2","Metropolitan and Large City Optimization Initiative","Optimalisasi Wilayah Metropolitan (WM) dan kota besar di luar Jawa, termasuk perencanaan ruang, pembangunan infrastruktur perkotaan, perencanaan investasi dan pembiayaan pembangunan dengan tetap mempertahankan pertumbuhan dan meningkatkan daya dukung lingkungan untuk WM dan kota besar di Jawa;",""],[2,"124","4","New National Capital Development","Pembangunan Ibu Kota Negara di luar pulau Jawa di posisi yang lebih seimbang secara spasial dan ekonomi, sebagai stimulus pertumbuhan perekonomian melalui peningkatan permintaan agregat, mendorong diversifikasi ekonomi Pulau Kalimantan, sumber pertumbuhan ekonomi baru jangka panjang terutama untuk Wilayah Pulau Kalimantan dan Kawasan Timur Indonesia, dan mengurangi ketimpangan antar wilayah, didukung oleh kebijakan pengelolaan ASN berbasis smart governance;",""],[2,"136","3","National Capital Relocation to Kalimantan","Pemindahan Ibu Kota Negara (IKN) dari Pulau Jawa ke Pulau Kalimantan diharapkan dapat membantu mendorong diversifikasi ekonomi dan peningkatan output sektor ekonomi non tradisional seperti jasa, pemerintahan, transportasi, perdagangan, pengolahan akan terpacu untuk menopang pertumbuhan ekonomi Pulau Kalimantan.",""],[2,"140","3","Gradual Relocation of the National Capital","pemindahan Ibu Kota Negara (IKN) ke Pulau Kalimantan akan dilakukan secara bertahap didukung dengan pengembangan wilayah metropolitan dan kota baru di luar Pulau Jawa.",""],[2,"140","3","Development of Metropolitan Areas and New Cities Outside Java","pemindahan Ibu Kota Negara (IKN) ke Pulau Kalimantan akan dilakukan secara bertahap didukung dengan pengembangan wilayah metropolitan dan kota baru di luar Pulau Jawa.",""],[2,"140","5","Relocation of the National Capital and Government Center","Pemindahan pusat pemerintahan dan Ibu Kota Negara ke luar Pulau Jawa.",""],[2,"274","13","Presidential Regulation on the Detailed Spatial Plan for the IKN Government Center","RPerpres tentang Rencana Detail Tata Ruang (RDTR) Pusat Pemerintahan IKN",""]],"57":[[1,"115","3","Metropolitan Area Optimization and Urban Infrastructure Development","Optimizing Metropolitan Areas (WM) and big cities outside Java, including spatial planning, urban infrastructure development, investment planning, and development financing while maintaining growth and increasing environmental carrying capacity for WM and major cities in Java;",""],[1,"130","3","Urban Area and New City Development","developing urban areas and new cities",""],[1,"133","1","Urban Area and New City Development","developing urban areas and new cities",""]],"58":[[1,"86","8","Water Security and Watershed Management Measures","Increasing water security to support economic growth, which will be carried out using the following strategies: 1) safeguarding protected forests; (2) managing sustainable forests; (3) providing water for agriculture and inland fishery; (4) providing raw water to priority areas; (5) maintaining, restoring, and conserving water resources and their respective ecosystem, including revitalizing existing lakes and green infrastructure; and (6) developing multipurpose dams.",""],[1,"86","9","Raw Water Provision for Priority Areas","To increase water security, raw water is provided to: priority areas, with a focus on frontier, outermost, and least developed areas; small outermost islands; urban areas; strategic areas (i.e. KI and KEK); national tourism strategic areas (or KSPN); the northern coast of Java; and water- stressed regions.",""],[1,"86","9","Efficient Water Use for Agricultural Productivity","The value of water productivity can be increased through an efficient use of water, especially in agriculture.",""],[1,"225","4","Watershed Restoration and Conservation Measures","Strategies to support watershed restoration and conservation include: (a) Normalizing and building capacity of river basins; (b) Conserving swamp and peat areas; and (c) Controlling pollution in reservoirs and lakes with high levels of pollution.",""],[1,"225","6","Multipurpose Reservoir Optimization and Irrigation Modernization","The policy direction in the context of optimizing multipurpose reservoirs and irrigation modernization is increasing water reservoir capacity, increasing and utilizing the functions of water reservoirs, increasing dam performance and decreasing Dam Risk Index value, increasing the efficiency and performance of irrigation systems, and",""],[1,"225","8","Multipurpose Dam Planning and Construction Programme","Strategies to increase water storage capacity include: (a) Planning multipurpose dams with sustainable protocols; (b) Planning the use of natural reservoirs; (c) Rehabilitating critical dams; and (d) Constructing multipurpose dams that involve business entities.",""],[1,"226","1","Integrated Economic Zones Based on Multipurpose Dams","These strategies are supported by the development of integrated economic zones based on multipurpose dams and the application of new dam investment schemes that involve business entities.",""],[1,"226","1","New Dam Investment Schemes Involving Business Entities","These strategies are supported by the development of integrated economic zones based on multipurpose dams and the application of new dam investment schemes that involve business entities.",""],[1,"226","2","Integrated Reservoir and Lake Utilization Programme","Strategies to improve and utilize functions of water storage are: (a) Utilizing dams for various integrated purposes such as raw water, irrigation, and flood control; (b) Developing potential reservoirs for the supply of renewable energy; (c) Revitalizing critical lakes; and (d) Utilizing the potential of lakes for raw water and other needs.",""],[1,"226","2","Reservoir Condition Recovery and Partnership Scheme","These strategies are supported by the improvement and recovery of reservoir conditions and the development of cooperation schemes with BUMN and business entities in optimizing reservoir functions.",""],[1,"226","3","High-Risk Dam Safety Improvement","Increasing the level of safety of high-risk dams;",""],[1,"226","3","Dam Catchment Area Conservation","Conserving dam catchment areas;",""],[1,"226","3","Dam Management Human Resource Capacity Building","Increasing the capacity of human resources in dam management;",""],[1,"226","3","Standards-Based Dam Operations Improvement","Improving dam operation performance that is in accordance with standards and supported by competent dam management units.",""],[1,"226","3","Dam Asset Structuring as State Property","These strategies are supported by structuring dam assets as state property.",""],[1,"226","7","Multipurpose Reservoirs and Irrigation Modernization Programme","Priority projects that support multipurpose reservoirs and irrigation modernization include: i) Planning the development of multipurpose dams and the use of natural reservoirs; ii) Dam construction and rehabilitation including the Major Project \"18 Multipurpose Reservoirs\"; iii) Optimizing and utilizing reservoirs; iv) Improving operation and maintenance (OP), and dam safety; v) Developing and rehabilitating irrigation networks; vi) Improving management of irrigation water allocation and institutional capacity.",""],[2,"51","4","National Water Security Area Preservation","Agar kelangkaan air tidak sampai menghambat pembangunan maka wilayah aman air secara nasional perlu dipertahankan seluas minimal 175,5 juta ha (93 persen dari luas wilayah Indonesia);",""],[2,"51","4","Island-Level Water Availability Maintenance","sedangkan ketersediaan air pada setiap pulau harus dipertahankan di atas 1.000 m3/kapita/tahun.",""],[2,"51","4","Java Water Security Expansion","Khusus untuk Pulau Jawa, mengingat ancaman krisis air sudah sangat mengkhawatirkan maka proporsi wilayah aman air perlu ditingkatkan secara signifikan.",""],[2,"89","8","Water Quantity and Resilience Enhancement Strategy","(ii) Peningkatan kuantitas/ketahanan air untuk mendukung pertumbuhan ekonomi yang dilaksanakan dengan strategi: (1) memantapkan kawasan hutan berfungsi lindung; (2) mengelola hutan berkelanjutan; (3) menyediakan air untuk pertanian dan perikanan darat; (4) menyediakan air baku untuk kawasan prioritas; (5) memelihara, memulihkan, dan konservasi sumber daya air dan ekosistemnya termasuk revitalisasi danau dan infrastruktur hijau; serta (6) mengembangkan waduk multiguna.",""],[2,"89","9","Water Infrastructure Support for Priority Areas","Dukungan infrastruktur dalam ketahanan air meliputi penyediaan air baku untuk kawasan prioritas yang difokuskan pada daerah tertinggal, terdepan terluar; pulau kecil terluar; perkotaan; kawasan strategis (KI, KEK, KSPN); kawasan pantai utara Pulau Jawa; dan wilayah rawan air.",""],[2,"89","9","Agricultural Water Use Efficiency Improvement","Nilai produktivitas air dapat ditingkatkan melalui efisiensi penggunaan air, terutama dalam pertanian.",""],[2,"90","3","National Priority Lake Revitalization Programme","Pemeliharaan, pemulihan dan konservasi melalui revitalisasi danau difokuskan pada 15 danau prioritas nasional, yaitu: Danau Toba, Danau Maninjau, Danau Singkarak, Danau Kerinci, Danau Rawa Danau, Danau Rawa Pening, Danau Batur, Danau Sentarum, Danau Kaskade Mahakam (Semayang-Melintang-Jeumpang), Danau Tondano, Danau Limboto, Danau Poso, Danau Tempe, Danau Matano, dan Danau Sentani.",""],[2,"135","4","Sustainable Groundwater and Raw Water Security","Peningkatan ketersediaan air melalui pengamanan air tanah dan air baku berkelanjutan;",""]],"59":[[1,"204","4","Integration of National Water Supply Targets into Regional Planning","The regional government whose main responsibility is to provide access to drinking water for the public needs to increase its commitment through the integration of the national water supply targets in regional planning, which is supported by adequate budget allocation.",""],[1,"204","4","Expansion of Local Water Service Coverage","Local governments need to prioritize the expansion of service coverage through the utilization of its current capacity of",""],[1,"204","5","Water Supply System Improvement and Construction","the improvement and construction of SPAM",""],[1,"204","5","Water Utility Asset Management and Non-Revenue Water Reduction","asset management that is expected to reduce the level of non-revenue water from 33% to 25% and ensuring the sustainability of the newly-built infrastructure.",""],[1,"213","5","Urban Drinking Water and Wastewater Supply Expansion","Efforts and hard work should be made in accelerating the development of drinking water and wastewater supply, especially in urban areas as centers of economic activity.",""],[1,"221","3","Protected Raw Water Supply Expansion","The policy direction in the management of ground water and sustainable raw water is to accelerate the supply of raw water from protected water sources, increase integration in drinking water supply, and use technology in raw water management.",""],[1,"221","4","Raw Water Supply System Acceleration","Strategies to accelerate the supply of raw water from protected water sources include: (a) Increasing the capacity of raw water from dams and other water sources that are supported by the safeguarding of water quality; (b) Rehabilitating and improving infrastructure efficiency of raw water providers; and (c) Implementing groundwater conservation that is integrated with the raw water supply system and supported by the enforcement of groundwater extraction regulations.",""],[1,"221","4","Water Treatment and Distribution System Improvement","The strategy needs to be developed simultaneously with the improvement of the performance of water treatment plants and the water distribution system.",""],[1,"221","4","Water Supply Public Awareness and Business Participation Initiative","The acceleration of raw water supply systems also needs to involve business entities.",""],[1,"221","4","Water-Saving Public Awareness Campaign","Sustainable availability of water also needs to be supported by an increase in public awareness to encourage water-saving behavior; and (d) compiling the Water Resilience Index scores.",""],[1,"221","4","Water Resilience Index Compilation","and (d) compiling the Water Resilience Index scores.",""],[1,"221","6","Water Resources Regulation Completion","Completing government regulations related to the water resources law;",""],[1,"221","6","Integrated River Basin Management Improvement","Improving the performance of river basin management by optimizing natural resource planning for water, food and energy;",""],[1,"221","6","Water Resources Management Capacity Strengthening","Strengthening the management of water resources and increasing the capacity of state-, regionally-, and privately-owned enterprises and government-to-business entities for raw water/drinking water;",""],[1,"221","6","Water Resilience Index Compilation","Compiling the Water Resilience Index scores.",""],[1,"221","7","Water Resources Information Systems Development","Strategies for the use of technology in water resources management include: (a) Developing water resources information systems; and (b) Developing hydrological, hydrometeorological, and hydrogeological information systems.",""],[1,"221","8","Piped Drinking Water Access Major Project","Providing and securing raw water and ground water as the Major Project to provide access to piped drinking water (10 million house connections);",""],[1,"221","8","Natural Resource Regulation and Institutional Strengthening","Structuring regulations and strengthening natural resource institutions;",""],[1,"221","8","Integrated Water Resources Information System","Developing an integrated water resources information system (SISDA) based on smart technology (smart water management).",""],[1,"222","2","Institutional Governance Improvement for Safe Drinking Water Provision","Improving institutional governance for the provision of safe and proper drinking water, through: (a) Integrating policy directions and development targets for access to safe and proper drinking water in regional planning; (b) Improving commitment through adequate state budget allocation; (c) Strengthening the roles of provincial and district/city governments through tiered control and guidance mechanisms; (d) Enhancing the quality of planning for an integrated water supply (Jakstrada, RISPAM, RPP Drinking Water, and PDAM Business Plan) supported by data and information systems (e) Strengthening the institutional function of drinking water regulators; and (f) Optimizing funding and developing alternative funding including through performance-based grants and cooperation between the business-to- government entities (PPP).",""],[1,"222","3","Drinking Water Provider Capacity Strengthening","Increasing the capacity of drinking water providers, through: (a) Improving PDAM performance through technical and non-technical assistance to improve service quality, which includes reducing water loss, better production efficiency, better financial and human resource management, and applying adequate tariffs; and (b) Empowering and building capacity of other SPAM providers (UPTD, BUMDes, KPSPAM, etc.).",""],[1,"222","4","SPAM Development and Management Programme","Developing and managing SPAM, through: (a) Optimizing the SPAM capacity that can be utilized through expanding service coverage; (b) Improving and developing SPAM; (c) Asset management (network inventory, operations, maintenance, and repairs); (d) Providing access to drinking water for water-stressed areas and islands; and (e) Providing access to non-piped drinking water that is well managed independently, by the community, or by the government and regional government in specially assigned areas; (f) Developing drinking water treatment and safety technology.",""],[1,"222","5","Community Water-Saving and Safe Drinking Water Awareness","Awareness of the community to adopt water-saving behavior, to access piped drinking water services or use non-piped drinking water sources that are independently managed, and to implement safe drinking water management in the household;",""],[1,"223","6","Safe Drinking Water and Sanitation System Development","Priority projects that support the provision of access to safe and proper drinking water and sanitation include: i) Developing a safe and proper drinking water supply and sanitation system;",""],[1,"223","6","Safe Drinking Water and Sanitation Operations Support","ii) Fostering safe and proper drinking water and sanitation operations;",""],[1,"223","6","Water and Sanitation Administration Regulation","iii) Regulating safe and proper water and sanitation administration;",""],[1,"223","6","Drinking Water and Sanitation Quality Monitoring","iv) Monitoring the quality of drinking water and sanitation;",""],[1,"223","6","Piped Water Access Expansion Project","vi) Piped water access (10 million house connections) (Major Project).",""],[1,"231","6","Urban Drinking Water and Sanitation System Development","Developing a drinking water supply system (SPAM) and sanitation in urban areas, by: (a) strengthening the functions of operators and regulators; (b) preparing urban sludge services (fecal sludge management); (c) providing integrated services for drinking water, wastewater and solid waste; (d) developing areas with portable water services/prime drinking water zones (ZAMP); and (e) increasing the reliability of drinking water network management through Smart Grid Water Management.",""],[1,"231","8","Reliable and Integrated Urban Water Supply and Sanitation Project","The priority project that supports the provision of access to safe and proper drinking water and sanitation in urban areas is the \"Supplying and Implementing Reliable and Integrated Water Supply and Sanitation\".",""],[2,"193","5","Local Drinking Water Service Expansion and SPAM Development","Pemerintah Daerah perlu memprioritaskan perluasan cakupan layanan melalui pemanfaatan kapasitas yang telah terbangun sebesar 57.000 liter/detik, peningkatan dan pembangunan SPAM serta pengelolaan aset yang diharapkan dapat menurunkan tingkat non revenue water dari 33 persen menjadi 25 persen serta menjamin keberlanjutan dari infrastruktur yang telah terbangun.",""],[2,"193","5","Integration of National Drinking Water Targets into Local Planning and Budgeting","Pemerintah Daerah sebagai penanggung jawab utama dalam penyediaan akses air minum untuk masyarakat perlu meningkatkan komitmennya melalui pengintegrasian target dan sasaran penyediaan air minum nasional dalam dokumen perencanaan daerah dan didukung dengan alokasi APBD yang memadai.",""],[2,"195","4","Smart Water Technology Development","Perlu adanya pengembangan teknologi cerdas yang tepat guna seperti pengembangan SIH3 (sistem informasi hidrologi, hidrometeorologi, dan hidrogeologi), sistem informasi sumber daya air, dan teknologi integrasi pemanfaatan aneka sumber air.",""],[2,"195","4","Integrated Water Resources Governance Strengthening","Penguatan kelembagaan dan regulasi pengelolaan sumber daya air secara terpadu juga masih harus dikembangkan untuk menjawab tantangan dan kebutuhan penyediaan air baku yang terus berkembang, termasuk pengembangan skema kerjasama pembiayaan pemerintah dan swasta.",""],[2,"202","5","Urban Drinking Water and Wastewater Infrastructure Acceleration","Perlu upaya dan kerja lebih keras dalam percepatan pembangunan penyediaan air minum dan air limbah khususnya di perkotaan sebagai salah satu pusat kegiatan ekonomi.",""],[2,"210","3","Protected Raw Water Supply Expansion","percepatan penyediaan air baku dari sumber air terlindungi",""],[2,"210","3","Integrated Drinking Water Provision","peningkatan keterpaduan dalam penyediaan air minum",""],[2,"210","3","Raw Water Management Technology Adoption","pemanfaatan teknologi dalam pengelolaan air baku",""],[2,"210","4","Raw Water Supply Acceleration Strategy","Strategi untuk percepatan penyediaan air baku dari sumber air terlindungi antara lain: (a) Penambahan kapasitas air baku dari bendungan dan sumber air lainnya didukung oleh pengamanan kualitas air; (b) Rehabilitasi dan peningkatan efisiensi infrastruktur penyedia air baku; dan (c) Pelaksanaan konservasi air tanah yang terintegrasi dengan sistem penyediaan air baku serta didukung oleh penegakan peraturan pengambilan air tanah.",""],[2,"210","4","Integrated Groundwater Conservation and Enforcement","Pelaksanaan konservasi air tanah yang terintegrasi dengan sistem penyediaan air baku serta didukung oleh penegakan peraturan pengambilan air tanah.",""],[2,"210","4","Water Supply Utility Performance Improvement","Strategi tersebut perlu dikembangkan secara bersamaan dengan peningkatan kinerja Instalasi Pengolahan Air (IPA) dan sistem distribusi air bersih.",""],[2,"210","4","Private Sector Participation in Raw Water Supply","Percepatan sistem penyediaan air baku juga perlu melibatkan badan usaha.",""],[2,"210","4","Water Conservation Awareness Campaign","Ketersediaan air secara berkelanjutan juga perlu didukung oleh peningkatan kesadaran masyarakat terhadap perilaku hemat air; dan (d) Penyusunan Indeks Ketahanan Air.",""],[2,"210","4","Water Resilience Index Development","(d) Penyusunan Indeks Ketahanan Air.",""],[2,"210","9","Institutional Governance Strengthening for Safe Drinking Water Provision","Peningkatan tata kelola kelembagaan untuk penyediaan air minum layak maupun aman, melalui: (a) Integrasi arah kebijakan dan sasaran pembangunan akses air minum layak maupun aman dalam dokumen perencanaan daerah; (b) Peningkatan komitmen melalui alokasi APBD yang memadai; (c) Perkuatan peran dan Pemerintah Provinsi dan Kabupaten/Kota melalui mekanisme pengendalian dan pembinaan secara berjenjang; (d) Peningkatan kualitas perencanaan penyediaan akses air minum yang terintegrasi",""],[2,"211","2","Drinking Water Institutional Strengthening and Financing Optimization","Perkuatan fungsi kelembagaan regulator air minum; serta (f) Optimalisasi pendanaan dan pengembangan alternatif pendanaan diantaranya melalui hibah berbasis kinerja serta kejasama pemerintah dan badan usaha (KPBU).",""],[2,"211","3","Drinking Water Provider Capacity Building","Peningkatan kapasitas penyelenggara air minum, melalui: (a) Peningkatan kinerja PDAM melalui pendampingan teknis dan non teknis untuk meningkatkan mutu layanan antara lain penurunan tingkat kehilangan air, efisiensi produksi, pengelolaan keuangan dan SDM, penerapan tarif yang memadai, serta peningkatan kualitas pelayanan; serta (b) Pemberdayaan dan peningkatan kapasitas penyelenggara SPAM lainnya (UPTD, BUMDes, KPSPAM, dll).",""],[2,"211","5","Drinking Water Supply System Expansion and Improvement","(a) Optimalisasi dan pemanfaatan kapasitas SPAM yang dapat dimanfaatkan melalui perluasan cakupan layanan; (b) Peningkatan dan pembangunan SPAM;",""],[2,"211","5","Water Supply Asset Management","(c) Pengelolaan aset (inventarisasi jaringan, operasi, pemeliharaan, dan perbaikan);",""],[2,"211","5","Safe Drinking Water Access for Water-Scarce and Island Areas","(d) Penyediaan akses air minum untuk daerah rawan air dan kepulauan; dan (e) Penyediaan akses air minum bukan jaringan perpipaan terlindungi baik secara swadaya oleh masyarakat maupun oleh pemerintah dan pemerintah daerah di lokasi khusus;",""],[2,"211","5","Drinking Water Treatment and Protection Technology Development","(f) Pengembangan teknologi pengolahan dan pengamanan air minum.",""],[2,"211","6","Community Water Conservation and Safe Drinking Water Management Awareness","Penyadaran masyarakat untuk menerapkan perilaku hemat air, mengakses layanan air minum perpipaan atau menggunakan sumber air minum bukan jaringan perpipaan terlindungi secara swadaya, serta menerapkan pengelolaan air minum aman dalam rumah tangga;",""],[2,"212","5","Safe Drinking Water and Sanitation Service Delivery Program","Proyek prioritas mendukung penyediaan akses air minum dan sanitasi yang layak dan aman meliputi: i) Pengembangan Penyelenggaraan Sistem Penyediaan Air Minum dan Sanitasi Layak dan Aman; ii) Pembinaan Penyelenggaraan Air Minum dan Sanitasi Layak dan Aman; iii) Pengaturan Penyelenggaraan Air Minum dan Sanitasi Layak dan Aman; iv) Pengawasan Kualitas Air Minum dan Sanitasi; v) Akses Sanitasi (Air Limbah) Layak dan Aman (90 persen RT) (Major Project); vi) Akses Air Minum Perpipaan (10 Juta Sambungan Rumah) (Major Project).",""]],"60":[[1,"206","4","Intelligent Water Resources Technology Development","It is necessary to develop appropriate intelligent technologies such as to developed SIH3 (hydrological, hydrometeorological and hydrogeological information systems), water resources information systems, and integrated technologies for the utilization of various water sources.",""],[1,"206","4","Water Resource Management Institutional Strengthening and Regulation","Institutional strengthening and integrated regulation of water resource management must be developed to respond to the growing challenges and needs for raw water supply, including developing public and private financing collaboration schemes.",""],[1,"218","16","Construction of New Irrigation Networks","Construction of new (cumulative) irrigation networks",""],[1,"218","20","Construction of Multipurpose Dams","Construction of multipurpose dams (unit)",""],[2,"207","22","Multipurpose Dam Construction","Pembangunan bendungan multiguna (unit)",""],[2,"210","5","Integrated Water Resources Management Policy Reform","Strategi untuk peningkatan kebijakan pengelolaan sumber daya air terpadu antara lain: (a) Penyelesaian peraturan pemerintah terkait UU Sumber Daya Air;",""],[2,"210","5","River Basin Management Performance Improvement","Peningkatan kinerja pengelolaan wilayah sungai melalui optimalisasi pola rencana SDA dalam jejaring air, pangan, dan energi;",""],[2,"210","5","Water Resources Capacity Building for State and Regional Enterprises","Perkuatan pengelolaan sumber daya air dan peningkatan kapasitas BUMN/D/S dan KPBU air baku/air minum;",""],[2,"210","5","Water Resilience Index Development","Penyusunan Indeks Ketahanan Air.",""],[2,"210","6","Water Resources Information System Development","Strategi untuk pemanfaatan teknologi dalam pengelolaan sumber daya air antara lain: (a) Pengembangan sistem informasi sumber daya air; dan (b) Pengembangan sistem informasi hidrologi, hidrometeorologi, dan hidrogeologi.",""],[2,"210","6","Hydrological and Hydrogeological Information System Development","Strategi untuk pemanfaatan teknologi dalam pengelolaan sumber daya air antara lain: (a) Pengembangan sistem informasi sumber daya air; dan (b) Pengembangan sistem informasi hidrologi, hidrometeorologi, dan hidrogeologi.",""],[2,"210","7","Sustainable Groundwater and Raw Water Management Priority Projects","Proyek prioritas mendukung Pengelolaan Air Tanah dan Air Baku Berkelanjutan meliputi: i) Penyediaan dan pengamanan air baku dan air tanah termasuk Major Project Akses Air Minum Berpiped (10 Juta Sambungan Rumah); ii) Penataan regulasi serta perkuatan kelembagaan SDA; dan iii) Pengembangan SISDA Terpadu berbasis teknologi cerdas (smart water management).",""],[2,"214","2","Multi-purpose Reservoir Optimization and Irrigation Modernization","Arah kebijakan dalam rangka optimalisasi waduk multiguna dan modernisasi irigasi adalah penambahan kapasitas tampungan air, peningkatan dan pemanfaatan fungsi tampungan air, peningkatan kinerja bendungan dan penurunan indeks risiko bendungan, peningkatan efisiensi dan kinerja sistem irigasi, dan penyediaan air untuk komoditas pertanian bernilai tinggi.",""],[2,"214","3","Multipurpose Dam Capacity Expansion Strategy","Strategi untuk penambahan kapasitas tampungan air antara lain: (a) Perencanaan bendungan multiguna dengan protokol berkelanjutan; (b) Perencanaan pemanfaatan tampungan alami; (c) Rehabilitasi bendungan kritis; dan (d) Pembangunan bendungan multiguna dengan melibatkan badan usaha.",""],[2,"214","4","Integrated Reservoir and Dam Utilization Strategy","Strategi untuk peningkatan dan pemanfaatan fungsi tampungan air adalah: (a) Pemanfaatan bendungan untuk berbagai keperluan secara terpadu seperti air baku, irigasi, dan pengendali banjir; (b) Pengembangan potensi waduk untuk penyediaan energi terbarukan; (c) Revitalisasi danau kritis; dan (d) Pemanfaatan potensi danau untuk air baku, dan kebutuhan lainnya.",""],[2,"214","5","High-Risk Dam Safety Improvement","Peningkatan tingkat keamanan bendungan dengan risiko tinggi",""],[2,"214","5","Dam Catchment Area Conservation","Konservasi daerah tangkapan air bendungan",""],[2,"214","5","Dam Management Human Resource Capacity Building","Peningkatan kapasitas SDM bidang pengelolaan bendungan",""],[2,"214","5","Standards-Based Dam Operations Improvement","Peningkatan kinerja operasi bendungan yang sesuai standar dan didukung oleh unit pengelola bendungan yang kompeten",""],[2,"214","5","Dam Asset Management Reform","Strategi tersebut didukung oleh penataan aset bendungan sebagai barang milik negara",""],[2,"214","6","Irrigation Modernization and Efficiency Improvement Program","Strategi untuk peningkatan efisiensi dan kinerja sistem irigasi dengan penerapan konsep modernisasi irigasi antara lain: (a) Pembangunan jaringan irigasi baru; (b) Rehabilitasi jaringan irigasi; (c) Peningkatan kapasitas kelembagaan irigasi; (d) Peningkatan efektivitas alokasi air irigasi; dan (e) Pemanfaatan lahan sub-optimal melalui revitalisasi rawa.",""],[2,"214","7","Water Storage and Irrigation Development for High-Value Agricultural Commodities","Strategi untuk penyediaan air untuk komoditas pertanian bernilai tinggi antara lain: (a) Pembangunan tampungan air dan sistem irigasi untuk komoditas perkebunan, peternakan, hortikultura dan perikanan; (b) Pembangunan jaringan irigasi untuk tambak rakyat; dan (c) Pengembangan mikro irigasi terutama untuk lahan belum termanfaatkan dengan optimal.",""],[2,"214","7","Decentralized and Partnership-Based Irrigation Management","Strategi tersebut didukung oleh peningkatan peran pemerintah daerah, partisipasi masyarakat, dan kemitraan dengan badan usaha dalam pengelolaan irigasi.",""],[2,"214","8","Multipurpose Reservoir Development and Irrigation Modernization","Proyek prioritas mendukung waduk multiguna dan modernisasi irigasi meliputi: i) Perencanaan pengembangan bendungan multiguna dan pemanfaatan tampungan alami; ii) Pembangunan dan rehabilitasi bendungan termasuk komponen Major Project \"18 Waduk Multiguna\"; iii) Optimalisasi dan pemanfaatan tampungan; iv) Peningkatan OP dan keamanan bendungan; v) Pembangunan dan Rehabilitasi Jaringan Irigasi; vi) Peningkatan pengelolaan alokasi air dan kapasitas kelembagaan irigasi.",""]],"61":[[1,"222","6","Accelerated Sanitation Development in Human Settlements Program","The sustainable sanitation service system is realized through the Accelerated Sanitation Development in Human Settlements Program (PPSP), which is broken down into five policy directions and strategies, namely:",""],[1,"222","7","Sanitation Management Capacity Strengthening","Increasing institutional capacity in sanitation management services, through: (a) Developing wastewater management systems, sludge services, and waste management systems; (b) Confirming the role of regulators for domestic and wastewater management services; and (c) Strengthening the role and capacity of PDAMs as providers of",""],[1,"223","2","Regional Sustainable Sanitation Regulation and Financing Measures","Increasing the commitment of regional leaders to sustainable sanitation services, through: (a) Formulating regulations in regions regarding the management of domestic wastewater and waste; (b) Providing incentive mechanisms for local governments to allocate budget for sanitation infrastructure development and/or provide subsidies for operations and maintenance; and (c) Implementing regional regulations that govern payment obligations for sanitation services from consumers, and requiring households to become customers of sludge and waste management services.",""],[1,"223","3","Regional Sanitation Infrastructure and Housing Services Development","Developing infrastructure and housing sanitation services in accordance with the characteristics and needs of the region, through: (a) Technical guidance for sanitation infrastructure development; (b) Coordinating spatial planning with sanitation development; (c) Developing the concept of resource recovery and circular economy; (d) Developing guidelines at the central level regarding waste management; (e) Developing human resources and technology through collaboration with universities; (f) Developing sanitation infrastructure; (g) Developing technology using the incremental approach; and (h) Information technology-based data management, monitoring and evaluation, namely NAWASIS (National Water and Sanitation Information Services).",""],[1,"223","4","Village and Sub-district Sanitation Behavior Change Programs","Implementing behavior change programs in each village and sub-district where open defecation (BABS) is still practiced;",""],[1,"223","4","Scheduled Sanitation Monitoring Mechanism","Strengthening scheduled monitoring mechanisms;",""],[1,"223","4","Community-Based Total Sanitation Sustainability Support","Strengthening the sustainability of community-based total sanitation (STBM) at the regency/city level;",""],[1,"223","5","Community Capacity Subsidy Support","Providing appropriate subsidies to enhance community capacity",""],[1,"223","5","Innovative Sanitation Financing System","Developing sanitation services through an innovative financing system",""],[1,"223","5","Local Government Sanitation Collaboration","Facilitating local governments to collaborate with other entities",""],[1,"223","5","Sanitation Entrepreneurship Development","Creating sanitation entrepreneurship in areas that have potential",""],[1,"223","5","Sanitation Standards Compliance Support","Facilitating sanitation entrepreneurs to be able to create products that comply with standards",""],[1,"223","6","Sanitation Access Expansion Project","v) Safe and proper access to sanitation (wastewater) (90% of neighborhoods) (Major Project);",""],[1,"231","7","Behavior Change Programs for Safe Sanitation Access","Encouraging behavior change of the people to achieve safe access to sanitation, through (a) implementing behavior change programs in each sub-district where open defecation (BABS) is still practiced; (b) strengthening scheduled monitoring mechanisms; (c) strengthening the sustainability of community-based total sanitation (STBM) at the regency/city level.",""],[2,"211","7","Settlement Sanitation Acceleration Program","Sistem layanan sanitasi berkelanjutan diwujudkan melalui Program Percepatan Pembangunan Sanitasi Permukiman (PPSP), yang diterjemahkan menjadi lima arah kebijakan dan strateginya, yaitu:",""],[2,"211","8","Sanitation Management Institutional Capacity Strengthening","Peningkatan kapasitas institusi dalam layanan pengelolaan sanitasi, melalui: (a) Pengembangan sistem pengelolaan air limbah, layanan lumpur tinja dan sistem pengelolaan sampah; (b) Pemastian fungsi regulator layanan pengelolaan air limbah domestik dan sampah; dan (c) Penguatan peran dan kapasitas PDAM sebagai penyedia jasa layanan pengelolaan air limbah domestik, terutama bagi daerah dengan cakupan air perpipaan lebih dari 50 persen.",""],[2,"211","9","Local Sanitation Regulation and Financing Incentive Framework","Peningkatan komitmen kepala daerah untuk layanan sanitasi yang berkelanjutan, melalui: (a) Penyusunan regulasi di daerah mengenai pengelolaan air limbah domestik dan sampah; (b) Penyediaan mekanisme insentif bagi pemerintah daerah untuk mengalokasikan anggaran pembangunan infrastruktur sanitasi dan/atau penyediaan subsidi bagi operasional dan pemeliharaan; dan (c) Penerapan regulasi daerah yang mengatur kewajiban pembayaran layanan sanitasi oleh masyarakat/ konsumen dan mewajibkan rumah tangga untuk menjadi pelanggan layanan pengelolaan lumpur tinja dan dan sampah.",""],[2,"211","10","Settlement Sanitation Infrastructure and Services Development","Pengembangan infrastruktur dan layanan sanitasi permukiman sesuai dengan karakteristik dan kebutuhan daerah, melalui: (a) Bimbingan teknis pembangunan infrastruktur sanitasi; (b) Koordinasi perencanaan tata ruang dengan pembangunan sanitasi; (c) Pengembangan konsep resource recovery dan circular economy; (d) Penyusunan panduan di tingkat pusat mengenai pengelolaan sampah; (e) Pengembangan SDM dan teknologi melalui kerja sama dengan universitas; (f) Pembangunan infrastruktur sanitasi; (g) Pengembangan teknologi menggunakan pendekatan bertahap (incremental approach); dan (h) Pengelolaan data, pemantauan dan evaluasi berbasis teknologi informasi, yaitu",""],[2,"212","3","Community-Led Sanitation Behavior Change Program","Pelaksanaan program perubahan perilaku di tiap desa dan kelurahan yang belum Stop Buang Air Besar Sembarangan (BABS);",""],[2,"212","3","Scheduled Sanitation Monitoring Mechanism","Penguatan mekanisme pemantauan yang terjadwal;",""],[2,"212","3","Sustainable Community-Based Total Sanitation Strengthening","Penguatan keberlanjutan Sanitasi Total Berbasis Masyarakat (STBM) di tingkat kabupaten dan kota;",""],[2,"212","4","Sanitation Financing and Partnership Development","Pengembangan kerja sama dan pola pendanaan, melalui: (a) Penyediaan pola subsidi yang tepat untuk meningkatkan kemampuan masyarakat; (b) Pengembangan layanan sanitasi melalui sistem pembiayaan yang inovatif; (c) Fasilitasi pemerintah daerah untuk melakukan kerja sama dengan pihak lain; (d) Menciptakan wirausaha sanitasi di daerah yang memiliki potensi; dan (e) Fasilitasi wirausaha sanitasi agar mampu menciptakan produk yang sesuai dengan standar.",""],[2,"219","3","Urban Drinking Water and Sanitation System Development","Pembangunan Sistem Penyediaan Air Minum (SPAM) dan Sanitasi di Perkotaan, melalui (a) penguatan fungsi operator dan regulator; (b) penyiapan layanan lumpur tinja perkotaan (Fecal Sludge Management); (c) penyediaan layanan terintegrasi air minum, air limbah dan persampahan; (d) pengembangan kawasan dengan layanan air siap minum (portable water) / Zona Air Minum Prima (ZAMP); dan (e) peningkatan keandalan pengelolaan jaringan air minum melalui Smart Grid Water Management.",""],[2,"219","4","Community Sanitation Behavior Change Program","Peningkatan perubahan perilaku masyarakat dalam mencapai akses aman sanitasi, melalui (a) pelaksanaan program perubahan perilaku di tiap kelurahan yang belum Stop Buang Air Besar Sembarangan (BABS);",""],[2,"219","4","Scheduled Sanitation Monitoring Mechanism","penguatan mekanisme pemantauan yang terjadwal;",""],[2,"219","4","Sustainable Community-Led Total Sanitation Strengthening","penguatan keberlanjutan Sanitasi Total Berbasis Masyarakat (STBM) di tingkat kabupaten dan kota.",""],[2,"219","5","Reliable and Integrated Drinking Water and Sanitation Provision and Management","Proyek prioritas mendukung penyediaan akses air minum dan sanitasi yang layak dan aman di perkotaan adalah Penyediaan dan Penyelenggaraan Air Minum dan Sanitasi yang Andal dan Terintegrasi",""]],"62":[[1,"88","4","Sustainable Fisheries Management and WPP Governance Reform","using fishery management areas (WPP) as a basis for sustainable fishery; transforming the institutional and functional framework of WPP; improving governance of WPP; and structuring coastal and sea spatial plans",""],[1,"88","4","Marine Ecosystem Management and Sustainable Resource Use","managing marine ecosystems and using marine resources in a sustainable manner",""],[1,"88","5","Maritime and Fisheries Governance Strengthening","efforts to strengthen the implementation and governance of maritime activities will continue",""],[1,"88","6","Fish Stock Data and Marine Spatial Planning Framework","The first strategy is to strengthen data for fish stocks and develop the institutional framework of WPP, manage fishery activities in public waters, finalize ocean zoning plans, and control the use of ocean space and small islands by considering marine spatial planning (or RZWP3K) and provincial spatial planning (RTRW).",""],[1,"88","7","Sustainable Marine Conservation Area Management","The second strategy is to strengthen the management of marine conservation areas in a sustainable manner and increase the use of marine bioproducts and biotechnology.",""],[2,"91","2","Sustainable Fisheries Area Management and Marine Spatial Planning","(iv) Peningkatan pengelolaan kemaritiman, perikanan dan kelautan yang meliputi strategi: (1) menjadikan Wilayah Pengelolaan Perikanan (WPP) sebagai basis spasial dalam pembangunan perikanan berkelanjutan (sustainable fisheries), transformasi kelembagaan dan fungsi WPP, meningkatkan kualitas pengelolaan WPP, serta pengelolaan dan penataan ruang laut dan rencana zonasi pesisir;",""],[2,"91","2","Sustainable Marine Ecosystem and Marine Services Management","(2) mengelola ekosistem kelautan dan pemanfaatan jasa kelautan secara berkelanjutan;",""],[2,"91","2","Marine Governance and SDG 14 Implementation Strengthening","Di samping itu, terus dilanjutkan upaya penguatan tata kelola dan implementasi kegiatan kemaritiman, serta memperkuat komitmen pelaksanaan target SDG 14 Ekosistem Lautan (Life Below Water).",""],[2,"91","3","Fisheries Resource Data and WPP Institutional Strengthening","Strategi pertama mencakup penguatan data stok sumber daya ikan dan pengembangan kelembagaan WPP, pengelolaan perikanan di Perairan Umum Daratan (PUD), penyelesaian rencana zonasi laut, serta pengendalian pemanfaatan ruang laut dan pulau-pulau kecil, termasuk penyelarasan RZWP3K dan RTRW Provinsi.",""],[2,"91","3","Sustainable Marine Conservation Area Management","Strategi kedua dilaksanakan melalui penguatan manajemen dan pemanfaatan kawasan konservasi perairan secara berkelanjutan, dan peningkatan pemanfaatan marine bioproduct dan bioteknologi.",""]],"63":[[2,"90","4","Food Availability, Access, and Consumption Quality Improvement","(iii) Peningkatan ketersediaan, akses dan kualitas konsumsi pangan yang dilaksanakan dengan strategi: (1) meningkatkan kualitas konsumsi, keamanan, fortifikasi dan biofortifikasi pangan; (2) meningkatkan ketersediaan pangan hasil pertanian, perikanan dan pangan hasil laut terutama melalui peningkatan produktivitas dan teknik produksi secara berkelanjutan untuk menjaga stabilitas pasokan dan harga kebutuhan pokok; (3) meningkatkan produktivitas, kesejahteraan sumber daya manusia (SDM) pertanian, perikanan serta kepastian pasar; (4) menjaga keberlanjutan produktivitas sumber daya pertanian yang adaptif terhadap perubahan iklim, sistem pertanian presisi, pengelolaan lahan dan air irigasi; serta (5) meningkatkan tata kelola sistem pangan nasional.",""],[2,"90","5","Biofortified Seed, Food Fortification, and Local Food Diversification","Pelaksanaan dari strategi pertama mencakup pengembangan benih padi biofortifikasi dan produk rekayasa genetik, fortifikasi beras, pengembangan nanoteknologi pangan, pengembangan pangan lokal, dan diversifikasi bahan pangan di tingkat masyarakat, serta penyediaan dan perbaikan kualitas pangan anak sekolah.",""],[2,"90","5","Strategic Food Crop Production Support and Input Provision","Fasilitasi budidaya padi, jagung, ternak, ikan dan komoditas pangan strategis, serta penyediaan input produksi diantaranya sistem perbenihan nasional, pupuk bersubsidi yang tepat sasaran, pupuk organik asal rumput laut, serta pengembangan koridor pangan dan pertanian berbasis korporasi petani di Kalimantan Selatan sebagai provinsi penyangga pangan dan pertanian Ibu Kota Negara baru menjadi fokus pelaksanaan dari strategi kedua.",""],[2,"90","5","Farmer and Fisher Data, Insurance, and Inclusive Finance Programme","Strategi ketiga mencakup penguatan basis data petani dan nelayan, pembentukan korporasi petani dan nelayan, asuransi pertanian, asuransi nelayan, dan asuransi usaha budidaya ikan, pembiayaan inklusif, pelatihan dan penyuluhan.",""],[2,"90","5","Agricultural Land Management and Production Infrastructure Development","Strategi keempat mencakup pengelolaan lahan, termasuk lahan suboptimal, lowland, upland, dan lahan kering, efisiensi air, jalan produksi sepanjang 9.500 km, jalan usaha tani sepanjang 3.500 km, pengembangan kawasan budidaya perikanan didukung sistem pengairannya, pertanian digital dan penggunaan teknologi pesawat nirawak.",""],[2,"90","5","National Food Logistics, Data Integration, and Food Waste Management System","Strategi kelima mencakup penguatan sistem logistik pangan nasional, integrasi sistem data produksi pangan nasional dan data ekspor impor produk pangan strategis termasuk ikan, platform pangan dan pertanian berbasis data driven, pengembangan resi gudang, pengelolaan sistem pangan berkelanjutan dan sistem pangan perkotaan (urban food) serta pengelolaan limbah pangan (food waste).",""]],"64":[[1,"55","15","Farming and Fishing Cooperative Establishment","Increasing ease of doing business and establish 350 farming and fishing cooperatives",""],[1,"87","6","Farmer and Fisher Cooperative Development and Support Package","The third strategy is to consolidate a database of farmers and fishermen; form cooperatives for farmers and fishermen; provide agricultural insurance, fishery insurance, and aquaculture insurance; and provide inclusive financing, training, and counseling.",""],[2,"173","2","Business Capacity Building and Strategic Partnership Scheme for Poor and Vulnerable Groups","penguatan kapasitas usaha kelompok miskin dan rentan dengan skema pembinaan usaha serta menghubungkan dengan mitra usaha strategis",""],[2,"173","2","Socially Impactful Productive Economy Financing Scheme","pengembangan skema pendanaan program ekonomi produktif yang berdampak sosial",""],[2,"173","2","Integrated Village Economic Transformation Program","transformasi ekonomi kampung terpadu (TEKAD)",""],[2,"173","2","Corporate Social Responsibility Forum Strengthening","penguatan forum tanggung jawab sosial perusahaan",""],[2,"173","2","Environmental and Forestry Community Outreach and Mentoring","penyuluhan dan/ atau pendampingan bagi kelompok masyarakat lingkungan hidup dan kehutanan",""],[2,"173","3","Agrarian Reform Programme","6.3) Reforma agraria, mencakup: (a) penyediaan sumber Tanah Obyek Reforma Agraria (TORA), termasuk melalui pelepasan kawasan hutan; (b) pelaksanaan redistribusi tanah, termasuk untuk pengembangan kawasan transmigrasi; (c) pemberian sertipikat tanah (legalisasi), termasuk untuk kawasan transmigrasi yang penempatan sebelum tahun 1998; dan (d) pemberdayaan masyarakat penerima TORA.",""],[2,"173","4","Social Forestry Community Forest Management Scheme","Pengelolaan kawasan hutan oleh masyarakat melalui skema perhutanan sosial, mencakup: (a) pemberian akses kelola kawasan hutan oleh masyarakat dalam skema Hutan Desa (HD), Hutan Kemasyarakatan (HKm), Hutan Tanaman Rakyat (HTR), Ijin Pemanfaatan Hutan Perhutanan Sosial (IPHPS) dan kemitraan kehutanan; (b) peningkatan kapasitas (kelola kawasan, kelembagaan, dan usaha) kelompok masyarakat; (c) membangun kemitraan investasi/usaha antara investor dengan kelompok usaha perhutanan sosial; (d) pembangunan industri untuk pengolahan produk hasil kelompok perhutanan sosial sebagai upaya peningkatan nilai tambah; dan (e) pemberian fasilitasi pemasaran/promosi produk perhutanan sosial kepada kelompok usaha perhutanan sosial.",""]],"65":[[1,"67","6","Strengthen Food Supply Chain Linkages and Data Integration","there must be stronger connections between food production centers and regions with high food demand; (2) there must be adequate supply and quality of food in areas prone to starvation, stunting, and poverty; and (3) there must be integration between the production data for strategic food commodities and data for imports.",""],[1,"88","2","National Food Logistics System Strengthening","The fifth strategy is to strengthen the food logistics system at the national level; integrate data for food production with data for strategic exports and imports that include fish; develop a platform for food production and agriculture based on data-driven methods; develop a warehouse receipt system; and manage a sustainable food system, urban food system, and food waste program.",""]],"66":[[1,"91","4","Medicinal Plant Mapping and Herbal Standardization Initiative","mapping the geographical locations of medicinal plants; and standardizing herbal processes and products at the national level.",""],[1,"91","4","Sustainable Agroforestry and Jurisdictional Farming Support","Their development is supported by a sustainable jurisdictional approach, sustainable farming practices, and agroforestry.",""],[2,"93","5","Sustainable Agriculture and Agroforestry Support","Pengembangannya juga diperkuat dengan pendekatan yurisdiksi berkelanjutan, praktik budidaya pertanian berkelanjutan, dan agroforestry.",""]],"67":[[1,"87","3","Agricultural, Fishery, and Seafood Supply Expansion Strategy","(2) increasing the availability of agricultural, fishery, and seafood products, mainly by increasing productivity and sustainable production techniques to maintain the stability of supply and the price of basic goods;",""],[1,"87","3","Agricultural and Fishery Productivity and Worker Welfare Improvement","(3) increasing productivity and the welfare of workers in agriculture and fishery, and ensuring market certainty;",""],[1,"87","5","Strategic Food Commodity Cultivation Support","The second strategy is to facilitate the cultivation of rice, corn, livestock, fish, and other strategic food commodities;",""],[1,"87","5","National Seed System Input Supply","provide production inputs through, among others, the national seed system;",""],[1,"87","5","Targeted Fertilizer Subsidy Scheme","provide targeted and subsidized fertilizer;",""],[1,"87","5","Seaweed-Based Organic Fertilizer Development","provide seaweed-based organic fertilizer;",""],[1,"87","7","Integrated Land Management and Agricultural Infrastructure Development","The fourth strategy includes effective management of various lands, including substandard lands, lowlands, uplands, and dry lands; building water efficiency; management of 9,500 km of production roads and 3,500 km of farming roads; and development of aquaculture areas that are supported by a sufficient irrigation system, development of digital agriculture,",""]],"68":[[1,"88","4","Marine and Fishery Product Quality and Safety Improvement","increasing production, productivity, quality assurance, and safety of marine and fishery products",""],[1,"88","4","Marine Fisheries Business, Finance, and Technology Support","facilitating business, financing, technology, and the marketplace",""],[1,"91","4","Fishery Value-Addition and Competitiveness Enhancement Programme","Specifically for fishery manufacturing, the increase in its value-added is carried out by improving the quality, capacity, and productivity of the manufacturing process; downstreaming the seaweed industry and adding value to marine natural resources; strengthening the competitiveness of fishery processing units; implementing quality control, certification, and traceability; providing facilities and infrastructure for cold chain systems; strengthening the efficiency of fish logistics systems, expanding access to the domestic and foreign market; developing marketing for fishery on an international scale; stronger branding of Indonesian fishery products; and developing digitally-based marketing systems for fishery products.",""]],"69":[[1,"88","4","Integrated Fishermen Empowerment and Welfare Support","empowering and improving the welfare of fishermen in an integrated",""],[1,"88","5","Small-Scale Marine and Fishery Business Protection","protecting small-scale marine and fishery businesses",""],[1,"89","2","Fisheries Business Support and Investment Facilitation Package","The fourth strategy is to facilitate business growth and investment in the form of insurance for fishermen and fish cultivators, provide land certification for fishermen and fish cultivators, develop advanced fishing settlements, develop financing schemes or microfinance products that are both affordable and accessible, strengthen fishermen's organizations, regulate fishermen's access to resource management, arrange and simplify business licensing, increase investment in fishery that is supported by conducive regulations, and increase compliance from marine and fishery business actors.",""]],"70":[[1,"88","5","Maritime Human Resource Development and Innovation Support","improving the quality and competency of human resources; boosting technological innovation and research in the collective maritime, marine, and fishery sector; and strengthening the maritime and fishery database",""],[1,"89","1","Digital Fisheries Development Initiative","develop digital-based fishery",""],[1,"89","3","Training and Digital-Based Counseling for Fisheries and Maritime Development","The fifth strategy is to provide training and digital-based counseling, strengthen vocational education, strengthen maritime literacy, develop fishery entrepreneurship, develop",""],[1,"89","4","Competency Certification for Fishery Workforce","competency certification, expand the fishery workforce to include younger generation of fishermen, develop research and innovation, disseminate sustainable and productive fishery/marine technology, establish leadings centers for marine and maritime research, and strengthen the database for the maritime and fishery sector.",""],[1,"89","4","Fishery Workforce Renewal and Youth Recruitment","expand the fishery workforce to include younger generation of fishermen",""],[1,"89","4","Marine and Fishery Research, Innovation, and Data Systems","develop research and innovation, disseminate sustainable and productive fishery/marine technology, establish leadings centers for marine and maritime research, and strengthen the database for the maritime and fishery sector.",""],[2,"91","2","Marine and Fisheries Production Quality Improvement","(3) meningkatkan produksi, produktivitas, standardisasi, jaminan mutu dan keamanan produk kelautan dan perikanan;",""],[2,"91","2","Marine and Fisheries Business Support and Financing","(4) meningkatkan fasilitasi usaha, pembiayaan, teknologi dan pasar; peningkatan kesejahteraan dan pemberdayaan nelayan terpadu; perlindungan usaha kelautan dan perikanan skala kecil;",""],[2,"91","2","Marine and Fisheries Human Resource, Innovation, and Data Strengthening","(5) meningkatkan kualitas dan kompetensi SDM, inovasi teknologi dan riset kemaritiman, kelautan dan perikanan serta penguatan database kelautan dan perikanan.",""],[2,"91","3","Aquaculture Production Acceleration and Modern Cluster Development","Strategi ketiga mencakup akselerasi produksi akuakultur, pengembangan klaster perikanan budidaya modern berkelanjutan, revitalisasi tambak udang dan bandeng, ekstensifikasi lahan budidaya; pengembangan sistem pembenihan dan induk unggul; pengembangan armada perikanan tangkap yang berskala ekonomi dan berkelanjutan, eksplorasi perikanan di ZEE dan laut lepas, penguatan kerjasama usaha kecil dan besar perikanan, pengembangan pelabuhan perikanan berwawasan lingkungan (eco fishing port), pengembangan perikanan berbasis digital, ekstensifikasi dan intensifikasi lahan garam, peningkatan kualitas garam, pengembangan sentra kelautan dan perikanan, dan penguatan sistem karantina ikan.",""],[2,"91","3","Fisheries Business Facilitation and Investment Support","Strategi keempat mencakup kemudahan fasilitasi usaha dan investasi pemberian asuransi nelayan dan usaha pembudidaya ikan, sertifikasi tanah nelayan dan pembudidaya ikan, pengembangan pemukiman nelayan maju, pengembangan skema pembiayaan/bank mikro nelayan yang murah dan mudah diakses, penguatan kelembagaan nelayan, pengaturan akses nelayan terhadap pengelolaan sumber daya, penataan dan penyederhanaan perizinan usaha, dan investasi perikanan kelautan yang efisien dan didukung regulasi yang kondusif, serta peningkatan kepatuhan pelaku usaha kelautan dan perikanan.",""],[2,"91","3","Digital Fisheries Training and Maritime Skills Development","Strategi kelima mencakup pelatihan dan penyuluhan berbasis digital, penguatan pendidikan vokasi, penguatan literasi maritim, pengembangan kewirausahaan perikanan, pengembangan sertifikasi kompetensi, pengembangan angkatan kerja perikanan generasi milenial, pengembangan riset dan inovasi, diseminasi teknologi perikanan dan kelautan yang berkelanjutan dan produktif, pembentukan pusat unggulan riset kelautan dan kemaritiman, serta penguatan basis data kelautan dan perikanan.",""],[2,"91","4","Priority Fisheries Commodity Development","Komoditas unggulan perikanan ditekankan pada tuna, cakalang, tongkol (TCT), rajungan, udang, nila, lele/patin, bandeng dan rumput laut serta komoditas bernilai ekonomis tinggi untuk dikembangkan sebagai komoditas untuk mendukung target ekspor dan ketahanan pangan.",""],[2,"91","4","Domestic Salt Production Expansion","Selain itu terus ditingkatkan produksi garam untuk memenuhi kebutuhan konsumsi dalam negeri.",""],[2,"92","2","Aquaculture Commodity Development","Komoditas udang dikembangkan di Sumatera, NTB, Jawa, dan Sulawesi.",""],[2,"92","2","Tilapia Commodity Development","Komoditas nila dikembangkan di Sumatera, Jawa, dan Sulawesi.",""],[2,"92","2","Seaweed Commodity Development","Komoditas rumput laut dikembangkan di Nusa Tenggara, Sulawesi, Maluku dan Kalimantan.",""],[2,"92","2","Salt Production Center Development","Selanjutnya, sentra garam dikembangkan di Jawa, Sumatera, Sulawesi dan Nusa Tenggara.",""]],"71":[[1,"180","6","Land Object of Agrarian Reform Resource Provision","Providing resources for Land Object of Agrarian Reform (TORA), including releasing forest areas;",""],[1,"180","7","Land Redistribution for Transmigration Area Development","Implementing land redistribution, among others, for the development of transmigration areas;",""],[1,"180","8","Land Certificate Granting and Legalization for Transmigration Areas","Granting and legalizing land certificates, among others, for transmigration areas that were implemented before 1998;",""],[1,"180","10","Community Forest Management through Social Forestry Schemes","Community forest management through social forestry schemes, including:",""],[1,"180","11","Community Forestry Access Expansion","Granting access to community forest management in the Village Forest scheme, Community Forests (HKM) scheme, Community Plantation Forests (HTR) scheme, Permits for the Utilization of Social Forestry (IPHPS) scheme, and forestry partnerships;",""]],"72":[[1,"170","2","National Health Insurance Effectiveness Enhancement Measures","Increasing the effectiveness of the National Health Insurance (JKN), which is supported by equitable supply of health services (supply side) and by the improvement in the quality of health services; formulating JKN benefit packages explicitly; implementing active purchasing including improving the payment system for health service facilities and developing cost-sharing mechanisms; strengthening health technology assessment (HTA), clinical boards, quality control teams, and cost control teams; developing",""],[1,"170","3","Health Service Provider Standards Improvement","improving health service providers according to standards in all regions, especially through cooperation with the private sector;",""],[1,"170","3","JKN Health Data Integration","integrating JKN data with health information systems;",""],[1,"170","3","BPJS Health Data Use for Policy Development","utilizing BPJS Health service data for the development of policies for stakeholders;",""],[1,"171","23","Primary Health Care Strengthening for Universal Health Coverage","Improving health services towards universal health coverage, especially strengthening primary health care by encouraging promotive and preventive efforts, supported by innovation and technology utilization, through:",""],[1,"174","2","Strengthening Basic Health Services and Referral Systems","Strengthening basic health services and referrals to reinforce the function of community health centers (Puskesmas) and their networks in an effort to improve quality in public health, which is supported by increasing the capacity of health workers, facilities, infrastructure, and financing; optimizing basic health services through a family approach; revitalizing integrated health post (Posyandu) and other community- based health efforts; developing special policies for health services in remote areas and areas with certain geographical characteristics (islands) including policies related to referral systems, financing patterns, regulations, and institutions; developing elderly health services; improving the accreditation system of government and private health services; fulfillment of the equitable provision of facilities, infrastructure, and medical devices that refer to the master plan for the provision of health service facilities; innovating and utilizing technology in health services that covers the expansion of online referral systems, including the integration of private health service facilities in the referral system, expanding coverage and development of types of telemedicine services, digitizing medical records and both hard copies and online; expanding mobile health services, including those on islands; developing and improving the quality of specialized hospitals; and providing medical waste",""],[2,"165","3","JKN Effectiveness Improvement and Health Service Quality Reform","Peningkatan efektivitas JKN didukung pemerataan penyediaan pelayanan kesehatan (supply side) dan peningkatan kualitas pelayanan kesehatan, perumusan paket manfaat JKN secara eksplisit, penerapan active purchasing termasuk perbaikan sistem pembayaran fasilitas pelayanan kesehatan dan pengembangan mekanisme cost-sharing, penguatan health technology assessment (HTA), dewan pertimbangan klinis, dan tim kendali mutu dan kendali biaya, pengembangan dan penerapan pedoman nasional pelayanan kesehatan, peningkatan penyedia pelayanan kesehatan sesuai standar di seluruh wilayah terutama melalui kerjasama dengan swasta, integrasi data JKN dengan sistem informasi kesehatan dan pemanfaatan data pelayanan BPJS kesehatan untuk penyusunan kebijakan bagi para pemangku kepentingan",""],[2,"166","4","Primary Health Care Strengthening for Universal Health Coverage","Meningkatkan pelayanan kesehatan menuju cakupan kesehatan semesta terutama penguatan pelayanan kesehatan dasar (Primary Health Care) dengan mendorong peningkatan upaya promotif dan preventif, didukung inovasi dan pemanfaatan teknologi, melalui:",""],[2,"168","4","Primary Health Care and Referral System Strengthening","Penguatan pelayanan kesehatan dasar dan rujukan yang difokuskan pada penguatan fungsi puskesmas dan jaringannya dalam upaya kesehatan masyarakat yang berkualitas dan didukung peningkatan kapasitas tenaga kesehatan, sarana dan prasarana, serta pembiayaan;",""],[2,"168","4","Family-Based Primary Health Care Optimization","optimalisasi penguatan pelayanan kesehatan dasar melalui pendekatan keluarga;",""],[2,"168","4","Community Health Post Revitalization","revitalisasi posyandu dan upaya kesehatan bersumber daya masyarakat lainnya;",""],[2,"168","4","Special Health Services for Remote and Island Areas","pengembangan kebijakan khusus untuk pelayanan kesehatan di daerah terpencil, sangat terpencil dan daerah dengan karakteristik geografis tertentu (kepulauan) termasuk sistem rujukan, pola pembiayaan, regulasi dan kelembagaan;",""],[2,"168","4","Elderly Health Services Development","pengembangan pelayanan kesehatan lanjut usia;",""],[2,"168","4","Health Service Accreditation System Improvement","penyempurnaan sistem akreditasi pelayanan kesehatan pemerintah dan swasta;",""],[2,"168","4","Health Facility and Medical Equipment Provision","pemenuhan dan pemerataan penyediaan sarana, prasarana, dan alat kesehatan yang mengacu rencana induk penyediaan fasilitas pelayanan kesehatan;",""],[2,"168","4","Digital Health Service Innovation and Expansion","inovasi dan pemanfaatan teknologi dalam pelayanan kesehatan meliputi perluasan sistem rujukan online termasuk integrasi fasilitas pelayanan kesehatan swasta dalam sistem rujukan, perluasan cakupan dan pengembangan jenis layanan telemedicine, digitalisasi rekam medis dan rekam medis online;",""],[2,"168","4","Mobile and Island Health Service Expansion","perluasan pelayanan kesehatan bergerak (flying dan sailing health care) dan gugus pulau;",""],[2,"168","4","Special Hospital Development and Quality Improvement","pengembangan dan peningkatan kualitas RS khusus;",""]],"73":[[1,"172","2","Maternal and Neonatal Health Service Improvement Programme","Continuous improvement of maternal and neonatal services in public and private health service facilities by encouraging all deliveries in health facilities capable of handling comprehensive emergency services supported by guaranteed financing; improving the competency of health workers including strengthening the ability to detect early risk factors in pregnancy; increasing coverage and quality of antenatal, neonatal, childbirth, and postpartum services; improving the maternal referral system that is supported by increasing the capacity of the health system and strengthening regulations; providing infrastructure and pharmaceutical facilities, as well as guaranteeing the availability of blood at any time; and recording maternal deaths in health facilities, especially for strengthening health care management;",""],[1,"172","3","Family Planning Services Expansion and Quality Improvement","Expanding access and quality of family planning services",""],[1,"172","4","Reproductive Health and Family Planning Service Strengthening","reproductive health according to regional characteristics through optimizing the role of the private sector and government through advocacy and information, education and communication (IEC) for Population, Family Planning and Family Development (KKBPK) programs; also family planning and reproductive health counseling; improving the family planning instructors (PKB) and family planning field officers (PLKB), field line workers, and health workers competencies in family planning services; strengthening health care facilities, networks of health service facilities, community-based health efforts; and increasing postpartum family planning uptake; and",""],[1,"172","7","Community Nutrition Improvement Campaign and Monitoring","Strengthening commitment, campaign, monitoring, and evaluating efforts to improve community nutrition;",""],[1,"172","8","Child Nutrition Support System","Developing a system to ensure enough nutrition supporting child growth and development by providing nutritious foods since pregnancy, improving family parenting, and improving clean water and environmental sanitation facilities;",""],[1,"172","9","Stunting Reduction Effectiveness Enhancement","Accelerating stunting reduction by increasing the effectiveness of",""],[1,"172","11","Evidence-Based Life-Saving Interventions and Food Fortification","Improving life-saving interventions supported by evidence-based policy including food fortification;",""],[1,"172","12","Nutrition Behavior Change Advocacy and Communication","Strengthening advocacy and communication of behavioral change, especially to encourage balanced nutrition based on food consumption (food-based approach);",""],[1,"173","1","Nutritional Surveillance System Strengthening","Strengthening the nutritional surveillance system;",""],[2,"166","5","Integrated Maternal, Newborn, Family Planning, and Reproductive Health Services","3.1) Peningkatan kesehatan ibu, anak, keluarga berencana (KB) dan kesehatan reproduksi, mencakup: a) peningkatan pelayanan maternal dan neonatal berkesinambungan di fasilitas pelayanan kesehatan publik dan swasta dengan mendorong seluruh persalinan di fasilitas pelayanan kesehatan yang mampu menangani pelayanan emergensi komprehensif didukung jaminan pembiayaan; peningkatan kompetensi tenaga kesehatan termasuk penguatan kemampuan deteksi dini faktor risiko dalam kehamilan; peningkatan cakupan dan kualitas pelayanan antenatal, neonatal, persalinan, dan pascapersalinan; perbaikan sistem rujukan maternal yang didukung dengan peningkatan kapasitas sistem kesehatan dan penguatan regulasi; penyediaan sarana prasarana dan farmasi serta jaminan ketersediaan darah setiap saat; dan pencatatan kematian ibu di fasilitas pelayanan kesehatan terutama untuk penguatan tata laksana; b) perluasan dan pengembangan imunisasi dasar lengkap, termasuk vaksin untuk pneumonia; c) peningkatan gizi remaja putri dan ibu hamil; d) perluasan akses dan kualitas pelayanan KB serta kesehatan reproduksi (kespro) sesuai karakteristik wilayah yang didukung oleh optimalisasi peran sektor swasta dan pemerintah melalui advokasi, komunikasi, informasi, edukasi (KIE) Program Kependudukan, KB dan Pembangunan Keluarga (KKBPK) dan konseling KB dan Kespro; peningkatan kompetensi Penyuluh Keluarga Berencana (PKB) dan Petugas Lapangan Keluarga Berencana (PLKB), tenaga lini lapangan, dan tenaga kesehatan dalam pelayanan KB; penguatan fasilitas pelayanan kesehatan, jaringan dan jejaring fasilitas pelayanan kesehatan serta upaya",""],[2,"167","2","Community-Based Health Services Strengthening","kesehatan bersumber daya masyarakat",""],[2,"167","2","Postpartum Family Planning Expansion","peningkatan KB pasca persalinan",""],[2,"167","2","Adolescent Reproductive Health Information and Access Programme","peningkatan pengetahuan, pemahaman dan akses layanan kesehatan reproduksi remaja secara lintas sektor yang responsif gender",""]],"74":[[1,"173","6","Disease Risk Prevention and Control Measures","Preventing and controlling risk factors for disease including expanding early detection coverage, strengthening real-time surveillance, vector control, and expanding smoking cessation services;",""],[1,"173","7","Health Security Capacity Building and Alert System Strengthening","Strengthening health security, especially capacity building for prevention, detection, and rapid response to disease threats, including strengthening alert system",""],[1,"173","9","Case Finding and Treatment Coverage Expansion","Increasing the coverage of case finding and treatment, as well as strengthening the management of diseases and injuries;",""],[1,"173","13","Healthy Zones Development Initiative","Developing healthy zones, including healthy districts/cities, healthy markets, school health efforts, and healthy work environments;",""],[1,"173","14","Healthy Urban Environment and Active Mobility Support","Providing an environment that encourages physical activities such as public open spaces, mass transportation and intermodal connectivity, a healthy environment, and reduction of air pollution;",""],[1,"173","15","Health-Oriented Development Regulations and Healthy Living Standards","Regulations that encourage central and regional governments as well as the private sector to implement health-oriented development and encourage healthy living, including the development of standards and guidelines for the non-health sector; gradually increasing tobacco product excise taxes while mitigating the impact on tobacco farmers",""],[1,"173","16","Tobacco Advertising and Promotion Ban","total prohibition against cigarette advertising and promotion; formulating warning signs of the dangers of smoking on tobacco products more conspicuous, expanding excise duty on food products that have high health risk and regulating food products containing sugar, salt and fat;",""],[1,"173","17","Healthy Lifestyle and Sports Promotion Initiative","Promoting innovative healthy behavior and sports, community empowerment, and mobilizing communities to live a healthy lifestyle;",""],[1,"173","18","Healthy Food Choice Promotion Measures","Increasing the provision of healthy food choices including food labelling, expanding access to fruits and vegetables, and expanding the",""],[2,"167","4","Disease Control and Health Security Strengthening","3.3) Peningkatan pengendalian penyakit, dengan perhatian khusus pada jantung, stroke, hipertensi, diabetes, kanker, tuberkulosis, malaria, HIV/AIDS, emerging diseases, penyakit yang berpotensi menimbulkan kejadian luar biasa, penyakit tropis terabaikan (kusta, filariasis, schistosomiasis), gangguan jiwa, cedera, gangguan penglihatan, dan penyakit gigi dan mulut, mencakup: a) pencegahan dan pengendalian faktor risiko penyakit termasuk perluasan cakupan deteksi dini, penguatan surveilans real time, pengendalian vektor dan perluasan layanan berhenti merokok; b) penguatan health security terutama peningkatan kapasitas untuk pencegahan, deteksi, dan respon cepat terhadap ancaman penyakit termasuk penguatan alert system kejadian luar biasa dan karantina kesehatan; c) peningkatan cakupan penemuan kasus dan pengobatan serta penguatan tata laksana penanganan penyakit dan cedera; d) pengendalian resistensi antimikroba; e) pemberdayaan masyarakat dalam pengendalian penyakit dan penguatan sanitasi total berbasis masyarakat.",""],[2,"167","5","Healthy Living Movement","Pembudayaan perilaku hidup sehat melalui Gerakan Masyarakat Hidup Sehat, mencakup: a) pengembangan kawasan sehat antara lain kabupaten/kota sehat, pasar sehat, upaya kesehatan sekolah (UKS) dan lingkungan kerja sehat; b) penyediaan lingkungan yang mendorong aktivitas fisik seperti penyediaan ruang terbuka publik, transportasi masal dan konektivitas antarmoda, lingkungan sehat, dan penurunan polusi udara; c) regulasi yang mendorong pemerintah pusat dan daerah serta swasta untuk menerapkan pembangunan berwawasan kesehatan dan mendorong hidup",""],[2,"168","2","Tobacco Tax Increase and Advertising Ban","peningkatan cukai hasil tembakau secara bertahap dengan mitigasi dampak bagi petani tembakau dan pekerja industri hasil tembakau, pelarangan total iklan dan promosi rokok, perbesaran pencantuman peringatan bergambar bahaya merokok",""],[2,"168","2","Healthy Lifestyle and Sports Promotion Campaign","promosi perubahan perilaku hidup sehat yang inovatif dan pembudayaan olahraga, pemberdayaan masyarakat dan penggerakan masyarakat madani untuk hidup sehat",""],[2,"168","2","Healthy Food Access and Nutrition Labelling Measures","peningkatan penyediaan pilihan pangan sehat termasuk penerapan label pangan, perluasan akses terhadap buah dan sayur, dan perluasan gerakan memasyarakatkan makan ikan",""]],"75":[[1,"175","1","Pharmaceutical Supply Quality and Logistics Strengthening","supply of drugs and vaccines by prioritizing product quality; strengthening electronic-based real- time pharmaceutical logistics systems; increasing promotion and supervision of rational drug use;",""],[1,"175","1","Halal-Certified Domestic Medicines and Life Sciences R&D","developing halal-certified domestic medicines, biological products, reagents, and vaccines supported by research and development of life sciences;",""],[1,"175","1","Medical Device Production and Certification Development","the developing production and certification of medical devices to encourage the independence of domestic production;",""],[1,"175","2","Food and Drug Supervision Strengthening Program","Increasing the effectiveness of food and drug supervision, which is focused on expanding the scope and quality of pre- and post-market surveillance of risky food and drug, which is supported by increasing the competency of supervising human resources and improving laboratories, and food and drug inspection centers; increasing research; accelerating and expanding public service processes including registration; expanding the use of information technology in food and drug control; increasing the compliance and independence of business actors in implementing quality management and product supervision systems; increasing community participation in supervising; and expanding investigations and bringing prosecution against violations of the",""],[2,"169","3","Pharmaceutical Supply Efficiency and Competitiveness Improvement","Pemenuhan dan peningkatan daya saing sediaan farmasi dan alat kesehatan yang difokuskan pada efisiensi penyediaan obat dan vaksin dengan mengutamakan kualitas produk;",""],[2,"169","3","Electronic Real-Time Pharmaceutical Logistics System","penguatan sistem logistik farmasi real time berbasis elektronik;",""],[2,"169","3","Rational Medicine Use Promotion and Oversight","peningkatan promosi dan pengawasan penggunaan obat rasional;",""],[2,"169","3","Domestic Halal Pharmaceutical and Vaccine Development","pengembangan obat, produk biologi, reagen, dan vaksin dalam negeri bersertifikat halal yang didukung oleh penelitian dan pengembangan life sciences;",""],[2,"169","3","Medical Device Production and Certification Development","pengembangan produksi dan sertifikasi alat kesehatan untuk mendorong kemandirian produksi dalam negeri;",""],[2,"169","4","Strengthening Food and Drug Supervision","Peningkatan efektivitas pengawasan obat dan makanan yang difokuskan pada perluasan cakupan dan kualitas pengawasan pre dan post market obat dan pangan berisiko yang didukung oleh peningkatan kompetensi SDM pengawas dan penguatan laboratorium dan balai pengawas obat dan makanan; peningkatan riset; percepatan dan perluasan proses layanan publik termasuk registrasi; perluasan pemanfaatan teknologi informasi dalam pengawasan obat dan makanan; peningkatan kepatuhan dan kemandirian pelaku usaha dalam penerapan sistem manajemen mutu dan pengawasan produk; peningkatan peran serta masyarakat dalam pengawasan; dan perluasan penyidikan dan penindakan terhadap pelanggaran ketentuan peraturan perundang-undangan di bidang obat dan makanan;",""],[2,"169","5","Health Governance, Financing, Research, and Digital Information System Strengthening","Penguatan tata kelola, pembiayaan, penelitian dan pengembangan kesehatan yang difokuskan pada pengembangan kebijakan untuk penguatan kapasitas pemerintah provinsi dan kabupaten/kota; pendampingan perbaikan tata kelola pada daerah yang memiliki masalah kesehatan untuk pencapaian target nasional dan mendorong pemenuhan standar pelayanan minimal (SPM) kesehatan; integrasi, sinkronisasi dan simplifikasi sistem informasi kesehatan pusat dan daerah termasuk penerapan sistem single entry; penguatan data rutin; inovasi dan pemanfaatan teknologi digital untuk pengumpulan data, termasuk big data, media promosi, komunikasi, dan edukasi kesehatan; peningkatan pemanfaatan anggaran untuk penguatan promotif dan preventif berbasis bukti; pengembangan sumber pembiayaan baru seperti penerapan earmark cukai dan pajak, pembiayaan bersumber masyarakat, dan kerjasama pemerintah dan swasta; peningkatan kapasitas dan kemandirian pembiayaan fasilitas pelayanan kesehatan milik pemerintah; dan penguatan penelitian dan pengembangan untuk efektivitas inovasi intervensi, dan evaluasi sistem kesehatan untuk mendukung pencapaian prioritas nasional.",""]],"76":[[2,"167","3","Community Nutrition Improvement Acceleration","3.2) Percepatan perbaikan gizi masyarakat untuk pencegahan dan penanggulangan permasalahan gizi ganda, mencakup: a) penguatan komitmen, kampanye, pemantauan dan evaluasi upaya perbaikan gizi masyarakat; b) pengembangan sistem jaminan gizi dan tumbuh kembang anak dengan pemberian jaminan asupan gizi sejak dalam kandungan, perbaikan pola asuh keluarga, dan perbaikan fasilitas air bersih dan sanitasi lingkungan; c) percepatan penurunan stunting dengan peningkatan efektivitas intervensi spesifik, perluasan dan penajaman intervensi sensitif secara terintegrasi; d) peningkatan intervensi yang bersifat life saving dengan didukung bukti (evidence based policy) termasuk fortifikasi pangan; e) penguatan advokasi dan komunikasi perubahan perilaku terutama mendorong pemenuhan gizi seimbang berbasis konsumsi pangan (food based approach); f) penguatan sistem surveilans gizi; g) peningkatan komitmen dan pendampingan bagi daerah dalam intervensi perbaikan gizi dengan strategi sesuai kondisi setempat; dan h) respon cepat perbaikan gizi dalam kondisi darurat.",""]],"77":[[2,"275","24","Revision of Tobacco Control Government Regulation No. 109/2012","Revisi PP Nomor 109 Tahun 2012 tentang Pengamanan Bahan yang Mengandung Zat Adiktif berupa Produk Tembakau bagi Kesehatan",""],[2,"276","11","Halal Certification Regulation for Medicines, Biological Products, and Medical Devices","RPerpres tentang Sertifikasi Halal Produk Obat, Produk Biologi dan Alat Kesehatan",""]],"78":[[1,"92","2","Vocational Workforce Development through Institutional Cooperation","To support the development of KI, it is important to prepare a skilled workforce through vocational cooperation among the ministry/institution, training institution, industry, and regional government.",""],[1,"162","2","Diaspora Talent Engagement System","the talent management system will harness Indonesia's exceptionally talented diaspora currently working abroad.",""],[1,"180","17","Industry and Private Sector Engagement in Vocational Education and Training","Enhancing the role and cooperation of industry/private sector in vocational education and training, including developing incentives/regulatory systems to encourage the role of industry/private sector in vocational education and training; increasing the role of the region in intensive coordination with industry/private sector for the development of vocational education and training in the region; and mapping the demand",""],[1,"180","19","Vocational Education and Training Implementation Reform","Reforming the implementation of vocational education and training, including strengthening innovative learning by aligning study programs/areas of expertise to support the development of leading sectors and industry/private needs; aligning curriculum and learning patterns according to industry needs; strengthening learning to build work ethic, soft skills, and foreign",""],[1,"181","1","Dual Vocational Education and Training System Strengthening","strengthening the implementation of vocational education and training in a dual system (dual TVET system) that emphasizes the mastery of practice- based skills and internships in the industry;",""],[1,"181","1","Teaching Factory and Teaching Industry Expansion","expanding the application of quality teaching factory/teaching industry as one of the industry standard learning systems;",""],[1,"181","1","Vocational Learning Facilities and Infrastructure Revitalization","revitalizing and improving the quality of learning facilities, infrastructure and vocational education and training work practices according to standards;",""],[1,"181","1","Industry Work Practice Facility Cooperation","increasing cooperation in the utilization of work practice facilities in the industry, including production units/teaching factory/teaching industry;",""],[1,"181","1","Work Skills and Entrepreneurship Training in Schools","strengthening work skills and entrepreneurship training in schools, madrasas, and boarding schools;",""],[1,"181","1","Apprenticeship Facilitation and Quality Improvement","improving the facilitation and quality of apprenticeship;",""],[1,"181","1","Graduate Placement Strategy Development","preparation of graduate placement strategies;",""],[1,"181","2","Vocational Educator and Instructor Capacity Development","Increasing the quality and competence of vocational educators/instructors, especially with the improvement of vocational educator/instructor training in accordance with their competencies; increasing involvement of instructors/practitioners from their respective industry to teach in vocational education and training units; and increasing",""],[1,"181","4","Vocational Competency Certification System Strengthening","Strengthening the vocational competency certification system, especially by developing competency standards according to industry needs; institutional strengthening and capacity building for the implementation of professional certification; and synchronizing the certification system in various sectors;",""],[1,"181","5","Vocational Education and Training Governance Reform","Improving vocational education and training governance, especially by coordinating permits to establish new vocational education units and study programs that are not in accordance with industry/labor market standards and needs; improving the assessment of the quality of education units through accreditation of study programs and vocational education units; arranging financial management flexibility in production units/teaching factory/teaching industry; developing funding schemes to improve expertise; establishing a single oversight institution at the national level that coordinates and controls the implementation of vocational education and training; and increasing access to vocational training through the application of Pre-Employment Cards.",""],[1,"183","14","Development Assistance Competency Standards and National Qualifications Framework","Developing competency standards and national qualifications for development assistance;",""],[1,"184","7","Talent Management Institution Establishment","e) Establishing a talent management institution in Indonesia.",""],[1,"217","2","ICT Vocational Education and Human Resource Development","it is necessary to develop human resources, including through vocational education in ICT.",""],[2,"94","4","Vocational Skills Development Cooperation for Industrial Zones","Dukungan untuk KI juga mencakup penyiapan SDM terampil melalui kerja sama vokasi antara Kementerian/Lembaga, lembaga diklat, industri dan Pemerintah Daerah.","Kementerian/Lembaga | Pemerintah Daerah"],[2,"173","6","Private Sector Engagement in Vocational Education and Training","Peningkatan peran dan kerja sama industri/swasta dalam pendidikan dan pelatihan vokasi, meliputi pengembangan sistem insentif/regulasi untuk mendorong peran industri/swasta dalam pendidikan dan pelatihan vokasi; peningkatan peran daerah dalam koordinasi intensif dengan industri/swasta untuk pengembangan pendidikan dan pelatihan vokasi di wilayahnya; dan pemetaan kebutuhan keahlian termasuk penguatan informasi pasar kerja;",""],[2,"173","7","Vocational Education and Training Reform","Reformasi penyelenggaraan pendidikan dan pelatihan vokasi, meliputi penguatan pembelajaran inovatif dengan penyelarasan program studi/bidang keahlian mendukung pengembangan sektor unggulan dan kebutuhan industri/swasta; penyelarasan kurikulum dan pola pembelajaran sesuai kebutuhan industri; penguatan pembelajaran untuk penguasaan karakter kerja, softskills dan bahasa asing; penguatan pelaksanaan pendidikan dan pelatihan vokasi sistem ganda (dual TVET system) yang menekankan pada penguasaan keterampilan berbasis praktik dan magang di industri; perluasan penerapan teaching factory/teaching industry berkualitas sebagai salah satu sistem pembelajaran standar industri; revitalisasi dan peningkatan kualitas sarana dan prasarana pembelajaran dan praktek kerja pendidikan dan pelatihan vokasi sesuai standar; peningkatan kerja sama pemanfaatan fasilitas praktik kerja di industri, termasuk unit produksi/ teaching factory/teaching industry; penguatan pelatihan kecakapan kerja dan kewirausahaan di sekolah, madrasah, dan pesantren; peningkatan fasilitasi dan kualitas pemagangan; dan penyusunan strategi penempatan lulusan;",""],[2,"174","2","Vocational Educator and Instructor Capacity Building","Peningkatan kualitas dan kompetensi pendidik/instruktur vokasi, terutama dengan peningkatan pelatihan pendidik/instruktur vokasi sesuai kompetensi; peningkatan keterlibatan instruktur/praktisi dari industri untuk mengajar di satuan pendidikan dan pelatihan vokasi; dan peningkatan pemagangan guru/instruktur di industri;",""],[2,"174","3","Vocational Competency Certification System Strengthening","Penguatan sistem sertifikasi kompetensi vokasi, terutama dengan pengembangan standar kompetensi sesuai kebutuhan industri; penguatan kelembagaan dan peningkatan kapasitas pelaksanaan sertifikasi profesi; dan sinkronisasi sistem sertifikasi yang ada di berbagai sektor;",""],[2,"174","4","Vocational Education and Training Governance Reform","Peningkatan tata kelola pendidikan dan pelatihan vokasi, terutama dengan pengendalian ijin pendirian satuan pendidikan vokasi baru dan program studi yang tidak sesuai standar dan kebutuhan industri/pasar kerja; peningkatan penilaian kualitas satuan pendidikan melalui akreditasi program studi dan satuan pendidikan vokasi; pengaturan untuk fleksibilitas pengelolaan keuangan pada unit produksi/ teaching factory/teaching industry; pengembangan skema pendanaan peningkatan keahlian; pembentukan lembaga single oversight di tingkat nasional yang mengoordinasikan dan mengendalikan pelaksanaan pendidikan dan pelatihan vokasi; dan peningkatan akses ke pelatihan vokasi melalui penerapan Kartu Pra- Kerja",""]],"79":[[1,"176","1","Early and New Literacy Instruction Strengthening","Strengthening early literacy instruction and new literacy (digital, data and social literacy) with effective and appropriate teaching strategies;",""],[1,"176","3","Student Learning Assessment Quality Improvement","Strengthening the quality of assessment of student learning outcomes, especially through strengthening the role of educators in the assessment of learning in the classroom, as well as increasing the use of evaluation to improve the learning process;",""],[1,"176","4","ICT-Enabled Distance and Online Learning Expansion","Increasing the use of ICT in learning, especially in synergizing distance learning models and online learning systems;",""],[1,"176","10","Smart Indonesia Program Educational Assistance","Providing adequate educational assistance for underprivileged children, children from underdeveloped areas, and high- achieving children, including assistance for secondary education graduates who are continuing their studies at the college or university level who come from poor families through the Smart Indonesia Program;",""],[1,"176","11","Equitable Regional Education Service Distribution","Equitable distribution of education services between regions, by providing partiality to regions with low fiscal capacity and educational performance, and applying appropriate service models in 3T regions (frontier, outermost, and disadvantaged), such as integrated education (One Roof School/SATAP), open schools,",""],[1,"176","14","Dropout Re-enrollment and Inclusive Learning Support","Handling dropouts to return to school through appropriate data collection, effective outreach and assistance, revitalizing the Go Back to School movement, and applying the right learning model for children with special needs, working children, children who are in trouble with the law, who are neglected, living on the streets, and in disaster areas;",""],[1,"176","16","One-Year Pre-School Services Improvement","Improvement of 1-year pre-school services.",""],[1,"176","18","Teacher Training Revitalization Programme","Improving the quality of education of prospective teachers through the revitalization of teacher training",""],[1,"177","3","Educator and Education Personnel Management Optimization","Improvement in management, optimization, and distribution of educators and education personnel based on comprehensive mapping of needs and availability;",""],[1,"177","4","Performance Appraisal System Improvement for Educators","Improving the quality of the performance appraisal system as a reference for coaching, awarding, and increasing the competence of educators and education personnel;",""],[1,"177","8","Education Unit and Study Program Accreditation Acceleration","Strengthening capacity and accelerating accreditation of education units and study programs;",""],[1,"177","10","School Quality Culture Strengthening Initiative","Strengthening quality culture by increasing the capability of principals and supervisors, the application of school-based management, and developing quality assurance units at the regional level and in each education unit.",""],[1,"177","12","Regional Education Data Validation and Verification","Improving the database's validity of education by increasing the role of regions in implementing validation and verification in each education unit;",""],[1,"177","13","Education Planning Quality Improvement for Minimum Service Standards","Improving the quality of planning in encouraging the fulfillment of minimum service standards (SPM) in education;",""],[1,"177","14","Education Planning and Implementation Synchronization Mechanism","Increasing synchronization of planning and implementation of education development between levels of government in maintaining the continuity of education across different levels;",""],[1,"177","15","Education Budget Utilization Effectiveness Improvement","Increasing the effectiveness of the utilization of the education budget to increase access, quality, relevance, and competitiveness of education, and fulfillment of the provisions of the education budget in the regions;",""],[1,"177","16","Operational Assistance for Education Units","Increasing the effectiveness of operational assistance for education units to improve service quality;",""],[1,"177","17","Control on Establishment of New Education Units","Controlling permission to establish a new education unit that is not in accordance with the needs and quality standards;",""],[1,"177","20","Regional Nutrition Education Capacity for School Children","Increasing regional commitment and capacity in nutrition education for school children.",""],[2,"170","3","Curriculum-Based Teaching and Learning Quality Improvement","4.1)Peningkatan kualitas pengajaran dan pembelajaran, mencakup: a) penerapan kurikulum dengan memberikan penguatan pengajaran berfokus pada kemampuan matematika, literasi dan sains di semua jenjang; b) penguatan pendidikan literasi kelas awal dan literasi baru (literasi digital, data, dan sosial) dengan strategi pengajaran efektif dan tepat; c) peningkatan kompetensi dan profesionalisme pendidik; d) penguatan kualitas penilaian hasil belajar siswa, terutama melalui penguatan peran pendidik dalam penilaian pembelajaran di kelas, serta peningkatan pemanfaatan hasil penilaian sebagai bagian dalam perbaikan proses pembelajaran; e) peningkatan pemanfaatan TIK dalam pembelajaran, terutama dalam mensinergikan model pembelajaran jarak jauh (distance learning), dan sistem pembelajaran online; f) integrasi softskill (keterampilan non-teknis) dalam pembelajaran, g) peningkatan kualitas pendidikan karakter, agama dan kewargaan; h) peningkatan kualitas pendidikan keagamaan, termasuk kualitas pendidikan di pesantren; dan i) peningkatan kualitas layanan pendidikan kesetaraan dan pendidikan keaksaraan.",""],[2,"170","4","Education Access Equity and 12-Year Compulsory Schooling Acceleration","Peningkatan pemerataan akses layanan pendidikan di semua jenjang dan percepatan pelaksanaan Wajib Belajar 12 Tahun, mencakup: a) pemberian bantuan pendidikan memadai bagi anak keluarga kurang mampu, dari daerah afirmasi, dan anak berprestasi, termasuk bantuan bagi lulusan pendidikan menengah yang melanjutkan ke Pendidikan Tinggi dari keluarga tidak mampu melalui Program KIP Kuliah; b) pemerataan layanan pendidikan antarwilayah, dengan memberikan keberpihakan kepada daerah yang kemampuan fiskal dan kinerja pendidikannya rendah, dan penerapan model layanan yang tepat untuk daerah 3T, seperti pendidikan terintegrasi (sekolah satu atap/SATAP), sekolah terbuka, pendidikan jarak jauh, dan pendidikan berpola asrama; c) pemerataan memperoleh pendidikan tinggi berkualitas melalui perluasan daya tampung terutama untuk bidang-bidang yang menunjang kemajuan ekonomi dan penguasaan sains dan teknologi; d) Penanganan ATS untuk kembali bersekolah, dengan pendataan tepat, penjangkauan dan pendampingan efektif, revitalisasi gerakan kembali bersekolah, dan model pembelajaran tepat untuk anak berkebutuhan khusus, anak yang bekerja, berhadapan dengan hukum, terlantar, jalanan, dan di daerah bencana; e) peningkatan pemahaman dan peran keluarga dan masyarakat mengenai pentingnya pendidikan; dan f) peningkatan layanan 1 tahun pra-sekolah.",""],[2,"170","5","Teacher Education Institution Revitalization and Professional Teacher Education Strengthening","a) peningkatan kualitas pendidikan calon guru melalui revitalisasi Lembaga Pendidikan Tenaga Kependidikan (LPTK) dan penguatan Pendidikan Profesi Guru (PPG);",""],[2,"170","5","Minimum Academic Qualification Compliance for Teachers and Lecturers","b) pemenuhan kualifikasi akademik minimal untuk guru (S1/DIV) dan dosen/peneliti (S2/S3);",""],[2,"170","5","Teacher and Education Personnel Management and Distribution Improvement","c) peningkatan pengelolaan, pemenuhan, dan pendistribusian pendidik dan tenaga kependidikan berdasarkan pemetaan komprehensif mengenai kebutuhan dan ketersediaan;",""],[2,"170","5","Teacher Performance Assessment System Enhancement","d) peningkatan kualitas sistem penilaian kinerja sebagai acuan untuk pembinaan, pemberian penghargaan, serta peningkatan kompetensi pendidik dan tenaga kependidikan;",""],[2,"170","5","Performance-Based Welfare Improvement for Educators","e) peningkatan kesejahteraan pendidik dan tenaga kependidikan berbasis kinerja.",""],[2,"171","2","Education Quality Assurance Strengthening","Penguatan penjaminan mutu pendidikan untuk meningkatkan pemerataan kualitas layanan antarsatuan pendidikan dan antarwilayah, mencakup: a) peningkatan kualitas peta mutu pendidikan sebagai acuan untuk upaya peningkatan mutu layanan pendidikan b) penguatan kapasitas dan akselerasi akreditasi satuan pendidikan dan program studi; c) penguatan Standar Nasional Pendidikan; dan d) penguatan budaya mutu dengan peningkatan kemampuan kepala sekolah dan pengawas, penerapan manajemen berbasis sekolah (MBS), serta pengembangan unit penjaminan mutu di tingkat daerah dan satuan pendidikan.",""],[2,"171","3","Education Governance and Financing Improvement","4.5) Peningkatan tata kelola pembangunan pendidikan, strategi pembiayaan, dan peningkatan efektivitas pemanfaatan Anggaran Pendidikan, mencakup: a) peningkatan validitas data pokok pendidikan dengan meningkatkan peran daerah dalam pelaksanaan validasi dan verifikasi di tingkat satuan pendidikan; b) peningkatan kualitas perencanaan dalam mendorong pemenuhan standar pelayanan minimal (SPM) bidang pendidikan; c) peningkatan sinkronisasi perencanaan dan pelaksanaan pembangunan pendidikan antartingkatan pemerintahan dalam menjaga kesinambungan pendidikan antarjenjang; d) peningkatan efektifitas pemanfaatan Anggaran Pendidikan untuk peningkatan akses, kualitas, relevansi, dan daya saing pendidikan, dan pemenuhan ketentuan Anggaran Pendidikan di daerah; e) peningkatan efektivitas pemanfaatan bantuan operasional satuan pendidikan untuk peningkatan kualitas layanan; f) pengendalian ijin pendirian satuan pendidikan baru yang tidak sesuai kebutuhan dan tidak memenuhi standar mutu; g) penguatan tata kelola pendidikan tinggi melalui upaya penyederhanaan jumlah dan penggabungan perguruan tinggi; h) peningkatan koordinasi lintas sektor dan antar tingkatan pemerintahan dalam penguatan pengembangan anak usia dini holistik integratif (PAUD HI); dan i) peningkatan komitmen dan kapasitas daerah dalam pendidikan gizi untuk anak sekolah.",""],[2,"276","8","National Strategy for Addressing Out-of-School Children to Access Education Services","RPerpres tentang Strategi Nasional Penanganan Penanganan Anak Tidak Sekolah untuk Mendapatkan Layanan Pendidikan",""],[2,"276","9","Presidential Regulation on Education Planning, Budgeting, and Budget Utilization Reform","RPerpres tentang Penataan Perencanaan, Penganggaran, dan Pemanfaatan Anggaran Pendidikan",""]],"80":[[1,"190","2","Sustainable Cultural Ecosystem Development","efforts should be made to promote culture by building a sustainable cultural ecosystem, as well as effective and efficient governance for development.",""],[1,"196","4","Cultural Heritage Preservation and Museum Services Improvement","protecting, developing and utilizing cultural values, traditions, history, and local wisdom; (b) improving access and quality of museums and archival services; and (c) preserving, developing, and utilizing manuscripts and archives as sources of the nation's cultural values, historical past, and collective record.",""],[1,"196","5","Arts, Cultural Products, and Film Development","developing the arts, cultural products, and films",""],[1,"196","5","Cultural Festivals and Opera Development Programme","organizing cultural festivals and developing operas that meet international standards",""],[1,"196","5","Cultural Heritage Management for Welfare Improvement","managing cultural heritage to improve people's welfare",""],[1,"196","5","Maritime Culture, Literacy, and Ocean Cleanliness Initiative","developing maritime culture and literacy, maritime resources, Save the Ocean movement, and Cleaner Indonesia movement",""],[1,"196","8","Cultural Diplomacy Promotion and Overseas Cultural Centers","Developing cultural diplomacy to strengthen the influence of Indonesia within the development of world civilization, including: (a) developing cultural diplomacy through the promotion of Indonesian as an international language, of Indonesia's cultural arts, and its rich cuisine across the archipelago; and (b) strengthening learning centers and Indonesian cultural houses abroad.",""],[1,"196","9","Cultural Governance Development and Coordination Framework","Developing governance of cultural development, including: (a) managing cultural trust funds; (b) enhancing the quality of human resources in the cultural sector; (c) improving cultural facilities and infrastructure; (d) developing an integrated cultural data collection system; and (e) developing cooperation and partnerships in the promotion of the nation's culture.",""],[1,"197","9","Literacy Culture and Reading Promotion Initiative","Amplifying the culture of literacy, including: (a) developing a culture and love for reading; (b) developing a bookkeeping system and strengthening literacy content; and (c)",""],[1,"198","1","Indonesian Language and Literature Promotion Programme","including: (a) promoting of Indonesian as an international language; (b) developing literature education at schools and in community; and (c) revitalizing local languages and their scripts as the nation's cultural treasures.",""],[1,"198","4","Library Partnership Development","developing library partners/supporters",""],[1,"198","4","Philanthropy-Supported Social Innovation Development","developing social innovation supported by philanthropy",""],[2,"186","7","People-Centered Economic System Development and Culture-Building","Pembangunan dan pembudayaan sistem ekonomi kerakyatan berlandaskan Pancasila, mencakup: (a) membangun budaya ekonomi nasional dengan platform koperasi dalam kegiatan usaha produktif; (b) peningkatan etos kerja dan kewirausahaan berlandaskan semangat gotong royong; dan (c) penumbuhan budaya konsumen cerdas dan cinta produk dalam negeri.",""],[2,"187","3","Local Culture and Heritage Revitalization Programme","Revitalisasi dan aktualisasi nilai budaya dan kearifan lokal untuk menumbuhkan semangat kekeluargaan, musyawarah, gotong-royong, dan kerja sama antarwarga, mencakup: (a) pelindungan, pengembangan, dan pemanfaatan nilai budaya, tradisi, sejarah dan kearifan lokal; (b) peningkatan akses dan kualitas pelayanan museum dan arsip; dan (c) pelestarian, pengembangan dan pemanfaatan manuskrip dan arsip sebagai sumber nilai budaya, sejarah, dan memori kolektif bangsa.",""],[2,"187","4","Cultural Product, Festival, and Opera Development","pengembangan produk seni, budaya, dan film; (b) penyelenggaraan festival budaya dan membangun opera berkelas internasional",""],[2,"187","4","Cultural Heritage Management for Community Welfare","pengelolaan cagar budaya untuk meningkatkan kesejahteraan rakyat",""],[2,"187","4","Maritime Culture and Literacy Development Initiative","pengembangan budaya bahari dan literasi maritim, gerakan cinta laut, gerakan Indonesia bersih dan pengembangan sumber daya maritim",""],[2,"187","5","Indigenous Territory Development for Cultural Preservation","pengembangan wilayah adat sebagai pusat pelestarian budaya dan lingkungan hidup",""],[2,"187","5","Indigenous and Cultural Community Empowerment Programme","pemberdayaan masyarakat adat dan komunitas budaya",""],[2,"187","5","Communal Cultural Heritage and Copyright Protection","pelindungan kekayaan budaya komunal dan hak cipta",""],[2,"187","6","Cultural Diplomacy Development Programme","Pengembangan diplomasi budaya untuk memperkuat pengaruh Indonesia dalam perkembangan peradaban dunia, mencakup: (a) pengembangan diplomasi budaya melalui pengembangan bahasa Indonesia sebagai bahasa internasional, muhibah seni budaya, dan kuliner nusantara; dan (b) penguatan pusat studi dan rumah budaya Indonesia di luar negeri.",""],[2,"187","7","Cultural Development Governance Strengthening","Pengembangan tata kelola pembangunan kebudayaan, mencakup: (a) pengelolaan dana perwalian kebudayaan; (b) peningkatan kualitas sumber daya manusia kebudayaan; (c) peningkatan sarana dan prasarana kebudayaan; (d) pengembangan sistem pendataan kebudayaan terpadu; dan (e) pengembangan kerja sama dan kemitraan dalam pemajuan kebudayaan.",""],[2,"188","9","Indonesian Language, Regional Languages, and Literature Development and Protection","Pengembangan, pembinaan, dan pelindungan Bahasa Indonesia, bahasa dan aksara daerah, serta sastra mencakup: (a) peningkatan fungsi Bahasa Indonesia menjadi bahasa internasional; (b) pengembangan pendidikan sastra di satuan pendidikan dan komunitas; dan (c) revitalisasi bahasa dan aksara daerah sebagai khazanah budaya bangsa.",""]],"81":[[1,"196","7","Indigenous Territories Cultural and Environmental Preservation Initiative","developing indigenous territories as centers of cultural and environmental preservation",""],[1,"196","7","Indigenous Peoples and Cultural Communities Empowerment Programme","empowering indigenous people and cultural communities",""],[1,"196","7","Communal Cultural Property and Copyright Protection Measures","protecting communal cultural property and copyright",""]],"82":[[1,"61","6","Affordable and Safe Housing Expansion","Increase public access to affordable, proper, and safe housing for 1 million households",""],[1,"61","6","Slum Area Management Programme","Manage slum areas",""],[1,"221","2","Slum Management Programme","managing slums",""],[1,"231","9","Integrated Public Housing System","The policy directions and strategies in the context of fulfilling the needs for adequate, safe and affordable housing and settlements in urban areas are to develop a public housing system through the provision of simple flats to own or rent that are integrated with the public transportation system, using the",""],[1,"231","10","Urban Public Housing Agency Formation and New Town Development","approach of forming urban public housing agencies in the respective metropolitan areas by providing land, managing assets, and rejuvenating areas including the developing new towns.",""],[1,"294","17","Public Housing Savings Scheme Implementation","PP draft on implementing a public housing savings scheme (also known as Tapera).",""],[2,"192","6","Strengthened Housing and Settlement Supervision","Di samping itu, pembinaan dan pengawasan di bidang perumahan dan kawasan permukiman perlu ditingkatkan untuk menjamin keandalan dan tertib bangunan dalam rangka mengurangi risiko terhadap bencana, serta mencegah tumbuhnya permukiman kumuh.",""],[2,"203","2","Urban Slum Upgrading, Renewal, and Resettlement","Untuk menangani permukiman kumuh di perkotaan dibutuhkan upaya pemugaran, peremajaan, dan permukiman kembali.",""],[2,"203","2","Vertical Land Consolidation for Affordable Urban Housing","Pada daerah tertentu, dibutuhkan konsolidasi tanah vertikal dalam rangka menangani permukiman kumuh sekaligus menyediakan pasokan rumah baru di perkotaan dan terintegrasi dengan sistem transportasi publik.",""],[2,"209","4","Housing Primary and Secondary Financing System Strengthening","Pemantapan sistem pembiayaan primer dan sekunder perumahan, termasuk optimalisasi pemanfaatan sumber pembiayaan jangka panjang seperti Tabungan dan Asuransi Pensiun (TASPEN) dan BPJS Ketenagakerjaan;",""],[2,"209","5","Housing Subsidy Reform","Reformasi subsidi perumahan yang lebih efisien dan tepat sasaran;",""],[2,"209","6","Housing Finance Expansion for Informal Income Households","Perluasan fasilitas pembiayaan perumahan terutama bagi masyarakat berpenghasilan tidak tetap dan membangun rumahnya secara swadaya;",""],[2,"209","7","BP Tapera Housing Finance Service Expansion","Pengembangan layanan Badan Tabungan Perumahan Rakyat (BP Tapera) untuk memperluas akses pembiayaan perumahan.",""],[2,"209","9","Integrated Housing and Basic Settlement Infrastructure Provision","Peningkatan penyediaan perumahan yang sesuai dengan tata ruang dan terpadu dengan layanan infrastruktur dasar permukiman, termasuk sistem transportasi publik;",""],[2,"209","10","Urban Public Housing Development Based on Apartment Blocks","Pengembangan sistem perumahan publik berbasis rumah susun di perkotaan;",""],[2,"209","11","Inclusive Urban Renewal and Land Consolidation","3) Peremajaan kota secara inklusif dan konsolidasi tanah dalam rangka mewujudkan kota tanpa permukiman kumuh;",""],[2,"209","12","Use of State and SOE Land for Affordable Housing","Pemanfaatan tanah milik negara/BUMN untuk mendukung penyediaan perumahan bagi masyarakat berpenghasilan menengah ke bawah;",""],[2,"209","13","Private Sector and State-Owned Enterprise Housing Provision Expansion","Pengembangan peran dunia usaha termasuk BUMN/BUMD dalam penyediaan perumahan, yaitu Perusahaan Umum Pembangunan Perumahan Nasional (Perumnas), PT. Sarana Multigriya Finansial (PT. SMF), dan Bank Tabungan Negara (BTN).",""],[2,"209","15","Building Reliability Standards and Permitting Reform","Penguatan implementasi standar keandalan dan tertib bangunan, kemudahan perizinan dan administrasi pertanahan, serta pengembangan teknologi dan bahan bangunan murah;",""],[2,"209","16","Housing Provision Capacity Building","Peningkatan kapasitas pemerintah/pemerintah daerah, masyarakat dan dunia usaha dalam penyediaan perumahan;",""],[2,"209","17","Housing Provision Collaboration Initiative","Peningkatan kolaborasi antara pemerintah, pemerintah daerah, masyarakat dan dunia usaha dalam penyediaan perumahan;",""],[2,"209","18","Housing Incentive and Disincentive System Development","Pengembangan sistem insentif dan disinsentif dalam penyediaan perumahan;",""],[2,"209","19","Development of National and Regional Public Housing Service Agencies","Pengembangan badan layanan umum perumahan nasional dan daerah.",""],[2,"210","2","New Housing Provision Facilitation","Peningkatan Fasilitasi Penyediaan Hunian Baru;",""],[2,"210","2","Housing Finance Facilitation","ii) Peningkatan Fasilitasi Pembiayaan Perumahan;",""],[2,"210","2","Housing Quality Improvement Facilitation","iii) Pengembangan Fasilitasi Peningkatan Kualitas Rumah;",""],[2,"210","2","Housing and Settlement Infrastructure Provision","iv) Penyediaan Prasarana, Sarana dan Utilitas Perumahan dan Permukiman;",""],[2,"210","2","Building Permit and Safety Standard Facilitation","v) Fasilitasi Peningkatan Standar Keandalan Bangunan dan Keamanan Bermukim (IMB dan SLF);",""],[2,"210","2","One Million Urban Apartment Provision","vi) Penyediaan 1 juta Rumah Susun Perkotaan (Major Project);",""],[2,"210","2","Slum Settlement Upgrading Facilitation","vii) Fasilitasi Penanganan Permukiman Kumuh.",""],[2,"219","6","Urban Public Housing System Development","Arah kebijakan dan strategi dalam rangka pemenuhan perumahan dan permukiman layak, aman dan terjangkau di perkotaan adalah mengembangkan sistem perumahan publik melalui penyediaan rumah susun sederhana sewa dan rumah susun sederhana milik yang terintegrasi dengan sistem transportasi publik, dengan pendekatan membentuk badan perumahan publik perkotaan di metropolitan terkait dengan penyediaan tanah, pengelolaan aset, dan peremajaan kawasan termasuk pengembangan kota baru (new town).",""],[2,"219","7","Urban Slum Upgrading and Renewal Facilitation","Proyek prioritas yang mendukung penyediaan perumahan dan permukiman layak, aman dan terjangkau di perkotaan adalah fasilitasi penanganan permukiman kumuh perkotaan melalui peremajaan permukiman kumuh.",""],[2,"276","19","Regulation for the Implementation of the Public Housing Savings Scheme","RPP untuk Penyelenggaraan Tabungan Perumahan Rakyat (TAPERA)",""]],"83":[[1,"203","5","Integrated Housing, Transport, and Basic Infrastructure Planning","the lack of integration of housing, public transport, and basic housing infrastructure.",""],[1,"203","5","Housing and Settlement Oversight Strengthening","guidance and supervision in housing and settlement areas need to be improved to ensure the reliability and orderliness of buildings in order to reduce the risk of disasters and prevent the growth of slums.",""],[1,"204","2","Housing Industry Licensing and Building Standards Compliance Reform","create a conducive climate for the housing industry that allows for licensing and compliance with building reliability and design standards to ensure the provision of housing that is compatible with spatial planning and is served by the availability of adequate basic infrastructure.",""],[1,"214","2","Vertical Land Consolidation for Slum Management and Urban Housing Supply","vertical land consolidation is needed in order to manage slums while providing a supply of new homes in urban areas that are integrated with the public transportation system.",""],[1,"220","3","Primary and Secondary Housing Finance System Strengthening","Strengthening the primary and secondary housing finance system, including optimizing the use of long- term financing sources such as Savings and Pension Insurance (TASPEN) and BPJS Employment;",""],[1,"220","4","Housing Subsidy Reform","Reforming housing subsidies that are more efficient and with effective targeting measures;",""],[1,"220","5","Housing Finance Expansion for Informal Income Households","Expanding housing finance facilities, especially for people with non- permanent income and who build their houses independently;",""],[1,"220","6","BP Tapera Housing Finance Expansion","Developing services from the People's Housing Savings Agency (BP Tapera) to expand access to housing finance.",""],[1,"220","8","Integrated Housing Provision with Basic Services and Public Transport","Increasing the provision of housing in accordance with spatial planning and integrated with the basic services infrastructure, including public transportation systems;",""],[1,"220","9","Urban Public Housing Development Based on Flats","Developing public housing systems based on flats in urban areas;",""],[1,"220","11","State-Owned Land for Affordable Housing Provision","Utilizing state-owned land to support the provision of housing for middle- and lower-income groups;",""],[1,"220","12","Business Community Housing Development Role Expansion","Developing the role of the business community including state or regionally owned enterprises (BUMN/BUMD in providing housing, namely the National Housing Development Corporation (Perumnas), PT. Sarana Multigriya Finansial (PT. SMF), and the National Savings Bank (BTN).",""],[1,"220","14","Building Reliability Standards and Land Administration Reform","Strengthening the implementation of reliability standards and orderliness of buildings, easing licensing and administration of land, as well as developing technology and inexpensive building materials;",""],[1,"220","15","Housing Provision Capacity Building","Increasing the capacity of the government/regional government, communities, and businesses in providing housing;",""],[1,"220","16","Collaborative Housing Provision Initiative","Increasing collaboration between the government, regional government, communities, and businesses in providing housing;",""],[1,"220","17","Housing Incentives and Disincentives System","Developing a system of incentives and disincentives in providing housing;",""],[1,"220","18","Development of National and Regional Public Housing Service Agencies","Developing national and regional public housing service agencies.",""],[1,"221","1","New Housing Provision","Priority projects that support the provision of access to decent, safe and affordable housing and settlements include: i) facilitating the provision of new housing;",""],[1,"221","1","Housing Finance Improvement","ii) improving housing financing;",""],[1,"221","1","Home Improvement Support Programme","iii) developing home improvement",""],[1,"221","2","Housing and Settlement Infrastructure Support","providing infrastructure, facilities, and utilities for housing and settlements",""],[1,"221","2","Building Safety Standards Improvement","improving building safety standards for housing (IMB and SLF)",""],[1,"221","2","Urban Flats Provision Major Project","providing 1 million urban flats (Major Project)",""]],"84":[[1,"230","4","Urban Mass Public Transport Development Program","Development of urban mass public transport systems is prioritized in 6 (six) major metropolitan cities, namely Jakarta, Surabaya, Bandung, Medan, Semarang, and Makassar.",""],[1,"230","6","Urban Mass Public Transport Development","Urban transport priority projects include: i) Developing mass public transport systems in 6 metropolitan areas (Major Projects);",""],[1,"230","6","Urban Grade-Separated Road and Rail Crossings","iii) Constructing grade-separated road and rail crossings in urban areas,",""],[1,"230","6","Urban Ring Road Development","iv) Developing urban ring roads,",""],[1,"230","6","Urban Mass Public Transport Subsidy Scheme","v) Providing PSOs and subsidies for urban mass public transport.",""],[2,"218","2","Urban Mass Public Transport Development Program","Dalam upaya percepatan pengembangan angkutan umum massal di perkotaan metropolitan, disiapkan program pembangunan angkutan umum massal perkotaan yang mengatur dukungan pendanaan Pemerintah Pusat kepada Pemerintah Daerah dengan sejumlah kriteria.",""],[2,"218","3","Urban Mass Transit System Development","Pembangunan sistem angkutan umum massal termasuk di 6 Wilayah Metropolitan (Major Project)",""],[2,"218","3","Integrated Transport Interchange Facilities","Pembangunan fasilitas alih moda yang terintegrasi dengan pusat kegiatan perekonomian, permukiman dan fasilitas umum pada simpul-simpul transportasi",""],[2,"218","3","Urban Grade-Separated Rail and Road Crossings","Pembangunan perlintasan tidak sebidang antara jalan dan KA di perkotaan",""],[2,"218","3","Urban Ring Road Development","Pembangunan jalan lingkar perkotaan",""],[2,"218","3","Public Service Obligation and Subsidy for Urban Mass Transit","Penyediaan PSO dan subsidi angkutan umum massal perkotaan",""]],"85":[[1,"135","2","Integrated Intermodal Connectivity Development","Strengthening connectivity is carried out, among others through: (a) developing and strengthening integrated intermodal connectivity via",""],[1,"137","4","Integrated Intermodal Connectivity Development","Strengthening connectivity is carried out, among others through: (a) developing and strengthening integrated intermodal connectivity via sea, river, land, and air; and (b) developing telecommunications and information network;",""],[1,"137","4","Telecommunications and Information Network Development","Strengthening connectivity is carried out, among others through: (a) developing and strengthening integrated intermodal connectivity via sea, river, land, and air; and (b) developing telecommunications and information network;",""],[1,"137","8","Donggala, Pantoloan, and Wani Port Reconstruction","Rekonstruksi Pelabuhan Donggala, Pantoloan, Wani\"",""],[1,"140","2","Integrated Intermodal Connectivity Development","Strengthening connectivity is carried out, among others through: (a) developing and strengthening integrated intermodal connectivity via sea, river, land, and air;",""],[1,"142","1","Integrated Intermodal Connectivity Development","developing and strengthening integrated intermodal connectivity via sea, river, land, and air",""],[1,"142","1","Telecommunications and Information Network Development","developing telecommunications and information network",""],[1,"142","1","Regional Logistics System Strengthening","strengthening the regional logistics system in supporting industrialization, especially in the east coast corridor of Sumatra",""],[1,"144","2","Integrated Intermodal Connectivity Development","Strengthening connectivity is carried out, among others through: (a) developing and strengthening integrated intermodal connectivity via sea, river, land, and air;",""],[1,"144","2","Multimodal Urban Mass Transit Improvement","improving the quality of multimodal mass urban transportation services;",""],[1,"144","2","Telecommunications and Information Network Development","developing telecommunications and information network.",""],[1,"219","12","Expansion of Mass Public Transportation Services","Increasing mass public transportation services in 6 (six) metropolitan cities",""],[2,"114","2","Transport Connectivity Improvement","melalui: (iii) peningkatan konektivitas transportasi darat, sungai, laut dan udara;",""],[2,"114","2","Digital Telecommunications and Information Network Development","melalui: (iv) pengembangan jaringan telekomunikasi dan informasi sebagai basis ekonomi digital;",""],[2,"114","4","Village-Urban Connectivity and Logistics Network Development","Penguatan keterkaitan desa-kota yang mendukung pusat pertumbuhan berbasis keunggulan wilayah desa, Kawasan Perdesaan Prioritas Nasional (KPPN), kawasan transmigrasi, dan Pusat Kegiatan Strategis Nasional (PKSN) perbatasan negara melalui: (i) peningkatan aksesibilitas dan konektivitas termasuk jaringan logistik dari desa ke pusat-pusat perdagangan baik pasar lokal, regional maupun internasional;",""],[2,"129","8","Transport and Intermodal Connectivity Development","Penguatan konektivitas dilakukan melalui antara lain (a) pembangunan jalan, pelabuhan laut, dan udara; dan (b) pengembangan dan penguatan konektivitas antarmoda laut, sungai, darat dan udara yang terintegrasi, khususnya pelabuhan hub komoditas mentah maupun barang hasil olahan.",""],[2,"131","2","Integrated Multimodal Connectivity Development","Penguatan konektivitas dilakukan melalui antara lain: (a) pengembangan dan penguatan konektivitas antarmoda laut, sungai, darat dan udara yang terintegrasi; dan (b) pengembangan jaringan telekomunikasi dan informasi.",""],[2,"133","3","Integrated Multimodal Connectivity Development","Penguatan konektivitas dilakukan melalui antara lain: (a) pengembangan dan penguatan konektivitas antarmoda laut, sungai, darat dan udara yang terintegrasi;",""],[2,"133","3","Telecommunications and Information Network Development","Penguatan konektivitas dilakukan melalui antara lain: (c) pengembangan jaringan telekomunikasi dan informasi.",""],[2,"135","3","Integrated Multimodal Connectivity Development","Penguatan konektivitas dilakukan melalui antara lain: (a) pengembangan dan penguatan konektivitas antarmoda laut, sungai, darat dan udara yang terintegrasi; dan (b) pengembangan jaringan telekomunikasi dan informasi;",""],[2,"135","11","Donggala, Pantoloan, and Wani Port Reconstruction","Rekonstruksi Pelabuhan Donggala, Pantoloan, Wani",""],[2,"137","3","Integrated Multimodal Connectivity Development","Penguatan konektivitas, infrastruktur pelayanan dasar pada wilayah metropolitan, kota, dan perkotaan dilakukan melalui antara lain: (a) pengembangan dan penguatan konektivitas antarmoda laut, sungai, darat dan udara yang terintegrasi; dan (b) pengembangan jaringan telekomunikasi dan informasi;",""],[2,"137","3","Telecommunications and Information Network Development","Penguatan konektivitas, infrastruktur pelayanan dasar pada wilayah metropolitan, kota, dan perkotaan dilakukan melalui antara lain: (b) pengembangan jaringan telekomunikasi dan informasi;",""],[2,"139","4","Integrated Urban Transport Connectivity and Service Quality Enhancement","Penguatan konektivitas dan kualitas pelayanan transportasi perkotaan yang dipadukan dengan jaringan multi moda pelabuhan, bandara, dan jaringan jalan non-tol, yang dilakukan melalui antara lain: (a) pengembangan dan penguatan konektivitas antarmoda laut, sungai, darat dan udara yang terintegrasi antara lain; (b) pengembangan jaringan telekomunikasi dan informasi; dan (c) memantapkan sistem logistik wilayah dalam mendukung industrialisasi khususnya di koridor pesisir timur Wilayah Sumatera;",""],[2,"141","3","Integrated Multimodal Connectivity Development","Penguatan konektivitas dilakukan melalui antara lain: (a) pengembangan dan penguatan konektivitas antarmoda laut, sungai, darat dan udara yang terintegrasi antara lain;",""],[2,"141","3","Urban Multimodal Mass Transit Service Improvement","(c) meningkatkan kualitas pelayanan transportasi perkotaan massal multimoda;",""],[2,"141","3","Telecommunications and Information Network Development","(d) pengembangan jaringan telekomunikasi dan informasi.",""]],"86":[[1,"224","5","Railroad Safety Infrastructure and Fleet Renewal","Improving railroad safety is carried out through the provision of railroad facilities and infrastructure that meet feasibility standards, including railroad facilities, infrastructure, and signaling.",""],[1,"224","5","Railroad Infrastructure Maintenance and Fleet Rejuvenation","To guarantee the condition of railroad infrastructure, the needs of infrastructure maintenance must be met.",""],[1,"228","1","Makassar-Parepare Railway Connectivity Development","The Makassar- Parepare railroad development is carried out through integrated railway network construction, regional development, and railroad access to the port.",""],[1,"228","1","Java High-Speed Intercity Passenger Rail Construction","The construction of high-speed intercity passenger trains is focused on the Java conurbation corridor, especially between Jakarta-Bandung and Jakarta- Semarang.",""],[1,"228","1","Trans-Sumatra and Java-Sumatra Rail Line Expansion","The construction of rail lines in other corridors includes the continuation of the Trans-Sumatra railroad, and the construction of double- track rail and reactivation of rail lines in Java and Sumatra.",""],[1,"228","1","Airport and Seaport Rail Link Construction","In order to support inter-modal transportation to the airport and seaport, construction of airport and seaport rail links will be carried out.",""],[1,"228","2","Rail Infrastructure Maintenance and Operation Mechanism","the rail infrastructure maintenance and operation (IMO) mechanism is to be implemented",""],[1,"228","2","Public Service Obligation and Pioneer Subsidy Schemes for Rail Services","public service obligation schemes (PSO) and pioneer subsidies are also to be implemented",""],[1,"228","3","Rail Connectivity Priority Projects","Priority projects that support rail connectivity include: i) High-Speed Rail (Jakarta-Semarang & Jakarta-Bandung) (Major Project); ii) Makassar-Parepare Rail (Major Project); iii) constructing new rail lines (including double-track and reactivating existing lines) and improving rail lines in Java and Sumatra; iv) Developing airport and seaport rail links; v) Maintaining and operating rail infrastructure and facilities (IMO), and vi) Providing PSOs and pioneer subsidies.",""],[2,"215","5","Makassar-Parepare Railway Development","Pengembangan KA Makassar-Parepare dilaksanakan melalui keterpaduan pembangunan jaringan KA, pembangunan kawasan,",""],[2,"215","5","Java High-Speed Rail Development","Pembangunan konektivitas kereta api diprioritaskan pada pengembangan KA Makassar- Parepare dan KA kecepatan tinggi Pulau Jawa.",""],[2,"216","2","Integrated Rail and Port Access Development Scheme","Pendekatan terpadu ini diterapkan dengan skema KPBU yang terhubung dengan kawasan industri di Makassar dan sepanjang koridor KA serta dengan Pelabuhan Makassar New Port dan Pelabuhan Garongkong.",""],[2,"216","2","Intercity High-Speed Passenger Rail Development","Pembangunan KA kecepatan tinggi penumpang antarkota difokuskan pada koridor konurbasi Pulau Jawa khususnya antara Jakarta-Bandung dan Jakarta-Semarang.",""],[2,"216","2","Trans-Sumatra Rail Line Expansion and Rail Rehabilitation","Pembangunan jalur KA pada koridor lain termasuk melanjutkan pembangunan jalur KA Trans Sumatera serta pembangunan jalur ganda dan reaktivasi jalur KA di Pulau Jawa dan Sumatera.",""],[2,"216","2","Airport and Port Rail Access Development","Dalam rangka mendukung transportasi antarmoda menuju bandara dan pelabuhan, akan dilaksanakan pembangunan KA akses bandara dan pelabuhan.",""],[2,"216","3","Railway Infrastructure Maintenance and Operation Mechanism","untuk memenuhi pemeliharaan, perawatan, dan pengoperasian prasarana serta fasilitas perkeretaapian dilaksanakan melalui mekanisme Infrastructure Maintenance and Operation (IMO) perkeretaapian.",""],[2,"216","3","Affordable Railway Service Support Scheme","Dalam rangka penyediaan layanan perkeretaapian dengan tarif yang terjangkau oleh masyarakat, diselenggarakan melalui skema PSO dan subsidi perintis.",""],[2,"216","4","High-Speed Rail Connectivity Development","Proyek prioritas mendukung konektivitas KA meliputi: i) KA Kecepatan Tinggi Pulau Jawa (Jakarta-Semarang & Jakarta-Bandung) (Major Project);",""],[2,"216","4","Makassar-Pare Pare Railway Project","ii) Kereta Api Makassar-Pare Pare (Major Project);",""],[2,"216","4","New Railway Construction and Upgrading Programme","iii) pembangunan jalur KA baru (termasuk jalur ganda dan reaktivasi) dan peningkatan jalur KA di Pulau Jawa dan Sumatera;",""],[2,"216","4","Airport and Port Rail Access Lines","iv) Pembangunan jalur KA akses bandara dan pelabuhan;",""],[2,"216","4","Rail Infrastructure Maintenance and Operations","v) Pemeliharaan, perawatan, dan pengoperasian prasarana dan fasilias perkeretaapian (IMO),",""],[2,"216","4","Public Service Obligation and Pioneer Rail Services","serta vi) Penyediaan PSO dan perintis KA",""]],"87":[[1,"228","4","Maritime Transport Connectivity and Port Performance Standardization","The development of maritime transport connectivity to support national logistics performance is carried out through performance standardization set by the Ministry of Transportation at a number of major ports, including port depth, dock length, and loading/unloading performance.","Ministry of Transportation"],[1,"228","5","Port Institutional Coordination Mechanism","Institutional coordination between operators in the seven ports needs to be established to ensure the standards and compatibility of the infrastructure and services in these seven ports, so as to encourage shipping efficiency.",""],[1,"228","5","Logistics Information Systems Development","Improving logistics performance also needs to be done through the development of logistical information systems (e-logistics) that",""],[1,"229","1","Logistics Data Exchange and Multimodal Transport Development","facilitate the exchange of data and information among all logistical actors, as well as through the development of more efficient multi-modal and inter-modal transport for access that also involve port support areas (hinterland).",""],[1,"229","1","Domestic Shipyard Commercial Vessel Renewal","it is necessary to rejuvenate commercial vessels by prioritizing the role of domestic shipyards for shipbuilding.",""],[1,"229","1","Integrated Marine Connectivity for Disadvantaged Regions","the development of marine connectivity is aimed at strengthening the integration of subsidized sea toll transport with other modes of transportation including the subsidized transportation of air cargo (air bridges) and ground transportation.",""],[1,"229","2","Maritime Connectivity Priority Projects","Priority projects that support maritime connectivity include: i) Developing major ports, for example: Integrated Main Port Networks (Major Project), ii) Developing and expanding ports that support sea tolls, iii) Developing and expanding ports that priority areas, for example: cruise ports, iv ) Implementing sea toll subsidies and pioneering sea transport services, v) Procuring sea transport facilities and infrastructure, and vi) Developing shipping information technology.",""],[1,"294","23","Integrated Container Terminal Operations Management Regulation","Perpres draft on managing integrated container terminal operations.",""],[2,"216","5","Maritime Transport Connectivity and Port Standardization Program","Pembangunan konektivitas transportasi laut untuk mendukung kinerja logistik nasional dilaksanakan melalui standardisasi kinerja yang ditetapkan oleh Kementerian Perhubungan pada sejumlah pelabuhan utama, antara lain meliputi tingkat kedalaman pelabuhan, panjang dermaga, dan kinerja bongkar muat.","Kementerian Perhubungan"],[2,"216","5","Port Area Development for Domestic Cargo Consolidation","Standardisasi kinerja yang disertai dengan pengembangan kawasan pada sejumlah pelabuhan utama diharapkan meningkatkan konsolidasi angkutan barang domestik serta memungkinkan kapal- kapal berukuran lebih besar untuk singgah membentuk rute jaringan saling terhubung (loop).",""],[2,"216","6","Port Operator Coordination Mechanism","Kelembagaan koordinasi antara operator pada ketujuh pelabuhan tersebut perlu dibangun untuk menjamin tingkat standardisasi dan kompatibilitas infrastruktur dan pelayanan pada tujuh pelabuhan, sehingga mendorong terwujudnya efisiensi pelayaran.",""],[2,"216","6","Logistics Information System Development","Peningkatan kinerja logistik juga perlu dilakukan melalui pengembangan sistem informasi logistik (e-logistic) yang memudahkan pertukaran data dan informasi diantara seluruh pelaku logistik serta pengembangan angkutan multimoda dan antarmoda yang lebih efisien untuk akses maupun pada kawasan pendukung pelabuhan (hinterland).",""],[2,"216","6","Merchant Vessel Renewal and Domestic Shipbuilding Support","Selain itu perlu dilakukan peremajaan kapal niaga dengan mengutamakan peran galangan kapal dalam negeri untuk pembuatan kapal.",""],[2,"216","6","Integrated Sea Toll Connectivity for Remote Areas","Untuk mendukung pembangunan di wilayah 3T, pembangunan konektivitas laut diarahkan pada penguatan keterpaduan angkutan tol laut bersubsidi dengan moda transportasi lain termasuk angkutan barang udara bersubsidi (jembatan udara) dan angkutan perintis darat.",""],[2,"217","2","Shipping Information Technology Development","vi) Pengembangan teknologi informasi pelayaran.",""]],"88":[[1,"229","3","Airport Capacity Expansion and Regional Air Connectivity Programme","The development and improvement of airport capacity are carried out through the construction of new airports, development of primary hub airports, rehabilitation and development of airports, development of airports that support priority areas (KSPN, KEK, and KI), as well as construction of water- based airports to support water tourism destinations.",""],[1,"229","3","Pioneering Flight Services and Air Bridge Subsidy Scheme","The accessibility to and from the 3T regions is carried out by increasing the scope of pioneering flight services, the implementation of the air bridge program that is integrated with sea toll routes in Papua, and the revitalization of a pioneering flight subsidy scheme that",""],[1,"229","5","Air Connectivity Regulatory Support and Oversight","The need for air connectivity in remote areas, especially in Papua, which is reflected in the high number of airstrips, needs to be accommodated through regulatory support, guidance, and supervision including safety aspects.",""],[1,"229","5","KPBU-AP Financing Scheme Exploration","including exploring the potential use of the KPBU- AP financing schemes.",""],[1,"229","6","Priority Air Connectivity Projects","Priority air connectivity projects include: i) 37 Air Bridge Routes in Papua (Major Project), ii) Developing 21 new airports, iii) Developing 10 primary hub airports, iv) Rehabilitating and developing 175 airports to support priority areas (KSPN, KEK, and KI), and v) Constructing water- based airports in 5 locations to support water tourism destinations.",""],[2,"217","3","Airport Capacity Expansion and Air Connectivity Improvement","Pembangunan/peningkatan kapasitas bandara dilakukan melalui pembangunan bandara baru pengembangan bandara hub primer, rehabilitasi dan pengembangan bandara, pengembangan bandara mendukung kawasan prioritas (KSPN, KEK, dan KI), serta serta pembangunan bandara perairan (waterbased airport) untuk mendukung destinasi pariwisata perairan.",""],[2,"217","3","Remote Area Air Service Access Support","Dukungan aksesibilitas daerah 3T dilaksanakan melalui peningkatan cakupan layanan penerbangan perintis, implementasi Program Jembatan Udara terpadu dengan Tol Laut di Papua, serta revitalisasi skema subsidi perintis penerbangan yang menjamin kepastian dan keberlanjutan layanan (multiyears), termasuk menggali potensi pemanfaatan skema pembiayaan KPBU-AP.",""],[2,"217","3","Remote Air Connectivity Regulation and Safety Oversight","Kebutuhan konektivitas udara di wilayah terpencil, terutama di Papua yang tergambar dari keberadaan lapangan terbang (airstrip) yang cukup dominan, perlu diakomodasi melalui dukungan regulasi, pembinaan dan pengawasan termasuk aspek keselamatan.",""],[2,"217","4","Air Connectivity Priority Projects","Proyek prioritas konektivitas udara meliputi: i) Jembatan Udara 37 Rute di Papua (Major Project), ii) Pembangunan 21 bandara baru, iii) Pengembangan 10 bandara hub primer, iv) Rehabilitasi dan pengembangan 175 bandara mendukung kawasan prioritas (KSPN, KEK, dan KI), serta v) Pembangunan bandara perairan (waterbased airport) di 5 lokasi mendukung destinasi pariwisata perairan.",""]],"89":[[1,"230","1","Intermodal Transport Connectivity and Ferry Support Programme","constructing new ferry ports, constructing ferry vessels to support 3T regions, and providing pioneer subsidies for ferries, buses, and modes of transport over bodies of water such as rivers and lakes.",""],[1,"230","3","Land Connectivity Priority Projects","Land connectivity priority projects include: i) Constructing international passenger and freight terminals, ii) Constructing 26 ferries, iii) Constructing 36 new ferry ports, and iv) Providing pioneering land transportation services for passengers and goods.",""],[1,"230","6","Integrated Inter-Modal Transport Facilities","ii) Developing inter-modal facilities that are integrated with centers of economic activities, housing, and public facilities via transportation nodes,",""],[2,"217","5","Integrated Road Weighbridge and Road Facility Development","Pembangunan transportasi darat diprioritaskan untuk mengurangi praktik pembebanan berlebih di jalan (road overloading) melalui penyelenggaraan jembatan timbang yang terintegrasi dengan penyelenggaraan jalan (skema KPBU-AP), pengembangan fasilitas dan perlengkapan jalan",""],[2,"217","5","Border Intercity Terminal Development","serta pembangunan terminal antarnegara untuk mendukung kemudahan arus penumpang dan barang di wilayah perbatasan negara",""],[2,"217","5","New Ferry Port and Vessel Provision for Remote Areas","pembangunan pelabuhan penyeberangan baru, pembangunan kapal penyeberangan untuk mendukung daerah 3T, dan penyediaan subsidi perintis untuk angkutan penyeberangan, sungai, danau dan bus",""],[2,"217","5","Feeder Bus Services for Transport Hubs and Tourism Areas","penyediaan angkutan bus yang terhubung dengan simpul- simpul transportasi serta Kawasan Strategis Pariwisata Nasional (KSPN)",""],[2,"217","6","Land Connectivity Priority Projects","Proyek prioritas konektivitas darat meliputi: i) Pembangunan terminal penumpang dan barang antarnegara, ii) Pembangunan 26 unit kapal penyeberangan, iii) Pembangunan 36 pelabuhan penyeberangan baru, serta iv) Penyediaan layanan perintis angkutan darat untuk penumpang dan barang.",""]],"90":[[1,"283","25","Cyber Security Rapid Response Team Development and Strengthening","Developing and strengthening the cyber security rapid response team;",""],[1,"283","26","Cybersecurity Infrastructure, Human Resources, and Regulatory Strengthening","Strengthening infrastructure, human resources, and regulations concerning cyber security;",""],[2,"65","12","Strengthening NSOC-SOC and Establishing CSIRTs","Penguatan NSOC - SOC dan Pembentukan 121 CSIRT",""],[2,"266","26","Cyber Security Rapid Response Team Development and Strengthening","Pembangunan dan penguatan Tim Cepat Tanggap Keamanan Siber;",""],[2,"266","27","Cybersecurity Infrastructure, Human Resources, and Regulatory Strengthening","Penguatan infrastruktur, SDM, dan regulasi keamanan siber;",""]],"91":[[1,"26","17","ICT-Based Infrastructure for Digital Transformation","Developing and utilizing ICT-based infrastructure for digital transformation.",""],[1,"53","5","Digital Transformation Mainstreaming Initiative","Mainstreaming digital transformation is an effort to optimize the role of digital technology in enhancing the nation's competitiveness and serving as one of the sources for Indonesia's future economic growth",""],[1,"53","6","Digital Transformation Mainstreaming Strategy","Mainstreaming strategies for digital transformation consist of aspects of stabilizing the ecosystem (supply), utilization (demand), and managing big data.",""],[1,"59","20","Digital Gap Reduction and Fast Internet Expansion","Reduce the digital gap · Provide fast internet services to support the digitization of the economic, social, and government sectors",""],[2,"56","2","Four Mainstreaming Priorities for the 2020-2024 National Development Plan","Dalam RPJMN 2020-2024 telah ditetapkan 4 (empat) pengarusutamaan (mainstreaming) sebagai bentuk pembangunan inovatif dan adaptif, sehingga dapat menjadi katalis pembangunan untuk menuju masyarakat sejahtera dan berkeadilan.",""],[2,"57","1","Social and Cultural Mainstreaming in National Development Planning","Pengetahuan tradisional (local knowledge), kearifan local (local wisdom), pranata sosial di masyarakat sebagai penjelmaan nilai-nilai sosial budaya komunitas harus menjadi pertimbangan dalam proses perencanaan serta penyusunan kebijakan dan program pembangunan nasional.",""],[2,"57","2","Digital Transformation Mainstreaming Strategy","Pengarustamaan transformasi digital merupakan upaya untuk mengoptimalkan peranan teknologi digital dalam meningkatkan daya saing bangsa dan sebagai salah satu sumber pertumbuhan ekonomi Indonesia ke depan.",""],[2,"80","6","Comprehensive Digital Adaptation Policy","Kondisi ini mengharuskan adanya kebijakan dan pola adaptasi yang menyeluruh dalam pemanfaatan transformasi digital bagi keberlanjutan dan pemerataan pertumbuhan ekonomi, serta perbaikan kualitas kehidupan sosial dan lingkungan.",""]],"92":[[1,"135","3","Telecommunications and Information Network Development","developing telecommunications and information network",""],[1,"137","4","Telecommunications and Information Network Development","Strengthening connectivity is carried out, among others through: (a) developing and strengthening integrated intermodal connectivity via sea, river, land, and air; and (b) developing telecommunications and information network;",""],[1,"142","1","Telecommunications and Information Network Development","developing telecommunications and information network",""],[1,"144","2","Telecommunications and Information Network Development","developing telecommunications and information network.",""],[1,"202","20","Optic Fiber Backbone Network Expansion","All regencies/cities are connected to an optic fiber backbone network",""],[1,"215","8","ICT Infrastructure Expansion and Broadband Improvement","ICT infrastructure development needs to be improved in line with technological developments and public needs.",""],[1,"215","8","Universal ICT Infrastructure Expansion","ICT infrastructure needs to be expanded to reach all regions and all community groups.",""],[1,"216","2","Fixed Broadband and Village Telecommunications Expansion","The fixed broadband network needs to be expanded to reach sub-districts, while the telecommunications and internet access through broadband network need to be extended to all villages.",""],[1,"216","5","Fixed and Mobile Broadband Network Expansion","The expansion of fixed and mobile broadband networks will facilitate public access to government services.",""],[1,"216","6","Digital Broadcasting Switchover","the migration of broadcasting technology from analog to digital is also needed to improve the efficiency of frequency spectrum usage and broadcast quality, especially for television.",""],[1,"230","8","Fixed Broadband Network Infrastructure Deployment","Deploying fixed broadband network infrastructure for urban areas (residential areas, economic centers, and education centers), through (a) facilitating license grants for fixed broadband network infrastructure; (b) increasing the capacity of local industries that support fixed",""],[1,"233","5","Universal Service Obligation Telecommunications Access Expansion","Optimizing Universal Service Obligation (USO) funds in providing and maintaining the quality of telecommunications and internet services, by constructing base transceiver stations (BTS) for non- commercial villages, and providing multi-functional satellites for internet access;",""],[1,"233","6","Telecommunications and Internet Infrastructure Licensing Facilitation","Providing telecommunications and internet services that can be accessed by the public, by facilitating licensing for the deployment of telecommunications and internet infrastructure;",""],[1,"233","7","Fixed Broadband Network Expansion to Sub-Districts","Deploying fixed broadband network infrastructure to sub-districts, while prioritizing strategic tourism areas, industrial zones, tertiary institutions, by facilitating licensing for the deployment of fixed broadband network infrastructure and increasing",""],[1,"233","9","Frequency Spectrum Allocation Reform","Structuring the allocation of the frequency spectrum to encourage economic activities, and provide both basic services and a safe intra- government network",""],[1,"233","12","Shared Passive Infrastructure Development","Encouraging the implementation of passive infrastructure development that can be shared to accelerate the",""],[1,"234","8","Broadband Infrastructure Development","Developing broadband infrastructure, which also includes the Major Project component, namely \"ICT Infrastructure to Support Digital Transformation\"",""],[1,"234","8","Government ICT Infrastructure Development","developing government ICT infrastructure",""],[2,"190","2","Digital Transformation Implementation","Fokus utama tersebut akan ditopang oleh pembangunan energi dan ketenagalistrikan, serta pelaksanaan transformasi digital.",""],[2,"205","2","Expansion of ICT Infrastructure and Broadband Networks","Pembangunan infrastruktur TIK perlu ditingkatkan sejalan dengan perkembangan teknologi dan kebutuhan masyarakat.",""],[2,"205","3","Fixed and Mobile Broadband Network Expansion","Jaringan tetap pitalebar perlu diperluas hingga menjangkau kecamatan sementara akses telekomunikasi dan internet melalui jaringan pitalebar perlu diperluas hingga seluruh desa.",""],[2,"205","4","Digital Broadcasting Migration","Di samping itu, migrasi penyiaran dari sistem analog ke sistem digital juga diperlukan untuk meningkatkan efisiensi penggunaan spektrum frekuensi dan kualitas penyiaran khususnya televisi.",""],[2,"221","3","Universal Service Obligation Telecommunications Access Support","Optimalisasi dana Universal Service Obligation (USO) dalam menyediakan dan menjaga kualitas layanan akses telekomunikasi dan internet, melalui penyediaan BTS untuk desa non komersil, dan penyediaan satelit multifungsi untuk akses internet;",""],[2,"221","4","Affordable Telecommunications and Internet Service Provision","Penyediaan layanan telekomunikasi dan internet yang dapat dijangkau masyarakat, melalui pemberian kemudahan perizinan penggelaran infrastruktur telekomunikasi dan internet;",""],[2,"221","5","Fixed Broadband Network Rollout to Districts","Penggelaran infrastruktur jaringan tetap pitalebar hingga ke kecamatan-kecamatan, dengan prioritas pada kawasan pariwisata strategis, kawasan industri, perguruan tinggi, melalui pemberian kemudahan perizinan penggelaran infrastruktur jaringan tetap pitalebar, dan peningkatan kapasitas industri lokal pendukung jaringan tetap pitalebar.",""],[2,"221","6","Spectrum Allocation Reorganization for Economic Activity and Secure Government Networks","Penataan alokasi spektrum frekuensi untuk mendorong kegiatan ekonomi, penyediaan layanan dasar dan jaringan intra pemerintah yang aman;",""],[2,"221","7","Domestic Industry Use for Intra-Government Network Development","Pengembangan jaringan intra pemerintah didorong melalui pemanfaatan industri dalam negeri untuk meningkatkan kemandirian dan daya saing nasional;",""],[2,"221","8","Analog-to-Digital Broadcasting Migration","Pelaksanaan migrasi penyiaran analog ke digital yang ditandai dengan Analog Switch Off (ASO), dengan memperhatikan kesiapan industri, masyarakat, serta mempercepat selesainya regulasi yang mendukung pelaksanaan tersebut;",""],[2,"221","9","Shared Passive Infrastructure Development","Mendorong terlaksananya pembangunan infrastruktur pasif yang dapat digunakan secara berbagi-pakai dalam rangka percepatan penggelaran infrastruktur dan menurunkan biaya pembangunan;",""],[2,"221","10","Public Broadcasting Facilities and Infrastructure Revitalization","Mendorong revitalisasi sarana dan prasarana Lembaga Penyiaran Publik dengan memperhatikan perkembangan teknologi.",""],[2,"221","11","Broadband Infrastructure Development","i) Pengembangan infrastruktur pitalebar termasuk di dalamnya komponen Major Project \"Infrastruktur TIK untuk Mendukung Transformasi Digital\";",""],[2,"221","11","Broadcasting Infrastructure Development","ii) Pengembangan infrastruktur penyiaran termasuk di dalamnya komponen Major Project \"Infrastruktur TIK untuk Mendukung Transformasi Digital\";",""],[2,"221","11","Government ICT Infrastructure Development","dan iii) Pengembangan infrastruktur TIK pemerintahan",""]],"93":[[1,"231","4","Urban ICT Development","The priority project that supports urban ICT infrastructure and ecosystems is \"Urban ICT Development\".",""],[1,"233","11","Analog-to-Digital Broadcast Migration","Implementing analog to digital broadcast migration as part of the analog switch-off (ASO) plan by considering the readiness of the industry and society, and by accelerating the completion of regulations that support such implementation;",""],[1,"234","2","Revitalization of Public Broadcasting Facilities and Infrastructure","Encouraging the revitalization of facilities and infrastructure of public broadcasting institutions",""],[1,"234","8","Broadcast Infrastructure Development","Developing broadcast infrastructure, which includes the Major Project component \"ICT Infrastructure to Support Digital Transformation\"",""],[1,"234","8","Government ICT Infrastructure Development","developing government ICT infrastructure",""],[2,"218","5","Urban Fixed Broadband Network Deployment","Penggelaran infrastruktur jaringan tetap pitalebar untuk perkotaan (kawasan perumahan, pusat ekonomi, pusat pendidikan), melalui (a) pemberian kemudahan perijinan penggelaran infrastruktur jaringan tetap pitalebar; (b) meningkatkan kapasitas industri lokal pendukung jaringan tetap pitalebar; dan (c) mendorong pengembangan layanan, aplikasi, maupun konten yang mencerdaskan dan sesuai dengan kebutuhan masyarakat perkotaan;",""],[2,"218","6","Emergency Call Service 112 System Development","Pengembangan sistem layanan panggilan darurat 112, melalui (a) pengembangan sistem layanan panggilan darurat dan pedoman penyelenggaraan bagi kabupaten/kota; (b) implementasi dan pendampingan sistem layanan panggilan darurat mandiri pada kabupaten/kota terpilih; dan (c) memperluas penggunaan sistem layanan panggilan ke kabupaten/kota;",""],[2,"218","8","Urban ICT Development","Proyek prioritas mendukung infrastruktur dan ekosistem TIK perkotaan adalah Pengembangan TIK Perkotaan.",""]],"94":[[1,"234","7","Startup Growth Facilitation","Increasing and facilitating the growth of existing start-ups, especially those",""],[1,"234","10","ICT Adoption in Growth Sectors","Expanding the use of ICTs in growth sectors to increase efficiency, productivity, value-added, and creating demand, through increasing the productivity of the economic sector by utilizing ICT, such as digitizing the economic sector.",""],[1,"234","13","Domestic ICT Industry Development and Human Resource Capacity Building","Increasing the independence of the domestic ICT industry and human resources, by (a) harmonizing policies and regulations to encourage the development of the domestic ICT industry;(b) increasing the capacity of ICT-based human resources to meet domestic needs in a well-targeted",""],[1,"235","2","Digital Transformation Support Facilities","Priority projects that assist digital transformation support facilities include: i) Securing and integrating information management that also includes the Major Project component \"ICT Infrastructure to Support Digital Transformation\"; ii) Developing ICT literacy and expertise; and iii) Developing and facilitating the ICT industry.",""],[1,"235","2","ICT Literacy and Expertise Development","Priority projects that assist digital transformation support facilities include: i) Securing and integrating information management that also includes the Major Project component \"ICT Infrastructure to Support Digital Transformation\"; ii) Developing ICT literacy and expertise; and iii) Developing and facilitating the ICT industry.",""],[1,"235","2","ICT Industry Development and Facilitation","Priority projects that assist digital transformation support facilities include: i) Securing and integrating information management that also includes the Major Project component \"ICT Infrastructure to Support Digital Transformation\"; ii) Developing ICT literacy and expertise; and iii) Developing and facilitating the ICT industry.",""],[2,"206","3","Expansion of ICT Use Across Development Sectors","pemanfaatan TIK diharapkan dapat diperluas untuk digitalisasi seluruh sektor pembangunan.",""],[2,"206","3","Development of Digital Start-up Innovation","Inovasi start up digital tersebut perlu terus dikembangkan dan dimanfaatkan untuk meningkatkan pertumbuhan ekonomi nasional.",""],[2,"206","4","Digital Literacy Capacity Building","Agar dapat mengoptimalkan pemanfaatan pengembangan barang dan jasa hasil TIK, perlu ditingkatkan kemampuan literasi digital masyarakat dalam memahami dan menggunakan informasi.",""],[2,"206","5","ICT Vocational Education and STEM Human Resource Development","Untuk itu perlu dilakukan pengembangan SDM termasuk melalui pendidikan vokasi bidang TIK.",""],[2,"206","6","ICT Human Resource Development and Domestic ICT Industry Strengthening","Pengembangan kemampuan SDM dalam memproduksi barang dan jasa TIK diperlukan agar Indonesia tidak hanya menjadi konsumen pasar TIK.",""],[2,"206","6","ICT Research and Development Expansion","Peningkatan penelitian dan pengembangan (research and development) TIK serta penyempurnaan kebijakan industri seperti insentif pasar dan fiskal perlu diberlakukan agar dapat mendorong peningkatan kemampuan industri TIK dalam negeri terutama menghadapi industri 4.0.",""],[2,"208","27","Startup Unicorn Facilitation","Fasilitasi start up unicorn baru (perusahaan)",""],[2,"221","13","Expansion of Digital Social Service Content and Startup Incentives","Perluasan layanan bantuan sosial non tunai, konten digital pendidikan, konten digital informasi publik, layanan digital kesehatan serta informasi pertanian, melalui pemberian insentif start up yang fokus pada layanan sosial, pendidikan, kesehatan, informasi publik serta informasi pertanian;",""],[2,"222","2","Startup Growth and Global Investor Financing Facilitation","Meningkatkan dan memfasilitasi pertumbuhan start up yang ada, terutama yang mempunyai potensi untuk mendapatkan pendanaan dari investor global; dan",""],[2,"222","3","Expansion of ICT Use in Growth Sectors","Perluasan pemanfaatan TIK pada sektor-sektor pertumbuhan dalam rangka peningkatan efisiensi, produktivitas, nilai tambah, dan penciptaan permintaan, melalui peningkatan produktivitas sektor ekonomi dengan pemanfaatan TIK (digitalisasi sektor ekonomi).",""],[2,"222","6","Domestic ICT Industry and Workforce Development","Peningkatan kemandirian industri dan SDM TIK dalam negeri, melalui (a) harmonisasi kebijakan dan regulasi untuk mendorong pengembangan industri TIK dalam negeri; (b) peningkatan kapasitas SDM TIK yang tepat sasaran untuk memenuhi kebutuhan dalam negeri; (c) peningkatan literasi digital masyarakat; dan (d) membangun industri perangkat TIK (5G, IoT, AI, dan lain-lain) di Indonesia, dengan tingkat komponen dalam negeri yang tinggi.",""],[2,"222","8","ICT Literacy and Skills Development","ii) Pengembangan literasi dan keahlian TIK;",""],[2,"222","8","ICT Industry Development and Facilitation","iii) Pengembangan dan fasilitasi industri TIK.",""]],"95":[[1,"178","2","Child Protection System Strengthening","Realizing a child-friendly Indonesia, by strengthening the system for child protection that is responsive to the diversity and characteristics of the regions to ensure that children enjoy their rights, including:",""],[1,"178","3","Child Protection Regulation and Law Enforcement Strengthening","Strengthening regulations and law enforcement in proportion to the best interests of children;",""],[1,"178","4","Institutional Effectiveness Strengthening Initiative","Strengthening institutional effectiveness through increasing the capacity of human resources, service providers, coordination, data, information systems, as well as the guidance and supervision functions;",""],[1,"178","6","Government-Community and Stakeholder Network Strengthening","Strengthening networks between the government and communities, mass media, the business world, and community institutions;",""],[1,"178","8","Child Protection and Violence Prevention Measures","Strengthening efforts to prevent and deal with various acts of violence, exploitation, child labor, and child neglect;",""],[1,"178","9","Child Marriage Prevention Coordination and Synergy Mechanism","Strengthening coordination and synergy in efforts to prevent child marriages by involving various stakeholders;",""],[1,"178","12","Special Protection Services and Rehabilitation for Children","Improving services and rehabilitation for children who need special protection.",""],[1,"178","15","Gender Mainstreaming Institutionalization and Gender-Responsive Planning and Budgeting","Accelerating the implementation of gender mainstreaming (gm) in the ministries/institutions, provincial/district/city governments, and village governments through strengthening institutionalization of gm and strengthening gender responsive planning and budgeting,",""],[1,"179","2","Capacity Building on Violence Against Women and Human Trafficking","Increasing the capacity of law enforcement officers and government administrators regarding violence against women and human trafficking;",""],[1,"179","3","Institutional Capacity Strengthening for Protection of Women Against Violence","Strengthening the institutional capacity of protecting women against violence through increasing the capacity of human resource service providers, coordination among service provider units,",""],[1,"179","5","Integrated Data Systems on Violence Against Women and Human Trafficking","Developing integrated data systems on violence against women and human trafficking;",""],[1,"179","6","Integrated Service Systems for Violence Against Women and Human Trafficking","Developing integrated service systems for handling violence against women and human trafficking;",""],[1,"179","8","Innovation in Violence Against Women and Human Trafficking Prevention","Developing innovation in the prevention of violence against women and human trafficking.",""],[1,"179","10","Integrated Youth Services Coordination and Capacity Strengthening","Strengthening institutional capacity, strategic coordination across stakeholders, and developing the role of the business community and the people in providing integrated youth services, including facilitating positive creative spaces for youth;",""],[1,"292","20","Draft Gender Equality Bill","Draft bill on gender equality.",""],[1,"294","4","National Strategy for Child Marriage Prevention","Perpres draft on national strategy for child marriage prevention.",""],[1,"294","14","National Strategy for Accelerating Gender Mainstreaming","Perpres draft on the national strategy for the acceleration of gender mainstreaming.",""],[2,"171","4","Child Protection System Strengthening","penguatan Sistem Perlindungan Anak yang responsif terhadap keragaman dan karakteristik wilayah anak untuk memastikan anak menikmati haknya, mencakup: a) penguatan regulasi dan penegakkan hukum yang proporsional terhadap kepentingan terbaik anak; b) penguatan efektivitas kelembagaan melalui peningkatan kapasitas SDM, penyedia layanan, koordinasi, sistem data dan informasi, serta fungsi pembinaan dan pengawasan; c) peningkatan pemahaman tentang perlindungan anak bagi para pemangku kepentingan, masyarakat, keluarga, dan anak; d) penguatan jejaring antara pemerintah dengan komunitas, media massa, dunia usaha, dan lembaga masyarakat; e) peningkatan partisipasi anak dalam pembangunan sesuai dengan tingkat kematangan usianya; f) penguatan upaya pencegahan dan penanganan berbagai tindak kekerasan, eksploitasi, termasuk isu pekerja anak, dan penelantaran pada anak; g) penguatan koordinasi dan sinergi upaya pencegahan perkawinan anak dengan melibatkan berbagai pemangku kepentingan; h) penguatan pengasuhan di lingkungan keluarga dan pengasuhan sementara di institusi lainnya; i) peningkatan akses layanan dasar yang terpadu, ramah dan inklusif bagi seluruh anak terutama bagi anak yang berada pada situasi dan kondisi khusus, dan j) peningkatan layanan dan rehabilitasi bagi anak yang membutuhkan perlindungan khusus.",""],[2,"172","2","Gender Equality Policy and Regulation Strengthening","5.2) Peningkatan kesetaraan gender dan pemberdayaan perempuan, mencakup: (a) penguatan kebijakan dan regulasi",""],[2,"172","2","Gender Mainstreaming Acceleration Across Government","(b) percepatan pelaksanaan PUG di kementerian/ lembaga, pemerintah provinsi/kabupaten/kota, dan pemerintah desa melalui penguatan pelembagaan PUG dan penguatan perencanaan dan penganggaran yang responsif gender (PPRG)",""],[2,"172","2","Gender Awareness and Capacity Building Initiative","(c) peningkatan pengetahuan dan pemahaman individu baik perempuan maupun laki-laki, keluarga, komunitas, lembaga masyarakat, media massa, dan dunia usaha",""],[2,"172","2","Women's Participation in Development and Decision-Making","(d) peningkatan peran dan partisipasi perempuan dalam pembangunan, terutama dalam pendidikan, kesehatan, ekonomi, tenaga kerja, serta politik, jabatan publik, dan pengambilan keputusan",""],[2,"172","2","Multi-Stakeholder Gender Coordination Network","(e) peningkatan jejaring dan koordinasi antara pemerintah pusat, pemerintah daerah, masyarakat, media massa, dunia usaha, dan lembaga masyarakat",""],[2,"172","3","Women's Protection and Anti-Trafficking Strengthening Measures","5.3) Peningkatan perlindungan perempuan, termasuk pekerja migran dari kekerasan dan TPPO, mencakup: a) penguatan kebijakan dan regulasi pencegahan, penanganan, rehabilitasi, pemulangan, dan reintegrasi; b)peningkatan pengetahuan dan pemahaman individu baik perempuan maupun laki-laki, keluarga, masyarakat, dunia usaha, dan pemangku kepentingan lainnya tentang KtP dan TPPO; c) peningkatan kapasitas aparat penegak hukum dan penyelenggara pemerintahan tentang KtP dan TPPO; d) penguatan kelembagaan perlindungan perempuan dari tindak kekerasan melalui peningkatan kapasitas SDM penyedia layanan, koordinasi antarunit penyedia layanan, penguatan data dan informasi, serta pengawasan; e) pengembangan sistem data terpadu KtP dan TPPO; f) pengembangan sistem layanan terpadu penanganan KtP dan TPPO; g) penguatan jejaring dan kerja sama antara pemerintah (pusat dan daerah), komunitas, media massa, dunia usaha dan lembaga bantuan hukum; dan h) pengembangan inovasi dalam upaya pencegahan KtP dan TPPO.",""],[2,"172","4","Integrated Youth Services and Positive Youth Spaces","penguatan kapasitas kelembagaan, koordinasi strategis lintas pemangku kepentingan, serta pengembangan peran dunia usaha dan masyarakat dalam menyelenggarakan pelayanan kepemudaan yang terintegrasi, termasuk memfasilitasi ruang-ruang kreasi positif bagi pemuda",""],[2,"172","4","Youth Civic and Political Participation Promotion","peningkatan partisipasi aktif sosial dan politik pemuda, diantaranya melalui peran pemuda di forum internasional, pertukaran pemuda, dan keikutsertaan dalam pelestarian lingkungan",""],[2,"172","4","Youth Risk Behavior Prevention Programme","pencegahan perilaku berisiko pada pemuda, termasuk pencegahan atas bahaya kekerasan, perundungan, penyalahgunaan napza, minuman keras, penyebaran penyakit HIV/AIDS, dan penyakit menular seksual",""],[2,"172","6","Family Economic Empowerment Acceleration","6.1) Akselerasi penguatan ekonomi keluarga, mencakup: (a) pembinaan rencana keuangan keluarga pra dan paska pernikahan, termasuk rencana investasi keluarga; dan (b) pelatihan usaha serta pemberian akses usaha produktif bagi keluarga miskin dan rentan; (c) fasilitasi pendanaan ultra mikro bagi individu atau kelompok usaha produktif dari keluarga miskin dan rentan; (d) pemberian stimulan usaha ekonomi produktif bagi kelompok miskin dan rentan untuk peningkatan pendapatan keluarga; dan (e) penyelenggaraan kewirausahaan sosial.",""]],"97":[[1,"94","1","Labor Relations and Worker Protection Reform","create a conducive labor climate supported by harmonizing industrial relations, strengthening collective bargaining, improving labor regulations, increasing labor expertise and productivity, increasing the role of the regional government, and increasing labor protection both here and abroad.",""],[1,"94","1","Universal Social Protection for Workers","Workers' protection will be realized through the application of a universal social protection system for workers, improvements to the service system for the placement and protection of migrant workers, and effective application of a labor inspection system;",""],[2,"95","7","Labor Market Reform and Worker Protection System","reformasi ketenagakerjaan melalui upaya penciptaan iklim ketenagakerjaan yang kondusif yang didukung oleh hubungan industrial yang harmonis, penguatan collective bargaining, penyempurnaan peraturan ketenagakerjaan, peningkatan keahlian dan produktivitas tenaga kerja, peningkatan peran pemerintah daerah, serta peningkatan perlindungan tenaga kerja baik di dalam negeri maupun di luar negeri.",""],[2,"95","7","Universal Social Protection for Workers","Perlindungan tenaga kerja akan diwujudkan melalui penerapan sistem perlindungan sosial universal bagi pekerja, pembenahan sistem pelayanan penempatan dan perlindungan pekerja migran, dan penerapan sistem pengawasan ketenagakerjaan secara efektif;",""]],"98":[[1,"134","3","Disadvantaged Area Development Acceleration","accelerating the development of disadvantaged areas by focusing on meeting basic services, developing a commodity-based local economy using digital technology, and developing infrastructure;",""],[1,"134","4","Border District Basic Services and Governance Improvement","fulfilling basic services and improving governance in the border districts",""],[1,"134","4","Integrated Village Development Acceleration","accelerating village development in an integrated manner to encourage social, cultural, and economic transformation of villages",""],[1,"134","4","Affirmative Development Implementation","implementing affirmative development",""],[1,"136","3","Underdeveloped Regions Local Commodity Economy Development","accelerating the development of underdeveloped regions with a focus on developing local commodity-based economy by utilizing digital technology, fulfilling basic services that pay attention to aspects of disaster mitigation and",""],[1,"138","2","Integrated Village Development","Integrated village development that includes increasing the capacity of village officials to improve good governance, including the utilization of village funds and village asset management; strengthening village facilitators that focus on disadvantaged villages and inclusive",""],[1,"138","3","Village Community Participation and Economic Transformation Programme","village community participation; determining village boundaries, developing tourist villages, digital villages, and leading products of villages and rural areas; village economic transformation and increasing the role of Village-Owned Enterprises (BUMDes); improving basic services for drinking water, sanitation, and electricity in villages; and utilizing village funds to encourage productive sectors and empower village communities through local village facilitators.",""],[1,"140","9","Development Acceleration in Disadvantaged Areas","accelerating development in disadvantaged areas with a focus on",""],[1,"141","1","Basic Services and Governance Improvement in Border Districts","fulfilling basic services and improving governance in the border districts;",""],[1,"141","1","Integrated Village Development Acceleration","accelerating village development in an integrated manner to encourage social, cultural, and economic transformation of villages;",""],[1,"141","1","Community Empowerment and Local Economic Development for Transition Areas","community empowerment and local economic development to encourage the transformation from marijuana- dependent areas into local economic zones as an integrated part of Aceh's development;",""],[1,"141","1","Affirmative Development Initiative","implementing affirmative development.",""],[1,"141","3","Transmigration Area Revitalization","revitalizing transmigration areas",""],[1,"141","3","Border Region Commodity-Based Economic Development","economic development of leading commodity-based border regions",""],[1,"141","3","Alternative Development for Aceh Marijuana-Dependent Areas","alternative development in Aceh to transform marijuana-dependent areas into local economic zones as an integrated part of regional development",""],[1,"143","5","Integrated Village Development Acceleration","and (c) accelerating village development in an integrated manner to encourage social, cultural,",""],[2,"113","12","Affirmative Development Policy and Implementation for Lagging and Border Areas","Pengembangan kebijakan dan pelaksanaan pembangunan afirmatif untuk mempercepat pembangunan daerah tertinggal, kecamatan lokasi prioritas perbatasan, pulau-pulau kecil terluar dan terdepan, serta kawasan transmigrasi,",""],[2,"114","2","Transmigrant Rights Fulfillment","serta (vii) pemenuhan hak-hak transmigran sesuai mandat regulasi yang berlaku.",""],[2,"128","2","Transmigration Area Revitalization","revitalisasi kawasan transmigrasi;",""]],"99":[[1,"171","9","Implementation of the Masterplan for Persons with Disabilities","Implementing the Masterplan for Persons with Disabilities (RIPD) in accordance with Government",""],[1,"171","12","Disability Rights Planning, Conduct, and Evaluation Regulation","Regulation No. 70/2019, concerning Planning, Conducting and Evaluating with regard to Respect, Protection, and Fulfillment of the Rights of Persons with Disabilities, to realize inclusive development;",""],[1,"171","13","Institutional Implementation Strengthening for Elderly Programs","Strengthening the institutional implementation of programs for the elderly,",""],[2,"166","2","Integrated Long-Term Care System Development","pengembangan sistem perawatan jangka panjang (long term care) terintegrasi dan holistik",""],[2,"166","2","Minimum Social Service Standards Strengthening","penguatan implementasi standar pelayanan minimal bidang sosial untuk memenuhi kebutuhan dasar penduduk",""],[2,"166","2","Child, Older Person, and Disability-Friendly Infrastructure Development","pembangunan masyarakat, lingkungan, dan sarana prasarana ramah anak, lanjut usia dan penyandang disabilitas",""],[2,"166","2","Rights Protection and Fulfilment for Children, Older Persons, and Persons with Disabilities","penghormatan, pelindungan, dan pemenuhan terhadap hak anak, lanjut usia dan penyandang disabilitas",""],[2,"166","2","Disability Master Plan Implementation","implementasi Rencana Induk Penyandang Disabilitas (RIPD) sesuai dengan peraturan Pemerintah No. 70 Tahun 2019, tentang Perencanaan, Penyelenggaraan, dan Evaluasi terhadap Penghormatan, Pelindungan, dan Pemenuhan Hak Penyandang Disabilitas, untuk mewujudkan pembangunan inklusif",""],[2,"166","2","Institutional Strengthening for Elderly Program Delivery","penguatan kelembagaan pelaksana program kelanjutusiaan",""],[2,"166","2","Elderly Empowerment Programme","pemberdayaan kelanjutusiaan bagi lanjut usia",""],[2,"166","2","Lifelong Education and Skills Development for Older Persons","pengembangan pendidikan dan keterampilan sepanjang hayat bagi lanjut usia",""],[2,"166","2","Social Services Strengthening for Vulnerable Groups","penguatan pelayanan sosial bagi kelompok rentan diantaranya kelompok masyarakat adat, orang dengan HIV/AIDS serta korban penyalahgunaan napza",""]],"101":[[1,"159","1","Macro Policy Framework for Poverty Alleviation","Within the framework of macro policies, the government needs to continue to maintain inflation stability, create inclusive economic growth, create productive employment, maintain the investment climate and trade regulations, increase the productivity of the agricultural sector, and develop infrastructure in disadvantaged regions.",""]],"102":[[2,"275","33","Revision of Presidential Regulation No. 96/2015 on Accelerated Poverty Reduction","Revisi Perpres Nomor 96 Tahun 2015 tentang Perubahan atas Peraturan Presiden Nomor 15 Tahun 2010 tentang Percepatan Penanggulangan Kemiskinan",""]],"103":[[1,"150","4","Integrated and Targeted Social Assistance and Subsidy Delivery","The implementation of social assistance and subsidies will continue to be improved through an integrated and targeted implementation, so that it is more effective and efficient in reducing poverty.",""],[1,"162","20","Conditional Assistance for Families for Health and Education","Conditional assistance for families for health and education (million family)",""],[1,"169","15","National Social Security System Development","Developing a comprehensive and integrated National Social Security System (SJSN), including developing Unemployment Benefit, contribution-based Long-Term Care, and the Return to Work programs;",""],[1,"169","16","SJSN Funding and Governance Strengthening","Sustaining funding and strengthening SJSN governance, including expanding and developing membership systems;",""],[1,"169","17","Integrated Social Protection Data and Governance System","Integrated Social Welfare Data (DTKS) and BPJS's health and labor data; adjusting contribution systems, tariffs and benefit packages; and improving SJSN governance through the development of an integrated monitoring and evaluation system, as well as the development of a system",""],[1,"170","1","Social Security Fraud Prevention and Management","to prevent and manage fraud while implementing social security;",""],[1,"170","5","Integrated Food and Energy Assistance Card","Integrating well-targeted distribution of food assistance and energy subsidies to increase accountability and transparency of assistance through the \"Sembako Program\", which will integrate the provision of food and energy assistance (electricity and LPG) into a single card;",""],[1,"170","6","Conditional Cash Transfer for Health and Education Integration","Integrating conditional cash transfer for health and education, which provides incentives to encourage educational participation up to the university level for children from families receiving social education and health assistance;",""],[1,"170","7","Integrated Social Welfare Data Synergy with Population and Social Assistance Databases","Increasing the synergy of Integrated Social Welfare Data (DTKS) with the population database and other social assistance program databases;",""],[1,"170","8","Cashless Social Assistance Distribution Expansion","Expanding and strengthening distribution of cashless social assistance that provides a wide selection of interconnected payment channels and instruments, utilizing",""],[1,"170","10","Diversified Food Aid for Nutritional Support","Developing varied food aid, not only limited to rice and eggs but also local foodstuffs that meet nutritional needs and contain plant-based and animal protein such as vegetables, meat, fish, and weaning food, to ensure nutritional intake for pregnant women, children aged two years and under, to improve the nutrition of school-age children from families receiving social assistance, and to ensure that aid is not used for cigarette consumption;",""],[1,"170","11","Social Assistance Implementation and Beneficiary Education Support","Strengthening assistance to facilitate data collection, and implementation of social assistance programs and beneficiary education to encourage behavior change through Family Development Sessions (P2K2);",""],[1,"170","12","Regional Government Aid Assistance and Distribution","Increasing the role of the regional government in assistance and distribution of aid.",""],[1,"171","2","Integrated Social Protection for Climate and Disaster Risks","Developing social protection that is integrated with economic and social risks to climate change and natural disasters;",""],[1,"171","6","Strengthening Minimum Service Standards in the Social Sector","Strengthening the implementation of minimum service standards in the social sector to meet the basic needs of the population;",""],[1,"171","11","Social Protection Financing System for Climate and Disaster Risks","Developing a social protection financing system to address the risks of climate change and natural disasters.",""],[1,"171","16","Strengthening Social Services for Vulnerable Groups","Strengthening social services for vulnerable groups, including indigenous groups, people with HIV/AIDS, and victims of drug abuse.",""],[1,"171","18","Human Resources Structuring for Social Welfare Management","Structuring management of human resources in relation to social welfare management, especially competency standards and incentive mechanisms;",""],[1,"171","19","Human Resource Certification and Accreditation for Social Welfare Institutions","Expanding human resource certification and accreditation of social welfare institutions;",""],[1,"171","22","Complaints, Data Collection, Referral, and Integrated Services Mechanism","Strengthening mechanisms for complaints, data collection, referrals, and integrated services.",""],[2,"146","4","Integrated and Targeted Social Assistance and Subsidy Delivery","Pelaksanaan bantuan sosial dan subsidi akan terus disempurnakan melalui penyelenggaraan yang terintegrasi dan tepat sasaran, agar lebih efektif dan efisien dalam menurunkan angka kemiskinan.",""],[2,"146","4","Social Assistance Data Improvement and Non-Cash Expansion","Dibutuhkan penanganan yang lebih komprehensif serta didukung dengan perbaikan data dan perluasan penyaluran secara non-tunai, untuk mempercepat integrasi bantuan sosial.",""],[2,"154","3","Macroeconomic Poverty Reduction Measures","Dalam kerangka kebijakan makro, pemerintah perlu terus menjaga stabilitas inflasi, menciptakan pertumbuhan ekonomi yang inklusif, menciptakan lapangan kerja produktif, menjaga iklim investasi dan regulasi perdagangan, meningkatkan produktivitas sektor pertanian, serta mengembangkan infrastruktur di wilayah tertinggal.",""],[2,"154","3","Social Assistance Policy Improvement","Sedangkan dalam kerangka mikro, upaya mengurangi kemiskinan dikelompokkan dalam dua strategi utama, yaitu penyempurnaan kebijakan bantuan sosial yang bertujuan untuk menurunkan beban pengeluaran dan peningkatan pendapatan kelompok miskin dan rentan melalui program ekonomi produktif.",""],[2,"154","3","Productive Economic Programmes for Poor and Vulnerable Groups","Sedangkan dalam kerangka mikro, upaya mengurangi kemiskinan dikelompokkan dalam dua strategi utama, yaitu penyempurnaan kebijakan bantuan sosial yang bertujuan untuk menurunkan beban pengeluaran dan peningkatan pendapatan kelompok miskin dan rentan melalui program ekonomi produktif.",""],[2,"154","3","Community Initiative Financing Support","Selain itu, pemerintah mengupayakan pendanaan bagi inisiatif-inisiatif masyarakat yang terbukti memiliki dampak sosial ekonomi.",""],[2,"165","5","Integrated Social Assistance and Subsidy Delivery Program","Penguatan pelaksanaan penyaluran bantuan sosial dan subsidi yang terintegrasi dan tepat sasaran, mencakup: a) integrasi penyaluran bantuan sosial pangan dan subsidi energi tepat sasaran untuk meningkatkan akuntabilitas dan transparansi bantuan melalui Program Sembako yang akan mengintegrasikan pemberian bantuan pangan dan energi (listrik dan LPG) ke dalam satu kartu;",""],[2,"165","5","Conditional Cash Transfer Integration for Health and Education","b) integrasi penyaluran bantuan tunai bersyarat untuk kesehatan dan pendidikan, yang menyediakan insentif untuk mendorong partisipasi sekolah hingga perguruan tinggi bagi anak-anak dari keluarga penerima bantuan sosial pendidikan dan kesehatan;",""],[2,"165","5","Integrated Social Welfare Data System Strengthening","c) peningkatan sinergi Data Terpadu Kesejahteraan Sosial (DTKS) dengan data dasar kependudukan serta basis data program bantuan sosial lainnya;",""],[2,"165","5","Non-Cash Social Assistance Expansion and Digital Payment Integration","d) perluasan dan penguatan penyaluran bantuan sosial secara non-tunai yang menyediakan berbagai pilihan saluran dan instrumen pembayaran yang saling terkoneksi, dengan memanfaatkan berbagai teknologi digital, didukung dengan edukasi untuk meningkatkan literasi dan inklusi keuangan;",""],[2,"165","5","Nutrition-Sensitive Food Assistance Diversification","e) pengembangan variasi bantuan pangan, tidak hanya terbatas beras dan telur tetapi juga bahan pangan lokal yang memenuhi kebutuhan gizi protein nabati dan hewani seperti sayuran, daging, ikan, dan Makanan Pendamping ASI (MPASI), untuk menjamin asupan gizi bagi ibu hamil, anak usia dibawah dua tahun dan perbaikan gizi anak usia sekolah dari keluarga penerima bantuan sosial serta memastikan bantuan tidak dipergunakan untuk konsumsi rokok;",""],[2,"165","5","Family Capacity Building and Beneficiary Mentoring","f) penguatan fungsi pendampingan untuk fasilitasi pendataan dan pelaksanaan program bantuan sosial dan edukasi penerima manfaat untuk mendorong perubahan perilaku melalui Pertemuan Peningkatan Kemampuan Keluarga (P2K2);",""],[2,"165","5","Local Government Role Enhancement in Social Assistance Delivery","g) peningkatan peran Pemda dalam pendampingan dan penyaluran bantuan.",""],[2,"166","3","Integrated Assistance and Service Delivery Strengthening","Penguatan pelaksanaan pendampingan dan layanan terpadu, mencakup: a) penataan manajemen pengelolaan sumber daya manusia kesejahteraan sosial, terutama standar kompetensi dan mekanisme insentif; b) perluasan sertifikasi sumber daya manusia dan akreditasi lembaga kesejahteraan sosial; c) peningkatan peran dan kapasitas pendamping masyarakat; d) peningkatan pengetahuan, pemahaman mengenai pendidikan anak, kesehatan dan gizi serta pengelolaan keuangan bagi keluarga; dan e) penguatan mekanisme pengaduan, pendataan, rujukan dan layanan terpadu.",""]],"104":[[2,"165","6","Adaptive Social Protection Development","Perlindungan sosial adaptif, mencakup: a) pengembangan perlindungan sosial yang terintegrasi dengan risiko ekonomi dan sosial terhadap perubahan iklim dan bencana alam; b) penguatan sistem kelembagaan perlindungan sosial yang responsif terhadap risiko sosial dan ekonomi akibat perubahan iklim dan bencana alam; c) pengembangan sistem pembiayaan perlindungan sosial untuk mengatasi risiko perubahan iklim dan bencana alam.",""],[2,"165","6","Climate-Responsive Social Protection Institutional Strengthening","b) penguatan sistem kelembagaan perlindungan sosial yang responsif terhadap risiko sosial dan ekonomi akibat perubahan iklim dan bencana alam;",""],[2,"165","6","Social Protection Financing System Development","c) pengembangan sistem pembiayaan perlindungan sosial untuk mengatasi risiko perubahan iklim dan bencana alam.",""]],"105":[[2,"276","17","National Strategy for Accelerating Gender Mainstreaming Implementation Regulation","RPerpres tentang Strategi Nasional Percepatan Pelaksanaan Pengarusutamaan Gender",""]],"106":[[1,"62","9","Natuna Waters Maritime Security Enforcement","Increase deterrent effect and enforce sovereignty in Natuna waters",""],[1,"62","9","Maritime Crime Reduction and Navigation Security Management","Reduce piracy, violence, and crime at sea; transnational crimes; and strengthen the navigation/security management systems",""],[1,"276","3","Marine Security Regulatory and Institutional Strengthening","To respond to the problems, it is necessary to strengthen regulations, infrastructure, and institutions that regulate the duties, functions, and authority of stakeholders related to marine security.",""],[1,"280","2","Border Negotiation and National Border Mapping Initiative","Increasing and intensifying the effectiveness of border negotiations, and accelerating the mapping of national borders;",""],[1,"283","18","Maritime Security Regulatory Improvement","Improving regulations on maritime security.",""],[2,"259","5","Marine Security Regulatory, Infrastructure, and Institutional Strengthening","Untuk merespons permasalahan di atas diperlukan penguatan regulasi, infrastruktur, dan kelembagaan yang mengatur tugas, fungsi, dan kewenangan pemangku kepentingan terkait keamanan laut.",""],[2,"263","16","Border Delimitation Completion and National Boundary Mapping Acceleration","Peningkatan dan intensifikasi efektivitas penyelesaian perbatasan dan percepatan pemetaan batas negara;",""],[2,"266","19","Marine Security Regulatory Improvement","Penyempurnaan regulasi tentang keamanan laut.",""]],"107":[[1,"58","2","Science Technoparks Development Programme","Developing Science Technoparks: Optimizing Triple Helix in 4 major universities",""],[1,"58","3","National Innovation Capability Enhancement","Increase capability to create innovation and national innovation products",""],[2,"157","2","National Innovation Ecosystem Development","Untuk mendorong produktivitas ekonomi melalui inovasi teknologi, perlu dibangun ekosistem inovasi yang didukung dengan komitmen peningkatan belanja litbang nasional.",""]],"108":[[1,"183","5","Sports Regulations Strengthening and Structuring","a) Strengthening and structuring sports regulations;",""],[1,"183","6","Sports Culture Development Initiative","Developing sports culture through families, educational units, and communities, that focuses on recreational sports, traditional sports, sports-related special services, and educational sports;",""],[1,"183","7","Sports Coaching System Development","Structuring a gradual and continuous system of sports coaching based on Olympic sports and the regional potential, particularly through the synergy of sports coaching in educational units supported by training concentration, and",""],[1,"183","11","Inclusive Sports Infrastructure Upgrading","Improving sports infrastructure and facilities of international standards that are handicapped-friendly;",""],[1,"183","12","Business Community Support for Sports Industry Development","Developing the role of the business community in providing assistance, financing, and building the sports industry.",""],[2,"175","3","Sports Governance and Performance Development Programme","7.4) Pengembangan budaya dan peningkatan prestasi olahraga di tingkat regional dan internasional, mencakup: (a) Penguatan dan penataan regulasi keolahragaan; (b) Pengembangan budaya olahraga melalui keluarga, satuan pendidikan dan masyarakat, baik mencakup olahraga rekreasi, olahraga tradisional dan layanan khusus maupun olahraga pendidikan; (c) Penataan sistem pembinaan olahraga secara berjenjang dan berkesinambungan berbasis cabang olahraga Olimpiade dan potensi daerah, khususnya melalui sinergi pembinaan olahraga di satuan pendidikan dengan olahraga prestasi didukung dengan pemusatan pelatihan, penerapan sport science, statistik keolahragaan serta sistem remunerasi dan penghargaan; (d) Penataan kelembagaan olahraga untuk meningkatkan prestasi keolahragaan; (e) Peningkatan ketersediaan tenaga keolahragaan berstandar internasional; dan (f) Peningkatan prasarana dan sarana olahraga berstandar internasional yang ramah difabel; dan (g) Pengembangan peran dunia usaha dalam pendampingan, pembiayaan, dan industri olahraga.",""],[2,"275","4","Revision of the National Sports System Law","Revisi UU Nomor 3 Tahun 2005 tentang Sistem Keolahragaan Nasional (SKN).",""],[2,"275","28","Revision of Government Regulation No. 17 of 2007 on the Organization of Sports Weeks and Championships","Revisi PP Nomor 17 Tahun 2007 tentang Penyelenggaraan Pekan dan Kejuaraan Olahraga",""]],"109":[[2,"20","5","Infrastructure Connectivity and Access Improvement","Melanjutkan pembangunan infrastruktur untuk menghubungkan kawasan produksi dengan kawasan distribusi, mempermudah akses ke kawasan wisata, mendongkrak lapangan kerja baru, dan mempercepat peningkatan nilai tambah perekonomian rakyat.",""],[2,"37","22","Infrastructure Development for Connectivity and Energy","Melanjutkan pembangunan infrastruktur terutama konektivitas dan energi untuk mendukung ekspansi ekonomi dan pertumbuhan inklusif",""],[2,"38","4","Public Investment and SOE Infrastructure Expansion","Peningkatan investasi juga didorong oleh peningkatan investasi pemerintah, termasuk BUMN, terutama untuk infrastruktur",""],[2,"38","4","Infrastructure Stock Expansion","Hal ini ditunjukkan salah satunya dengan peningkatan stok infrastruktur menjadi 49,4 persen PDB pada tahun 2024",""],[2,"38","8","Business and Investment Facilitation and Infrastructure Development","Memberikan fasilitas kemudahan usaha dan investasi, meningkatkan kepastian hukum, dan melanjutkan pembangunan infrastruktur",""],[2,"41","7","Interregional Connectivity Infrastructure Strengthening","Kebijakan hilirisasi komoditas unggulan, pengembangan potensi pariwisata, perkuatan infrastruktur konektivitas antarwilayah menjadi kunci percepatan pertumbuhan Pulau Sumatera.",""],[2,"42","2","National Capital City Development Investment","Pertumbuhan ekonomi Pulau Kalimantan akan meningkat terutama didorong oleh investasi untuk pembangunan Ibu Kota Negara yang menciptakan efek pengganda besar bagi perekonomian serta hilirisasi sumber daya alam untuk energi.",""],[2,"42","5","Papua Economic Upgrading and Connectivity Strengthening","Pulau Papua diharapkan tumbuh lebih tinggi untuk meningkatkan skala ekonomi di Kawasan Timur Indonesia dengan didorong oleh hilirisasi sumber daya alam dan diversifikasi industri pengolahan berbasis perkebunan, pangan, dan perikanan.",""],[2,"42","5","Regional Connectivity Improvement for Price and Logistics Reduction","Penguatan konektivitas juga dilakukan untuk menurunkan disparitas harga komoditas dan biaya logistik.",""]],"110":[[1,"201","1","Infrastructure Development for Basic Services, Economic Growth, and Cities","Therefore, in the period of 2020-2024, infrastructure development to support basic services, economic development, and cities is to be prioritized.",""],[1,"201","3","Innovative Infrastructure Financing through PPP and Creative Schemes","innovative efforts are needed to encourage the participation of the community and business entities through the government-to-business (KPBU) schemes and other creative financing schemes.",""],[1,"204","7","Investment and Business Cooperation Policy Formulation","it is necessary to formulate policies that can increase interest in investment and business cooperation.",""],[2,"190","2","Basic Services Infrastructure Development","pada periode 2020-2024, pembangunan infrastruktur diprioritaskan pada infrastruktur untuk mendukung pelayanan dasar, pembangunan ekonomi, dan perkotaan.",""],[2,"190","2","Energy and Electricity Infrastructure Development","Fokus utama tersebut akan ditopang oleh pembangunan energi dan ketenagalistrikan, serta pelaksanaan transformasi digital.",""],[2,"190","3","Public-Private Partnership and Creative Infrastructure Financing Schemes","Untuk itu diperlukan upaya inovatif untuk mendorong peran serta investasi masyarakat dan badan usaha melalui skema Kerjasama Pemerintah dan Badan Usaha (KPBU) dan skema pembiayaan kreatif lainnya.",""],[2,"193","7","Investment Incentive and Public-Private Cooperation Policy","dengan keterbatasan pembiayaan dari pemerintah perlu dirumuskan kebijakan yang lebih dapat meningkatkan minat investasi dan kerja sama badan usaha.",""]],"111":[[2,"286","5","Phased Minimum Service Standards Fulfillment","Mendorong pemenuhan standar pelayanan minimum (SPM) secara bertahap terutama pelayanan dasar yang menjadi kewajiban pemerintah daerah dengan memperhitungkan kapasitas fiskal daerah dan kemampuan keuangan negara, serta tindakan afirmatif kepada daerah-daerah tertinggal, terluar dan terdepan, kawasan perbatasan, pulau-pulau kecil terluar dan daerah berciri kepulauan;",""],[2,"287","3","Local Government Basic Services and Infrastructure Acceleration Scheme","Meningkatkan kemampuan pemerintah daerah dalam menyediakan pelayanan dasar sesuai SPM dan percepatan pembangunan infrastruktur yang berdampak langsung bagi kesejahteraan rakyat (skema reguler) yang mencakup pendidikan, kesehatan, air minum dan sanitasi, perumahan dan permukiman, dan transportasi;",""]],"112":[[1,"36","1","Tax Administration System Upgrade","On the administration side, the tax administration system continues to undergo updates in order to improve the tax database and increase compliance.",""],[1,"36","1","Revenue Mobilization and Tax Policy Reform","On the policy side, the government continues to explore other potential sources of revenue, including: increasing revenue from international digital services, reforming tax policies by simplifying the structure of the excise tax rates for tobacco products, increasing excise the tax rates for tobacco products, and extensifying the",""],[1,"97","3","Tax Administration and Excise Reform","Tax optimization includes updating the core tax administration system, customs, and excise administration; intensifying and extending both taxable objects and taxation subjects, as well as expanding taxable goods; simplifying the structure of tobacco excise tax rates; increasing tobacco excise tax rates; and strengthening institutions that provide revenue to the state.",""],[2,"40","2","Tax Administration System Modernization","Dari sisi administrasi, terus dilakukan pembaruan sistem administrasi perpajakan sebagai upaya perbaikan basis data perpajakan dan peningkatan kepatuhan.",""],[2,"40","2","Digital Cross-Border Services Tax Revenue Mobilization","Dari sisi kebijakan, pemerintah terus melakukan penggalian potensi penerimaan, antara lain potensi yang berasal dari aktivitas jasa digital lintas negara, reformasi kebijakan cukai melalui penyederhanaan struktur tarif cukai Hasil Tembakau (HT), peningkatan tarif cukai HT, dan ekstensifikasi barang kena cukai.",""]],"113":[[1,"143","1","Industry 4.0 Technology Development","advanced technology towards Industry 4.0",""],[1,"177","18","Higher Education Institutional Consolidation and Management Reform","Strengthening the management of higher education through efforts to simplify the number and integration of tertiary institutions;",""],[1,"181","7","Higher Education Science and Innovation Development","Developing higher education as a producer of science and technological innovations and center of excellence that focuses on the field of science according to the potential of the local area, and enhancing the cooperation of",""],[1,"181","9","University-Industry-Government Cooperation Incentive Scheme","Developing cooperation among universities, industries, and the government by providing incentives for universities and industries to",""],[1,"182","1","Strategic Research and Development Collaboration and Researcher Mobility","develop strategic research and development collaboration, and facilitate the mobility of researchers between universities and industries;",""],[1,"182","3","Adaptive Tertiary Curriculum and Certification Reform","Improving skills of tertiary education graduates through the development of adaptive study programs and learning curriculum designs that are in line with industry and regional development needs, expanding certification and programs to accelerate work waiting periods, and entrepreneurship training to encourage the growth of young entrepreneurs;",""],[1,"182","3","Youth Entrepreneurship Training Programme","Improving skills of tertiary education graduates through the development of adaptive study programs and learning curriculum designs that are in line with industry and regional development needs, expanding certification and programs to accelerate work waiting periods, and entrepreneurship training to encourage the growth of young entrepreneurs;",""],[1,"182","4","Tertiary Institution Endowment Fund Development","Developing endowment funds in tertiary institutions sourced from public funds, including the private sector, and philanthropy for the development of education and learning in tertiary institutions;",""],[1,"182","5","University Mission Differentiation Policy","Manifesting mission differentiation by encouraging universities to focus on carrying out the Tridharma of higher education, which is being a research university, a teaching university, or a vocational university;",""],[1,"182","6","Strengthening Governance of Autonomous State Universities","Strengthening the governance of State Universities of Legal Entities (PTN-BH) that is more autonomous and accountable;",""],[1,"182","7","Development of Private Tertiary Institutions","Strengthening the development of private tertiary institutions in the context of improving the quality of higher education.",""],[1,"182","8","Science, Technology, and Innovation Application in Priority Development Areas","Utilizing science and technology and innovation in the focus areas stipulated in the National Research Masterplan 2017-2045 for sustainable development, which includes",""],[1,"182","9","National Research Priority Flagship Scheme","research implementation with the National Research Priority flagship scheme to produce research products and strategic innovative products, including industrial-scale nuclear power plants, alternative fuels from palm oil, electric vehicles that use lithium ion batteries and fast charging systems, fast trains, amphibious aircraft, unmanned aircraft, pharmaceutical raw materials, and industrial salt manufacturing; mapping the potential of natural resources and cultural resources of the region with a multidisciplinary approach;",""],[1,"182","10","Innovative Production Technology for Sustainable Resource Use","innovative production technology for sustainable use of natural resources (appropriate technology in agriculture and fishery, followed by social research and social innovation that contribute to the development of science and public policy);",""],[1,"182","10","Disaster Prevention and Post-Disaster Mitigation Technology Application","applying technology for disaster prevention and post-disaster mitigation;",""],[1,"182","10","Scientific Temper and Innovation Culture Development","developing a scientific temper and innovation culture;",""],[1,"182","10","Frontier Technology Mastery in Strategic Sectors","and mastering frontier technology in strategic fields such as health and pharmacy, digital technology and cyber security, advanced materials, renewable energy, nuclear power, defense and security, and space;",""],[1,"182","11","Research Powerhouse Development Initiative","Developing a research powerhouse, which includes increasing the quantity and capability of science and technology human resources, developing and strengthening",""],[1,"183","1","Strategic R&D Infrastructure and Research Cooperation Network","strategic R&D infrastructure, strengthening science and technology center for excellence, managing biological and intellectual property data, and developing a network of domestic and foreign research cooperation;",""],[1,"183","2","Innovation Ecosystem Strengthening","Creating an innovation ecosystem that includes strengthened triple- helix cooperation, improving patent/IP governance, strengthening major Science Techno Parks (STP), pioneering the function of Technology Commercialization Office within the Innovation Management framework in universities, pioneering the Technology Transfer Office at STPs or in non-ministry government institutions that focus on science and",""],[1,"183","4","Research and Development Financing and Incentive Support","Increasing the amount and the quality of research and development spending through the coordination of the National Research and Innovation Agency (BRIN), which is supported by increasing research and developing spending from the development of the Endowment Fund for Research, Development and Application to produce inventions and innovations, strengthening data collection and facilitation of alternative funding from outside the government, and providing fiscal incentives for research and development of science and technology-based innovation.",""],[1,"217","4","ICT Human Resource and Domestic Industry Capability Development","development of human resource capabilities in producing ICT-based goods and services is needed so that Indonesia is not only a consumer in the ICT market.",""],[1,"217","4","ICT Research and Development and Industrial Policy Incentives","Increased research and development of ICT as well as improvements to industrial policies, such as market and fiscal incentives, need to be implemented in order to encourage the improvement of the capability of the domestic ICT industry, especially when facing Industrial Revolution 4.0.",""],[2,"174","5","Higher Education Quality Strengthening Program","Penguatan pendidikan tinggi berkualitas mencakup: (a) Pengembangan perguruan tinggi sebagai produsen Iptek-inovasi dan pusat keunggulan (center of excellence) yang mencakup penguatan fokus bidang ilmu sesuai potensi daerah setempat dan peningkatan kerja sama konsorsium riset antarperguruan tinggi maupun antarperguruan tinggi dan lembaga penelitian di dalam dan luar negeri; (b) Pengembangan kerja sama perguruan tinggi dengan industri dan pemerintah dengan menyediakan insentif bagi perguruan tinggi dan industri yang mengembangkan kerja sama litbang strategis dan memfasilitasi mobilitas peneliti antarperguruan tinggi dengan pihak industri; (c) Peningkatan kualitas dan pemanfaatan penelitian dengan meningkatkan interaksi perguruan tinggi dan industri; (d) Peningkatan kualitas lulusan perguruan tinggi melalui pengembangan prodi yang adaptif dan desain kurikulum pembelajaran yang sesuai dengan kebutuhan industri dan pembangunan daerah, perluasan sertifikasi, program untuk percepatan masa tunggu bekerja, dan pelatihan kewirausahaan untuk mendorong tumbuhnya wirausahawan muda; (e) Pengembangan dana abadi (endowment fund) di perguruan tinggi yang bersumber dari dana masyarakat, termasuk sektor swasta dan filantropi untuk pengembangan pendidikan dan pembelajaran di perguruan tinggi; (f) Perwujudan diferensiasi misi dengan mendorong fokus perguruan tinggi dalam mengemban tridharma perguruan tinggi, yakni sebagai research university, teaching university, atau vocational university; g) Penguatan tata kelola PTN-BH yang lebih otonom dan akuntabel; dan (h) Penguatan pembinaan perguruan tinggi swasta (PTS) dalam rangka peningkatan kualitas pendidikan tinggi.",""],[2,"174","6","Integration of Research Implementation with National Research Priority Flagship Schemes","Pemanfaatan Iptek dan inovasi di bidang-bidang fokus Rencana Induk Riset Nasional 2017-2045 untuk pembangunan yang berkelanjutan yang mencakup integrasi pelaksanaan riset dengan skema flagship Prioritas Riset Nasional untuk menghasilkan produk riset dan produk inovasi strategis, diantaranya adalah pembangkit listrik tenaga nuklir skala industri, bahan bakar alternatif dari kelapa sawit, kendaraan listrik termasuk baterai lithium ion dan sistem fast charging, kereta cepat, pesawat amphibi, pesawat terbang tanpa awak, bahan baku obat, dan pabrik garam industri, pemetaan potensi sumber daya alam dan sumber daya budaya wilayah dengan pendekatan",""],[2,"175","2","Applied Technology and Frontier Technology Development","multidisiplin, inovasi teknologi produksi untuk pemanfaatan sumber daya alam yang berkelanjutan (teknologi tepat guna bidang pertanian dan perikanan, serta riset dan inovasi sosial yang berkontribusi bagi pengembangan ilmu pengetahuan dan kebijakan publik), penerapan teknologi untuk pencegahan bencana dan mitigasi pascabencana, pengembangan budaya riset ilmiah dan inovasi, dan penguasaan Teknologi Garda Depan untuk bidang-bidang strategis seperti kesehatan dan farmasi, teknologi digital dan cyber security, material maju, energi baru terbarukan, tenaga nuklir, pertahanan dan keamanan, serta keantariksaan",""],[2,"175","2","National Research Power-House Development","b) Pengembangan Research Power-House yang mencakup peningkatan kuantitas dan kapabilitas SDM Iptek, pengembangan dan penguatan infrastruktur litbang strategis, penguatan Pusat Unggulan Iptek, pengelolaan data kekayaan hayati dan kekayaan intelektual, serta pengembangan jaringan kerja sama riset dalam dan luar negeri",""],[2,"175","2","National Innovation Ecosystem Strengthening","c) Penciptaan ekosistem inovasi yang mencakup penguatan kerja sama triple-helix, perbaikan tata kelola paten/KI, penguatan Science Techno Park (STP) utama, perintisan fungsi Technology Commercialization Office dalam kerangka Manajemen Inovasi di perguruan tinggi, perintisan Technology Transfer Office di STP atau LPNK Iptek, dan pembinaan Perusahaan Pemula Berbasis Teknologi (PPBT)",""],[2,"175","2","R&D Spending Quality Improvement and Fiscal Incentives","d) Peningkatan kualitas belanja litbang melalui koordinasi Badan Riset dan Inovasi Nasional (BRIN) yang ditunjang oleh peningkatan belanja litbang dari hasil pengembangan Dana Abadi Penelitian Pengembangan, Pengkajian, dan Penerapan untuk menghasilkan Invensi dan Inovasi, penguatan pendataan dan fasilitasi pendanaan alternatif dari luar pemerintah, serta pemberian insentif fiskal untuk penelitian dan pengembangan Iptek-inovasi","Badan Riset dan Inovasi Nasional (BRIN)"],[2,"175","4","Development Facilitator Capacity Strengthening Programme","7.5) Penguatan pendamping pembangunan, mencakup: (a) Pengembangan standar kompetensi dan jenjang kualifikasi nasional pendamping pembangunan; (b) Program pendidikan dan pelatihan yang mengacu pada standar kompetensi dan jenjang kualifikasi; (c) Sertifikasi kompetensi pendamping yang mengacu pada skema sertifikasi pendamping pembangunan; dan (d) pengembangan komponen pendukung yaitu sistem insentif, rekognisi, regulasi, dan basis data pendamping yang terpadu.",""],[2,"175","5","National Talent Management System","7.6) Pengelolaan manajemen talenta nasional, mencakup: (a) Pemetaan kebutuhan dan persediaan talenta berdasarkan bidang keahlian dan profesi; (b) Pengelolaan database persediaan dan kebutuhan talenta (talent pool); (c) Peningkatan keahlian, kapasitas, dan kinerja, serta pengembangan karir dan prestasi talenta; (d) Penciptaan lingkungan yang kondusif sebagai daya tarik untuk mengakuisisi talenta, serta bagi pengembangan potensi, minat, keahlian, dan prestasi talenta; dan (e) Pembentukan Lembaga Manajemen Talenta Indonesia.",""]],"114":[[1,"283","3","Counterterrorism Prevention, Prosecution, and Deradicalization Measures","Increasing the prevention, prosecution, and deradicalization of terrorism acts;",""],[1,"283","8","Defense Capability Strengthening with Confidence-Building Measures and Budget Reforms","Strengthening defense capability accompanied by confidence building measures (CBM) and budget reforms by:",""],[1,"283","9","Defense Procurement Prioritization and Domestic Production Policy","Determining priority in the procurement of defense equipment by considering maintenance capacity and prioritizing domestic production;",""],[1,"283","13","Defense Industry Legal and Regulatory Revision","Compiling and revising laws and regulations concerning the defense industry.",""],[1,"283","20","Illicit Narcotics Trafficking and Abuse Prevention","Preventing and eradicating illicit traffic in narcotics drugs, narcotics abuse, and precursors;",""],[1,"283","22","Police Service Professionalization and Modernization","Improving police services to be more professional, modern, and reliable;",""],[2,"266","4","Counterterrorism Prevention, Enforcement, and Deradicalization","Peningkatan pencegahan, penindakan dan deradikalisasi tindak pidana terorisme;",""],[2,"266","9","Defense Capability Strengthening with Confidence-Building Measures and Budget Reform","Penguatan Kemampuan Pertahanan dibarengi dengan pendekatan Confidence Building Measures (CBM) dan reformasi anggaran diwujudkan dengan:",""],[2,"266","10","Defense Equipment Procurement Prioritization","Penajaman prioritas pengadaan alutsista dengan mempertimbangkan kapasitas pemeliharaan dan perawatan dan mengutamakan produksi dalam negeri;",""],[2,"266","14","Preparation and Revision of Defense Industry Regulations","(5) Penyusunan/revisi peraturan perundang-undangan tentang inhan.",""]],"115":[[1,"133","26","Climate Change Mitigation and Disaster Risk Reduction Investment","increasing investment in climate change mitigation and disaster risk reduction",""],[1,"133","26","Coastal Abrasion Management and Forest Conservation","improving management of coastal abrasion in coastal and archipelago areas, and of forest conservation",""],[1,"135","4","Disaster Management and Climate Change Adaptation Mainstreaming","Mainstreaming of disaster management and climate change adaptation is carried out, among others through: (a) increasing the capacity of the people and officials; (b) enhancing the resilience in the northern and southern regions of the Nusa Tenggara Islands and strengthening post-disaster recovery on the island of Lombok and its surroundings; (c) adapting the people to climate change in disaster-prone areas based on local wisdom; (d) increasing investment in climate change mitigation and disaster risk reduction; and (e) improving management of coastal abrasion in coastal and archipelago areas, and of forest conservation.",""],[1,"136","1","Sulawesi Disaster Mitigation and Adaptation Planning","development plans in Sulawesi need to consider approaches to disaster mitigation and adaptation.",""],[1,"137","33","Disaster Management and Climate Change Adaptation Mainstreaming","Mainstreaming of disaster management and climate change adaptation is carried out, among others through: (a) increasing the",""],[1,"137","34","Central Sulawesi Resilience and Post-Disaster Recovery Programme","increasing the resilience in the Central Sulawesi region and strengthening post-disaster recovery in the City of Palu and its surrounding areas",""],[1,"137","34","Climate Change Adaptation in Disaster-Prone Areas","adapting the people to climate change in disaster-prone areas based on local wisdom",""],[1,"138","1","Climate Change Mitigation and Disaster Risk Reduction Investment","increasing investment in climate change mitigation and disaster risk reduction;",""],[1,"138","1","Coastal Abrasion Management","improving the management of coastal abrasion in coastal areas and on islands, and the management of forest conservation;",""],[1,"138","4","Kalimantan Environmental Conservation and Rehabilitation Programme","the development of Kalimantan in the next five years is directed to maintain the function of the island as the world's lungs (Heart of Borneo) by preserving the area's environmental and ecological assets; improving the conservation and rehabilitation of watersheds, critical lands, protected forests, and production forests",""],[1,"138","4","Kalimantan Disaster Risk Mitigation Plan","developing a mitigation plan for natural disasters, floods, and forest fires",""],[1,"140","4","Disaster Management and Climate Change Adaptation Mainstreaming","Mainstreaming of disaster management and climate change adaptation is carried out, among others through: (a) increasing the capacity of the people and officials; (b) increasing the resilience in the eastern region of Kalimantan; (c) adapting the people to climate change in disaster-prone areas based on local wisdom; (d) increasing investment in climate change mitigation and disaster risk reduction; and (e) improving management of coastal abrasion in coastal and archipelago areas, and of forest conservation.",""],[1,"141","1","Human Resource Capacity and Basic Services for Disaster Preparedness","increasing the capacity of human resources, and fulfilling basic services that pay attention to aspects of disaster mitigation and preparedness;",""],[1,"142","2","Disaster Management and Climate Change Adaptation Mainstreaming","Mainstreaming of disaster management and climate change adaptation is carried out, among others through: (a) increasing the capacity of the people and officials;(b) enhancing the resilience in the west coast of Sumatra and strengthening post-disaster recovery in the Sunda Strait and its surrounding areas; (c) adapting the people to climate change in disaster-prone areas based on local wisdom; (d) increasing investment in climate change mitigation and disaster risk reduction; and (e) improving management of coastal abrasion in coastal areas and on islands, and of forest conservation.",""],[1,"144","3","Disaster Management and Climate Change Adaptation Mainstreaming","Mainstreaming of disaster management and climate change adaptation is carried out, among others through: (a) increasing the capacity of the people and officials; (b) increasing the resilience in the southern coast of Java-Bali and stabilizing post-disaster recovery in the Sunda Strait and its surrounding areas; (c) adapting the people to climate change in disaster-prone areas based on local wisdom; (d) increasing investment in climate change mitigation and disaster risk reduction; and (e) improving management of coastal abrasion.",""]],"116":[[1,"224","4","Disaster-Resilient Infrastructure Development","Policy directions in developing disaster- resilient infrastructure include developing resilient infrastructure and strengthening vital infrastructure, integrated management of disaster-prone areas,",""],[1,"225","1","Disaster-Resilient Infrastructure Development and Standards Programme","Developing and improving the quality of disaster-resilient infrastructure in disaster-prone priority areas; (b) Assessing and improving vital infrastructure security against disasters; (c) Establishing standards for disaster- resilient buildings; and (d) Developing green infrastructure.",""],[1,"225","1","Disaster Resilience Financing Innovation","In addition, funding innovations are needed to improve budgeting efficiency in efforts to increase disaster resilience.",""],[1,"225","2","Integrated Urban Flood Risk Management Programs","Strategies to support integrated management of disaster-prone areas include: (a) Integrated programs in disaster risk management, especially concerning the risk of flooding in urban areas, with a combination of structural and non-structural approaches including",""],[1,"225","5","Regional Disaster Resilience Policy and Critical Infrastructure Strengthening","Developing regional policies and strengthening vital infrastructure for disaster resilience",""],[1,"225","5","Disaster-Resilient Infrastructure Development and Rehabilitation","Developing and rehabilitating disaster-resilient infrastructure including the Major Project \"Recovering 4 Critical Watersheds\" and \"Integrated Management of 5 Coastal Urban Areas Along Pantura\"",""],[1,"225","5","Integrated Early Warning and Emergency Response System","Providing an integrated system for early warning and emergency response",""],[1,"225","5","Natural Infrastructure Restoration and Conservation","Restoring and conserving natural infrastructure",""],[1,"240","18","Strategic Infrastructure Development for Adaptive Capacity","Mitigation and improvement efforts to increase adaptive capacity are carried out by developing strategic infrastructure in priority sectors; strengthening human resources in regional government level and community level by providing",""],[2,"213","4","Disaster-Resilient Infrastructure Development","Arah kebijakan dalam pembangunan infrastruktur ketahanan bencana mencakup pengembangan infrastruktur tangguh bencana dan penguatan infrastruktur vital, pengelolaan terpadu kawasan rawan bencana, serta restorasi dan konservasi daerah aliran sungai.",""],[2,"213","5","Disaster-Resilient Infrastructure Development and Critical Infrastructure Protection","Strategi untuk pengembangan infrastruktur tangguh bencana dan penguatan infrastruktur vital terhadap risiko bencana banjir, gempa bumi, tsunami, tanah longsor, lumpur, dan sedimen antara lain: (a) Pembangunan dan peningkatan kualitas infrastruktur tangguh bencana di kawasan prioritas rawan bencana; (b) Penilaian dan peningkatan keamanan infrastruktur vital terhadap bencana; (c) Penetapan standar bangunan tangguh bencana; dan (d) Pengembangan infrastruktur hijau.",""],[2,"213","5","Disaster-Resilience Financing Innovation","Selain itu, perlu adanya inovasi pendanaan untuk meningkatkan efisiensi penganggaran dalam upaya peningkatan ketahanan bencana.",""],[2,"213","6","Integrated Disaster Risk Management Programme","Program terintegrasi dalam pengelolaan risiko bencana, khususnya risiko banjir pada daerah perkotaan, dengan kombinasi pendekatan struktural dan non-struktural termasuk infrastruktur hijau;",""],[2,"213","6","Regional Disaster Resilience Master Plan","Penetapan rencana induk ketahanan wilayah terhadap bencana;",""],[2,"213","6","Disaster Risk Mapping Development","Penyusunan peta risiko bencana berdasarkan karakteristik wilayah;",""],[2,"213","6","Land Subsidence Monitoring System","Pengembangan sistem pemantauan penurunan tanah;",""],[2,"213","6","Flood and Landslide Early Warning System","Penyediaan sistem peringatan dini bencana banjir dan tanah longsor.",""],[2,"213","8","Disaster-Resilient Infrastructure Policy and Vital Infrastructure Strengthening","Pengembangan kebijakan wilayah untuk ketangguhan bencana dan penguatan infrastruktur vital tahan bencana;",""],[2,"213","8","Disaster Resilience Infrastructure Construction and Rehabilitation","Pembangunan dan rehabilitasi infrastruktur ketahanan bencana termasuk Major Project \"Pemulihan 4 Daerah Aliran Sungai Kritis\" dan \"Pengelolaan Terpadu Pesisir 5 Perkotaan Pantura Jawa\";",""],[2,"213","8","Integrated Early Warning and Emergency Response System","Penyediaan sistem terpadu peringatan dini dan tanggap darurat bencana;",""],[2,"213","8","Natural Infrastructure Restoration and Conservation","Restorasi dan konservasi infrastruktur alami.",""],[2,"218","7","Public Protection and Disaster Relief System Development","Pengembangan sistem Public Protection and Disaster Relief (PPDR), melalui (a) pengembangan pilot project sistem PPDR dan ujicoba penggunaan spektrum frekuensi khusus untuk kebencanaan; (b) penyusunan regulasi, standar layanan dan perangkat untuk sistem PPDR; dan (c) implementasi sistem PPDR terutama pada kabupaten/kota rawan bencana",""],[2,"224","3","Disaster and Climate Resilience Policy","Secara lebih spesifik, prioritas nasional tersebut diuraikan ke dalam tiga kelompok kebijakan, yakni: (2) meningkatkan ketahanan bencana dan perubahan iklim;",""],[2,"225","7","Establishment of Regional Disaster Management Agencies","Pembentukan 34 Badan Penanggulangan Bencana Daerah (BPBD) di tingkat provinsi dan 481 BPBD di tingkat kabupaten/kota",""],[2,"227","2","Disaster Risk Assessment and Mapping in 34 Provinces and 170 Districts/Cities","Penyusunan kajian & peta risiko bencana di 34 provinsi 170 Kab/Kota",""],[2,"227","3","District and City Disaster Management Plan Preparation","Penyusunan rencana penanggulangan bencana (RPB) di 118 Kab/Kota",""],[2,"227","5","Contingency Planning and Field Testing Programme","Penyusunan 64 rencana kontingensi & uji lapangan di 36 lokasi",""],[2,"227","6","Disaster-Resilient Village Formation","Pembentukan desa tangguh bencana di 594 desa/kelurahan di 186 kab/kota",""],[2,"227","7","Establishment and Equipment Support for Operations Centers","Pembentukan dan pemberian bantuan peralatan pusat dalops di 104 lokasi",""],[2,"227","9","Multi-Hazard Early Warning System Installation","Instalasi sistem peringatan dini multiancaman bencana di 58 lokasi",""],[2,"228","2","Disaster Risk Reduction and Disaster Management Strengthening","Peningkatan ketahanan (resilience) terhadap bencana dilakukan melalui beberapa perbaikan kerangka peraturan perundangan dan kelembagaan yang terkait dengan pengurangan risiko bencana dan penanggulangan bencana baik di tingkat pusat maupun daerah.",""],[2,"228","2","Disaster Financing and Recovery Investment Framework","Dalam kerangka pembiayaan, telah dilanjutkan komitmen Pemerintah dalam pembiayaan penanggulangan bencana, khususnya dalam rangka investasi pengurangan risiko bencana, rehabilitasi dan rekonstruksi pasca bencana serta inisiasi berbagai inovasi pembiayaan kebencanaan.",""],[2,"228","3","Meteorology, Climatology, and Geophysics Information Development Program","Peningkatan ketahanan iklim juga didukung dengan penyediaan informasi iklim yang cepat dan akurat melalui program pengembangan dan pembinaan meteorologi, klimatologi dan geofisika yang juga berperan penting untuk mendukung pengurangan risiko bencana.",""],[2,"228","4","Climate Adaptation and Disaster Risk Reduction Convergence Agenda","Kedepannya, agenda konvergensi antara adaptasi perubahan iklim (API) dengan pengurangan risiko bencana (PRB) akan semakin ditingkatkan, baik melalui kegiatan perencanaan dan upaya terintegrasi secara lintas sektor, antar wilayah dan para pemangku kepentingan serta kerja sama di tingkat global.",""]],"117":[[1,"301","4","Public-Private Partnership Infrastructure Financing Scheme","Cooperation among government and business entities, or public-private partnership (PPP), is a collaboration among the government and business entities in providing public service facilities and infrastructure based on a risk-sharing framework.",""],[1,"307","3","Creative Financing for Public Service and Facility Delivery","Developing new potential funding sources is carried out through creative financing, which then accelerates the achievement of development targets and increases cooperation between the government and business entities for the purpose of reducing the burden of government spending.",""],[1,"308","3","Emergency Response Insurance Scheme","the government is developing an insurance scheme for emergency response financing",""],[1,"308","3","Joint Rehabilitation and Reconstruction Financing Scheme","it is also preparing a joint financing scheme by pooling funds for rehabilitation and reconstruction",""],[1,"308","4","Public-Private Partnership Scheme Development","it is important to continually develop public-private partnership (PPP) schemes, increase the role of the private sector through corporate social responsibility (CSR), develop direct lending from development",""],[1,"308","4","Corporate Social Responsibility Financing Expansion","increase the role of the private sector through corporate social responsibility (CSR), develop direct lending from development",""],[1,"308","7","Expansion of Public-Private Partnership Schemes in the Social Sector","The utilization of PPP schemes for national development will continue to be expanded and developed for the social sector, including education, health, and others.",""],[1,"308","7","Legal and Regulatory Improvement for Social Sector PPPs","The utilization of PPP schemes in the social sector is accompanied by improvements to applicable laws and regulations.",""],[1,"308","7","CSR Alignment with Government Development Programs","Whereas that of CSR is directed at harmonizing development projects with government programs in support of national development.",""],[1,"310","9","Public-Private Partnership Scheme Strengthening","The government will continue to increase the utilization of PPP schemes by strengthening the following aspects: regulation; joint office functions; the role of the four pillars of PPP (the regulator, the person in charge of the collaborative project or investee, the transaction advisor, and the investors), project planning and preparation, and the internalization of PPP in the planning and budgeting by the central and regional governments",""]],"118":[[1,"16","6","Omnibus Law Regulatory Reform","Comprehensive regulatory reform through the Omnibus Law, especially on two key issues: job creation and empowerment of micro, small, and medium enterprises.",""],[1,"16","7","Job Creation Investment Prioritization and Administrative Reform","Prioritizing investment for job creation, streamlining administrative procedures and bureaucracy, and reforming departmental organizational structure.",""],[1,"34","4","Investment Deregulation and Licensing Integration Reform","To achieve this target, private investment, both foreign and domestic, is encouraged by deregulating investment procedures, integrating licensing regulations, and increasing Indonesia's rank for ease of doing business (EoDB) from 73rd in 2019 to 40th by 2024.",""],[1,"34","9","Business and Investment Facilitation and Infrastructure Development","Providing ease of business and investment facilities, increasing legal certainty, and developing infrastructure",""],[1,"70","7","Infrastructure, Skills, Land Tenure, and Regulatory Harmonization for Investment Diversification","Accelerating infrastructure development, preparing a skilled workforce, ensuring land tenure security, and harmonizing regulations are key to distributing investment outside",""],[1,"71","2","Investment Permit Facilitation for Growth Centers","Ways to increase investment in these growth centers are by easing permits and facilitating investment.",""],[1,"76","6","New Industry Expansion Through Investment","The expansion of new industry through investment, and the acceleration of ease of doing business are expected to foster fairer business competition, efficiency, and inclusive growth.",""],[1,"76","6","Ease of Doing Business Acceleration","The expansion of new industry through investment, and the acceleration of ease of doing business are expected to foster fairer business competition, efficiency, and inclusive growth.",""],[1,"83","16","Electronically Integrated Business Licensing System","Application of electronically integrated business licenses",""],[1,"90","4","Business Climate Improvement and Investment Promotion Reform","improving business climate and increasing investment, including through labor reform",""],[1,"93","8","Business Climate and Investment Facilitation Reform","Improving business climate and increasing investment are carried out through: (1) harmonization and synchronization of regulations and policies among various sectors and regions; (2) facilitation of business and investment, including facilitation of customs and taxation; preparation of regulations to improve business climate and investment through the Omnibus Law, and of tax policies that will regulate income tax, VAT, and regional taxes and levies; improvement in the ease of doing business score; and application of an integrated business licensing system; (3) labor reform through efforts to",""],[1,"94","2","Business Climate and Investment Improvement Measures","Improvements to business climate and investment will be prioritized to support national priority sectors such as energy, export-oriented manufacturing, tourism, creative and digital economy, and vocational education and training.",""],[1,"117","6","Regional Regulatory Streamlining for Ease of Doing Business","Structuring regional regulations to support ease of doing business;",""],[2,"95","7","Regulatory Harmonization for Business Climate Improvement","Perbaikan iklim usaha dan peningkatan investasi dilaksanakan melalui: (1) harmonisasi dan sinkronisasi peraturan serta kebijakan antar sektor dan wilayah;",""],[2,"95","7","Business and Investment Facilitation Measures","fasilitasi kemudahan usaha dan investasi, antara lain pemberian fasilitasi kepabeanan dan perpajakan, penyusunan peraturan untuk meningkatkan iklim usaha dan investasi melalui Omnibus Law perpajakan yang akan mengatur tentang PPh, PPN, pajak dan retribusi daerah, serta ketentuan umum perpajakan, perbaikan peringkat kemudahan berusaha, dan penerapan sistem perizinan berusaha terintegrasi secara elektronik;",""],[2,"96","2","Business Competition Policy and Institutional Strengthening","penguatan kebijakan dan kelembagaan persaingan usaha",""],[2,"96","3","Business Climate Improvement and Investment Promotion","Perbaikan iklim usaha dan peningkatan investasi akan difokuskan untuk mendukung sektor prioritas nasional seperti energi, industri pengolahan terutama yang berorientasi ekspor, pariwisata, ekonomi kreatif, ekonomi digital, serta pendidikan dan pelatihan vokasi.",""],[2,"125","5","Strengthening PTSP for Faster Public and Business Licensing Services","Penguatan peran PTSP sebagai percepatan pelayanan dan perijinan kepada masyarakat dan dunia usaha;",""]],"119":[[1,"51","4","Early Environmental Damage Prevention","Early prevention, where if there is a significant threat that may cause irreversible environmental damage, the lack of conclusive and definite scientific findings or evidence cannot be used as a reason to delay efforts to prevent environmental damage.",""],[2,"55","4","Precautionary Environmental Damage Prevention Measures","Pencegahan dini, dimana apabila terjadi ancaman yang berarti yang menyebabkan kerusakan lingkungan yang tidak dapat dipulihkan maka ketiadaan temuan atau pembuktian ilmiah yang konklusif dan pasti tidak dapat dijadikan alasan untuk menunda upaya-upaya untuk mencegah terjadinya kerusakan lingkungan.",""]],"120":[[1,"57","6","Post-Disaster Rehabilitation and Reconstruction Programme","Improve quality of life of people affected by disasters through post- disaster rehabilitation and reconstruction",""],[1,"57","6","Economic Infrastructure Recovery and Local Economy Support","Accelerate the recovery of supporting infrastructure for the economy, improve economic conditions, and boost the improvement of the local economy of the people in the affected areas",""],[1,"126","4","Post-Earthquake Rehabilitation and Reconstruction Program","KI Palu facilitated by the Post-Earthquake Rehabilitation and Reconstruction program",""],[2,"61","4","Post-Disaster Rehabilitation and Reconstruction","kehidupan masyarakat terdampak bencana melalui kegiatan rehabilitasi dan rekonstruksi pascabencana",""],[2,"61","4","Recovery of Economic Support Infrastructure and Local Economies in Disaster Areas","Percepatan pemulihan infrastruktur pendukung ekonomi, peningkatan kondisi ekonomi, serta mendorong peningkatan ekonomi lokal masyarakat pada daerah terdampak bencana",""]],"121":[[1,"90","4","Halal Industry Development","developing a halal industry",""],[1,"94","3","Halal Industry Development and Sharia Economic Coordination Framework","Development of the halal industry is carried out as part of the Islamic economic and financial development in Indonesia, which covers: (1) policy coordination and synchronization; (2) development of the halal industry; (3) establishment of a sharia economic development body (i.e. national sharia economic and finance committees); (4) implementation of sharia economic and financial master plans;",""],[2,"96","4","Halal Industry Development and Islamic Economy Coordination","Peningkatan industri halal dilaksanakan sebagai bagian dari pengembangan ekonomi dan keuangan syariah yang mencakup: (1) koordinasi dan sinkronisasi kebijakan; (2) pengembangan industri halal; (3) pembentukan suatu badan pengembangan ekonomi syariah (komite nasional ekonomi dan keuangan syariah); (4) pelaksanaan rencana induk ekonomi dan keuangan syariah; dan (5) penerapan kebijakan perlindungan konsumen dan tertib niaga.",""]],"122":[[1,"95","3","Domestic Tourism Promotion and Travel Facilitation","Promotion of tourism through various events and ease of travel within the country are expected to push domestic tourists to travel domestically so that service imports can be managed better.",""],[1,"95","6","Tourism Marketing Integration and National Branding Development","The tourism sector also focuses on building image and diversifying tourism marketing methods through innovation, marketing integration, and development of national branding.",""],[1,"95","6","Tourism Promotion Events and Gastronomic Diplomacy","Various tourism promotion events will be used as a vehicle to increase appreciation and celebration of the natural, cultural, and social diversity of Indonesia; and to strengthen its regeneration and image in the eyes of the world.",""],[1,"95","6","Diaspora-Engaged Tourism Marketing Integration","Marketing integration will also involve the Indonesian diaspora in celebrating Indonesia's cultural wealth, including Indonesian culinary treasures through gastronomic diplomacy.",""],[2,"96","8","Domestic Tourism Promotion and Travel Access Facilitation","Promosi pariwisata melalui berbagai event dan kemudahan akses perjalanan di dalam negeri diharapkan meningkatkan pilihan wisatawan nusantara untuk berwisata di dalam negeri sehingga impor jasa dapat dikelola lebih baik.",""],[2,"97","3","Integrated Tourism Marketing and Nation Branding Initiative","Peningkatan citra dan diversifikasi pemasaran pariwisata difokuskan pada inovasi dan keterpaduan pemasaran, serta penguatan nation branding.",""],[2,"97","3","Tourism Promotion Events for Cultural and Natural Heritage","Berbagai ajang promosi pariwisata akan dijadikan sebagai wahana untuk meningkatkan penghargaan dan perayaan terhadap warisan alam, budaya dan keragaman tatanan sosial masyarakat yang memperkuat regenerasi dan citra bangsa Indonesia.",""],[2,"97","3","Diaspora Engagement for Gastronomic Diplomacy","Keterpaduan pemasaran juga melibatkan diaspora Indonesia dalam perayaan kekayaan budaya, termasuk kekayaan kuliner Indonesia melalui diplomasi gastronomi.",""],[2,"97","4","Strengthening Overseas Tourism, Trade, and Investment Representation","Salah satu langkah konkrit yaitu melalui penguatan perwakilan pariwisata, perdagangan dan investasi di luar negeri, promosi terintegrasi, dan memperluas partisipasi aktif Indonesia di organisasi dan inisiatif internasional seperti Association of Southeast Asian Nations (ASEAN), World Trade Organization (WTO), Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation (APEC), Belt Road Initiatives (BRI), Organisation for Economic Co-operation and Development (OECD), serta kerja sama regional/sub-regional lainnya.",""]],"123":[[1,"96","2","Sustainable Practices in Manufacturing and Tourism","increasing the application of sustainable practices in manufacturing and tourism",""],[1,"96","6","Sustainable Practices Implementation in Industry and Tourism","The government's strategy to implement sustainable practices in the industrial sector and tourism is a form of commitment to the implementation of the 12th goal of",""],[1,"97","1","Green Industry Standard Implementation in Manufacturing","The focus of its implementation includes the application of Green Industry Standard/SNI/ISO 14001 in manufacturing to mitigate environmental risks, and certification of sustainable tourism practices.",""],[1,"97","1","Sustainable Tourism Certification Programme","The focus of its implementation includes the application of Green Industry Standard/SNI/ISO 14001 in manufacturing to mitigate environmental risks, and certification of sustainable tourism practices.",""],[2,"97","5","Sustainable Practices in Manufacturing and Tourism","(iv) Penguatan pilar pertumbuhan dan daya saing ekonomi yang dilaksanakan dengan strategi: (4) meningkatkan penerapan praktik berkelanjutan pada industri pengolahan dan pariwisata;",""],[2,"98","4","Sustainable Practices Implementation in Industry and Tourism","Pelaksanaan strategi penerapan praktik berkelanjutan di sektor industri dan pariwisata merupakan bentuk komitmen pelaksanaan SDG ke-12 yaitu memastikan pola konsumsi dan produksi yang berkelanjutan.",""]],"124":[[1,"105","2","One Map Policy and One Data Indonesia Integration","there are still overlapping spatial use permits that will be resolved through the implementation of the One Map policy, which is integrated in the implementation of One Data Indonesia.",""],[1,"111","11","Land Bank Formation and Operationalization","Formation and operationalization of a land bank",""],[1,"118","3","Land Rights Certification and Boundary Delineation Programme","Improving the legal certainty of land rights through: (i) certification of land rights especially in areas directed as corridors of economic growth and equity, and also in the surrounding areas including transmigration areas; (ii) arrangement and publication of forest and non-forest area boundaries on a cadastral scale; and (iii) delineation of customary territorial boundaries;",""],[1,"118","4","Land Bank Establishment and Land Services Modernization","Providing land for development in the public interest through the establishment of a land bank, and improvement of land services through modern, digital-based services and recruitment of civil servants as land measurement officers;",""],[2,"105","3","One Map Policy Implementation","masih adanya tumpang tindih perizinan pemanfaatan ruang yang akan diselesaikan melalui pelaksanaan kebijakan Satu Peta yang diintegrasikan dalam pelaksanaan Satu Data Indonesia.",""],[2,"111","15","Land Bank Establishment and Operationalization","Pembentukan dan operasionalisasi Bank Tanah",""],[2,"126","5","Land Bank for Public Interest Development","Penyediaan tanah bagi pembangunan untuk kepentingan umum melalui pembentukan bank tanah",""]],"125":[[1,"87","3","Climate-Resilient Sustainable Agricultural Resource Management","(4) maintaining sustainable productivity of agricultural resources that are adaptive to climate change, developing precision farming systems, improving land management, and strengthening irrigation;",""]],"126":[[1,"134","3","Coordination of Development Actors in Uplifted Disadvantaged Areas","guiding and aligning ministries/institutions and other development actors in disadvantaged areas that have been uplifted in 2019, for a maximum of 3 years (2020-2022);",""],[1,"135","1","Regional Government Capacity Strengthening","The implementation of regional autonomy is carried out through: (a) increasing the capacity of regional government (institutional, apparatus and. regional finance);",""],[1,"135","1","Sub-district Service and Development Center Strengthening","developing and strengthening the role of the sub- district as a center for data, information and knowledge, center for basic services, center for community empowerment, center for innovation and entrepreneurship development, center for natural resource management and the environment, and center for economic growth of the district;",""],[1,"135","1","Minimum Service Standards and Interregional Cooperation Expansion","accelerating the application of Minimum Service Standards (SPM), increasing investment licensing services, and expanding cooperation between regions.",""],[1,"137","2","Regional Autonomy Implementation Capacity Building","The implementation of regional autonomy is carried out through: (a) increasing the capacity of regional government (institutional, apparatus, and regional finance);",""],[1,"137","2","Sub-district Service and Development Strengthening","(b) developing and strengthening the role of the sub- district as a center for data, information and knowledge, center for basic services, center for community empowerment, center for innovation and entrepreneurship development, center for natural resource management and the environment, and",""],[1,"137","3","Minimum Service Standards Implementation and Investment Licensing Improvement","accelerating the application of Minimum Service Standards (SPM), increasing investment licensing services, and expanding regional cooperation",""],[1,"137","3","Metropolitan Inter-Regional Cooperation for Area Development","increasing cooperation between autonomous regions in metropolitan areas, including tourism, industrial, and island development areas",""],[1,"139","36","Regional Government Capacity Building for Autonomy Implementation","The implementation of regional autonomy is carried out through: (a) increasing the capacity of regional government (institutional, apparatus,",""],[1,"140","1","District Service Centers and Regional Cooperation Expansion","services, center for community empowerment, center for innovation and entrepreneurship development, center for natural resource management and the environment, and center for economic growth of the district; and (c) accelerating the application of Minimum Service Standards (SPM), increasing investment licensing services, and expanding cooperation between regions.",""],[1,"141","1","Coordination of Development Actors in Disadvantaged Areas","guiding and aligning ministries/institutions and other development actors in disadvantaged areas that have been uplifted in 2019, for a maximum of 3 years (2020-2022);",""],[1,"141","4","Regional Government Capacity Strengthening","The implementation of regional autonomy is carried out through: (a) increasing the capacity of regional government (institutional, apparatus, and regional finance);",""],[1,"141","4","Sub-district Service and Development Hub Strengthening","developing and strengthening the role of the sub- district as a data, information and knowledge center, center for basic services; center for community empowerment, center for innovation and entrepreneurship development, center for natural resource and environmental management, and center for economic growth of the district;",""],[1,"141","4","Minimum Service Standards Acceleration","accelerating the application of Minimum Service Standards (SPM), including sanitation and clean water, as well as waste management;",""],[1,"141","4","Investment Licensing Service Improvement","improving investment licensing services, and expanding cooperation between regions;",""],[1,"141","4","Interregional Cooperation Expansion","improving investment licensing services, and expanding cooperation between regions;",""],[1,"141","4","Regional Budget Fund Management Improvement","the management and quality of regional budget funds for specific regions and of the Aceh's Special Autonomy funds can continue to be improved.",""],[1,"143","8","Regional Autonomy Implementation Capacity Strengthening","The implementation of regional autonomy is carried out through: (a) increasing the capacity of regional government (institutional, apparatus, and regional finance);",""],[1,"143","8","Sub-district Service and Development Center Strengthening","developing and strengthening the role of the sub- district as a center for data, information and knowledge, center for basic services, center for community empowerment, center for innovation and entrepreneurship development, center for natural resource management and the environment, and center for economic growth of the district;",""],[1,"143","8","Minimum Service Standards Acceleration","accelerating the application of Minimum Service Standards (SPM) including sanitation,",""]],"127":[[1,"187","1","Mental Revolution National Movement","\"Mental Revolution\" is a national movement to change the perspective, attitude, and behavior of the people toward progress by internalizing the essential values of Mental Revolution in individuals, communities, families, social institutions, and state institutions.",""],[1,"187","5","Mental Revolution Movement","in the RPJMN 2020-2024, the Mental Revolution movement is developed to be more holistic and integrated on the basis of: (1) Mental Revolution in the education system by emphasizing the values of integrity, work ethic, mutual cooperation, and character in learning; (2) Mental Revolution in governance by acculturating the values of transparency and accountability; and (3) Mental Revolution in the social system",""],[1,"187","6","Mental Revolution and Social Cohesion Strengthening","the Mental Revolution is also strengthened through efforts to promote and preserve culture, strengthen religious moderation, and strengthen harmony; and enhancing the culture of literacy, innovation, and creativity for the realization of a knowledgeable, innovative, and creative society.",""],[1,"189","1","Pancasila Ideology Strengthening","Facing this problem, Pancasila as the foundation and ideology of the nation must be strengthened",""],[1,"189","2","Pancasila Ideology Development Board","Institutionally, the Government formed the Presidential Working Group for the Development of the Pancasila Ideology in 2017, which later was changed to the Pancasila Ideology Development Board in 2018.",""],[1,"189","2","Pancasila Ideology Policy and Strategy Formulation","This institution together with relevant ministries/institutions formulate policy directions and strategies to foster the ideology of Pancasila.","relevant ministries/institutions"],[1,"189","2","Pancasila Values Socialization and Internalization","This step forward needs to be followed by fostering and actualizing Pancasila for all citizens starting from the family and local communities.",""],[1,"195","2","Mental Revolution in Education System","Mental Revolution in the education system to strengthen integrity, work ethic, mutual cooperation, and character, including: (a) developing a learning culture and a bully-free school environment; (b) strengthening religious education, religious tolerance, and the students' character in the education system; and (c) promoting innovation and volunteerism, and elaborate scout educational values.",""],[1,"195","3","Mental Revolution in Governance","Mental Revolution in governance to strengthen righteous, attentive, and responsive bureaucratic culture, including: (a) improving public service work culture that is friendly, fast, effective, efficient, and reliable; and (b) incorporating discipline, rewards, and punishment in the bureaucracy.",""],[1,"195","6","Strengthening the Mental Revolution Movement Centers of Change","Strengthening the centers of change within the Mental Revolution movement, including: (a) strengthening the implementation of the five National Mental Revolution Movement programs to realize an Attentive Indonesia, Righteous Indonesia, Orderly Indonesia, Independent Indonesia, and United Indonesia; and (b) strengthening the centers of change within the Mental Revolution movement in various regions.",""],[1,"195","8","Pancasila and Civic Education Strengthening","fostering the ideology of Pancasila, civic education, the concept of being a nation, and a sense of duty to defend the country in order to foster the spirit of nationalism and patriotism, including: (a) fostering the ideology of Pancasila, strengthening civic education, national values, and national defense",""],[2,"177","4","Bhinneka Tunggal Ika Civic Education and Social Cohesion Program","Untuk memperkuat Bhinneka Tunggal Ika, kesadaran sebagai negara-bangsa yang majemuk harus ditanamkan sejak dini di dalam keluarga, diperkuat di dalam sistem pendidikan, dan terus dipupuk dan dirawat di dalam sistem sosial-kemasyarakatan.",""],[2,"177","5","Holistic and Integrated Mental Revolution Program","Untuk itu dalam RPJMN Tahun 2020-2024, revolusi mental terus dilanjutkan secara lebih holistik dan integratif yang bertumpu pada: (1) revolusi mental dalam sistem pendidikan dengan menekankan nilai-nilai integritas, etos kerja, gotong royong, dan budi pekerti dalam pembelajaran; (2) revolusi mental dalam tata kelola pemerintahan dengan pembudayaan nilai-nilai transparansi dan akuntabilitas; dan (3) revolusi mental dalam sistem sosial dengan pembudayaan nilai-nilai luhur budaya bangsa dalam institusi keluarga dan interaksi antarwarga.",""],[2,"179","2","Strengthening Pancasila as State Ideology","kedudukan Pancasila sebagai dasar dan ideologi negara harus diperkuat",""],[2,"179","3","Pancasila Ideology Development and Actualization","Untuk itu pembinaan dan aktualisasi Pancasila dalam setiap sendi kehidupan berbangsa dan bernegara mutlak diperlukan.",""],[2,"179","3","Pancasila Ideology Policy and Strategy Formulation","Lembaga ini bersama dengan Kementerian/Lembaga terkait menyusun arah kebijakan dan strategi pembinaan ideologi Pancasila.","Kementerian/Lembaga terkait"],[2,"179","3","Family and Community Pancasila Education","Langkah maju ini perlu diikuti dengan pembinaan dan aktualisasi Pancasila bagi seluruh warga negara mulai dari lingkup keluarga dan masyarakat.",""],[2,"179","4","Pancasila Development and Actualization Programme","Berbagai upaya pembinaan dan aktualisasi Pancasila yang dilaksanakan perlu ditingkatkan untuk merespons arus globalisasi yang membawa dampak sangat luas, baik sosial, budaya, ekonomi, maupun politik.",""],[2,"186","2","Mental Revolution and Pancasila Ideology Development","Revolusi mental dan pembinaan ideologi Pancasila untuk memperkukuh ketahanan budaya bangsa dan membentuk mentalitas bangsa yang maju, modern, dan berkarakter, melalui:",""],[2,"186","3","Mental Revolution in the Education System","Revolusi mental dalam sistem pendidikan untuk memperkuat nilai integritas, etos kerja, gotong royong, dan budi pekerti, mencakup: (a) pengembangan budaya belajar dan lingkungan sekolah yang menyenangkan dan bebas dari kekerasan (bullying free school environment); (b) penguatan pendidikan agama, nilai toleransi beragama, dan budi pekerti dalam sistem pendidikan; dan (c) peningkatan kepeloporan dan kesukarelawanan pemuda, serta pengembangan pendidikan kepramukaan.",""],[2,"186","4","Mental Revolution in Public Governance","Revolusi mental dalam tata kelola pemerintahan untuk penguatan budaya birokrasi yang bersih, melayani, dan responsif, mencakup: (a) peningkatan budaya kerja pelayanan publik yang ramah, cepat, efektif, efisien, dan terpercaya; dan (b) penerapan disiplin, penghargaan (reward) dan sanksi (punishment) dalam birokrasi.",""],[2,"186","6","Strengthening of Mental Revolution Change Centers","Penguatan pusat-pusat perubahan gerakan revolusi mental, mencakup: (a) pemantapan pelaksanaan lima program Gerakan Nasional Revolusi Mental untuk mewujudkan Indonesia Melayani, Indonesia Bersih, Indonesia Tertib, Indonesia Mandiri, dan Indonesia Bersatu; dan (b) penguatan pusat-pusat perubahan gerakan revolusi mental di daerah.",""],[2,"186","8","Pancasila Ideology and Civic Education Strengthening","Pembinaan ideologi Pancasila, pendidikan kewargaan, wawasan kebangsaan, dan bela negara untuk menumbuhkan jiwa nasionalisme dan patriotisme, mencakup: (a) pembinaan ideologi Pancasila, penguatan pendidikan kewargaan, nilai-nilai kebangsaan, dan bela negara;",""],[2,"186","8","Strengthening the Pancasila Ideology Development Agency","(b) peningkatan peran dan fungsi Badan Pembinaan Ideologi Pancasila (BPIP);",""],[2,"186","8","Legal Harmonization and Review for Pancasila Alignment","(c) harmonisasi dan evaluasi peraturan perundang-undangan yang bertentangan dengan ideologi Pancasila;",""],[2,"186","8","Removal of Threatening Elements to State Ideology","(d) membersihkan unsur-unsur yang mengancam ideologi negara.",""]],"128":[[1,"224","1","Integrated Road Traffic Safety Implementation","Improving traffic safety and road transport is directed through the integrated implementation of the five pillars of road safety, which include management of road safety, safe roads, safe vehicles, safe behavior of road users, and management of pre- and post-traffic accidents.",""],[1,"224","2","National Road Safety Action Plan Framework","This policy was strengthened by the issuance of Presidential Regulation on the National General Plan for Traffic Safety and Road Transportation (RUNK LLAJ) that contains road safety action plans for each pillar.",""],[1,"224","2","Multi-Stakeholder Road Safety Coordination Mechanism","Road safety management needs to focus on strengthening coordination among stakeholders in ministries/institutions at the levels of the central government, regional government, education and research institution, business entities, and community organizations.",""],[1,"224","2","Institutional Strengthening for Road Safety Planning and Implementation","Institutional strengthening is needed at both the central and regional levels through coordination, use of data and information, and research activities that can serve as the basis for planning and implementing national road safety action plans.",""],[1,"224","3","Transport Safety Policy Strengthening","safety policies are directed at strengthening the role of institutions, improving the safety of",""],[1,"224","6","Traffic Safety and Road Transport Action Plans","Implementing action plans for the five pillars of traffic safety and road transport",""],[1,"224","6","Transportation Safety and Search and Rescue Facilities Upgrade","Fulfilling the needs of facilities, infrastructure, institutions, transportation safety and security information systems, and search and rescue operations (SAR)",""],[1,"224","6","Transportation Safety and SAR Human Resource Development","Developing and educating human resources on transportation safety and SAR",""],[1,"229","4","Integrated Weighbridge System for Road Overloading Control","The development of land transportation is prioritized to reduce the practice of road overloading by implementing weighbridges that are integrated with the",""],[1,"229","7","Road Operations and Interstate Terminal Development","road operations (KPBU-AP scheme), developing road facilities and tools, and constructing interstate terminals to support the ease of flow of passengers",""],[2,"212","6","Integrated Five-Pillar Road Safety Implementation","Peningkatan keselamatan lalu lintas dan angkutan jalan diarahkan melalui pelaksanaan terpadu lima pilar keselamatan jalan yang meliputi manajemen keselamatan jalan, jalan yang berkeselamatan, kendaraan yang berkeselamatan, perilaku pengguna jalan yang berkeselamatan, dan penanganan pra dan pasca kecelakaan lalu lintas.",""],[2,"212","7","National Road Safety Action Plan Regulation","Kebijakan ini diperkuat dengan penerbitan regulasi Peraturan Presiden tentang Rencana Umum Nasional Keselamatan Lalu Lintas dan Angkutan Jalan (RUNK LLAJ) yang memuat rencana aksi keselamatan jalan pada masing-masing pilar.",""],[2,"212","7","Road Safety Coordination Strengthening","Manajemen keselamatan jalan perlu berfokus pada penguatan koordinasi antarunit kerja pemangku kepentingan pada kementerian/lembaga tingkat pemerintah pusat, pemerintah daerah, lembaga pendidikan dan penelitian, badan usaha dan organisasi masyarakat.",""],[2,"212","7","Road Safety Institutional Strengthening","Diperlukan penguatan kelembagaan baik di tingkat pusat maupun di tingkat daerah yang dilakukan melalui keterpaduan koordinasi, pemanfaatan data dan informasi, dan kegiatan penelitian yang dapat menjadi basis bagi perencanaan dan pelaksanaan rencana aksi keselamatan jalan nasional.",""],[2,"212","8","Transport Safety Institutional Strengthening and Capacity Building","Untuk moda transportasi lainnya, kebijakan keselamatan diarahkan pada penguatan peran kelembagaan, peningkatan kelaikan keselamatan sarana dan prasarana, serta peningkatan kapasitas SDM untuk mendukung kinerja keselamatan.",""],[2,"212","8","Railway Safety Infrastructure Provision and Maintenance","Peningkatan keselamatan perkeretaapian dilakukan melalui penyediaan sarana dan prasarana perkeretaapian yang memenuhi kelaikan, termasuk sarana kereta, prasarana rel dan persinyalan.",""],[2,"212","8","Railway Infrastructure Maintenance Requirement","Untuk menjamin kondisi prasarana perkeretaapian maka kebutuhan perawatan prasarana harus dipenuhi.",""],[2,"213","2","Maritime and Ferry Transport Safety Improvement","Keselamatan transportasi laut dan penyeberangan ditingkatkan melalui penguatan kelembagaan syahbandar, penyediaan infrastruktur keselamatan, standardisasi kapal yang memenuhi aspek keselamatan, dan pengembangan sistem informasi penumpang (tiket) dan barang (manifes) untuk mencegah muatan berlebih.",""],[2,"213","3","Five-Pillar Road Traffic Safety Action Plan Implementation","Pelaksanaan rencana aksi lima pilar keselamatan lalu lintas dan angkutan jalan;",""],[2,"213","3","Transport Safety and SAR Facilities and Information Systems Upgrade","Pemenuhan sarana, prasarana, fasilitas, kelembagaan dan sistem informasi keselamatan dan keamanan transportasi dan SAR;",""],[2,"213","3","Transport Safety and SAR Human Resource Development","Pembinaan dan pendidikan SDM keselamatan transportasi dan SAR.",""],[2,"276","22","National Road Safety Master Plan","RPerpres Rencana Umum Nasional Keselamatan Jalan",""]],"129":[[1,"291","27","National Strategy for Accelerating Development of Underdeveloped Regions (STRANAS-PPDT) Draft Presidential Regulation","Perpres draft on the national strategy for the acceleration of development of underdeveloped regions (STRANAS-PPDT) in the 2020-2024 period (revokes the Perpres on 2015-2019 STRANAS PPDT)",""],[1,"292","1","Annual National Action Plan for Accelerating Development of Disadvantaged Regions","Perpres draft on the yearly national action plan for the acceleration of development of disadvantaged regions (RAN- PPDT)",""],[1,"292","2","Draft Presidential Regulation on Determining Underdeveloped Regions","Perpres draft on determining underdeveloped regions for the 2020-2024 period (revokes Perpres No. 131/2015 concerning the determination of underdeveloped regions in 2015- 2019)",""],[2,"274","15","National Strategy for Accelerating Development of Disadvantaged Regions 2020-2024","RPerpres tentang Strategi Nasional Percepatan Pembangunan Daerah Tertinggal (STRANAS-PPDT) 2020-2024",""],[2,"274","16","Annual Presidential Regulation on the National Action Plan for Accelerating Development of Disadvantaged Regions","RPerpres tentang Rencana Aksi Nasional Percepatan Pembangunan Daerah Tertinggal (RAN-PPDT) Setiap Tahun",""],[2,"274","17","Presidential Regulation on Designation of Disadvantaged Areas 2020-2024","RPerpres tentang Penetapan Daerah Tertinggal 2020-2024 (mencabut Perpres Nomor 131 Tahun 2015 tentang Penetapan Daerah Tertinggal 2015-2019)",""],[2,"287","4","Affirmative Action Scheme for Disadvantaged and Border Areas","serta mendorong tindakan afirmatif (skema afirmasi) bagi daerah-daerah tertinggal, terluar dan terdepan, kawasan perbatasan, pulau-pulau kecil terluar dan daerah berciri kepulauan;",""]],"130":[[1,"292","17","Revision of the National Social Security Law","a. Revision of Law No. 40/2004 on the national social security system.",""],[1,"292","28","Revision of Work Accident and Life Insurance Regulation","Revision of PP No. 22/2015 on implementing work accident insurance and life insurance.",""],[1,"292","29","Revision of Pension Benefits Regulation","Revision of PP No. 45/2015 on implementing pension benefits.",""],[1,"293","1","Revision of Retirement Plan Implementation Regulation","Revision of PP No. 46/2015 on implementing retirement plans.",""],[1,"293","2","Revision of Old Retirement Plan Regulations","Revision of PP No. 60/2015 on amendments to PP No. 46/2015 concerning the implementation of old retirement plans.",""],[1,"293","3","Revision of Health Insurance Beneficiary Regulations","Revision of PP No. 76/2015 on changes to PP No. 101/2012 concerning beneficiaries of health insurance schemes.",""],[1,"293","22","Revision of Cashless Social Assistance Presidential Regulation","Revision of Perpres No. 63/2017 on cashless social assistance.",""],[1,"293","23","Revision of Presidential Regulation No. 15/2010 on Accelerating Poverty Reduction Programs","Revision of Perpres No. 15/2010 on accelerating poverty reduction programs.",""],[1,"293","24","Revision of Poverty Reduction Acceleration Presidential Regulation","Revision of Perpres No. 96/2015 on amendments to Perpres No. 15/2010 concerning poverty reduction acceleration.",""],[2,"274","29","Revision of the National Social Security System Law","Revisi UU Nomor 40 Tahun 2004 Tentang Sistem Jaminan Sosial Nasional",""],[2,"275","9","Revision of Government Regulation No. 44 of 2015 on Employment Injury and Death Insurance","Revisi PP Nomor 44 Tahun 2015 tentang Penyelenggaraan Jaminan Kecelakaan Kerja dan Jaminan Kematian",""],[2,"275","12","Revision of the Old-Age Security Regulation","4) Revisi PP Nomor 60 tahun 2015 tentang Perubahan atas peraturan PP Nomor 46 Tahun 2015 tentang Penyelenggaraan Jaminan Hari Tua (JHT)",""],[2,"275","13","Revision of Health Insurance Premium Assistance Regulation","Revisi PP Nomor 76 Tahun 2015 tentang Perubahan Atas Peraturan Pemerintah Nomor 101 Tahun 2012 tentang Penerima Bantuan Iuran Jaminan Kesehatan",""],[2,"275","29","Revision of Presidential Regulation No. 46/2014 on the National Social Security Council","Revisi Perpres Nomor 46 Tahun 2014 tentang Susunan Organisasi dan Tata Kerja, Tata Cara Pengangkatan, Penggantian, dan Pemberhentian anggota Dewan Jaminan Sosial Nasional",""],[2,"276","13","Presidential Regulation on Integration of Social Assistance and Targeted Subsidies","RPerpres tentang Integrasi Bantuan Sosial dan Subsidi Tepat Sasaran",""],[2,"276","16","Adaptive Social Protection Presidential Regulation","23) RPerpres tentang Perlindungan Sosial Adaptif",""]],"131":[[1,"292","18","Revision of Population Growth and Family Development Law","b. Revision of Law No. 52/2009 on population growth and family development.",""],[2,"143","3","Population Control and Governance Strengthening","kebijakan pembangunan manusia diarahkan pada pengendalian penduduk dan penguatan tata kelola kependudukan",""],[2,"143","3","Basic Services and Social Protection Expansion","pemenuhan pelayanan dasar dan perlindungan sosial",""],[2,"143","3","Child, Women, and Youth Development Initiative","peningkatan kualitas anak, perempuan dan pemuda",""],[2,"143","3","Poverty Reduction Policy","pengentasan kemiskinan",""],[2,"143","3","Labor Force Productivity and Competitiveness Enhancement","peningkatan produktivitas dan daya saing angkatan kerja",""],[2,"143","3","Life-Cycle and Inclusive Human Development Approach","Kebijakan pembangunan manusia tersebut dilakukan berdasarkan pendekatan siklus hidup, dan inklusif termasuk memperhatikan kebutuhan penduduk usia lanjut maupun penduduk penyandang disabilitas, dan pengelolaan SDM bertalenta.",""],[2,"157","3","Mass Sports Promotion and Sports Culture Development","Pembangunan budaya olahraga perlu ditempuh melalui pemassalan olahraga untuk mengembangkan kesadaran masyarakat dalam meningkatkan kesehatan, kebugaran, kegembiraan, dan hubungan sosial.",""],[2,"157","4","Systematic Development Facilitation Strengthening","Dibutuhkan upaya yang lebih sistematis untuk penguatan pendampingan pembangunan agar berbagai program yang dilaksanakan pemerintah, dunia usaha dan masyarakat menjadi lebih efisien, efektif dan mencapai tujuan yang diharapkan.",""]],"132":[[1,"304","4","Phased Fulfillment of Minimum Service Standards","Encouraging, in stages, the fulfillment of minimum service standards, especially basic services that local governments are obliged to provide by taking into account the regional fiscal capacity, country's financial capacity, and affirmative action in disadvantaged, outermost and frontier regions, border areas, small outermost islands, and island groups;",""]],"133":[[2,"274","7","Revision of Village Law Implementation Regulation","Revisi Peraturan Pemerintah Nomor 43 Tahun 2014 tentang Peraturan Pelaksanaan Undang-Undang Nomor 6 Tahun 2014 tentang Desa",""],[2,"288","5","Village Fund Optimization for Sustainable Village Development","Mendorong pemerintah desa untuk mengoptimalkan pemanfaatan Dana Desa untuk: (a) mewujudkan kemandirian masyarakat desa dan menciptakan desa- desa berkelanjutan yang memiliki ketahanan sosial, ekonomi, dan ekologi; (b) meningkatkan pelayanan dasar dan prasarana dasar desa; (c) meningkatkan kapasitas aparatur desa dalam tata kelola pemerintahan yang baik; (d) mengembangkan sistem informasi desa terpadu termasuk penataan wilayah desa dan penetapan batas desa; (e) transformasi ekonomi desa melalui pengembangan desa wisata, desa digital, produk unggulan desa, pengembangan kawasan perdesaan, dan peningkatan peran Badan Usaha Milik Desa (BUMDes)/BUMDes Bersama; dan (f) penguatan dan pengembangan desa adat, kampung adat, nagari dan sebutan lain setara dengan desa;",""],[2,"288","6","Village Fund Allocation Improvement and Performance Incentives","Menyempurnakan pengalokasian Dana Desa dengan memperhatikan keadilan dan keberpihakan (afirmasi) kepada desa-desa tertinggal dan pemberian insentif bagi desa yang mempunyai kinerja sangat baik;",""],[2,"289","2","Village Fund Coordination and Management Strengthening","Memperkuatkoordinasi, kerjasamadan kemitraandalam perencanaan, pengalokasian, penganggaran, penyaluran, pelaporan, pemantauan, pengendalian dan evaluasi dana desa dengan mengembangkan: (a) data dasar dan sistem informasi terpadu berbasis website, (b) pendampingan pemerintah daerah, termasuk pengembangan dan penguatan peran kecamatan sebagai pusat pelayanan, pemberdayaan dan pertumbuhan, melalui Dana APBD dalam optimalisasi pengelolaan Dana Desa, (c) pengendalian penyaluran berbasis kinerja, dan (d) pelaporan secara rutin;",""],[2,"289","3","Inter-Village Village Fund Development Program","Meningkatkan pemanfaatan Dana Desa untuk kegiatan pembangunan antardesa termasuk pembagian kewenangan dan batas desa, kepemilikan aset, dan tanggung jawab operasional dan pemeliharaan.",""]],"134":[[2,"168","5","Health Workforce Competency and Redistribution Support","Pemenuhan dan peningkatan kompetensi tenaga kesehatan yang difokuskan pada afirmasi pemenuhan tenaga kesehatan strategis termasuk pengembangan paket pelayanan kesehatan (tenaga kesehatan, farmasi dan alat kesehatan); afirmasi pendidikan (beasiswa dan tugas belajar) tenaga kesehatan di daerah tertinggal, perbatasan, dan kepulauan (DTPK) dan daerah kurang diminati; afirmasi pendayagunaan dan mekanisme redistribusi tenaga kesehatan yang",""],[2,"169","2","Health Workforce Fulfillment and Deployment Mechanism","pengembangan mekanisme kerjasama pemenuhan tenaga kesehatan melalui penugasan sementara dan kontrak pelayanan; perluasan pendidikan dan pelatihan tenaga kesehatan fokus pada pelayanan kesehatan dasar; pengembangan tenaga kesehatan untuk penguatan fungsi pelayanan kesehatan dasar seperti promosi kesehatan dan perawat komunitas; penyesuaian program studi dan lembaga pendidikan bidang kesehatan dengan kebutuhan dan standar; dan pemenuhan tenaga kesehatan sesuai standar dan tenaga non-kesehatan termasuk tenaga sistem informasi dan administrasi keuangan untuk mendukung tata kelola di fasilitas pelayanan kesehatan;",""]],"135":[[1,"16","5","Production and Distribution Connectivity Infrastructure Development","Continue developing infrastructure to connect production areas to distribution areas, facilitating access to tourist sites, boosting employment, and accelerating the increase in value-added of the local economy.",""],[1,"18","2","Tollway, Road, and Ferry Port Development","Tollways, new roads, trans- roads on frontier, outermost, and least developed islands (or 3T), new ferry ports",""],[1,"33","26","Infrastructure Development for Connectivity and Energy","Continue to develop infrastructure, especially for connectivity and energy, to support economic expansion and inclusive growth",""],[1,"34","4","Government and SOE Infrastructure Investment Expansion","Increased investment is also driven by increased government investment, among others from state owned enterprises (BUMN), especially for infrastructure development.",""],[1,"57","3","Transportation and Distribution Access Improvement for Leading Commodities","Increase accessibility of transportation and distribution of leading commodities",""],[1,"58","23","Industrial Zone Port Connectivity Improvement","Connect industrial zones with Garongkong Port and Makassar New Port",""],[1,"59","3","Port Performance Standardization and Domestic Shipping Efficiency Improvement","Increase port performance by standardizing major ports; increase efficiency of domestic shipping routes by forming loops regularly to 27%; and increase port integration with hinterland regions",""],[1,"60","3","Semarang-Demak Travel Time Reduction Project","Reduce travel time between Semarang and Demak from 1 hour to 25 minutes",""],[1,"60","12","Connectivity and Mobility Improvement","Increase connectivity and mobility of goods and passengers to reduce commodity prices",""],[1,"101","5","Growth Corridor Development Acceleration","The growth corridor is oriented to spur national economic growth by accelerating the development of growth areas, including national activity centers (PKN), regional activity centers (PKW), special economic zones, industrial estates (KI), national tourism strategic areas (KSPN), as well as cities and urban agglomeration areas in regencies/cities located along the growth corridors.",""],[1,"132","1","Transport and Intermodal Connectivity Infrastructure Development","Strengthening connectivity is carried out through: (a) constructing roads, seaports, and airports; and (b) developing and strengthening integrated intermodal connectivity via sea, river, land, and air, particularly hubs that serve raw commodities and processed goods.",""],[1,"133","4","Integrated Intermodal Connectivity Development","Strengthening connectivity is carried out through: (a) developing and strengthening integrated intermodal connectivity via sea, river, land, and air; and (b) developing telecommunications and information network.",""]],"136":[[1,"19","27","Oil Refinery Development and Expansion","Development and expansion of oil refineries (2 grassroots refineries and 4 existing refineries as part of the Refinery Development Master Plan (RDMP))",""],[1,"59","10","Oil Refinery Development and Expansion","Developing and expanding oil refineries",""],[1,"59","11","Oil Production Capacity Expansion","Increase oil production capacity to 1.9 million barrels a day by 2026",""]],"137":[[1,"24","4","Regional Development Integration with Spatial Data","Regional development is intended to boost economic growth and fulfill the needs for basic services by integrating development with spatial data.",""],[1,"65","3","Cross-Sectoral Policy Integration Framework","These two approaches form the foundation for integration of cross-sectoral policies that cover food, agriculture, fishery, maritime affairs, marine affairs, manufacturing, tourism, and the creative economy and digital economy.",""],[1,"112","2","Integrated Regional Development Coordination Mechanism","Regional development is carried out in an integrated manner by prioritizing cooperation and integration of programs and activities between ministries and institutions, between ministries/institutions and regional governments, between regional governments themselves, and between the government and business entities in planning, funding, financing, implementing, controlling, and evaluating development.",""],[1,"113","2","Growth Corridor and Regional Growth Center Development","The growth corridor approach prioritizes the development of growth centers -- on the basis of regional excellence -- that can encourage value-added, increase, and/or save foreign exchange earnings, expand employment opportunities and real economic growth in the next five years.",""],[1,"114","7","Development of Priority Strategic Growth Areas","Optimizing the development of priority strategic areas as centers of regional growth, namely Special Economic Zones (KEK), Industrial Estates (KI), Free Trade Areas and Ports (KPBPB), Priority Tourism Destinations, and other zones that",""],[1,"115","1","Regional Commodity Downstreaming and Infrastructure Support","strengthening the production base and processing of regional leading commodities that are spread throughout centers of downstream agriculture and fishery in the National Priority Rural Areas (KPPN), transmigration areas, National Strategic Activity Centers (PKSN), and Integrated Marine Fishery Centers (SKPT)/Fishery Management Areas (WPP); (ii) constructing smelters in potential areas to support the downstreaming of natural resources; (iii) providing integrated infrastructure networks that include transportation networks (roads, ports, airports, and others), energy systems (electricity, gas, solar, coal, and others), raw water and clean water facilities, and sewage treatment systems; (iv) fast licensing and investment services; (v) strengthening connectivity with raw material production centers in rural areas, transmigration areas, small and medium cities in the procurement of raw and supporting materials; (vi) developing cooperation and partnerships in financing government and business entities; (vii) strengthening cooperation between regional governments, management bodies, communities, universities. and the",""],[1,"117","10","Strengthening the Governor's Role in Regional Development Coordination","Strengthening the role of the governor as a representative of the central government in the coordination and control of regional development;",""]],"138":[[1,"36","2","Fiscal Incentives for Value-Adding Investment","These plans are also balanced with the role of taxation policymaking as an instrument to encourage investment by providing fiscal incentives that support activities that add value, especially in manufacturing, tourism, and the creative and digital economy.",""],[1,"86","7","Fiscal Incentives for New and Renewable Energy","The development of renewable energy potential is supported by fiscal incentives for the new and renewable energy sector.",""],[1,"95","4","Export Incentives and Import Facilitation for Exporters","The strategy for increasing and expanding exports, and for managing imports is also implemented in synergy with the strategy for increasing participation in the global production chain, among others by providing fiscal incentives for access to raw materials through easing import on exporters.",""],[1,"97","2","Fiscal Incentives for Competitiveness and Business Support","Optimization of state revenue is directed to support competitiveness with more realistic and optimal targets, which are accompanied by fiscal incentives that support the economy and businesses.",""]],"139":[[1,"48","2","High-Quality Public Investment Framework","These targets can be achieved through high-quality public investment, particularly investment that: 1) is well- targeted and on schedule; 2) has a positive impact that is both significant and sustainable; 3) consistent with the direction of policies, programs, and development plans; and 4) makes efficient use of resources and funding.",""],[1,"48","6","High-Leverage Development Investment Promotion","Funding for development is prioritized for meeting the basic needs of citizens by implementing minimum service standards and boosting investment that provides high leverage for national development.",""],[1,"54","5","Major Projects Funding and Implementation Update Mechanism","The progress of the Major Projects and their funding data can be updated through the government work plans (RKP) by first studying the readiness of their implementation, and later updating the amount and sources of funding while considering the President's directives.",""],[1,"54","6","Major Projects Development Control and Monitoring Mechanism","the Major Projects also serve as a tool for development control so that the development targets of the 2020- 2024 RPJMN can be continuously monitored and controlled.",""]],"140":[[1,"48","6","Minimum Service Standards Implementation","Funding for development is prioritized for meeting the basic needs of citizens by implementing minimum service standards and boosting investment that provides high leverage for national development.",""],[1,"48","6","Basic Service Delivery by Central and Regional Governments","The central and regional governments are directed toward providing basic services to citizens, while business entities, both BUMN and private, are focused on strengthening economic growth and achieving development targets.",""],[1,"129","5","Basic Services Improvement and Regional Disparity Reduction","Improving basic services, including: (a) improving the quality of human resources; (b) accelerating development of hilly and mountainous areas to reduce regional disparity between coastal and mountainous areas, and to take into account the region of Papua contextually; (c) accelerating development of disadvantaged areas with a focus on meeting basic services, improving connectivity, and developing infrastructure including service networks/internet access; (d) guiding and aligning ministries/institutions and other development actors in disadvantaged areas that have been uplifted in 2019, for a maximum of 3 years (2020-2022);",""],[1,"132","7","Basic Services Enhancement Programme","Enhancing basic services that include: (a) enhancing the quality of human resources, especially increasing access to education and health services, (b) accelerating the development of disadvantaged areas by focusing on meeting basic services, increasing human resource capacity, and developing the",""],[1,"133","3","Minimum Service Standards Implementation Acceleration","accelerating the application of Minimum Service Standards (SPM)",""]],"141":[[1,"56","3","Aquaculture Production Expansion","Increase aquaculture production (of fish to 10.32 million tons)",""],[1,"56","3","Shrimp Export Growth Target","Increase shrimp exports to 8% p.a.",""],[1,"88","8","Aquaculture Production and Sustainable Fisheries Development","The third strategy is to accelerate aquaculture production, develop modern and sustainable aquaculture clusters, revitalize shrimp and milkfish ponds, and expand cultivated lands; develop a system for leading hatcheries; develop capture fishery that is economical and sustainable, promote fishery exploration in KEK and open seas, strengthen cooperation between small and large fishery, develop eco-friendly fishing",""],[1,"89","5","Fishery Product Development for Export and Food Security","Main fishery products include tuna, skipjack, cob, small crab, shrimp, tilapia, catfish, milkfish, seaweed, and other commodities of high economic value that are to be developed in support of export targets and food security.",""],[1,"89","6","Aquaculture and Marine Product Development Centers","Shrimp-based products will be developed in Sumatra, West Nusa Tenggara, Java, and Sulawesi; tilapia- based products in Sumatra, Java, and Sulawesi; seaweed-based products in Nusa Tenggara, Sulawesi, Maluku and Kalimantan; and lastly salt production centers in Java, Sumatra, Sulawesi, and Nusa Tenggara.",""]],"142":[[1,"58","11","Social Assistance Targeting Improvement","Improve targeting accuracy and effectiveness of social assistance programs",""],[1,"58","11","Cashless and Formal Financial Services Expansion","Increase coverage of cashless and formal financial services, especially for the poor and vulnerable",""]],"143":[[1,"61","19","Trans-Kalimantan Gas Pipeline Connection","Connect the national gas pipelines in Kalimantan (Trans- Kalimantan)",""],[1,"61","19","Natural Gas Supply Expansion for Industry, Power, and Domestic Networks","Fulfill needs for natural gas in the industrial sector; for electricity generation; and fulfill the needs of the domestic and commercial gas network in Kalimantan",""],[1,"61","19","Natural Gas Supply for the New Capital City","Provide energy for the new capital city",""],[1,"61","19","Natural Gas Utilization Expansion in Natuna","Increase the use of natural gas in the Natuna region",""],[1,"67","5","Expansion of Natural Gas Access and Pipeline Networks","Access to other energy sources such as natural gas has been continually expanded.",""],[1,"86","3","Domestic Natural Gas and Coal Utilization and Coal Gasification Development","Natural gas and coal production will be focused on: (1) domestic use where natural gas and coal are used as an energy source and as raw materials for various industries to increase economic value-added; and (2) the coal gasification industry to meet domestic industrial demand for raw materials.",""]],"144":[[1,"61","21","Toxic and Hazardous Waste Processing Facilities","Constructing processing facilities for toxic and hazardous waste",""]],"145":[[1,"91","1","Industrial Policy Harmonization and Supply Chain Efficiency Reform","chains by harmonizing policies that affect the efficiency of the input- processing-output-distribution flow, and of suppliers;",""],[1,"91","1","Industrial Product Diversification and Quality Improvement","(3) diversifying and improving the quality of upstream, intermediate, and downstream industrial products for the supply of raw materials, intermediate or auxiliary goods, and finished goods;",""],[1,"91","1","Industrial Machinery Development and Rural Industrial Expansion","(4) expanding machinery development to maintain industrial machinery and expand industrial activities in rural areas;",""],[1,"91","1","Industrial Standardization and Certification Strengthening","(5) strengthening the process of standardization and certification for industries;",""],[1,"91","1","Industrial Services Strengthening","(6) strengthening industrial services;",""],[1,"91","1","Modern Industrial Management Adoption","(7) strengthening the application of modern industrial management;",""],[1,"91","1","Circular Economy Promotion for Industrial Efficiency","(8) strengthening circular economy as a source of efficiency and value-added;",""],[1,"91","1","Industrial Financing Incentive Scheme","(9) providing incentives for the growth and scaling-up of industries through industrial financing.",""]],"146":[[1,"60","3","Tidal Flood Mitigation in Coastal Cities","Overcome tidal floods in Jakarta, Semarang, Pekalongan, Demak, and Cirebon",""],[1,"118","5","Community Climate Adaptation in Disaster-Prone Areas","adapting communities to climate change in disaster-prone areas;",""],[1,"118","5","Coastal Abrasion Control Measures","increasing efforts to stymie coastal abrasion that can threaten borders.",""],[1,"132","3","Climate Change Adaptation in Disaster-Prone Areas","adapting the people to climate change in disaster-prone areas based on local wisdom, with a primary focus on improving the resilience of watersheds",""],[1,"132","3","Climate Mitigation and Disaster Risk Reduction Investment","increasing investment in climate change mitigation and disaster risk reduction",""],[1,"132","3","Coastal Abrasion and Forest Conservation Management","improving management of coastal abrasion in island areas, and of forest conservation",""],[1,"133","26","Climate Change Mitigation and Disaster Risk Reduction Investment","increasing investment in climate change mitigation and disaster risk reduction",""]],"147":[[1,"118","5","Multi-Sector Climate and Disaster Risk Partnership Expansion","expanding and strengthening multi-sector partnerships in climate change mitigation and disaster risk reduction;",""]],"148":[[1,"87","2","National Priority Lake Revitalization Program","Maintenance, recovery, and conservation for lake revitalization are focused on 15 national priority lakes, namely: Danau Toba, Danau Maninjau, Danau Singkarak, Danau Kerinci, Danau Rawa Danau, Danau Rawa Pening, Danau Batur, Danau Sentarum, Danau Kaskade Mahakam (Semayang-Melintang-Jeumpang), Danau Tondano, Danau Limboto, Danau Poso, Danau Tempe, Danau Matano, and Danau Sentani.",""]],"149":[[1,"87","3","Food Consumption Quality and Safety Improvement Strategy","(iii) Increasing availability, access, and quality of food consumption, which will be carried out using the following strategies: (1) improving the quality of consumption, safety, food enrichment, and seed biofortification;",""],[1,"87","4","Biofortified Rice and Food Quality Improvement Initiative","The implementation of the first strategy incorporates the development of biofortified rice seeds, genetically engineered products, enriched rice, food nanotechnology, local produce, food diversification at the household level, and improvements to food quality for school children.",""]],"150":[[1,"87","3","Food Systems Governance Improvement","(5) improving governance of food systems.",""]],"151":[[1,"87","5","Agricultural Corridor Development in South Kalimantan","develop agricultural corridors based on cooperative farming in South Kalimantan, which will provide food and agricultural support for the new capital city.",""]],"152":[[1,"89","1","Port Development and Marine Fisheries Infrastructure Programme","ports, develop digital-based fishery, expand and intensify salt flats, improve salt quality, develop marine and fishery centers, and strengthen the fish quarantine system.",""],[1,"89","1","Marine and Fisheries Centers Development Programme","develop marine and fishery centers",""]],"153":[[1,"89","1","Fish Quarantine System Strengthening","strengthen the fish quarantine system.",""]],"154":[[1,"89","1","Salt Flat Expansion and Salt Quality Improvement Programme","expand and intensify salt flats, improve salt quality",""],[1,"89","5","Domestic Salt Production Development","In addition, salt production continues to be developed to meet domestic consumption needs.",""]],"155":[[1,"90","1","Export-Oriented Financial Incentives for MSMEs","the development of entrepreneurial capacity and UMKM is supported by the provision of export-oriented financial incentives.",""]],"156":[[1,"129","3","Conservation Area Expansion and Low-Carbon Development Support","and increasing conservation areas and environmental carrying capacity for low carbon development.",""],[1,"131","4","Natural Resource Management and Environment Center","center for natural resource management and the environment;",""]],"157":[[1,"130","3","Local Economic Development and Entrepreneur Empowerment","local economic development and empowerment of local entrepreneurs",""],[1,"131","4","Papuan Human Resources Placement in State-Owned Enterprises and Institutions","optimizing leading native Papuan human resources in BUMN and ministries/institutions;",""],[1,"131","4","Papua Youth Creative Hub","developing innovation and creativity of young Papuans (Papua Youth Creative Hub);",""],[1,"131","4","Local Entrepreneur Empowerment Programme","empowering local entrepreneurs;",""],[1,"132","8","Digital Local Economy Development","local economy based on leading commodities by utilizing digital technology;",""]],"158":[[1,"133","3","Investment Licensing Service Improvement","increasing investment licensing services",""],[1,"133","3","Interregional Cooperation Expansion","expanding cooperation between regions",""]],"159":[[1,"134","1","MICE Industry Development","The development policy for Nusa Tenggara is directed at encouraging economic transformation by strengthening its role as a gateway to ecological tourism through developing the Meeting, Incentive, Convention, Exhibition (MICE) industry;",""],[1,"134","1","Culture-Based Creative Industry Development","The development policy for Nusa Tenggara is directed at encouraging economic transformation by strengthening its role as a gateway to ecological tourism through developing the Meeting, Incentive, Convention, Exhibition (MICE) industry; culture-based creative industry; accelerating maritime-based economic development through the development of the fishery, salt, and seaweed industries; developing cattle-based industry and corn plantations; and developing the manganese and copper industries.",""],[1,"134","1","Maritime-Based Economic Development","The development policy for Nusa Tenggara is directed at encouraging economic transformation by strengthening its role as a gateway to ecological tourism through developing the Meeting, Incentive, Convention, Exhibition (MICE) industry; culture-based creative industry; accelerating maritime-based economic development through the development of the fishery, salt, and seaweed industries; developing cattle-based industry and corn plantations; and developing the manganese and copper industries.",""],[1,"134","1","Livestock and Corn Plantation Development","The development policy for Nusa Tenggara is directed at encouraging economic transformation by strengthening its role as a gateway to ecological tourism through developing the Meeting, Incentive, Convention, Exhibition (MICE) industry; culture-based creative industry; accelerating maritime-based economic development through the development of the fishery, salt, and seaweed industries; developing cattle-based industry and corn plantations; and developing the manganese and copper industries.",""],[1,"134","1","Manganese and Copper Industry Development","The development policy for Nusa Tenggara is directed at encouraging economic transformation by strengthening its role as a gateway to ecological tourism through developing the Meeting, Incentive, Convention, Exhibition (MICE) industry; culture-based creative industry; accelerating maritime-based economic development through the development of the fishery, salt, and seaweed industries; developing cattle-based industry and corn plantations; and developing the manganese and copper industries.",""],[1,"134","5","Regional Growth Center Strengthening Program","Strengthening regional growth centers, among others through: (a) developing leading commodities in Nusa Tenggara, namely pepper, nutmeg, cloves, coffee, coconut, sugar cane, salt, copper, gold, aquaculture, and capture fishery; (b) developing fishery centers and fishery processing industries in Marine and Fishery Centers (SKPT)/Fishery Management Areas (WPP); (c) developing livestock and plantation production centers, which are scattered in several National Priority Rural Areas (KPPN); (d) revitalizing transmigration areas; (e) economic development of leading commodity-based border regions; (f) developing strategic areas, and natural resource manufacturing in the form of plantations and mining; (g) developing natural, cultural, and historical tourism destinations to drive local economic development through the service sector, which is focused on Priority Tourism Destinations (DPP)/Special Economic Zones (KEK); (h) urban area development; (i) developing new growth centers with a focus on private investment schemes; (j) increasing the role and efficiency of large, medium, and small city services to increase the synergy of urban and rural development; and (k) strengthening rural-urban linkages that support regional growth centers.",""],[1,"135","3","Trade Centers Development in Nusa Tenggara","providing trade centers for raw commodities and manufactured goods in Nusa Tenggara",""],[1,"136","1","Sulawesi Logistics-Based Industrial Development","develop logistics-based industries",""],[1,"136","1","Sulawesi Food Crop Industrial Development","as a national food bowl with the development of cocoa, rice, and maize-based industries",""],[1,"136","1","Sulawesi Resource-Based Industrial Downstreaming","develop rattan, asphalt, nickel, iron ore, and natural gas-based industries",""],[1,"136","1","Sulawesi Maritime Economic Development Initiative","accelerate maritime-based economic development through the development of the fishing industry and marine tourism",""],[1,"136","1","Agriculture, Plantation, Fishery, and Mining Downstreaming Program","The economic transformation in Sulawesi is directed at realizing the downstreaming of agriculture, plantation, fishery. and mining-based industries to create value- added through processing raw materials into semi-finished or finished materials.",""],[1,"136","5","Growth Center Strengthening and Leading Commodity Development","Strengthening growth centers, among others through: (a) developing leading commodities in Sulawesi, namely coconut, palm oil, pepper, cloves, nutmeg, cocoa, coffee, sugar cane, gold, nickel, iron ore, coal, oil and natural gas, capture fishery, and aquaculture; (b) developing fishery production centers in Marine and Fishery Centers (SKPT)/Fishery Management Areas (WPP); (c) developing agricultural and plantation production centers, which are scattered in several National Priority Rural Areas (KPPN); (d) revitalizing transmigration areas; (e) economic development of leading commodity-based border regions; (f) developing leading commodities and manufacturing (downstreaming) of natural resources (agriculture, plantations, basic metals, and maritime) through the utilization an integration of infrastructure development in special economic zones (KEK) and industrial estates (KI); and (g) developing tourism based priority areas in priority tourism destinations (DPP); (h) developing urban areas including metropolitan areas to drive economic",""],[1,"138","4","Kalimantan Coal Downstreaming and Renewable Energy Development","maintaining its role as a national energy source through the development of coal commodity downstreaming, including the development of renewable energy based on biomass, water, solar power, or in accordance with regional conditions",""],[1,"138","4","Kalimantan Commodity-Based Industrial Development","developing commodity-based industries including palm oil, rubber, bauxite, ores, liquefied natural gas, zircon sand, and quartz sand",""],[1,"139","2","Regional Growth Center Development","Strengthening regional growth centers, among others through: (a) developing leading commodities in Kalimantan including rubber, palm oil, coconut, pepper, nutmeg, cloves, cocoa, bauxite, gold, petroleum, natural gas, coal , aquaculture, and capture fishery; (b) developing fishery production centers in Marine and Fishery Centers (SKPT)/Fishery Management Areas (WPP); (c) developing agricultural and",""],[1,"139","3","Rural Plantation Production Center Development","plantation production centers, which are scattered in several National Priority Rural Areas (KPPN);",""],[1,"139","3","Natural Resource Downstreaming in Industrial Estates and Special Economic Zones","developing leading commodities and manufacturing of (downstreaming) natural resources (plantations and mining) in Industrial Estates (KI) and/or Special Economic Zones (KEK);",""],[1,"140","5","Sumatra Regional International Cooperation and Market Diversification Initiative","Various international cooperation initiatives covering the Sumatra region such as the Indonesia-Malaysia-Thailand Growth Triangle, regional integration (Belt and Road Initiatives), and the ASEAN Economic Community will expand investment, trade, and diversify regional and global markets.",""],[1,"140","6","Downstreaming of Agriculture, Fishery, and Mining-Based Industries","In the next five years, the economic transformation in Sumatra will be directed towards realizing downstreaming of agriculture, fishery, and mining-based industries to create value-added through processing raw materials into semi- finished and finished materials by optimizing the benefits of the construction of the Trans-Sumatra toll road, airports and seaports.",""],[1,"140","7","East Coast Economic Zone Development","development of economic zones along the east coast corridor of Sumatra is directed at the downstreaming of leading commodities and export-oriented growth centers supported by the development of an international hub in Kuala Tanjung as a trading center in the region of Western Indonesia.",""],[1,"141","2","Regional Growth Center Strengthening Programme","Strengthening regional growth centers is carried out, among others through: (a) development leading commodities in Sumatra, which include cocoa, coconut, palm oil, rubber, coffee, pepper, nutmeg, sugar cane, gold, tin, petroleum, natural gas, coal, capture fishery, and aquaculture; (b) developing fishery production centers in Marine and Fishery Centers (SKPT)/Fishery Management Areas (WPP); (c) developing agricultural and plantation production centers, which are scattered in several National Priority Rural Areas (KPPN); (d) developing strategic areas and the manufacturing of natural resources such as plantations, fishery and mining; and developing the aerospace industry in several Special Economic Zones (KEK) and Industrial Zones (KI), as well as the Free Trade Zones and Ports (KPBPB);",""],[1,"141","3","Aerospace Industry Development","developing the aerospace industry",""],[1,"143","7","Java-Bali Growth Support through Commodity, Industry, Tourism, Urban, Agriculture, and Fisheries Development","Maintaining growth in Java-Bali is carried out by: (a) developing leading commodities in Java-Bali, including cloves, pepper, nutmeg, coconut, coffee, sugarcane, cocoa, gold, salt, capture fishery, and aquaculture; (b) developing high-tech industrial sector, creative industries, services, and manufacturing industrial centers in several Special Economic Zones (KEK) and Industrial Estates (KI); (c) developing strategic areas based on natural, cultural, and MICE in several Priority Tourism Destinations (DPP); (d) developing urban areas, through enhancing the quality of metropolitan areas, constructing new cities and others; (e) developing agricultural and plantation production centers, which are scattered in several National Priority Rural Areas (KPPN); (f) developing agropolitan areas; and (g) developing fishery production centers in Fishery Management Areas (WPP).",""],[1,"144","2","Hub Port Commodity Outlet Development","developing outlets for raw commodities and processed goods at hub ports;",""]],"160":[[1,"134","3","Basic Services Enhancement and Human Resource Development","Enhancing basic services include: (a) enhancing the quality of human resources, especially improving access to education and health services, vocational education in agriculture, mining, fishery, and tourism; and revitalizing vocational training centers;",""],[1,"136","3","Basic Services and Human Resource Development Initiative","enhancing the quality of human resources, especially improving access to education and health services, vocational education in agriculture, fishery and tourism; and revitalizing vocational training centers",""],[1,"138","8","Basic Services and Human Resources Enhancement","Enhancing basic services include: (a) enhancing the quality of human resources, especially improving access to education and health services, vocational education in agriculture, fishery and tourism; and revitalizing vocational training centers; (b) guiding and aligning ministries/institutions and other development actors in",""],[1,"140","9","Basic Services Improvement and Vocational Training Revitalization","Enhancing basic services include: (a) improving the quality of human resources, especially improving access to education and health services, vocational education in agriculture, fishery and tourism; and revitalizing vocational training centers;",""],[1,"143","5","Basic Services Enhancement and Human Resource Development","Enhancing basic services include: (a) enhancing the quality of human resources, especially improving access to education and health services, vocational education in agriculture, fishery and tourism; and revitalizing vocational training centers;",""]],"161":[[1,"159","2","Productive Economic Programs for Poor and Vulnerable Groups","increase the income of the poor and vulnerable groups through productive economic programs.",""],[1,"159","2","Government Support for Community Initiatives","the government is seeking funding for community initiatives that have been proven to have socio-economic impacts.",""],[1,"179","15","Strengthening of the Family Economy","Accelerating the strengthening of the family economy, including:",""],[1,"179","16","Family Financial Planning Development","Developing pre- and post-wedding family financial plans, including family investment plans; and",""],[1,"179","17","Business Training and Productive Business Access for Poor and Vulnerable Families","Providing business training and productive business access for poor and vulnerable families;",""],[1,"179","18","Ultra-Micro Funding for Poor and Vulnerable Families","Facilitating ultra-micro funding for individuals or groups who come from poor and vulnerable families;",""],[1,"179","22","Business Development Schemes for Poor and Vulnerable Groups","Strengthening business capacity of the poor and vulnerable groups with business development schemes",""],[1,"180","1","Funding Schemes for Social-Impact Small Businesses","Developing funding schemes for small businesses that have social impacts;",""]],"162":[[1,"180","4","Environmental and Forestry Community Group Counseling and Mentoring","Counseling and/or mentoring for environmental and forestry community groups, including increasing the capacity of extension workers and forming independent forest farmer groups, for the development of productive enterprises.",""],[1,"180","12","Capacity Building for Community Groups","Capacity building for community groups (regional, institutional, and business management);",""],[1,"180","13","Investment and Business Partnerships for Social Forestry Groups","Establishing investment/business partnerships between investors and social forestry business groups;",""],[1,"180","14","Social Forestry Product Processing Industry Development","Developing the industry to process products of social forestry groups in to increase added value;",""],[1,"180","15","Social Forestry Product Marketing and Promotion Support","Facilitating marketing/promotion of social forestry products to social forestry business groups.",""]],"163":[[1,"226","4","Irrigation Modernization Programme","Strategies to increase the efficiency and performance of irrigation systems by applying the concept of irrigation modernization include: (a) Constructing",""],[1,"226","5","Irrigation Network Development and Rehabilitation","new irrigation networks; (b) Rehabilitating existing irrigation networks;",""],[1,"226","5","Irrigation Institutional Capacity Building","(c) Building capacity of irrigation institutions;",""],[1,"226","5","Improved Irrigation Water Allocation","(d) Increasing the effectiveness of irrigation water allocation;",""],[1,"226","5","Swamp Revitalization for Land Utilization","(e) Utilizing sub- optimal land through swamp revitalization.",""],[1,"226","6","Water Reservoir and Irrigation System Development for High-Value Agriculture","Developing water reservoirs and irrigation systems for estate crops, livestock, horticulture, and fishery",""],[1,"226","6","Smallholder Farm Pond Irrigation Network Development","Developing irrigation networks for smallholder farm ponds",""],[1,"226","6","Micro-Irrigation Expansion for Underutilized Land","Developing micro-irrigation especially in land that has not been utilized optimally",""],[1,"226","6","Participatory Irrigation Management Strengthening","These strategies are supported by increasing the role of local government, community participation, and partnerships with business entities in irrigation management.",""]],"164":[[1,"227","1","Road Maintenance Governance and Performance-Based Financing Expansion","Meeting road maintenance needs is encouraged through improved governance in the management of roads that prioritize routine and periodic maintenance activities.",""],[1,"227","1","Availability Payment Scheme for Road Maintenance","Cooperation schemes between government-to-business entities (KPBU) such as the Availability Payment Scheme (AP) based on performance and the Regional Road Grant Program that encourages road maintenance performance need to be expanded.",""],[1,"227","1","Regional Road Grant Program","Cooperation schemes between government-to-business entities (KPBU) such as the Availability Payment Scheme (AP) based on performance and the Regional Road Grant Program that encourages road maintenance performance need to be expanded.",""],[1,"227","1","Integrated Road Management and Weighbridge Operations","The KPBU-AP scheme also supports the quality of roads through integrated road management and weighbridge operations to control road overloading behavior, which is the main cause of road damage.",""],[1,"227","2","Road Network Expansion for Regional Development","Increasing the availability of road networks that support regional development is carried out through the construction of roads on the main road network of island-regions, roads that support priority industrial and tourism areas, access roads to priority transportation nodes, outer ring/trans- island roads, and access roads supporting disadvantaged, frontier, and outermost areas (3T) and border areas.",""],[1,"227","2","Trans-Sumatra Toll Road Completion","For example, the completion of the Trans- Sumatra toll road connecting Aceh- Lampung has become a priority program to reduce travel time and provide access to the main port of Kuala Tanjung to",""],[1,"227","4","Strategic Road Development Projects","Priority projects that support road connectivity include: i) Strategic road development, for example: Trans-Papua Merauke-Sorong (Major Project) and Trans-Roads on 18 Disadvantaged, Frontier, and Outermost Islands (Major Projects);",""],[1,"227","4","Toll Road Construction Programme","ii) Toll road construction, for example: Trans-Sumatra Toll Road Aceh - Lampung (Major Project);",""],[1,"227","4","Road Construction for Priority Areas","iii) Road construction that supports priority areas (KI, KEK, KSPN, and border areas);",""],[1,"227","4","Access Road Development to Transport Nodes","iv) Developing access roads to transportation nodes (seaports, airports, and bus terminals);",""],[1,"227","4","National Road Preservation Programme","v) Preserving national roads (including improving/widening roads);",""],[1,"227","4","Regional Road Development and Maintenance Programme","and vi) Developing and maintaining regional roads.",""],[2,"215","2","Road Maintenance and Road Equipment Provision","Peningkatan kualitas jalan dilaksanakan melalui pemenuhan kebutuhan pemeliharaan jalan, termasuk pemeliharaan rutin jalan serta pemenuhan kelengkapan jalan.",""],[2,"215","2","Performance-Based PPP Availability Payment Scheme for Roads","Skema kerjasama antara Pemerintah dan Badan Usaha (KPBU) Availability Payment (AP) yang berbasis kinerja serta Program Hibah Jalan Daerah yang mendorong kinerja pemeliharaan jalan perlu diperluas.",""],[2,"215","2","Regional Road Grant Program","Skema kerjasama antara Pemerintah dan Badan Usaha (KPBU) Availability Payment (AP) yang berbasis kinerja serta Program Hibah Jalan Daerah yang mendorong kinerja pemeliharaan jalan perlu diperluas.",""],[2,"215","2","Road Overloading Control Through Weighbridge Operations","Skema KPBU-AP juga mendukung kualitas jalan melalui keterpaduan penyelenggaraan jalan dan pengoperasian jembatan timbang untuk mengendalikan perilaku pembebanan berlebih di jalan (road overloading) yang menjadi penyebab utama kerusakan jalan.",""],[2,"215","4","Strategic Road Connectivity Development","Proyek prioritas mendukung konektivitas jalan meliputi: i) Pembangunan jalan strategis, contoh: Jalan Trans Papua Merauke - Sorong (Major Project) dan Jalan Trans pada 18 Pulau Tertinggal, Terluar, dan Terdepan (Major Project); ii) Pembangunan jalan tol, contoh: Jalan Tol Trans Sumatera Aceh - Lampung (Major Project); iii) Pembangunan jalan mendukung kawasan prioritas (KI, KEK, KSPN, dan kawasan perbatasan); iv) Pembangunan jalan akses simpul transportasi (pelabuhan, bandara, dan terminal); v) Preservasi jalan nasional (termasuk peningkatan/pelebaran); serta vi) Pembangunan dan pemeliharaan jalan daerah.",""]],"165":[[1,"232","3","Renewable Energy Expansion and Clean Power Infrastructure","Diversifying energy and electricity to meet certain needs, by (a) increasing new and renewable energy sources (EBT) such as geothermal, water, solar, and biomass, and other EBTs; (b) developing mini-/micro-grids based on clean energy; (c) developing and utilizing energy storage systems including batteries; and (d) utilizing solar rooftop panels and floating solar power plants while simultaneously developing the domestic solar-cell industry;",""],[1,"232","4","Energy Efficiency and Electricity System Upgrade Programme","Increasing the efficiency of energy and electricity use, through (a) developing energy service companies (ESCO); (b) expanding, rehabilitating and increasing the capacity of transmission and distribution systems; (c) developing an information management and data control system; (d) developing and utilizing smart grid technology and (e) utilizing technology that has high efficiency and low emission (HELE).",""],[1,"265","3","Sustainable Energy Development Programme","Developing sustainable energy, which is carried out by: (a) managing new and renewable energy through developing renewable energy generation and increasing the supply of biofuels from low-carbon raw materials; and through (b) energy efficiency and conservation.",""]],"166":[[1,"232","7","Energy and Electricity Governance Reform","Improving energy and electricity governance, which is pursued by (a) improving institutional tasks and functions in the electricity sector; (b) strengthening the independence of transmission system operators; and (c) encouraging energy price/tariff policies and their application so as to gradually achieve economic prices.",""],[1,"232","8","Funding and Financing Policy Development","Developing funding and financing policies, which is pursued by (a) developing targeted subsidies through direct subsidies and reallocating expenditure; (b) implementing adjustments to electricity and energy pricing; (c) utilizing financing with simple and reasonable requirements, alternative instruments, and asset leverage; and",""],[1,"233","1","Sustainable Funding Scheme Development","developing suitable and sustainable funding schemes.",""]],"167":[[1,"241","4","Disaster Risk Reduction and Post-Disaster Financing","the Government's commitment to financing disaster management has been continued, particularly its commitment to investing in disaster risk reduction, in rehabilitation and reconstruction after disasters, and in initiating financing innovations for disaster-related programs.",""],[1,"255","4","Disaster Risk Management Financing Innovation Schemes","The government is currently drafting legislation, institutional framework, and various financing innovation schemes that focus on the capacity of disaster risk management, which includes emergency response, rehabilitation, and reconstruction.",""],[1,"255","4","Disaster Risk Management Management Body","Apart from the contribution of the state/regional budget, financing can come from a collection of private funds, public funds, international bodies, and BUMN, which will be implemented by a management body appointed through regulation.",""],[1,"255","4","Pooling Fund and Risk Transfer Instruments","The formation of pooling funds and their derivative products will be formulated as targeted risk transfer instruments that strengthen funding from the current state budget.",""],[1,"264","6","Alternative Disaster Mitigation Financing Scheme Development","increasing the development and innovation of alternative disaster mitigation financing schemes.",""],[1,"295","6","Revision of Disaster Management Regulation","d. Revision of PP No. 21/2008 on implementing disaster",""]],"168":[[1,"292","23","Draft Drug and Food Control Bill","g. Draft bill on drug and food control.",""],[1,"292","24","Hospital Law Revision","h. Revision of Law No. 44/2009 on hospitals.",""],[1,"292","25","Medical Practice Law Revision","Revision of Law No. 29/2004 on medical practice.",""],[1,"292","26","Communicable Diseases Law Revision","Revision of Law No. 4/1984 on communicable diseases.",""],[1,"293","11","Health Quarantine Regulations Drafting","PP draft on implementing regulations on health quarantine laws.",""],[1,"293","12","Pharmaceutical and Medical Devices Availability Policy Draft","PP draft on securing the availability of pharmaceutical and medical devices.",""],[1,"293","14","Revision of Regulation on Addictive-Substance Materials","Revision of PP No. 109/2012 on safeguarding materials containing addictive substances such as tobacco products.",""],[1,"294","7","Health-Oriented Regencies and Cities Presidential Regulation Draft","Perpres draft on health-oriented regencies/cities.",""],[1,"294","8","Halal Certification Regulation for Medicinal Products, Bioproducts, and Medical Devices","Perpres draft on halal certification of medicinal products, bioproducts and medical devices.",""]],"169":[[1,"292","22","Revision of the National Sports System Law","Revision of Law No. 3/2005 on the national sports system.",""],[1,"293","17","Revision of Sports Scheme Implementation Regulation","Revision of PP No. 16/2007 on implementing sports schemes.",""],[1,"293","18","Revision of the Sports Week and Championships Regulation","Revision of PP No. 17/2007 on holding sports week and championships.",""]],"170":[[1,"294","5","National Strategy for Out-of-School Children Education Support","Perpres draft on national strategy for helping out-of-school children to receive education.",""]],"171":[[1,"291","6","Revision of Special Autonomy Law for Papua","Revision of Law Number 21/2001 on special autonomy for Papua",""],[1,"291","7","Revision of Regional Taxes and Levies Law","Revision of Law Number 28/2009 on regional taxes and regional levies",""],[1,"291","10","Revision of the Jakarta Special Capital Region Law","Revision of Law Number 29/2007 on the Special Capital Region of Jakarta as the capital of the Unitary State of the Republic of Indonesia",""],[1,"291","13","Revision of Law on Central-Regional Financial Balance","h. Revision of Law Number 33/2004 on financial balance between the central government and regional governments",""],[1,"291","19","Revision of Village Implementation Regulations","Revision of PP No. 43/2014 on regulations for implementing Law No. 6/2014 concerning villages",""]],"172":[[1,"291","4","Draft Presidential Regulation on Improving Corporate Farmer Welfare","Draft Perpres on improving welfare of corporate farmers",""],[1,"291","14","Revision of the Abandoned Land Control and Utilization Regulation","Revision of PP No. 11/2010 on control and utilization of abandoned land",""]],"173":[[1,"307","1","Village Fund Optimization for Sustainable Village Development","Encouraging village governments to optimize the use of village funds to: (a) realize the independence of village communities and create sustainable villages that have developed social, economic and ecological resilience; (b) improve basic services and basic village infrastructure; (c) increase the capacity of village officials for good governance; (d) develop an integrated village information system that details the arrangement of village territories and the determination of village boundaries;(e) transform the village economy by developing tourism villages, digital villages, leading products, rural areas, and increasing the role of village-owned enterprises (also known as BUMDes or BUMDes Bersama); and (f) strengthen and develop traditional villages, nagari, and other subdivisions equivalent to villages;",""],[1,"307","2","Village Fund Allocation Reform for Disadvantaged Villages","Improving the allocation of village funds by taking into account fairness and affirmation for disadvantaged villages,",""],[1,"307","5","Village Fund Coordination and Monitoring Strengthening","Strengthening coordination, cooperation, and partnership in planning, allocating, budgeting, channeling, reporting, monitoring, controlling, and evaluating village funds by developing: (a) integrated web- based information systems and databases, (b) assisting regional governments to develop and strengthen, among others, the role of the district as a center for public services, empowerment, and growth, by utilizing funds from the regional budget to optimize the management of village funds, (c) controlling performance-based distribution, and (d) regular reporting;",""],[1,"307","6","Village Fund Support for Inter-Village Development Activities","Increasing the use of village funds for inter-village development activities, including distributing village authority, and determining boundaries and ownership of assets, and emphasizing operational and maintenance responsibilities.",""]],"174":[[1,"309","1","Low-Carbon Development Strategy Integration","The government formulates strategies and policies that include improving low-carbon development strategies that are aligned with the Paris Agreement, and integrating them into the national economic and development plans.",""],[1,"309","2","Sustainable Government Procurement Reform","the government also continues to develop and implement government procurement processes that incorporate sustainability criteria with a more systematic and consistent approach based on best practice",""]],"175":[[1,"309","3","Private Investment Framework for Energy Sector Expansion","the government will also set the terms, conditions, and frameworks in which private investment is expected to play a greater role, and even exceed government funding in, for example, the energy sector.",""],[1,"309","3","International Support for Financial Access, Clean Technology, Capacity Building, and Governance","international support, and cooperation in terms of financial access, access to clean technology, capacity building, and effective governance will still be needed.",""]],"176":[[2,"25","3","Public Service Bureaucratic Reform for Export, Import, Customs, and Port Activities","REFORMASI BIROKRASI PELAYANAN PUBLIK UNTUK KEGIATAN EKSPOR/ IMPOR, KEPABEANAN, DAN KEPELABUHAN",""]],"177":[[2,"52","6","Stakeholder Participation Synchronization for Development Financing","Untuk itu, perlu mendorong dan mensinergikan partisipasi berbagai pemangku kepentingan untuk memperkuat pemanfaatan pendanaan pembangunan.",""],[2,"52","7","Integrated Development Financing and Innovative Financing Schemes","Untuk mengoptimalkan pemanfaatan pendanaan perlu dilakukan integrasi pendanaan pembangunan pada sumber pemerintah (K/L, Non K/L, Transfer Ke Daerah dan Dana Desa) serta pembiayaan yang berasal dari BUMN, kerjasama pemerintah dan badan usaha, maupun masyarakat yang selaras dengan implementasi prinsip Money Follow Program.",""],[2,"52","7","Public-Private Partnership and Innovative Financing Promotion","Selain itu, pemerintah perlu lebih mendorong pemanfaatan sumber-sumber pendanaan yang berasal dari masyarakat dan swasta melalui skema-skema pembiayaan yang inovatif termasuk melalui pengembangan skema Kerjasama Pemerintah dan Badan Usaha (KPBU) maupun bentuk pendanaan inovatif (innovative financing) lainnya.",""],[2,"58","4","Major Project Financing Integration and Innovative Financing Schemes","Major Project menjadi acuan penekanan kebijakan dan pendanaan dalam RPJM, RKP dan APBN tahunannya.",""],[2,"58","5","Major Project Updating through the Annual Work Plan","Di dalam pelaksanaannya, Major Project dan indikasi pendanaannya dapat dimutakhirkan melalui RKP dengan mempertimbangkan kesiapan pelaksanaan, pemutakhiran besaran dan sumber pendanaan serta Direktif Presiden.",""],[2,"58","6","Major Project Development Control and Monitoring Tool","Major Project dapat menjadi alat kendali pembangunan sehingga sasaran dan target Pembangunan dalam RPJMN 2020-2024 dapat terus dipantau dan dkendalikan.",""]],"178":[[2,"30","16","Justice System Improvement, Regulatory Reform, and Cybersecurity Governance","3) Perbaikan sistem peradilan, penataan regulasi dan tata kelola keamanan siber;",""],[2,"65","16","Natuna Maritime Deterrence and Sovereignty Enforcement","Peningkatan deterrent effect dan penegakan kedaulatan di perairan Natuna;",""],[2,"65","16","Maritime Crime Reduction and Navigation Security Management System","Penurunan aktivitas perompakan, kekerasan dan tindak kejahatan di laut, IUUF, trans-national crimes dan penguatan sistem pengelolaan pengamanan navigasi.",""]],"179":[[2,"36","3","Inflation Stabilization and Coordination Measures","Pencapaian sasaran tersebut diupayakan melalui penyelesaian permasalahan struktural, pengelolaan ekspektasi, dan penguatan koordinasi.",""],[2,"41","2","Inflation Stabilization Policy","Pemerintah dan Bank Indonesia berkomitmen untuk menjaga laju inflasi rendah dan stabil dalam jangka menengah.",""],[2,"41","3","Inflation Control Policy Package","Dalam kurun waktu tahun 2020-2024, kebijakan pengendalian inflasi diarahkan untuk: (i) meningkatkan ketersediaan komoditas pangan strategis; (ii) memperkuat tata kelola sistem logistik nasional dan konektivitas antarwilayah; (iii) meningkatkan kerjasama antardaerah; (iv) menjangkar ekspektasi inflasi dalam sasaran yang ditetapkan; serta (iv) meningkatkan kualitas data/statistik.",""]],"180":[[2,"41","7","Commodity Downstreaming Policy","Kebijakan hilirisasi komoditas unggulan, pengembangan potensi pariwisata, perkuatan infrastruktur konektivitas antarwilayah menjadi kunci percepatan pertumbuhan Pulau Sumatera.",""],[2,"41","7","Tourism Potential Development","Kebijakan hilirisasi komoditas unggulan, pengembangan potensi pariwisata, perkuatan infrastruktur konektivitas antarwilayah menjadi kunci percepatan pertumbuhan Pulau Sumatera.",""],[2,"42","2","Natural Resource Downstreaming for Energy","Pertumbuhan ekonomi Pulau Kalimantan akan meningkat terutama didorong oleh investasi untuk pembangunan Ibu Kota Negara yang menciptakan efek pengganda besar bagi perekonomian serta hilirisasi sumber daya alam untuk energi.",""],[2,"89","4","Domestic Natural Gas and Coal Utilization for Value Addition","Pemanfaatan sumber daya gas bumi dan batu bara difokuskan pada: (1) pemanfaatan dalam negeri baik sebagai sumber energi maupun bahan baku industri untuk meningkatkan nilai tambah; dan (2) peningkatan industri pengolahan batubara menjadi gas untuk kebutuhan bahan baku industri dalam negeri.",""],[2,"93","5","Agricultural and Forestry Downstream Processing Development","Pengembangan hilirisasi industri pertanian dan kehutanan difokuskan pada pengolahan turunan komoditas utama seperti peternakan, kelapa sawit, kelapa, karet, kayu, rotan, sagu, kakao, kopi, tanaman obat, buah-buahan, florikultura dan rempah-rempah, pengembangan indikasi geografis tanaman jamu/obat, serta standardisasi proses dan produk jamu nasional.",""],[2,"93","5","Fish Processing Value-Addition and Market Expansion","Khusus untuk industri pengolahan perikanan dan hasil laut, peningkatan nilai tambah juga dilaksanakan melalui perbaikan kualitas, kapasitas dan produktivitas industri pengolahan, hilirisasi industri rumput laut dan sumber daya alam laut bernilai tambah, penguatan daya saing Unit Pengolahan Ikan (UPI), penerapan standardisasi mutu, sertifikasi dan ketelusuran produk (traceability), penyediaan sarana dan prasarana sistem rantai dingin, penguatan sistem logistik ikan yang efisien, perluasan akses pasar dalam dan luar negeri, pembangunan fasilitas pemasaran perikanan berskala internasional, penguatan branding produk perikanan Indonesia, dan pengembangan sistem pemasaran produk perikanan berbasis digital.",""],[2,"93","6","Entrepreneurship, Cooperatives, and MSME Development Synergy","Pelaksanaan industrialisasi yang berbasis investasi juga disinergikan dengan kebijakan dan strategi pengembangan kewirausahaan, koperasi dan UMKM.",""]],"181":[[2,"96","5","High-Value Export Promotion and Domestic Content Strengthening","Peningkatan ekspor bernilai tambah tinggi dan penguatan Tingkat Komponen Dalam Negeri (TKDN) dilaksanakan dengan strategi (1) meningkatkan diversifikasi, nilai tambah, dan daya saing produk ekspor dan jasa; (2) meningkatkan akses dan pendalaman pasar ekspor; (3) mengelola impor; (4) meningkatkan kandungan dan penggunaan produk dalam negeri termasuk melalui pengadaan pemerintah yang efektif; (5) meningkatkan partisipasi dalam jaringan produksi global; (6) meningkatkan citra dan diversifikasi pemasaran pariwisata, serta produk kreatif dan digital; serta (7) meningkatkan efektivitas Preferential Trade Agreement (PTA)/ Free Trade Agreement (FTA)/ Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement (CEPA) dan diplomasi ekonomi.",""],[2,"96","6","Export Expansion Strategy for Industrial Goods, Services, and Branding","Strategi peningkatan dan perluasan ekspor akan difokuskan pada: (1) peningkatan ekspor produk industri yang lebih kompleks termasuk yang berteknologi menengah dan tinggi; (2) peningkatan ekspor jasa melalui peningkatan kapasitas dari pelaku sektor jasa dalam negeri berdasarkan peta kompetensi, harmonisasi regulasi sektor jasa, serta penyediaan statistik perdagangan jasa; (3) penguatan platform informasi ekspor dan impor yang mencakup informasi pasar, regulasi dan prosedur, serta insentif dan advokasi termasuk tentang kerja sama bilateral dan multilateral; (4) pengembangan marketplace berorientasi ekspor, termasuk yang dapat dimanfaatkan oleh UMKM dan start-up teknologi untuk memasok produk dan jasa ke pasar internasional; dan (5) fasilitasi peningkatan daya saing brand barang dan jasa Indonesia.",""],[2,"96","7","Export and Import Financing Support","Peningkatan akses dan pendalaman pasar ekspor didukung diantaranya dengan pembiayaan ekspor dan impor, serta penguatan skema kerja sama business-to-business.",""],[2,"96","7","Business-to-Business Cooperation Strengthening Scheme","Peningkatan akses dan pendalaman pasar ekspor didukung diantaranya dengan pembiayaan ekspor dan impor, serta penguatan skema kerja sama business-to-business.",""],[2,"96","7","Export Market Expansion to Africa, Latin America, and Eastern Europe","Perluasan pasar ekspor mencakup kawasan Afrika, Amerika Latin, dan Eropa Timur.",""],[2,"97","2","Export Expansion and Import Management Strategy","Strategi peningkatan dan perluasan ekspor, serta pengelolaan impor juga dilaksanakan secara sinergi dengan peningkatan partisipasi di rantai produksi global antara lain dengan memberikan insentif fiskal terhadap bahan baku melalui Kemudahan Impor Tujuan Ekspor.",""],[2,"97","2","Import Raw Material Facilitation for Export Promotion","Selain itu, peningkatan ekspor juga dilaksanakan melalui pendekatan fasilitasi bahan baku impor untuk tujuan ekspor.",""],[2,"141","3","Hub Port Commodity Outlet Development","(b) pengembangan outlet untuk komoditas mentah maupun barang hasil olahan di pelabuhan hub;",""]],"182":[[2,"97","4","Government Governance and Policy Reform for International Standards","Pelaksanaannya membutuhkan reformasi tata kelola dan kebijakan pemerintahan dalam rangka mencapai standar yang berlaku dan mendukung pelaksanaan kebijakan-kebijakan yang disepakati dan direkomendasikan.",""]],"183":[[2,"108","10","Regional Development Priorities Framework","Sasaran pembangunan kewilayahan tahun 2020-2024 akan dicapai melalui lima (5) prioritas, yaitu: pengembangan kawasan strategis; pengembangan sektor unggulan; pengembangan kawasan perkotaan; pembangunan daerah tertinggal, kawasan perbatasan, perdesaan, dan transmigrasi; serta pengelolaan kelembagaan dan keuangan daerah (Tabel 3.4).",""],[2,"112","2","Integrated Regional Development Planning and Coordination","Pembangunan kewilayahan tahun 2020-2024 menekankan keterpaduan pembangunan dengan memperhatikan pendekatan spasial yang didasarkan bukti data, informasi dan pengetahuan yang baik, akurat dan lengkap, skenario pembangunan nasional, serta lokasi yang jelas sesuai rencana tata ruang dan daya dukung lingkungan.",""],[2,"112","2","Holistic and Thematic Regional Development Approach","Selain itu, pembangunan kewilayahan juga mengutamakan pendekatan holistik dan tematik yang didasarkan penanganan secara menyeluruh dan terfokus pada prioritas pembangunan dan lokasi yang paling relevan sesuai dengan pendekatan koridor pertumbuhan dan pemerataan.",""],[2,"112","2","Intergovernmental Regional Development Integration","Pembangunan kewilayahan dilaksanakan secara terintegrasi dengan mengutamakan kerjasama dan keterpaduan program dan kegiatan antarkementerian/lembaga, antara Kementerian/Lembaga dan Pemerintah Daerah, antarpemerintah daerah, serta antara Pemerintah dan Badan Usaha dalam perencanaan, pendanaan dan pembiayaan, pelaksanaan, pengendalian dan evaluasi pembangunan",""],[2,"112","7","Growth Corridor and Equity Corridor Regional Development Approach","pembangunan wilayah kedepan akan diterjemahkan melalui dua pendekatan utama yaitu pendekatan koridor pertumbuhan dan koridor pemerataan berbasiskan wilayah pulau (Gambar 3.1).",""],[2,"126","7","Regional Development Policy Zoning Framework","kebijakan pembangunan wilayah tahun 2020-2024 dijabarkan ke dalam tujuh (7) wilayah pembangunan, yaitu: Wilayah Papua, Wilayah Maluku, Wilayah Nusa Tenggara, Wilayah Sulawesi, Wilayah Kalimantan, Wilayah Jawa-Bali dan Wilayah Sumatera, sesuai dengan Rencana Tata Ruang Wilayah Pulau untuk menjamin kebijakan, program dan kegiatan yang konsisten, terpadu dan bersifat lintas sektor",""],[2,"127","2","Integrated Island Region Development","Pembangunan wilayah pulau dilakukan secara terintegrasi, yaitu dengan memperhitungkan (1) keberlanjutan daya dukung pembangunan secara menyeluruh; (2) pengembangan ekonomi wilayah, baik berskala lokal maupun nasional dan internasional, melalui pengembangan komoditas dan hilirisasi komoditas melalui pengembangan kawasan strategis berbasis sumberdaya alam, pengembangan kawasan strategis berbasis non sumber daya alam, pengembangan kawasan perkotaan dan perdesaan, revitalisasi kawasan transmigrasi, serta pengembangan kawasan perbatasan dan daerah tertinggal; (4) pembangunan sumberdaya manusia melalui pemenuhan layanan dasar serta peningkatan produktivitas dan daya saing; (5) pengembangan pelaksanaan desentralisasi dan otonomi khusus (untuk Provinsi Aceh, Papua dan Papua Barat); serta (6) pengembangan infrastruktur pendukung aktivitas ekonomi dan sosial",""]],"184":[[2,"114","2","Expansion of Basic Education and Health Services","melalui: (i) perluasan akses pelayanan dasar pendidikan dan kesehatan;",""],[2,"114","2","Provision of Basic Housing, Water, Sanitation, and Electricity Infrastructure","melalui: (ii) penyediaan prasarana dan sarana dasar perumahan, air bersih dan sanitasi, dan listrik;",""],[2,"127","5","Basic Services Improvement and Regional Equity Acceleration","Peningkatan pelayanan dasar, antara lain: (a) peningkatan kualitas SDM; (b) percepatan pembangunan kawasan perbukitan dan pegunungan untuk mengurangi kesenjangan antarwilayah antara kawasan pesisir dan pegunungan serta memperhatikan kontekstual Papua; (c) percepatan pembangunan daerah tertinggal dilakukan dengan fokus pada pemenuhan pelayanan dasar, peningkatan konektivitas dan pengembangan infrastruktur termasuk jaringan layanan/akses internet; (d) pembinaan dan keberpihakan dari K/L serta pelaku pembangunan lainnya juga dilakukan terhadap daerah tertinggal yang telah terentaskan tahun 2019, selama maksimal 3 tahun (2020-2022); (e) pemenuhan pelayanan dasar dan peningkatan tata kelola di kecamatan perbatasan; (f) percepatan pembangunan desa secara terpadu untuk mendorong transformasi sosial, budaya dan ekonomi desa, dan (g) pelaksanaan pembangunan afirmatif.",""],[2,"130","4","Basic Services Improvement and Human Capital Development","Peningkatan pelayanan dasar antara lain: (a) peningkataan kualitas SDM khususnya peningkatan akses layanan pendidikan dan kesehatan",""],[2,"130","4","Accelerated Development of Disadvantaged Regions","percepatan pembangunan daerah tertinggal dilakukan dengan fokus pada pemenuhan pelayanan dasar, peningkatan kapasitas sumber daya manusia, dan pengembangan ekonomi lokal berbasis komoditas unggulan dengan memanfaatkan teknologi digital",""],[2,"130","4","Support and Affirmative Measures for Previously Disadvantaged Regions","pembinaan dan keberpihakan dari K/L serta pelaku pembangunan lainnya dilakukan terhadap daerah tertinggal yang telah terentaskan tahun 2019, selama maksimal 3 tahun (2020-2022)",""],[2,"130","4","Border Subdistrict Basic Services and Governance Improvement","pemenuhan pelayanan dasar dan peningkatan tata kelola di kecamatan perbatasan",""],[2,"130","4","Affirmative Development Implementation","pelaksanaan pembangunan afirmatif",""],[2,"132","4","Basic Services Improvement and Human Capital Development","Peningkatan pelayanan dasar antara lain: (a) peningkatkan kualitas SDM khususnya peningkatan akses layanan pendidikan dan kesehatan, pendidikan vokasional pertanian, perikanan pertambangan dan pariwisata; dan revitalisasi Balai Latihan Kerja;",""],[2,"132","4","Acceleration of Underdeveloped Region Development","percepatan pembangunan daerah tertinggal dilakukan dengan fokus pada pemenuhan pelayanan dasar, pengembangan ekonomi lokal berbasis komoditas unggulan dengan memanfaatkan teknologi digital, dan pengembangan infrastruktur;",""],[2,"132","4","Support and Advocacy for Previously Disadvantaged Regions","pembinaan dan keberpihakan dari K/L serta pelaku pembangunan lainnya dilaksanakan terhadap daerah tertinggal yang telah terentaskan tahun 2019, selama maksimal 3 tahun (2020-2022);",""],[2,"132","4","Basic Services and Governance Improvement in Border Districts","pemenuhan pelayanan dasar dan peningkatan tata kelola di kecamatan perbatasan;",""],[2,"132","4","Affirmative Development Implementation","pelaksanaan pembangunan afirmatif.",""],[2,"134","4","Basic Services Improvement and Human Capital Development","Peningkatan pelayanan dasar antara lain: (a) peningkatkan kualitas SDM khususnya peningkatan akses layanan pendidikan dan kesehatan, pendidikan vokasional pertanian, perikanan dan pariwisata; dan revitalisasi Balai Latihan Kerja;",""],[2,"134","4","Accelerated Development of Disadvantaged Regions","percepatan pembangunan daerah tertinggal dengan fokus pada pengembangan ekonomi lokal berbasis komoditas unggulan dengan memanfaatkan teknologi digital, pemenuhan pelayanan dasar yang memperhatikan aspek mitigasi dan kesiapsiagaan terhadap resiko bencana;",""],[2,"134","4","Support for Previously Resolved Disadvantaged Regions","pembinaan dan keberpihakan dari K/L serta pelaku pembangunan lainnya dilakukan terhadap daerah tertinggal yang telah terentaskan tahun 2019, selama maksimal 3 tahun (2020-2022);",""],[2,"134","4","Basic Services and Governance Improvement in Border Subdistricts","pemenuhan pelayanan dasar dan peningkatan tata kelola di kecamatan perbatasan;",""],[2,"134","4","Affirmative Development Implementation","pelaksanaan pembangunan afirmatif.",""],[2,"136","5","Basic Services Improvement and Human Capital Development","Peningkatan pelayanan dasar antara lain: (a) peningkatkan kualitas SDM khususnya peningkatan akses layanan pendidikan dan kesehatan, pendidikan vokasional pertanian, perikanan dan pariwisata; dan revitalisasi Balai Latihan Kerja;",""],[2,"136","5","Targeted Support for Previously Disadvantaged Regions","pembinaan dan keberpihakan dari K/L serta pelaku pembangunan lainnya terhadap daerah tertinggal yang telah terentaskan tahun 2019, selama maksimal 3 tahun (2020-2022);","K/L"],[2,"136","5","Basic Services and Governance Improvement in Border Districts","pemenuhan pelayanan dasar dan peningkatan tata kelola di kecamatan perbatasan;",""],[2,"138","5","Basic Services Improvement and Human Capital Development","Peningkatan pelayanan dasar antara lain: (a) peningkatan kualitas SDM khususnya peningkatan akses layanan pendidikan dan kesehatan, pendidikan vokasional pertanian, perikanan dan pariwisata; dan revitalisasi Balai Latihan Kerja;",""],[2,"138","5","Accelerated Development of Disadvantaged Regions","percepatan pembangunan daerah tertinggal dilaksanakan dengan fokus pada peningkatan kapasitas sumber daya manusia, dan pemenuhan pelayanan dasar yang memperhatikan aspek mitigasi dan kesiapsiagaan terhadap resiko bencana;",""],[2,"138","5","Support and Guidance for Previously Disadvantaged Regions","pembinaan dan keberpihakan dari K/L serta pelaku pembangunan lainnya dilakukan terhadap daerah tertinggal yang telah terentaskan tahun 2019, selama maksimal 3 tahun (2020 - 2022);","K/L"],[2,"138","5","Basic Services and Governance Improvement in Border Districts","pemenuhan pelayanan dasar dan peningkatan tata kelola di kecamatan perbatasan;",""],[2,"138","5","Affirmative Development Implementation","pelaksanaan pembangunan afirmatif.",""],[2,"140","6","Basic Services Improvement and Human Capital Development","(2) Peningkatan pelayanan dasar antara lain: (a) peningkatkan kualitas SDM khususnya peningkatan akses layanan pendidikan dan kesehatan, pendidikan vokasional pertanian, perikanan, industri dan pariwisata, dan revitalisasi Balai Latihan Kerja;",""]],"185":[[2,"114","2","Exclusive Economic Zone Surveillance and Protection","melalui: (vi) meningkatkan pengawasan dan penjagaan pada Zona Ekonomi Eksklusif (ZEE);",""]],"186":[[2,"114","5","Priority Strategic Area Development and Downstreaming Support","Optimalisasi pembangunan kawasan strategis prioritas sebagai pusat-pusat pertumbuhan wilayah, yaitu KEK, KI, KPBPB, Destinasi Pariwisata Prioritas, dan kawasan lainnya yang telah ditetapkan untuk mendorong hilirisasi dan penciptaan nilai tambah komoditas unggulan, perluasan kesempatan kerja, peningkatan pendapatan devisa dan penghematan devisa dari substitusi impor, khususnya hasil- hasil perkebunan, pertambangan, dan perikanan antara lain melalui: (i) penguatan basis produksi dan pengolahan komoditas unggulan daerah yang tersebar pada sentra-sentra hilirisasi pertanian dan perikanan di Kawasan Perdesaan Prioritas Nasional (KPPN), kawasan transmigrasi, Pusat Kegiatan Strategis Nasional (PKSN), dan Sentra Kelautan Perikanan Terpadu (SKPT)/Wilayah Pengelolaan Perikanan (WPP); (ii) pembangunan smelter pada kawasan potensial dalam mendukung hilirisasi Sumber Daya Alam (SDA); (iii) penyediaan jaringan infrastruktur secara terpadu yang meliputi jaringan transportasi (jalan, pelabuhan, bandara dan lainnya), sistem energi (listrik, gas, surya, batubara dan lainnya), fasilitas air baku dan air bersih, dan sistem pengolahan limbah; (iv) pelayanan perijinan dan investasi yang cepat; (v) penguatan konektivitas dengan pusat-pusat produksi bahan baku di kawasan perdesaan dan transmigrasi, kota-kota kecil, dan kota-kota menengah dalam pengadaan bahan baku dan pendukung; (vi) pengembangan kerjasama dan kemitraan pembiayaan pemerintah dan badan usaha; (vii) penguatan kerjasama Pemerintah Daerah, badan pengelola, masyarakat, perguruan tinggi dan media dalam promosi dan pengembangan kawasan strategis; serta (viii) perluasan kerjasama dan kemitraan dalam kerjasama mata rantai produksi global.",""]],"187":[[2,"124","6","Regional Research and Innovation Strengthening","peningkatan riset dan inovasi daerah untuk peningkatan kualitas pelayanan publik dan percepatan pembangunan",""],[2,"125","4","Interregional Cooperation for Regional Competitiveness and New Economic Centers","Pengembangan kerja sama antardaerah otonom dalam peningkatan daya saing daerah dan membangun sentra-sentra ekonomi baru, melalui;",""],[2,"125","8","Expansion of Local Government Partnerships and Collaboration","Perluasan kerjasama, kemitraan dan kolaborasi pemerintah daerah dengan mitra pembangunan dalam pelayanan publik, pengelolaan sumber daya alam dan lingkungan, pembiayaan dan investasi pembangunan, penyelesaian permasalahan publik bersama, dan pengembangan daya saing dan inovasi daerah.",""],[2,"135","2","Inter-Regional Cooperation in Metropolitan and Tourism-Industrial Areas","peningkatan kerja sama antardaerah otonom di wilayah metropolitan, termasuk wilayah pengembangan pariwisata, industri dan kepulauan.",""]],"188":[[2,"125","10","Strengthening the Governor's Role in Regional Development Coordination and Control","Penguatan peran gubernur melalui sebagai wakil Pemerintah Pusat dalam koordinasi dan pengendalian pembangunan daerah;",""],[2,"125","11","Harmonization and Synchronization of Planning, Budgeting, Procurement, Monitoring, Evaluation, and Audit Regulations","Harmonisasi dan sinkronisasi peraturan tentang perencanaan, penganggaran, pengadaan barang dan jasa, pengendalian dan evaluasi, serta audit antara pusat dan daerah; dan",""],[2,"125","12","Revision of Central-Regional Financial Relations Law","Penguatan hubungan keuangan pusat dan daerah melalui percepatan penyelesaian revisi Undang-undang Nomor 33 Tahun 2004 tentang Hubungan Keuangan Pusat dan Daerah, dan peraturan perundang-undangan lain mengenai manajemen keuangan daerah.",""]],"189":[[2,"130","6","Subdistrict Service and Innovation Hub Development","pengembangan dan penguatan peran kecamatan sebagai pusat data, informasi dan pengetahuan, pusat pelayanan dasar, pusat pemberdayaan masyarakat, pusat pengembangan inovasi dan kewirausahaan, pusat pengelolaan sumber daya alam dan lingkungan, serta pusat pertumbuhan ekonomi kabupaten;",""],[2,"133","2","Subdistrict Service and Innovation Hub Development","pengembangan dan penguatan peran kecamatan sebagai pusat data, informasi dan pengetahuan, pusat pelayanan dasar, pusat pemberdayaan masyarakat, pusat pengembangan inovasi dan kewirausahaan, pusat pengelolaan sumber daya alam dan lingkungan, serta pusat pertumbuhan ekonomi kabupaten;",""],[2,"134","6","Subdistrict Data and Knowledge Hub Development","(b) pengembangan dan penguatan peran kecamatan sebagai pusat data, informasi dan pengetahuan,",""],[2,"135","2","District Service, Empowerment, Innovation, Natural Resource, and Economic Growth Centers","pusat pelayanan dasar, pusat pemberdayaan masyarakat, pusat pengembangan inovasi dan kewirausahaan, pusat pengelolaan sumber daya alam dan lingkungan, serta pusat pertumbuhan ekonomi kabupaten;",""],[2,"137","2","Subdistrict Service and Innovation Hub Development","pengembangan dan penguatan peran kecamatan sebagai pusat data, informasi dan pengetahuan, pusat pelayanan dasar, pusat pemberdayaan masyarakat, pusat pengembangan inovasi dan kewirausahaan, pusat pengelolaan sumber daya alam dan lingkungan, serta pusat pertumbuhan ekonomi kabupaten;",""],[2,"139","3","Subdistrict Service and Innovation Hub Development","pengembangan dan penguatan peran kecamatan sebagai pusat data, informasi dan pengetahuan, pusat pelayanan dasar; pusat pemberdayaan masyarakat, pusat pengembangan inovasi dan kewirausahaan, pusat pengelolaan sumber daya alam dan lingkungan, serta pusat pertumbuhan ekonomi kabupaten;",""],[2,"140","8","Subdistrict Service and Innovation Center Development","(b) pengembangan dan penguatan peran kecamatan sebagai pusat data, informasi dan pengetahuan, pusat pelayanan dasar, pusat pemberdayaan masyarakat, pusat pengembangan inovasi dan kewirausahaan, pusat pengelolaan sumber daya alam dan lingkungan, serta pusat",""]],"190":[[2,"164","9","Population Control Policy Synergy Strengthening","Penguatan sinergitas kebijakan pengendalian penduduk dalam mewujudkan penduduk tumbuh seimbang;",""],[2,"164","10","Institutional Capacity Strengthening for Population Control","Penguatan kapasitas dan kapabilitas kelembagaan pusat, provinsi serta kabupaten dan kota dalam bidang pengendalian penduduk; dan",""]],"191":[[2,"164","13","Comprehensive and Integrated SJSN Development Program","Pengembangan program SJSN yang komprehensif dan terintegrasi, termasuk pengembangan Jaminan Pekerjaan (Unemployment Benefit), Perawatan Jangka Panjang (Long Term Care) berbasis kontribusi, dan Program Rehabilitasi Kerja (Return to Work);",""],[2,"165","2","SJSN Financing Sustainability and Governance Strengthening","Keberlanjutan pendanaan dan penguatan tata kelola SJSN, termasuk perluasan dan pengembangan sistem kepesertaan, sinergi data dasar kependudukan, Data Terpadu Kesejahteraan Sosial (DTKS) dan data BPJS kesehatan dan ketenagakerjaan, penyesuaian sistem iuran, tarif dan paket manfaat, dan perbaikan sistem tata kelola SJSN didukung dengan pembangunan sistem monitoring dan evaluasi yang terintegrasi, serta pengembangan sistem pencegahan dan penanganan kecurangan pelaksanaan jaminan sosial;",""],[2,"165","4","Strengthening of SJSN Institutional Framework","Penguatan kelembagaan SJSN termasuk perbaikan tata kelola hubungan antarlembaga dan harmonisasi peraturan perundangan yang terkait, dan integrasi implementasi operasional JKN dan SJSN Ketenagakerjaan.",""]],"192":[[2,"168","4","Medical Waste and Hazardous Substance Management","penyediaan pengelolaan limbah medis fasilitas pelayanan kesehatan dan pengendalian bahan berbahaya dan beracun (B3);",""]],"193":[[2,"95","4","Marine Tourism Development in Water Tourism Parks and Marine Nature Reserves","serta 6 wisata bahari yang berbasis Taman Wisata Perairan dan Suaka Alam Perairan",""]],"194":[[2,"188","8","Literacy Culture Enhancement Programme","Peningkatan budaya literasi, mencakup: (a) pengembangan budaya kegemaran membaca; (b) pengembangan sistem perbukuan dan penguatan konten literasi; dan (c) peningkatan akses dan kualitas perpustakaan berbasis inklusi sosial.",""],[2,"188","10","Science, Technology, Innovation, and Creativity Culture Development","Pengembangan budaya Iptek, inovasi, kreativitas, dan daya cipta, mencakup: (a) peningkatan budaya riset dan ekperimentasi ilmiah sejak usia dini; dan (b) pengembangan budaya produksi dan kreativitas berbasis inovasi.",""],[2,"188","11","Social Institution Strengthening for Literacy and Innovation","Penguatan institusi sosial penggerak literasi dan inovasi, mencakup: (a) pengembangan mitra perpustakaan (library supporter); (b) pengembangan inovasi sosial yang didukung oleh pendanaan filantropi.",""]],"195":[[2,"213","7","River Flow Normalization and Capacity Enhancement","Normalisasi dan peningkatan kapasitas aliran sungai",""],[2,"213","7","Wetland and Peatland Conservation","Konservasi kawasan rawa dan gambut",""],[2,"213","7","Pollution Control for Reservoirs and Lakes","Pengendalian pencemaran pada waduk dan danau dengan tingkat pencemaran tinggi",""]],"196":[[2,"220","3","Energy and Electricity Diversification Programme","Diversifikasi energi dan ketenagalistrikan untuk pemenuhan kebutuhan, ditempuh melalui (a) peningkatan EBT seperti panas bumi, air, surya, dan biomasa, serta EBT lainnya; (b) pengembangan mini/micro grid berbasis energi bersih; (c) pengembangan dan pemanfaatan teknologi penyimpanan energi (energy storage system) termasuk baterai; serta (d) pemanfaatan energi surya atap (solar rooftop) dan PLTS terapung (floating solar power plant) beserta pengembangan industri sel surya dalam negeri;",""],[2,"220","4","Energy Service Company Development","Peningkatan efisiensi pemanfaatan energi dan tenaga listrik, melalui (a) pengembangan Energy Service Company (ESCO);",""],[2,"220","4","Transmission and Distribution System Expansion and Rehabilitation","memperluas, merehabilitasi dan peningkatan kapasitas sistem transmisi dan distribusi;",""],[2,"220","4","Energy Information and Data Control Management System Development","pengembangan sistem manajemen informasi dan kontrol data;",""],[2,"220","4","Smart Grid Development and Deployment","pengembangan dan pemanfaatan teknologi jaringan cerdas (smart grid)",""],[2,"220","4","High-Efficiency and Low-Emission Technology Adoption","pemanfaatan teknologi yang lebih efisien dan rendah emisi (high efficiency and low emission/HELE).",""],[2,"220","6","Energy and Electricity Governance Improvement","Peningkatan tata kelola energi dan ketenagalistrikan, ditempuh melalui (a) peningkatan tugas dan fungsi kelembagaan di sektor ketenagalistrikan; (b) penguatan independensi operator sistem transmisi; serta (c) mendorong kebijakan harga/tarif energi dan penerapannya sehingga mencapai harga keekonomian secara bertahap.",""],[2,"220","7","Targeted Subsidy and Sustainable Financing Policy Development","Pengembangan kebijakan pendanaan dan pembiayaan, ditempuh melalui (a) pengembangan subsidi tepat sasaran melalui subsidi langsung dan realokasi belanja; (b) penerapan penyesuaian tarif listrik dan harga energi; (c) memanfaatkan pembiayaan dengan persyaratan yang ringan dan wajar, alternatif instrumen dan leverage asset; serta (d) pengembangan skema pendanaan yang sesuai dan berkesinambungan.",""],[2,"220","8","Energy Efficiency and Emissions Reduction Project","Proyek prioritas mendukung keberlanjutan penyediaan energi ketenagalistrikan meliputi: perbaikan efisiensi dan penurunan emisi.",""]],"197":[[2,"226","6","Environmental and Forestry Law Enforcement","Capaian kinerja penegakan hukum untuk mendukung pengelolaan lingkungan hidup dan kehutanan semakin meningkat dalam aspek penanganan pengaduan, pengawasan izin; pemberian sanksi administratif, penyelesaian sengketa di luar pengadilan, serta penegakan hukum pidana.",""],[2,"226","6","Interagency Cooperation for Court Decision Enforcement","Kedepannya dalam penyelesaian eksekusi akan dicoba melalui pendekatan kerja sama dengan melibatkan institusi penegakan hukum lainnya.",""]],"198":[[2,"249","7","Sustainable Energy Development","Pembangunan Energi Berkelanjutan, yang dilaksanakan melalui: (a) Pengelolaan Energi Baru Terbarukan melalui pengembangan pembangkit energi terbarukan serta meningkatkan pasokan bahan bakar nabati dari bahan baku rendah karbon; serta (b) Efisiensi dan Konservasi Energi.",""],[2,"276","14","Revision of the 3 Kg LPG Cylinder Supply, Distribution, and Pricing Regulation","Revisi Perpres Nomor 104 / Tahun 2007 tentang Penyediaan, Pendistribusian dan Penetapan Harga LPG Tabung 3 Kg",""],[2,"276","15","Revision of the Presidential Regulation on LPG Provision, Distribution, and Pricing","Revisi Perpres Nomor 38 / Tahun 2019 tentang Penyediaan, Pendistribusian dan Penetapan Harga LPG untuk Kapal Penangkap Ikan Bagi Nelayan Sasaran dan Mesin Pompa Air bagi Petani Sasaran",""]],"199":[[2,"249","8","Sustainable Land Restoration Program","Pemulihan Lahan Berkelanjutan yang dilaksanakan melalui: (a) Restorasi dan Pemulihan Lahan Gambut; (b) Rehabilitasi Hutan dan Lahan; (c) Pengurangan Laju Deforestasi; serta (d) Peningkatan Produktivitas dan Efisiensi Pertanian menuju Pertanian Berkelanjutan.",""],[2,"249","11","Low-Carbon Coastal and Marine Program","Rendah Karbon Pesisir dan Laut yang dilaksanakan melalui Inventarisasi dan Rehabilitasi Ekosistem Pesisir dan Kelautan.",""]],"200":[[2,"256","4","Public Diplomacy Synergy for Indonesia's International Image","perlunya sinergi diplomasi publik yang lebih mengaktualisasi kekayaan sosial budaya, seperti: kuliner, kebhinekaan, dan toleransi, guna meningkatkan citra positif Indonesia di pergaulan internasional.",""],[2,"256","4","Agreement on Indonesia's International Image Vision","Selain itu, perlu ada kesepakatan tentang visi citra Indonesia yang akan ditampilkan kepada publik internasional.",""],[2,"256","5","Total Diplomacy Foreign Policy Governance Strengthening","Keempat, perlunya penguatan kepemimpinan dan tata kelola dalam merespons perkembangan dinamika global dengan pendekatan diplomasi total.",""],[2,"263","19","Strengthening Protection of Citizens Abroad","Penguatan perlindungan WNI dan BHI di tingkat bilateral, regional, dan multilateral serta meningkatkan upaya pencegahan terjadinya masalah WNI di luar negeri;",""],[2,"263","27","Indonesia Public Diplomacy Policy Development","Penyusunan kebijakan diplomasi publik Indonesia untuk meningkatkan koordinasi di tingkat nasional;",""],[2,"264","5","Domestic Coordination for International Commitments","Peningkatan koordinasi di dalam negeri untuk melaksanakan komitmen internasional;",""]],"201":[[2,"283","4","Project-Based Sukuk for Infrastructure and Public Services","SBSN Sukuk Berbasis Proyek (Project Based Sukuk) (SBSN-PBS) pemanfaatannya lebih diutamakan untuk pembangunan infrastrukur dan penyediaan sarana pelayanan umum.",""],[2,"283","7","Public-Private Partnership Scheme for Public Infrastructure","Kerjasama Pemerintah dan Badan Usaha (KPBU), merupakan kerjasama antara pemerintah dengan badan usaha dalam menyediakan sarana dan prasarana layanan umum berdasarkan pembagian risiko antara pemerintah dan swasta.",""],[2,"289","8","Public-Private Partnership Financing Expansion","Untuk pembiayaan program di pusat maupun di daerah, skema Kerjasama Pemerintah Badan Usaha/ Public Private Partnership (KPBU/PPP), peningkatan peran swasta melalui kegiatan Tanggung Jawab Sosial Perusahaan (Corporate Social Responsibility/CSR), pinjaman langsung (direct lending) dari mitra pembangunan kepada BUMN, dan Dana Pembangunan Daerah (Municipal Development Fund/MDF) akan terus dikembangkan.",""],[2,"290","2","Expansion of Public-Private Partnership Use in Social Sectors","Pemanfaatan KPBU untuk pembangunan nasional akan terus diperluas dan dikembangkan untuk sektor sosial antara lain pendidikan, kesehatan, dan lain- lain.",""],[2,"290","2","Regulatory Improvement for Social Sector PPPs","Pengembangan pemanfaatan KPBU di sektor sosial disertai dengan penyempurnaan terhadap peraturan perundangan yang berlaku.",""],[2,"290","2","Alignment of CSR Activities with Government Programmes","Sedangkan pemanfaatan CSR diarahkan pada peningkatan keselarasan kegiatannya dengan program pemerintah dalam mendukung pembangunan nasional.",""],[2,"290","4","Public Investment Management Improvement","Untuk itu, diperlukan adanya pendekatan pengelolaan pendanaan untuk mendorong pertumbuhan dan kinerja investasi publik.",""],[2,"290","4","Public Investment Planning Process Reform","Peningkatan efisiensi dan kinerja investasi publik mensyaratkan adanya perbaikan proses perencanaan investasi di semua sektor dan tingkat pemerintahan, termasuk dalam mengalokasikan investasi Pemerintah untuk sektor dan proyek yang tepat sehingga memberi daya ungkit (leverage), melaksanakan proyek tepat waktu dan tepat biaya serta peningkatan kapasitas dan efisiensi kelembagaan.",""],[2,"290","4","Private Sector and Community Financing Incentive Measures","Upaya tersebut dilakukan bersamaan dengan pemberian stimulus bagi pihak swasta dan masyarakat melalui regulasi dan kebijakan yang memberikan insentif dalam rangka mengoptimalkan peran pembiayaan non- Pemerintah dalam pembiayaan pembangunan nasional (investasi publik).",""],[2,"290","5","Public Investment Planning and Governance Reform","Peningkatan kapasitas pembiayaan dan kualitas investasi Pemerintah dilakukan dengan memperbaiki perencanaan dan kebijakan investasi publik, manajemen, tata kelola dan kebijakan, serta pemilihan proyek yang didasarkan pada kriteria keberlanjutan lingkungan dan sosial.",""],[2,"290","5","Long-Term National, Regional, and Sectoral Investment Planning","Untuk itu strategi pembangunan nasional, wilayah dan sektoral akan diperjelas dengan menyertakan rencana investasi untuk memandu investasi publik maupun swasta dalam jangka panjang.",""],[2,"290","6","Sustainable Government Procurement Process","Pemerintah juga terus mengembangkan dan mengimplementasikan proses pengadaan Pemerintah yang memasukkan kriteria keberlanjutan dengan pendekatan yang lebih sistematis dan konsisten didasarkan pada praktik yang baik (best practice).",""],[2,"292","3","Public-Private Partnership Scheme Strengthening","Pemerintah akan terus meningkatkan pemanfaatan skema KPBU dengan melakukan perkuatan pada beberapa aspek yaitu: regulasi; fungsi kantor bersama; peran empat pilar KPBU (regulator, penanggung jawab proyek kerjasama (investee), konsultan pendamping (transaction advisor), dan investor), perencanaan dan penyiapan proyek, serta internalisasi KPBU dalam dokumen perencanaan dan penganggaran pemerintah pusat maupun daerah.",""]],"202":[[2,"273","8","Revision of Government Regulation No. 57 of 2010 on Mergers, Consolidations, and Share Acquisitions","Revisi PP No. 57 Tahun 2010 tentang Penggabungan atau Peleburan Badan Usaha dan Pengambilalihan Saham Perusahaan;",""],[2,"273","9","Competition Violation Case Handling and Administrative Sanctions Regulation","RPP Tata Cara Penanganan Perkara dan Pengenaan Sanksi Administratif Pelanggaran Persaingan Usaha;",""]]}});